1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,188
欢迎。
Welcome.

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:09,668
本课程旨在帮助你备考 AWS Certified Data Engineer Associate 认证考试，考试代码为 B，DEA-C01。
This course prepares you for the AWS Certified Data Engineer Associate Exam, exam code B, EAC01.

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:13,280
在进入任何技术内容之前，请先花 9 分钟听这里的内容。
Before any of the technical content, spend 9 minutes here.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:17,828
本模块涵盖了考试实际考核的内容以及评分方式。
This module covers what the exam actually measures and how it is scored.

5
00:00:18,318 --> 00:00:21,412
它还涵盖了近期大纲中的变化。
It also covers what changed in the syllabus recently.

6
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:28,580
接着，它会讲解如何高效学习，让你真正提高分数，而不仅仅是感觉在努力。
Then it covers how to study in a way that moves your score rather than just feeling productive.

7
00:00:29,422 --> 00:00:33,028
最后一部分的重要性比大多数人预想的要高。
That last part matters more than most people expect.

8
00:00:34,414 --> 00:00:40,612
关于这些内容来源的一点说明，因为它对你的学习效果有很大影响。
A word on where this content comes from because it makes a real difference to what you get out of it.

9
00:00:41,198 --> 00:00:45,732
这类类别中的大部分备考资料都是从泄露的题库中回收的。
Most preparation material in this category is recycled from leaked question banks.

10
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:49,700
那样的课程只是教你识别特定的题目。
Courses like that teach you to recognize specific questions.

11
00:00:50,414 --> 00:00:52,484
它们并没有教你如何回答新题。
They do not teach you to answer new ones.

12
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:55,108
本课程的构建方式不同。
This course was built differently.

13
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:02,404
我们分析了一个包含 341 道题的题库，但仅仅是为了找出考试测试哪些决策以及出现的频率。
A bank of 341 questions was analyzed, but only to work out which decisions the exam tests and how often.

14
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:07,460
这个题库中的任何选项或解释都不会出现在本课程中。
Not one question option or explanation from it appears anywhere in this course.

15
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:17,348
你将看到的每一个场景都是原创的，且每个解释都追溯到 AWS 文档或发布的考试指南。
Every scenario you will see is original and every explanation traces back to AWS documentation or the published exam guide.

16
00:01:19,022 --> 00:01:27,440
AWS 将目标候选人描述为具有 2 到 3 年数据工程经验，并有 1 到 2 年实操经验的人员
AWS describes the target candidate as someone with 2 to 3 years of data engineering experience and 1 to 2 years of hands-on

17
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,484
AWS。
AWS.

18
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:35,972
这就是题目设定的水平。注意第四项的重要性与你可能预想的前两项一样重要。
That is the level the questions are pitched at. Notice the fourth item carries as much weight as you might expect the first two.

19
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:43,600
安全和治理并不是这门考试中的次要内容。并且请注意哪些内容明确属于超出范围。
Security and governance is not a footnote on this exam. And notice what is explicitly out of scope.

20
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:49,360
你不需要训练机器学习模型。也不会被要求掌握特定语言的语法。
You are not asked to train machine learning models. You are not asked for language-specific syntax.

21
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:52,964
而且你永远不会被要求从数据中得出商业结论。
And you are never asked to draw a business conclusion from data.

22
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:59,140
如果某个选项似乎需要其中任何一项，那它几乎肯定是一个干扰项。
If an option seems to require one of those, it is almost certainly a distractor.

23
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:03,460
这些数据中的一些内容会影响你在考场上的应对策略。
Some of these numbers change how you should behave in the room.

24
00:02:03,982 --> 00:02:08,880
在 65 道题中，有 15 道是不计分的试题，且它们不会被标注出来。
15 of the 65 questions are unscored trial questions and they are not marked as such.

25
00:02:09,102 --> 00:02:13,604
所以，如果某道题目感觉很奇怪或者莫名其妙，它可能根本不计分。
So a question that feels bizarre or unreasonably obscure may simply not count.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,840
不要被它干扰。
Do not let it rattle you.

27
00:02:16,398 --> 00:02:24,772
评分是补偿性的，这意味着弱项可以由强项来弥补。你只需要总分达到 720 分，而不是每个部分都必须通过。
The scoring is compensatory, which means a weak domain can be carried by strong ones. You need 720 overall, not a pass in each section.

28
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:29,156
未回答的题目计为错误，但猜错不会扣分。
An unanswered question score as incorrect with no penalty for a wrong guess.

29
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,588
没有任何理由空着不填。
There is never a reason to leave one blank.

30
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:37,348
这些权重直接来自考试指南，本课程也与之对应。
These weights come straight from the exam guide, and this course mirrors them.

31
00:02:40,782 --> 00:02:44,480
这听起来显而易见，但很多自学的人就在这里出错。
That sounds obvious, but it is where a lot of self-study goes wrong.

32
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:53,120
题库高度偏向 Glue、S3 和 Redshift，因为这些服务几乎出现在每一个场景的描述中。
Question banks are heavily skewed towards Glue, S3, and Redshift because those services appear in the wording of almost every scenario.

33
00:02:53,774 --> 00:03:02,020
在为本课程分析的题库中，安全相关术语占比不到 5%，而安全在考试中占 18%。
In the bank, analyzed for this course, security terms accounted for under 5% of mentions, while security is 18% of the exam.

34
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:10,640
如果你只按那个重点去复习，你就会在那个完全可以避免出现差距的领域里，错过大约 9 道得分题。
Study from that emphasis and you walk in around 9 scored questions short in the one domain where the gap is entirely avoidable.

35
00:03:11,982 --> 00:03:18,308
现在是本模块最重要的内容，也是为什么要看这段介绍而不是直接跳到模块 1 的原因。
Now the most important thing in this module and the reason to watch an introduction rather than skip to module 1.

36
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:26,660
AWS 在 2025 年 12 月发布了考试指南的 1.1 版本。
AWS published version 1.1 of the exam guide in December 2025.

37
00:03:27,054 --> 00:03:29,252
它增加了 8 项新技能。
It added 8 new skills.

38
00:03:29,742 --> 00:03:34,212
目前几乎所有可用的题库和视频课程都早于这个版本。
Almost every question bank and video course currently available predates it.

39
00:03:36,046 --> 00:03:41,956
如果你已经开始用其他资料复习，很有可能存在盲点。
If you have already started studying from other material, there is a good chance you have a blind spot.

40
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:46,052
这是你在那些材料中看不出来的盲点。
It is a blind spot you cannot see from inside that material.

41
00:03:46,574 --> 00:03:49,680
接下来的两页幻灯片会准确告诉你是什么。
The next two slides tell you exactly what it is.

42
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:55,748
这些是真正全新的领域，而不是更名后的旧内容。
These are genuinely new areas, not renamed old ones.

43
00:03:58,222 --> 00:04:00,036
特别是 Iceberg，它已经更新了。
Iceberg in particular has moved on.

44
00:04:00,590 --> 00:04:03,140
它以前只是一个你可能会提到的文件格式。
It was a file format you might mention.

45
00:04:03,854 --> 00:04:10,596
现在它是一个拥有独立维护模型的托管功能，并且在本课程中有一个专门的模块。
It is now a managed capability with its own maintenance model and it has a dedicated module in this course.

46
00:04:11,694 --> 00:04:14,340
还有三个服务从考核范围中删除了。
Three services were also removed from scope.

47
00:04:15,182 --> 00:04:21,091
分别是 AWS Cloud9、AWS Code Commit 和 AWS Schema Conversion Tool。
AWS Cloud9, AWS Code Commit, and the AWS Schema Conversion Tool.

48
00:04:22,318 --> 00:04:24,548
有一件值得知道的怪事。
There is one oddity worth knowing.

49
00:04:26,446 --> 00:04:30,692
一个任务陈述仍然将 架构转换 tool 作为示例。
A task statement still names the schema conversion tool as an example.

50
00:04:32,174 --> 00:04:36,992
然而，该工具却从同一个部分的在范围内服务列表中被删除了。
Yet the tool was removed from the inScope service list in the same division.

51
00:04:37,518 --> 00:04:44,132
当指南出现这种自相矛盾的情况时，去学习相关概念，而不要纠结于产品的时间线。
When the guide contradicts itself like that, learn the concept and do not sync time into the product.

52
00:04:45,614 --> 00:04:51,140
认证内容总是滞后于产品目录，这次考试也不例外。
Certification content always lags the product catalog, and this exam is no exception.

53
00:04:51,566 --> 00:04:53,924
第一项是最典型的例子。
The first item is the sharpest example.

54
00:04:55,950 --> 00:05:00,324
Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 在旧材料中是一个正确答案。
Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL was a correct answer in older material.

55
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:05,700
而从 2026 年 1 月起，这些应用已经被彻底删除。
And as of January 2026, the applications have been deleted outright.

56
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:07,844
你现在无法购买它了。
You cannot buy it.

57
00:05:08,238 --> 00:05:10,308
它可能仍会出现在题目的措辞中。
It may still appear in question wording.

58
00:05:12,654 --> 00:05:14,596
这两个更名的情况影响不同。
The two renames matter differently.

59
00:05:15,246 --> 00:05:22,672
练习题中同时会出现旧名称和新名称，所以你需要识别出两者并知道它们是同一个产品。
Both old and new names circulate in practice questions, so you need to recognize either and know they are the same product.

60
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:28,484
每当这在课程中出现时，相关的幻灯片都会明确说明发生了什么变化。
Wherever this comes up in the course, the affected slide says plainly what changed,

61
00:05:29,198 --> 00:05:31,140
什么时候被替换以及被什么取代。
when and what replaced it.

62
00:05:32,782 --> 00:05:35,236
5个区块包含27个模块。
27 modules in 5 blocks.

63
00:05:35,712 --> 00:05:37,348
这个顺序是经过精心设计的。
The order is deliberate.

64
00:05:37,632 --> 00:05:40,612
领域模块在前，用来建立词汇基础。
The domain modules come first and build vocabulary.

65
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:46,212
当你到达混淆项对模块时，你不再是在学习服务了。
By the time you reach the confusion pairs module, you are not learning services.

66
00:05:46,672 --> 00:05:49,732
你是在学习在时间压力下区分它们。
You are learning to tell them apart under time pressure.

67
00:05:50,702 --> 00:05:57,796
那个模块几乎没有新内容，但在这种课程中，它往往是最有价值的20分钟。
That module contains almost no new content and it is often the most valuable 20 minutes in a course like this.

68
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:02,820
考试机制模块完全不包含产品内容。
The exam mechanics module contains no product content at all.

69
00:06:03,472 --> 00:06:13,540
它是关于AWS如何出题，而且能稳拿分数，因为很大一部分错误答案是由于误读而非知识匮乏造成的。
It is about how AWS writes questions and it reliably gains marks because a real share of wrong answers come from misreading rather than not knowing.

70
00:06:14,958 --> 00:06:20,676
这些模块中大约有90个工作场景，外加60道模拟考试题。
There are around 90 work scenarios across these modules plus 60 practice exam questions.

71
00:06:21,134 --> 00:06:22,724
每一项包含两页幻灯片。
Each one is two slides.

72
00:06:23,022 --> 00:06:27,236
首先是情况和选项，然后停顿一下，接着是解析过程。
First, the situation and the options, then a pause, then the walkthrough.

73
00:06:27,472 --> 00:06:29,700
当到停顿的时候，真的去选一个。
When the pause comes, actually choose.

74
00:06:30,222 --> 00:06:32,644
如果你是一个人，就把字母大声说出来。
Say the letter out loud if you are alone.

75
00:06:33,646 --> 00:06:40,740
在不先做决定的情况下看解析过程感觉像是在学习，但其实几乎毫无用处，因为你永远不知道自己原本会错在哪。
Watching a walkthrough without committing first feels like learning and is very close to worthless because you never find out what you would have got wrong.

76
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:46,244
做出选择并不舒服，但这正是它有效的核心原因。
Committing is uncomfortable, which is exactly why it works.

77
00:06:46,926 --> 00:06:50,948
让我先给你们展示一下这种形式，这样到关键时刻你就熟悉这个格式了。
Let me show you the shape once so the format is familiar when it matters.

78
00:06:52,718 --> 00:06:56,932
一家零售公司每晚将点击流文件上传到Amazon S3。
A retail company loads clickstream files into Amazon S3 every night.

79
00:06:57,454 --> 00:07:04,932
一名分析师每天早上对原始JSON文件运行相同的三个聚合查询，而这些查询变得缓慢且昂贵。
An analyst runs the same three aggregate queries each morning against the raw JSON files, and those queries have become slow and expensive.

80
00:07:05,422 --> 00:07:07,556
公司希望降低查询成本。
The company wants to reduce query cost.

81
00:07:08,462 --> 00:07:14,660
没有人会在早上9点前等待结果，而且工程团队没有能力去运营一个新的流水线。
Nobody is waiting on the results before 9 in the morning, and the engineering team has no capacity to operate a new pipeline.

82
00:07:15,662 --> 00:07:19,524
哪种改变能在产生最少运维开销的情况下降低查询成本？
Which change will reduce query cost with the least operational overhead?

83
00:07:20,718 --> 00:07:26,084
A. 将数据加载到Amazon Redshift预置集群中并在那里进行查询。
a Load the data into an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and query it there.

84
00:07:28,878 --> 00:07:34,916
B. 使用AWS Glue job将文件转换为Apache Parquet，并按日期进行分区。
Convert the files to Apache Parquet and partition by date using an AWS Blue job.

85
00:07:35,726 --> 00:07:36,032
C。
C.

86
00:07:36,654 --> 00:07:40,164
增加Amazon Athena工作组的数据扫描限制。
Increase the Amazon Athena work group data scan limit.

87
00:07:40,718 --> 00:07:40,992
D。
D.

88
00:07:41,582 --> 00:07:46,352
将文件移动到S3 Glacier，在查询之间进行深度归档。
Move the files to S3 Glacier, deep archive between queries.

89
00:07:47,534 --> 00:07:48,912
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

90
00:07:55,662 --> 00:07:59,620
答案是B，但这里的重点不在于答案本身。
The answer is B, but the answer is not the lesson here.

91
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:02,564
看看这道题是怎么决定的。
Look at how the question was decided.

92
00:08:02,816 --> 00:08:04,612
这两句话起到了关键作用。
Two sentences did the work.

93
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:12,484
没人会在早上 9 点之前等待，所以延迟不是约束条件，因此不需要昂贵的低延迟存储。
Nobody is waiting before 9 in the morning does you latency is not a constraint, so an expensive low latency store is not needed.

94
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:19,428
没有能力运营新的流水线，这在对比任何技术优势之前就排除了选项 A。
No capacity to operate a new pipeline eliminates option A before you compare a single technical merit.

95
00:08:20,014 --> 00:08:22,628
选项 C 是这次考试中的经典陷阱。
Option C is the classic trap on this exam.

96
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:27,236
这个设置的名字听起来相关，但实际操作却与要求的相反。
A setting whose name sounds relevant while doing the opposite of what was asked.

97
00:08:28,078 --> 00:08:35,812
学会把这两句话当作指令来读，而不是背景信息，这是区分通过和险些失败的关键。
Learning to read those two sentences as instructions rather than as background color is most of what separates a pass from a near miss.

98
00:08:38,606 --> 00:08:40,256
这是学习路线。
Here is the study route.

99
00:08:40,429 --> 00:08:45,988
按顺序看一遍所有模块。然后在限时条件下做模拟考试 1。
Watch the modules in order once. Then sit practice exam 1 under timed conditions.

100
00:08:46,256 --> 00:08:52,548
接着，这是很多人会跳过的部分：不要只看分数，要看看错误答案集中在哪些领域。
Then, and this is the part people skip, look at where the wrong answers cluster rather than at the score.

101
00:08:53,102 --> 00:08:54,948
只重温那个特定的领域。
Re-watch only that domain.

102
00:08:55,790 --> 00:09:03,204
几天后再做模拟考试 2，而不是就在同一天晚上做，因为拉开间隔能让它变成诊断性测试，而不是记忆力测试。
Take exam 2 a few days later, not the same evening, because spacing them is what makes them diagnostic rather than a memory test.

103
00:09:04,878 --> 00:09:10,500
左列是陷阱，因为它听起来很顺耳，所以才具有诱惑力。
The left column is the trap and it is seductive precisely because it is comfortable.

104
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:15,716
反复温习你已经掌握的内容只会让你的分数保持高位，但学不到任何东西。
Revising what you already know keeps your scores high and teaches you nothing.

105
00:09:17,486 --> 00:09:19,044
开始之前有五件事要注意。
Five things before we begin.

106
00:09:19,662 --> 00:09:25,540
在浏览器标签页中打开官方考试指南，因为它是唯一权威的考查范围清单。
Keep the official exam guide open in a tab because it is the only authoritative list of what is in scope.

107
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:30,736
如果你有 AWS 账号，就针对每个领域构建一个小的东西。
If you have an AWS account, build one small thing per domain.

108
00:09:30,976 --> 00:09:34,660
一个你实际运行过的 Glue作业，比看一小时视频更有用。
A single blue job you actually ran will outlast an hour of watching.

109
00:09:36,718 --> 00:09:38,500
留意那些限定词。
Expect the qualifier words.

110
00:09:39,374 --> 00:09:44,576
在为本课程分析的题库中，「运维开销最少」这个短语出现了 71 次。
In the bank analyzed for this course, least operational overhead appeared 71 times.

111
00:09:44,878 --> 00:09:47,556
这是在 341 道题目中出现的。
That is across 341 questions.

112
00:09:49,838 --> 00:09:52,416
「成本效益最高」出现了 42 次。
Most cost effective appeared 42 times.

113
00:09:52,576 --> 00:09:57,572
大约每三道题中就有一道是靠限定词决定的，而不是靠产品知识。
Roughly one question in three is decided by the qualifier rather than by product knowledge.

114
00:09:58,478 --> 00:10:02,884
接下来是模块 1，它是所有其他内容都基于的思维模型。
Module 1 is next, and it is the mental model that everything else hangs on.

115
00:10:04,494 --> 00:10:09,696
这个模块不包含新服务。它是后续所有模块赖以生存的框架。
This module has no new services in it. It is the frame that every later module hangs on.

116
00:10:09,966 --> 00:10:13,456
到最后，你将对任何数据流水线拥有一个五阶段的清晰概念。
By the end, you will have a 5-stage picture of any data pipeline.

117
00:10:13,616 --> 00:10:21,956
你会学会辨别题目真正涉及哪个约束条件，并掌握 AWS 用来标识每个条件的术语。
You will have a way of reading which constraint a question is really about, and you will have the vocabulary AWS uses to signal each one.

118
00:10:22,638 --> 00:10:25,956
花点时间在这上面，而不是直接跳到具体服务。
Spend the time here rather than skipping to the services.

119
00:10:26,446 --> 00:10:31,136
参加考试失败的候选人很少是因为没听说过某个服务。
Candidates who fail this exam rarely fail because they had never heard of a service.

120
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:36,708
他们失败是因为在倒计时还剩 40 秒时，四个选项听起来都像合理的答案。
They fail because four options all sounded plausible with 40 seconds left on the clock.

121
00:10:37,422 --> 00:10:40,708
本模块中的所有内容都是为了缩短那个过程。
Everything in this module exists to make that moment shorter.

122
00:10:41,998 --> 00:10:47,456
这是在学习任何服务之前最需要理解的一件事。
Here is the single most useful thing to understand before you study any service.

123
00:10:48,046 --> 00:10:49,696
这不是一道考查记忆的题目。
This is not a recall exam.

124
00:10:49,806 --> 00:10:53,188
你很少会遇到一个在技术上根本无法实现的选项。
You are rarely offered an option that is technically impossible.

125
00:10:53,934 --> 00:11:01,060
你会看到三个或四个都能成功传输数据的架构，然后被要求选出符合特定约束条件的那一个。
You are offered three or four architectures that would all move the data successfully and asked which one fits a stated constraint.

126
00:11:01,616 --> 00:11:04,900
这就是为什么仅仅知道一个服务的功能是不够的。
That is why knowing what a service does is not enough.

127
00:11:05,616 --> 00:11:11,972
你还需要了解每个选项在金钱、延迟以及运维工作上的成本。
You need to know what each one costs you in money, in latency, and in the work of running it.

128
00:11:13,230 --> 00:11:19,108
无论使用什么服务，考试中的每一个流水线都可以分解为这五个阶段。
Every pipeline on this exam decomposes into these five stages, whatever services it uses.

129
00:11:19,726 --> 00:11:24,804
当题目描述一个情景时，在阅读选项之前先把它放在这条线上。
When a question describes a situation, place it on this line before you read the options.

130
00:11:25,646 --> 00:11:30,692
关于早晨报告变慢的问题，是一个处理问题，可能也是一个存储问题。
A question about a slow morning report is a serve problem and possibly a store problem.

131
00:11:31,470 --> 00:11:37,220
无论题目中如何强调数据是如何到达的，这几乎绝不是一个摄入问题。
It is almost never an ingest problem, however much the question talks about how the data arrives.

132
00:11:37,774 --> 00:11:44,868
这听起来很简单，但它能让你避开一类错误答案，即那些优化了并非瓶颈环节的选项。
That sounds trivial and it saves you from a whole class of wrong answer where an option optimizes a stage that was never the bottleneck.

133
00:11:45,358 --> 00:11:46,564
注意这个特别说明。
Notice the call out.

134
00:11:47,374 --> 00:11:52,484
治理和监控不是在最后强加的第六个阶段，它们适用于所有五个阶段。
Governance and monitoring are not a sixth stage you bolt on at the end. They apply to all five.

135
00:11:53,230 --> 00:11:58,244
这就是为什么安全占考试的 18%，而考试中从未出现过纯粹的“安全流水线”。
That is exactly why security is 18% of an exam that never has a security-only pipeline.

136
00:11:59,726 --> 00:12:03,620
这种对应关系并非完美清晰，这个例外值得记住。
The mapping is not perfectly clean and the exception is worth remembering.

137
00:12:04,718 --> 00:12:12,656
编排在领域 1 中体现为构建工作流，在领域 3 中再次出现，作为自动化和故障排除。
Orchestration appears in domain 1 as building workflows and again in domain 3 as automating and troubleshooting them.

138
00:12:13,614 --> 00:12:21,284
它是少数几个能在两个领域中得分的主题之一，这让它的价值比表面看起来更高。
It is one of the few topics that earns marks in two domains, which makes it better value than its apparent size suggests.

139
00:12:23,374 --> 00:12:31,748
在为本课程分析的题库中，EventBridge 和 Step Functions 出现的频率比 Amazon Athena 还要高。
In the bank analyzed for this course, event bridge and step functions together appeared more often than Amazon Athena.

140
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:36,420
大多数学习计划给编排分配的时间很少。
Most study plans give orchestration a fraction of the time.

141
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,240
他们给 Athena 分配的时间多。
They give Athena.

142
00:12:39,854 --> 00:12:43,172
有三个约束条件决定了这套试卷中几乎所有的题目。
Three constraints decide almost every question on this paper.

143
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:48,964
成本多少、结果需要多快到达，以及维持运行需要多少人力。
How much it costs, how quickly the answer has to arrive, and how much human work it takes to keep the thing running.

144
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:54,180
第三点是考生最容易轻视的，也是 AWS 最常考查的。
The third is the one candidates underweight, and it is the one AWS asks about most often.

145
00:12:54,958 --> 00:13:01,252
运维开销意味着补丁、定容、扩容、升级和日常维护所需的持续劳动。
Operational overhead means the ongoing labor of patching, sizing, scaling, upgrading, and babysitting.

146
00:13:01,838 --> 00:13:03,332
它并不等同于难度。
It is not the same as difficulty.

147
00:13:05,006 --> 00:13:08,996
一个集群可能在周五很容易设置，但之后每周都会成为负担。
A cluster can be easy to set up on a Friday and a burden every week afterwards.

148
00:13:09,742 --> 00:13:13,636
AWS 是一家提供托管服务的公司，其考试也反映了这一观点。
AWS is a managed services company and its exams reflect that view.

149
00:13:14,478 --> 00:13:23,044
当题目提到运维开销时，答案几乎总是倾向于更具托管性的选项，即使存在更便宜的非托管选项。
When a question mentions operational overhead, the answer almost always moves toward the more managed option, even when a cheaper unmanaged one exists.

150
00:13:24,654 --> 00:13:28,160
把这些阶段当作操作指令来学习，而不是仅仅作为装饰。
Learn these phases as instructions rather than as decoration.

151
00:13:28,494 --> 00:13:30,800
这两个概念经常被搞混。
Two of them get confused constantly.

152
00:13:31,022 --> 00:13:32,196
所以现在就把它们分开。
So separate them now.

153
00:13:33,454 --> 00:13:36,900
运维开销最小是指长期运行这个东西时的成本。
Least operational overhead is about running the thing over time.

154
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:41,572
开发工作量最少是指在开始时需要写多少代码。
Least development effort is about how much code you write once at the start.

155
00:13:42,190 --> 00:13:52,772
这两个维度的指向往往和你预想的不同。如果你的团队已经有现成的 Spark 代码，那么在 EC2 上运行 Amazon EMR 就是低开发成本。
Those pull in different directions more often than you would expect. Amazon EMR on EC2 is low development effort if your team already has Spark code that runs.

156
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:57,540
但因为它需要有人去维护那个集群，所以它的运维开销一直都很高。
It is high operational overhead forever because somebody owns that cluster.

157
00:13:58,318 --> 00:14:01,604
而且「最具成本效益」并不简单等同于「最便宜」。
And most cost effective never simply means cheapest.

158
00:14:02,574 --> 00:14:07,920
它的意思是在满足题目中提到的所有其他要求的前提下，最便宜的那个选项。
It means the cheapest option that still satisfies every other requirement stated in the question.

159
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:14,564
如果一个选项更便宜但没达到延迟目标，那它就不是成本效益最高的答案，而是错误的答案。
An option that is cheaper and misses the latency target is not the cost-effective answer, it is the wrong answer.

160
00:14:16,110 --> 00:14:19,908
这个维度比任何其他单一概念都能排除掉更多的错误选项。
This axis explains more wrong answers than any other single idea.

161
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:27,556
直觉上，无服务器总是现代且正确的选择，考试确实倾向于这种做法，但并非无条件如此。
The instinct is that serverless is always the modern correct choice and the exam does lean that way, but not unconditionally.

162
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:31,108
你要思考你到底在为些什么付费。
Think about what you are actually paying for.

163
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:36,260
预置型意味着无论你是否使用，你都在租赁容量。
Provision means you rent capacity whether you use it or not.

164
00:14:36,974 --> 00:14:41,028
无服务器意味着你按请求或执行的秒数付费。
Serverless means you pay per request or per second of execution.

165
00:14:41,582 --> 00:14:46,372
所以，一个全天候持续运行的集群，通常用预置型会更便宜。
So a cluster running flat out 24 hours a day is usually cheaper provisioned.

166
00:14:46,926 --> 00:14:51,280
你租用的每一单位容量，都是你真正消耗的容量。
Every unit of capacity you rent is capacity you genuinely consume.

167
00:14:51,918 --> 00:14:58,852
当负载波动大、偶尔发生或不可预测时，无服务器就胜出，因为在两次运行之间你完全不需要付钱。
Serverless wins when the load is spiky, occasional or unpredictable because you stop paying entirely between runs.

168
00:14:59,598 --> 00:15:03,268
在你预设自己处于哪一边之前，先读一下工作负载的描述。
Read the workload description before you assume which side of this you are on.

169
00:15:04,078 --> 00:15:07,396
「稳定」、「恒定」和「持续」这些词指向一个方向。
The words steady, constant, and continuous point one way.

170
00:15:08,398 --> 00:15:12,292
「偶尔」、「即席」和「不可预测」则指向另一个方向。
Occasional, ad hoc, and unpredictable point the other.

171
00:15:13,902 --> 00:15:22,276
考试中几乎所有的服务现在都有多种形式，而考试要求你识别出某个选项指的是哪种形式。
Almost every service in this exam now exists in more than one form, and the exam expects you to know which one an option means.

172
00:15:23,982 --> 00:15:30,480
Amazon EMR 在 EC2 上有提供，还有 EMR 无服务器版本，以及在 EKS 上运行。
Amazon EMR exists on EC2 as EMR serverless and on EKS.

173
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:34,404
Redshift 有预置型和无服务器两种形式。
Redshift exists provisioned and serverless.

174
00:15:36,174 --> 00:15:39,684
Amazon MSK 有预置型和无服务器两种形式。
Amazon MSK exists provisioned and serverless.

175
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:44,324
Aurora 有预置型和无服务器版本 2。
Aurora exists provisioned and serverless version 2.

176
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:50,244
这很重要，因为同一个服务名称，根据其形式的不同，可能是正确答案也可能是错误答案。
This matters because the same service name can be the right answer or the wrong one depending on the form.

177
00:15:50,894 --> 00:15:56,400
当一个选项只提到服务名称而没说明具体形式时，去读该选项的其余部分来寻找线索。
When an option names a service without saying which form, read the rest of the option for the queue.

178
00:15:56,974 --> 00:16:03,972
「集群」这个词几乎总是指预置型。而「工作组」一词意味着 Redshift 无服务器。
The word cluster almost always means the provisioned form. The word workgroup means redshift serverless.

179
00:16:05,358 --> 00:16:10,564
如果一个选项提到了节点类型或实例大小，那它从定义上就是预置型。
And if an option mentions node types or instance sizing, it is provisioned by definition.

180
00:16:12,206 --> 00:16:18,240
一旦你不再只考虑价格，而是开始思考计费单位，成本问题就会变得简单得多。
Cost questions become much easier once you stop thinking about price and start thinking about the billing unit.

181
00:16:18,542 --> 00:16:21,156
看整体规律，而不是单独的行。
Look at the pattern rather than the individual rows.

182
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:24,836
有些服务会根据你持有的容量持续计费。
Some services charge you continuously for capacity you hold.

183
00:16:25,518 --> 00:16:31,140
Redshift 的 预置型 节点和 Kinesis 的分片无论是否有人使用都会计费。
Redshift provision nodes and kinesis shards keep billing whether anyone uses them or not.

184
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,628
其他的则只在实际发生工作时才收费。
Others charge only when work actually happens.

185
00:16:37,998 --> 00:16:39,396
Glue 按秒计费。
Glue builds the seconds.

186
00:16:39,822 --> 00:16:40,804
任务运行中。
A job runs.

187
00:16:41,326 --> 00:16:43,556
Lambda 按调用次数和持续时间计费。
Lambda builds invocations and duration.

188
00:16:44,526 --> 00:16:51,716
这给你提供了一个不需要记住任何具体价格的规则：任何按持续计费的，在闲置时都很贵。
That gives you a rule that works without memorizing a single price. Anything built continuously is expensive when idle.

189
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:56,484
任何按使用量计费的，在需求持续且高强度时就会变得很贵。
Anything built per use becomes expensive when demand is constant and heavy.

190
00:16:57,294 --> 00:17:03,300
所以，如果题目描述的是一个大部分时间闲置但成本高昂的服务，它指向的就是第一类。
So a question describing an expensive service that sits mostly unused is pointing at the first group.

191
00:17:03,726 --> 00:17:07,876
解决方法几乎总是转向第二类。
The fix is almost always to move to the second.

192
00:17:09,326 --> 00:17:13,796
这是大多数架构题目的第一个分叉点，而且有一个可靠的测试方法。
This is the first fork in most architecture questions, and there is a reliable test for it.

193
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:16,164
问谁在等待结果。
Ask who is waiting for the result.

194
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:22,564
如果欺诈检查必须在交易完成前拦截它，那么有人在等待，这就是流式处理。
If a fraud check must block a transaction before it completes, someone is waiting and it is streaming.

195
00:17:23,598 --> 00:17:29,348
如果分析师在早上 9 点打开仪表板，就没有人熬夜等结果，这就是批处理。
If an analyst opens a dashboard at 9 in the morning, nobody was waiting overnight and it is batch.

196
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:33,060
现在是陷阱，因为它会误导很多人。
Now the trap, because it catches a lot of people.

197
00:17:33,614 --> 00:17:39,044
注意那些描述数据持续到达但每天只消费一次的题目。
Watch for questions that describe data arriving continuously but being consumed once a day.

198
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:43,012
持续到达并不意味着它就是一个流式处理问题。
Continuous arrival does not make something a streaming problem.

199
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,220
持续消费才意味着它是流式处理。
Continuous consumption does.

200
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:51,492
每秒向 IT 报告发送数据的传感器，属于具有频繁源头的批处理工作量。
Sensors that emit every second into an IT report are a batch workload with a chatty source.

201
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,908
本模块中的第一个动词场景正是这种情况。
The first verb scenario in this module is exactly that shape.

202
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,796
所以记住这个想法。
So hold that thought.

203
00:17:59,406 --> 00:18:07,140
记住这些数字，因为题目会给出延迟要求，并期望你毫不犹豫地选出正确的选项。
Anchor these numbers because questions state a latency requirement and expect you to land on the right rung without hesitating.

204
00:18:07,822 --> 00:18:08,996
从最顶层往下推导。
Work down from the top.

205
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:15,012
亚秒级且按用户计费意味着内存或键值存储。
Subsecond and per user means an in-memory or key value store.

206
00:18:15,854 --> 00:18:18,148
以秒为单位意味着真正的流式处理。
Seconds means a genuine stream.

207
00:18:18,734 --> 00:18:20,804
分钟级别属于舒适的批处理范畴。
Minutes is comfortable batch territory.

208
00:18:21,582 --> 00:18:24,560
次日意味着成本最低且可行的方案。
Next day means the cheapest thing that works.

209
00:18:24,942 --> 00:18:29,348
有一个细节非常值得精确掌握，因为旧的资料里这个点是错的。
One detail is worth knowing precisely because older material gets it wrong.

210
00:18:29,870 --> 00:18:36,036
Amazon Data Firehose 通常被描述为近实时，因为它在交付前会进行缓冲。
Amazon data firehose is usually described as near real time because it buffers before delivering.

211
00:18:36,718 --> 00:18:40,324
从 2023 年 12 月起，它支持零缓冲。
Since December 2023, it supports zero buffering.

212
00:18:41,294 --> 00:18:46,308
当缓冲间隔设置为零时，大多数记录会在大约 5 秒内送达。
With the buffer interval set to zero, most records are delivered in about 5 seconds.

213
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:54,660
所以要求在几秒内送达的问题并不会自动排除 Firehose。而要求亚秒级处理的问题则会排除它。
So a question demanding delivery within a few seconds does not automatically rule firehose out. A question demanding sub-second processing does.

214
00:18:56,270 --> 00:19:01,028
一家物流公司接收来自 10,000 辆车辆的 GPS 定位信息。
A logistics company receives GPS pings from 10,000 vehicles.

215
00:19:01,902 --> 00:19:05,796
这些信息以每秒约 2000 条记录的速度持续到达。
They arrive continuously at about 2000 records per second.

216
00:19:06,702 --> 00:19:14,436
目前，这些定位信息由团队维护的一台运行在 Amazon EC2 上的自定义应用程序写入到 Amazon S3。
The pings are currently written to Amazon S3 by a custom application running on Amazon EC2 that the team maintains.

217
00:19:16,142 --> 00:19:17,956
这些数据只用于一件事。
The data is used for one thing.

218
00:19:18,926 --> 00:19:22,436
一份每天早上生成的报告，显示昨天路线的效率。
A report produced every morning showing yesterday's route efficiency.

219
00:19:23,438 --> 00:19:27,620
运营团队要求降低成本并减少维护工作量。
The operations team has asked for lower cost and less to maintain.

220
00:19:28,206 --> 00:19:36,560
目前有一个提议，即使用带有 Apache Flink 管理服务的 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 来重建数据摄取
A proposal on the table is to rebuild ingestion using Amazon Kinesis data streams with a managed service for Apache Flink

221
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,220
应用。
application.

222
00:19:38,190 --> 00:19:40,164
数据工程师应该推荐什么？
What should the data engineer recommend?

223
00:19:40,974 --> 00:19:43,108
A. 接受该提议。
a Adopt the proposal.

224
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:47,588
带有 Flink 应用的 Kinesis Data Streams 可以处理吞吐量。
Kinesis Data Streams with the Flink application handles the throughput.

225
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:55,748
B. 用直接交付到 Amazon S3 的 Firehose 替换 EC2 应用。
B Replace the EC2 application with Amazon data, fire hose delivering directly to Amazon S3.

226
00:19:56,430 --> 00:19:56,640
C。
C.

227
00:19:57,806 --> 00:20:04,772
保留 EC2 应用，但将其迁移到具有自动扩缩容功能的更大实例类型。
Keep the EC2 application but move it to a larger instance type with auto scaling.

228
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:05,680
D。
D.

229
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:12,420
接受提议，但使用 Amazon MSK 代替 Kinesis Data Streams。
Adopt the proposal but use Amazon MSK instead of Kinesis Data Streams.

230
00:20:12,942 --> 00:20:14,148
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

231
00:20:20,878 --> 00:20:26,340
答案是 B，有趣的是 A 和 D 在技术上并不错误。
The answer is B, and the interesting part is that A and D are not wrong technically.

232
00:20:26,798 --> 00:20:28,164
它们都能正常工作。
They would both work.

233
00:20:28,416 --> 00:20:31,716
它们之所以错误，是因为它们解决了一个没人需要的问题。
They are wrong because they solve a problem nobody has.

234
00:20:32,430 --> 00:20:35,684
在这种情况下，没有任何东西是实时消耗数据的。
Nothing in that situation consumes the data in real time.

235
00:20:36,398 --> 00:20:38,660
只是每天早上生成一份报告。
One report once a morning.

236
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:48,932
构建一个流处理应用来提供每日报告会增加成本并增加一个需要操作的应用，这与两个既定要求正好相反。
Building a stream processing application to feed a daily report adds cost and adds an application to operate, which is the opposite of both stated requirements.

237
00:20:49,376 --> 00:20:54,884
当提供了一个功能强大的工具但需求并不需要它时，这通常就是干扰项。
When the impressive tool is offered and the requirements do not need it, that is usually the distractor.

238
00:20:55,296 --> 00:20:57,028
还要注意选项 C。
Also notice option C.

239
00:20:57,614 --> 00:21:01,572
它解决了吞吐量问题，但吞吐量从未被描述为问题。
It fixes throughput, and throughput was never described as a problem.

240
00:21:03,214 --> 00:21:08,804
现在到第二个关键分叉点了，这是很多领域 2 分数拿走或丢掉的地方。
Now the second big fork, and it is where a lot of domain 2 marks are won or lost.

241
00:21:09,296 --> 00:21:16,196
考生往往会根据数据量来选择存储，认为大容量就意味着 Redshift 或 S3。
Candidates tend to reach for a store based on volume, thinking that large means red shift or S3.

242
00:21:17,358 --> 00:21:19,300
但这类题目并不是这么考的。
That is not how these questions work.

243
00:21:20,206 --> 00:21:25,696
数据量几乎从不作为决定因素，因为范围内的每种存储都能处理大量数据。
Volume is almost never the deciding factor because every store in scope handles large volumes.

244
00:21:26,158 --> 00:21:32,804
决定因素是数据的读取方式：是按键逐行读取，还是将数百万行汇总成一个总计。
What decides it is how the data is read, one row at a time by a key or millions of rows aggregated into a total.

245
00:21:33,454 --> 00:21:36,004
是固定的已知查询，还是自由文本搜索。
Fixed known queries or free text search.

246
00:21:38,478 --> 00:21:41,028
是你控制的模式，还是你发现的模式。
A schema you control or one you discover.

247
00:21:41,998 --> 00:21:46,788
只要搞对访问模式，存储选择几乎会自动匹配上。
Get the access pattern right and the store falls out of it almost mechanically.

248
00:21:47,566 --> 00:21:53,252
如果搞错了，每个选项看起来都有道理，这就是那种感觉——就像快要丢分了。
Get it wrong and every option looks defensible, which is the feeling of being about to lose a mark.

249
00:21:54,958 --> 00:21:56,164
记住这张表。
Memorize this table.

250
00:21:56,718 --> 00:21:59,204
它能独立解决很大一部分第二领域的题目。
It resolves a large share of domain 2 on its own.

251
00:21:59,822 --> 00:22:05,936
唯一需要拆解的是 Athena 和 Redshift 的组合，因为两者都在大规模数据集上运行 SQL。
The one row that needs unpacking is the Athena and Redshift pair because both run SQL over large datasets.

252
00:22:06,510 --> 00:22:08,060
这两个选项经常同时出现。
Both appear as options constantly.

253
00:22:09,166 --> 00:22:14,244
区分它们的不是查询的复杂程度，而是查询运行的频率。
The separator is not how complex the query is, it is how often the query runs.

254
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:21,668
Athena 按扫描字节数计费，如果没有人查询，就没有固定成本。
Athena charges per query by bytes scanned with no standing cost when nobody is querying.

255
00:22:22,256 --> 00:22:30,916
这非常适合偶尔或探索性的工作，但对于每分钟都要更新一次、供 400 人使用的仪表板来说，简直糟糕透顶。
That is ideal for occasional or exploratory work and genuinely terrible for a dashboard refreshing every minute for 400 people.

256
00:22:31,534 --> 00:22:35,524
Redshift 按你保留的容量计费，这是相反的逻辑。
Redshift charges for capacity you keep, which is the reverse shape.

257
00:22:36,430 --> 00:22:39,616
偶尔且不可预测的情况更倾向于 Athena。
Occasional and unpredictable favors Athena.

258
00:22:40,176 --> 00:22:42,916
持续且重复的情况更倾向于 Redshift。
Constant and repeated favors redshift.

259
00:22:44,782 --> 00:22:51,076
如果题目告诉你有多少分析师以及查询频率，那句话就是用来决定这一项的。
If a question tells you how many analysts and how often that sentence is there to decide this row.

260
00:22:52,656 --> 00:22:57,380
这通常被呈现为对立关系，但在实践中很少是这样。
This is usually presented as an opposition and in practice it rarely is one.

261
00:22:57,936 --> 00:23:00,644
常见的正确架构是同时使用两者。
The common correct architecture uses both.

262
00:23:01,936 --> 00:23:06,340
原始数据存放在 S3，因为那里的存储成本低且能容纳任何内容。
Raw data lands in S3 because storage there is cheap and accepts anything.

263
00:23:07,246 --> 00:23:13,456
它经过清洗和精选，然后将精选的子集加载到 Redshift 中，因为那是会被反复查询的内容。
It is cleaned and curated, and the curated subset is loaded into Redshift because that is what gets queried repeatedly.

264
00:23:13,616 --> 00:23:18,596
Redshift Spectrum 然后会去 S3 获取那些较冷的数据，而无需将其加载。
Redshift spectrum then reaches back into S3 for the colder data without loading it at all.

265
00:23:19,150 --> 00:23:26,148
所以当两者都作为选项出现时，仔细阅读题目是在问数据存放在哪里，还是从哪里提供服务。
So when both appear as options, read carefully for whether the question is asking where data lands or where it is served from.

266
00:23:27,502 --> 00:23:30,404
在同一个架构中，这两个问题有不同的答案。
Those have different answers within the same architecture.

267
00:23:31,278 --> 00:23:34,148
混淆这两者是丢分的稳妥方法。
Confusing the two is a reliable way to lose a mark.

268
00:23:35,022 --> 00:23:41,988
你会选出一个确实属于正确设计的一部分，但并不是题目所问答案的选项。
You choose an option that is genuinely part of the right design and still not the answer to the question asked.

269
00:23:43,630 --> 00:23:49,860
Lakehouse 这个词本身意义不大，所以要把它锚定到具体的组件上，而不是营销术语上。
Lakehouse is a word that means very little on its own, so anchor it to specific components rather than to the marketing.

270
00:23:50,286 --> 00:23:52,804
核心思想是数据只存放在 S3 一次。
The idea is that data sits once in S3.

271
00:23:53,262 --> 00:23:56,612
它在 Glue 数据目录中只被描述一次。
It is described once in the AWS Blue Data Catalog.

272
00:23:56,976 --> 00:24:01,028
所以每个引擎都知道这个表存在以及它包含哪些列。
So every engine knows the table exists and what columns it has.

273
00:24:01,936 --> 00:24:08,816
它在 AWS Lake Formation 中只配置一次权限，所以你不需要维护四套不同的访问规则。
It is permissioned once in AWS Lake Formation, so you are not maintaining four different sets of access rules.

274
00:24:08,976 --> 00:24:15,236
然后 Athena、Redshift、EMR 和 Glue 都可以读取它，而无需将其复制到任何地方。
And it is then readable by Athena, Redshift, EMR, and Blue without copying it anywhere.

275
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:22,276
Apache ICB 让这些变动的数据变得安全。
Apache ICB is what makes that safe for data that changes.

276
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:29,092
它为原本只是一堆文件的数据带来了事务、时间旅行和 模式 演进。
It brings transactions, time travel, and schema evolution to what is otherwise just a pile of files.

277
00:24:29,360 --> 00:24:31,600
第 9 模块会详细讲解这个内容。
Module 9 covers this properly.

278
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:35,236
目前，先记住这个架构和四个组件名称。
For now, hold the shape and the four component names.

279
00:24:36,782 --> 00:24:41,188
这比它最初看起来要重要得多，原因是计费问题。
This matters far more than it first appears, and the reason is pricing.

280
00:24:41,902 --> 00:24:45,444
Athena 和 Redshift Spectrum 会根据扫描字节数收费。
Athena and Redshift Spectrum charge you for bytes scanned.

281
00:24:46,094 --> 00:24:48,676
想想列式存储对这个数字有什么影响。
Think about what a columnar format does to that number.

282
00:24:49,806 --> 00:24:54,960
一个涉及 40 列中的 3 列的查询，大约只读取四分之三的数据。
A query touching three columns out of 40 reads roughly three-fortieths of the data.

283
00:24:55,502 --> 00:24:59,268
这些列是分开存储的，而不是按行交错排列。
The columns are stored separately rather than interleaved row by row.

284
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,908
压缩会再次缩小体积，而且比行格式压缩得更好，因为单列中包含相似的值且它们相邻排列。
Compression then shrinks it again and compresses better than a row format would because a single column holds similar values sitting next to each other.

285
00:25:08,814 --> 00:25:13,988
分区从另一个维度解决问题，因为它跳过了整个文件夹。
Partitioning attacks the same bin from the other direction by skipping entire folders.

286
00:25:14,286 --> 00:25:15,556
查询不需要这些数据。
The query does not need.

287
00:25:17,678 --> 00:25:23,076
转换为 Parquet 并进行合理的分区，是这次考试中最常用的正确答案。
Convert to parquet and partition sensibly is the single most reusable answer on this exam.

288
00:25:23,822 --> 00:25:28,932
当题目提到查询成本并提到原始文本文件时，这就是你要找的答案。
When a question mentions query cost and mentions raw text files, that is the answer forming.

289
00:25:30,702 --> 00:25:35,524
当问题描述数据湖运行缓慢或成本高昂时，按顺序应用这些方法。
Apply these in order when a question describes a slow or expensive data lake.

290
00:25:36,398 --> 00:25:41,028
先用分区，因为完全跳过数据比高效读取数据更好。
Partitioning first because skipping data entirely beats reading it efficiently.

291
00:25:41,742 --> 00:25:43,972
然后是格式，接着是压缩。
Then format, then compression.

292
00:25:44,846 --> 00:25:49,092
最后两个是人们容易忘记的，但它们都会出现在考试选项中。
The last two are the ones people forget and both appear as exam answers.

293
00:25:49,998 --> 00:25:57,220
当流式处理摄入每隔几秒写入一个对象时，就会产生小文件问题，留下数百万个微小的文件。
The small file problem happens when a streaming ingest writes an object every few seconds, leaving millions of tiny files behind.

294
00:25:58,702 --> 00:26:02,800
然后每个引擎花费在列出和打开文件上的时间就比读取数据的时间还要多。
Every engine then spends more time listing and opening files than reading data.

295
00:26:03,214 --> 00:26:06,404
这种现象就是查询没有明显原因却变慢了。
The symptom is a query that is slow for no obvious reason.

296
00:26:07,278 --> 00:26:10,020
总的来说，分区是镜像对称的失败案例。
Overall partitioning is the mirror image failure.

297
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:18,020
如果你总是按月查询，却按小时进行分区，就会产生数千个几乎为空的文件夹。
Partitioning by the hour when you always query by month creates thousands of nearly empty folders.

298
00:26:19,086 --> 00:26:22,596
元数据查询会变成瓶颈，而不是数据本身。
The metadata lookup becomes the bottleneck instead of the data.

299
00:26:23,054 --> 00:26:27,140
这两个问题看起来都是性能差，但它们的解决方法正好相反。
Both problems look like bad performance and have opposite fixes.

300
00:26:28,878 --> 00:26:36,324
考试指南明确列出了可重放性以及有状态与无状态的区别。所以这些不是背景词汇。
The exam guide names, replayability, and the stateful vs. stateless distinction explicitly. So these are not background terms.

301
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:38,880
这里有两个你可以依赖的要点。
Here are two anchors you can rely on.

302
00:26:39,342 --> 00:26:46,948
Amazon Data Firehose 使用至少一种语义，这意味着在超时后进行的交付重试可能会产生重复记录。
Amazon Data Firehose uses at least one semantics, meaning a delivery retry after a timeout can produce a duplicate record.

303
00:26:47,822 --> 00:26:54,180
除了 Amazon S3、Apache Iceberg 表和 Snowflake，这适用于所有目的地。
That applies to every destination except Amazon S3, Apache Icybug tables, and Snowflake.

304
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:59,236
掌握这个例外情况是区分两个看似完全相同的选项的关键细节。
Knowing that exception is the kind of detail that separates two otherwise identical options.

305
00:26:59,694 --> 00:27:02,756
其次，可重放性完全取决于保留期。
Second, replay depends entirely on retention.

306
00:27:03,758 --> 00:27:12,292
Kinesis DataStreams 在可配置的窗口内保留记录，所以你可以在修复 Bug 后回溯到某个时间点重新处理。
Kinesis DataStreams keeps records for a configurable window, so you can go back and reprocess from a point in time after fixing a bug.

307
00:27:13,038 --> 00:27:21,892
一旦消息被消费就会将其删除的队列无论多么可靠都无法做到这一点。持久性和可重放性是不同的属性。
A queue that deletes a message once it is consumed cannot do that, no matter how reliable it is. Durability and replayability are different properties.

308
00:27:23,566 --> 00:27:28,356
一家媒体公司将观看事件作为压缩的 JSON 文件存储在 Amazon 中。
A media company stores viewing events as compressed JSON files in Amazon.

309
00:27:30,030 --> 00:27:32,452
按摄入日期在 S3 中进行分区。
S3 Partition by ingestion date.

310
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:35,332
分析师使用 Amazon Athena 对它们进行查询。
Analysts query them with Amazon Athena.

311
00:27:36,142 --> 00:27:42,244
一个面向新客户的功能需要在用户打开应用时向单个观看者显示他们自己的观看历史。
A new customer facing feature needs to show a single viewer their own watch history when they open the app.

312
00:27:43,118 --> 00:27:46,052
该功能必须在 100 毫秒内做出响应。
The feature must respond in under 100 milliseconds.

313
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:49,220
在高峰时，它每秒会被调用数千次。
It will be called several thousand times per second at peak.

314
00:27:49,646 --> 00:27:52,836
团队的第一次尝试使用了 Athena，但页面超时了。
The team's first attempt used Athena and the page timed out.

315
00:27:53,966 --> 00:27:56,932
为什么第一次尝试失败了，以及应该用什么来替代它？
Why did the first attempt fail and what should replace it?

316
00:27:57,358 --> 00:27:59,812
a. Athena 没有正确分区。
a Athena was not partitioned correctly.

317
00:28:00,622 --> 00:28:04,484
按观看者 ID 进行重分区并继续使用 Athena。
Repartition by viewer ID and keep using Athena.

318
00:28:05,134 --> 00:28:11,012
b. 将 JSON 文件转换为 Apache Parquet，这将使查询达到延迟目标。
b. Convert the JSON files to Apache Parquet, which will bring the query under the latency target.

319
00:28:11,726 --> 00:28:16,000
c. 从以观看者为键的 Amazon DynamoDB 中提供该功能。
C. Serve the feature from Amazon DynamoDB keyed on viewer.

320
00:28:17,006 --> 00:28:19,524
ID 从相同的事件中获取。
ID populated from the same events.

321
00:28:20,302 --> 00:28:20,560
d
D

322
00:28:21,920 --> 00:28:27,108
将事件加载到 Amazon Redshift 并从应用程序中查询。
load the events into Amazon Redshift and query it from the application.

323
00:28:27,726 --> 00:28:29,280
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

324
00:28:35,918 --> 00:28:37,344
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

325
00:28:38,064 --> 00:28:43,584
在这种情况下，有两个词决定了结果：单个人观看者和 100 毫秒。
Two words in that situation decided it a single viewer and 100 milliseconds.

326
00:28:43,918 --> 00:28:50,404
低延迟下的按键查找单条项目几乎是 Dynamo DB 访问模式的定义。
Single item lookup by key at low latency is the Dynamo DB access pattern almost by definition.

327
00:28:51,182 --> 00:28:59,332
选项 B 是一个有趣的干扰项，因为转换为 Parquet 确实是很好的建议，并且是另一个问题的正确答案。
Option B is the interesting distractor because converting to Parquet is genuinely good advice and is the correct answer to a different question.

328
00:28:59,744 --> 00:29:01,604
它减少了扫描字节数。
It reduces bytes scanned.

329
00:29:01,824 --> 00:29:05,476
但它对 Athena 开始查询所花费的秒数没有任何影响。
It does nothing about the seconds Athena takes to start a query at all.

330
00:29:05,904 --> 00:29:08,708
注意，这被刻意与场景 1 配对。
Notice this pairs with scenario 1 deliberately.

331
00:29:09,390 --> 00:29:11,904
那里的工具过于复杂了。
There the sophisticated tool was too much.

332
00:29:12,206 --> 00:29:15,428
这里的分析工具完全不符合要求。
Here the analytical tool is the wrong shape entirely.

333
00:29:17,166 --> 00:29:21,732
这是最后一点思考，题目通常会在措辞中直接给出答案。
The last thought before we finish, and questions usually hand you the answer in the wording.

334
00:29:22,734 --> 00:29:26,756
“数据到达时”或“上传后立即执行”属于事件触发。
As soon as the data arrives or immediately after upload is an event trigger.

335
00:29:27,534 --> 00:29:31,396
每晚、每小时或每月初都属于定时任务。
Every night or hourly or on the first of the month is a schedule.

336
00:29:31,982 --> 00:29:33,540
有一种陷阱值得特别提一下。
One trap is worth naming.

337
00:29:34,510 --> 00:29:38,064
即使是运行后没找到任何结果的计划任务，依然会产生费用。
A scheduled job that runs and finds nothing still costs money.

338
00:29:38,254 --> 00:29:41,124
它仍被计为一次运行，并会出现在账单上。
It still counts as a run and still shows up in the bill.

339
00:29:41,744 --> 00:29:49,220
所以，如果题目抱怨浪费了运行次数或为无意义的任务付费，就是在提示你选择事件驱动。
So, a question complaining about wasted runs or about paying for jobs that did nothing is pointing you towards event driven.

340
00:29:49,998 --> 00:29:51,748
它可能根本不会用到那个词。
It may never use that phrase.

341
00:29:52,366 --> 00:29:54,224
反向的陷阱也同样存在。
The reverse trap also exists.

342
00:29:54,544 --> 00:29:59,684
对成千上万个微小文件进行事件驱动的摄入，可能会触发成千上万个微小的任务。
Event-driven ingestion of thousands of tiny files can trigger thousands of tiny jobs.

343
00:30:01,166 --> 00:30:04,548
这就是在两页前提到的“小文件问题”产生的原理。
That is how you create the small file problem from two slides ago.

344
00:30:06,062 --> 00:30:13,060
对每个场景按顺序运行这四个问题，在你对比任何技术优劣之前，选项范围就会缩小。
Run these four questions in order on every scenario and the field narrows before you have compared any technical merits at all.

345
00:30:13,486 --> 00:30:17,092
第四个问题起到的作用最大，但往往最容易被忽视。
The fourth one does the most work and gets the least attention.

346
00:30:17,486 --> 00:30:22,948
像“团队没有能力运营新流水线”这样的句子不是背景信息。
Sentences like the team has no capacity to operate a new pipeline are not seen setting.

347
00:30:23,694 --> 00:30:29,732
像“公司希望对现有架构进行最小更改”的句子也不是背景信息。
Sentences like the company wants minimal changes to the existing architecture are not background.

348
00:30:29,984 --> 00:30:37,316
它们是故意设置的排除项，通常能排除掉那两个最难区分的选项。
They are eliminations placed there deliberately, and they usually kill the two options that would otherwise be hardest to separate.

349
00:30:39,470 --> 00:30:43,424
练习识别这些信息，可以为你处理每个题目争取到更多时间。
Practice spotting them and you buy yourself time on every question.

350
00:30:43,984 --> 00:30:51,984
接下来我们进入领域 1，这是占比最大的部分（34%），从批处理摄入和 AWS Glue 开始。
From here we go into domain 1, the largest at 34%, starting with batch ingestion and the AWS Glue

351
00:30:52,144 --> 00:30:53,060
ETL引擎。
ETL engine.

352
00:30:53,344 --> 00:30:58,436
Glue 是整个题库中被提及最多的服务，它值得专门的模块讲解。
Glue was the single most mentioned service in the entire question bank and it earns its module.

353
00:30:59,758 --> 00:31:05,156
在为本课程分析的题库中，AWS Glue 出现了 485 次。
AWS Glue appeared 485 times in the question bank analyzed for this course.

354
00:31:05,870 --> 00:31:09,956
这比 Amazon S3 和 Amazon Redshift 的出现次数都要多。
That is more than Amazon S3 and more than Amazon Redshift.

355
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:16,132
没有其他服务能与之媲美，也没有其他内容能像它一样稳可地回报你的学习时间。
No other service comes close, and nothing else in the syllabus rewards study time as reliably.

356
00:31:16,864 --> 00:31:28,944
这是课程中最长的模块，值得投入时间。我们将涵盖批处理数据如何进入 AWS，然后深入讲解 Glue ETL 引擎，接着是连接性，然后是成本，
This is the longest module in the course and it earns the time. We will cover how batch data gets into AWS, then the Glue ETL engine in real detail, then connectivity, then cost,

357
00:31:29,184 --> 00:31:30,544
最后是故障模式。
then failure modes.

358
00:31:30,784 --> 00:31:32,804
过程中包含六个投票场景。
Six vote scenarios along the way.

359
00:31:33,424 --> 00:31:40,516
如果你在参加考试前只有时间掌握一个服务，那就是这个，而且不是勉强选择。
If you only have time to master one service before sitting this exam, it is this one and it is not close.

360
00:31:42,254 --> 00:31:49,184
首先，理清它的名称，因为题目会故意利用其中的歧义性。
Before anything else, unpangle the name because questions exploit the ambiguity deliberately.

361
00:31:49,504 --> 00:31:54,944
当选项提到使用 AWS Glue 时，它可能指代至少六种不同的产品。
When an option says use AWS glue, it could mean at least six different products.

362
00:31:55,104 --> 00:32:00,004
它们有不同的计费模型、不同的使用场景以及不同的正确答案。
They have different pricing models, different use cases, and different correct answers.

363
00:32:00,814 --> 00:32:08,704
如果考生把 Glue 仅仅看作一个东西，就会觉得这些题目非常困惑，因为有两个选项都写了 glue
Candidates who think of Glue as one thing find these questions genuinely confusing because two options both say glue

364
00:32:08,864 --> 00:32:10,436
但其中只有一个是正确的。
and only one of them is right.

365
00:32:10,784 --> 00:32:15,424
如果不清楚每个选项具体指代哪个组件，就无法区分它们。
There is no way to separate them without knowing which component each option means.

366
00:32:16,110 --> 00:32:20,612
把这六个分别学好，整类困惑就会彻底消失。
Learn the six separately and a whole category of confusion simply disappears.

367
00:32:21,390 --> 00:32:25,732
这也是为什么如果学习计划只写“复习 Glue”，那它就太笼统了，没法实用。
This is also why a study plan that says revise GU is too coarse to be useful.

368
00:32:27,342 --> 00:32:33,220
这六个组件在考试中被作为独立的课题来考查，并有各自对应的答案。
Six components and the exam tests them as separate topics with separate answers.

369
00:32:33,742 --> 00:32:37,988
Glue ETL 作业运行 Spark 并按 D 计费。
Blue ETL jobs run Spark and Bill per D.

370
00:32:38,830 --> 00:32:40,224
PU 小时。
PU hour.

371
00:32:40,910 --> 00:32:46,020
数据目录存储元数据，并根据存储对象和每百万次请求计费。
The data catalog stores metadata and bills per object stored and per million requests.

372
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:52,708
爬虫按 DPUR 构建，最低 10 分钟，这与作业使用的最小时间不同。
Crawlers build per DPUR with a 10 minute minimum, which is a different minimum to the one jobs use.

373
00:32:53,582 --> 00:32:58,544
Glue 的计费包含交互式会话和每个节点的费用，这些是在所有其他费用之上叠加的。
Data Blue bills per interactive session and per node are on top of everything else.

374
00:32:59,054 --> 00:33:01,444
数据质量又是单独计费的。
Data quality is metered separately again.

375
00:33:02,190 --> 00:33:04,900
这个模块深入讲解 ETL 作业。
This module covers ETL jobs in depth.

376
00:33:05,744 --> 00:33:10,916
目录和爬虫在模块 12 中，数据质量在模块 15 中。
The catalog and crawlers get module 12 and data quality gets module 15.

377
00:33:11,184 --> 00:33:14,500
所以如果你觉得这里的内容很少，那是故意设计的。
So if those feel thin here, that is deliberate.

378
00:33:15,664 --> 00:33:22,980
批处理摄入的题目几乎总是会说明源头，而源头能立即锁定工具，通常就能锁定到唯一的选项。
Batch ingestion questions almost always name the source, and the source narrows the tool immediately, often to a single option.

379
00:33:23,264 --> 00:33:28,704
正在迁移或保持同步的关系型数据库指向的是 AWS DMS。
A relational database being migrated or kept in sync points at AWSDMS.

380
00:33:31,214 --> 00:33:35,268
像 Salesforce 这样的销售应用指向的是 Amazon App Flow。
A sales application like Salesforce points at Amazon App Flow.

381
00:33:36,206 --> 00:33:42,276
具有弱连接的 PB 级数据指向 Snowball。存储在网络共享中的文件指向 Datasync。
Petabytes with poor connectivity points at Snowball. Files sitting on a network share point at Datasync.

382
00:33:42,768 --> 00:33:45,408
模块 5 会妥善涵盖所有这些内容。
Module 5 covers every one of these properly.

383
00:33:45,568 --> 00:33:47,780
所以现在先不要担心细节。
So do not worry about the detail yet.

384
00:33:48,128 --> 00:33:51,168
这里重要的是它们共同具备的特征。
What matters here is the shape they all share.

385
00:33:51,758 --> 00:33:58,116
几乎所有这些操作都会在进行任何转换之前，将原始数据存入 Amazon S3。
Almost every one of them lands raw data in Amazon S3 before anything transforms it.

386
00:33:58,798 --> 00:34:02,564
S3 成本低廉、容量几乎无限且持久可靠。
S3 is cheap, effectively unlimited and durable.

387
00:34:02,926 --> 00:34:06,692
它还能接受任何格式，而不需要提前告知是什么格式。
It also accepts any format without being told what it is.

388
00:34:08,333 --> 00:34:14,916
值得深入研究的是第一对，因为这两个选项经常同时出现，且两个都有道理。
The row worth dwelling on is the first pair because both options appear together constantly and both are defensible.

389
00:34:15,408 --> 00:34:16,996
DMS 和 Glue。
DMS and a glue.

390
00:34:17,518 --> 00:34:21,219
JDBC job 也可以从数据库中读取数据。
JDB, C job can both read from a database.

391
00:34:22,158 --> 00:34:26,371
DMS 是为持续复制而构建的，可以进行变更数据捕获。
DMS is built for continuous replication and can do change data capture.

392
00:34:27,277 --> 00:34:31,876
它先执行初始全量加载，然后无限期地流式传输持续发生的变更。
It performs an initial full load, then streams ongoing changes indefinitely.

393
00:34:32,494 --> 00:34:38,692
通过 JDBC 连接的 Glue 作业读取的是运行那一刻存在的数据，然后就停止了。
A glue job connecting over JDBC reads whatever is there at the moment it runs and then stops.

394
00:34:39,088 --> 00:34:45,636
所以关键词是“持续”、“连续”或“保持同步”，这些都指向 DMS。
So the signal words are ongoing, continuously or keep in sync, which all point at DMS.

395
00:34:46,368 --> 00:34:54,148
如果题目提到“每晚提取”或“每日快照”，Glue 作业更简单、成本更低，也是预设的正确答案。
If the question says nightly extract or daily snapshot, a glue job is simpler, cheaper, and the intended answer.

396
00:34:55,406 --> 00:35:02,404
每个批处理流水线都会面临这个选择，而考试通常通过成本问题来考查这一点，而不是直接提问。
Every batch pipeline makes this choice, and the exam usually asks about it through cost rather than asking directly.

397
00:35:02,798 --> 00:35:08,484
全量加载很简单且永远正确，它每天晚上都会重新读取昨天的所有数据，一直如此。
A full load is simple and always correct, and it rereads yesterday's data every single night, forever.

398
00:35:09,454 --> 00:35:15,940
增量处理只读取新内容，这需要一个能记住上次运行到哪里的机制。
Incremental processing reads only what is new, which requires something that remembers where the last run got to.

399
00:35:16,334 --> 00:35:20,100
在 AWS 上，这个机制通常是 Glue 作业书签。
On AWS, that something is usually a glue job bookmark.

400
00:35:20,494 --> 00:35:21,860
这是考试中的常见模式。
Here is the exam pattern.

401
00:35:22,702 --> 00:35:28,448
注意这种情况：尽管新数据的日更新量没变，但任务运行速度却在持续变慢且成本变高。
Watch for a job getting steadily slower and more expensive while the daily volume of new data has not changed.

402
00:35:28,686 --> 00:35:31,248
这就是一个本该采用增量处理的“全量加载”。
That is a full load that should be incremental.

403
00:35:31,726 --> 00:35:35,140
书签几乎总是正确答案，我们很快就会讲到这个内容。
Bookmarks are almost always the answer, and we come to them shortly.

404
00:35:36,398 --> 00:35:41,444
这是本模块剩余部分的思维模型，值得明确说明一下。
Here is the mental model for the rest of this module, and it is worth stating plainly.

405
00:35:41,728 --> 00:35:49,732
Glue ETL 作业就是 Spark，不是类似 Spark 的东西，不是对 Spark 的封装，也不是简化版。
A glue ETL job is Spark, not something Spark-like, not a wrapper around Spark, not a simplified version.

406
00:35:49,968 --> 00:35:55,428
它是运行在你看不到、也无法登录进去的基础设施上的 Apache Spark。
It is Apache Spark running on infrastructure you never see and never log into.

407
00:35:56,288 --> 00:36:00,932
所有影响 Spark 快慢的因素都同样适用。
Everything that makes Spark fast or slow applies unchanged.

408
00:36:01,328 --> 00:36:13,092
分区、洗牌、执行器上的内存压力、跨键的数据倾斜，以及 AWS 添加的所有功能，都是基于这个引擎运行的，而不是替换它。
Partitioning, shuffles, memory pressure on executors, data skew across keys, and everything AWS adds sits on top of that engine rather than replacing it.

409
00:36:13,728 --> 00:36:15,908
这在实际操作中非常重要。
This matters for a practical reason.

410
00:36:16,462 --> 00:36:19,012
Glue 排查问题通常是
Blue troubleshooting questions are usually

411
00:36:19,790 --> 00:36:26,768
穿着“蓝色”外衣的 Spark 问题，正确的答案是用 Glue 术语表达出的 Spark 解决方案。
Spark questions wearing a blue costume, and the correct answer is a spark fix expressed in blue vocabulary.

412
00:36:28,110 --> 00:36:32,164
你不需要背诵版本号，但有两个事实会考到。
You will not be asked to recite version numbers, but two facts here do come up.

413
00:36:32,686 --> 00:36:37,668
首先，自动缩放和弹性执行类都需要 Glue 3.0 或更高版本。
First, auto-scaling and the flex execution class both require Blue 3.0 or later.

414
00:36:38,382 --> 00:36:41,636
在旧任务中提出使用 Flex 的选项是错误的。
An option proposing Flex on an older job is quietly wrong.

415
00:36:41,888 --> 00:36:44,644
其次，Python shell 作业类型不是 Spark。
Second, the Python shell job type is not Spark.

416
00:36:45,582 --> 00:36:52,100
它是一个运行纯 Python 的单进程，占用 1/6 DPU 或一个完整的 DPU。
It is a single process running plain Python available at 116th of a DPU or one full DPU.

417
00:36:52,608 --> 00:36:59,428
对于调用 API 或执行一条 SQL 语句的小脚本，使用 Spark 集群是极大的浪费。
For a small script that calls an API or runs one SQL statement, a Spark cluster is absurd overkill.

418
00:36:59,888 --> 00:37:01,540
Python shell 是正确答案。
The Python shell is the answer.

419
00:37:03,246 --> 00:37:05,284
记住一个核心数字，其他的都会顺理成章。
Anchor one number and the rest follow.

420
00:37:05,870 --> 00:37:10,980
一个 DPU 等于 4 个虚拟 CPU 和 16GB 内存。
A DPU is 4 virtual CPUs and 16GB of memory.

421
00:37:11,822 --> 00:37:16,068
G1X 是 1 DPU，G2X 是 2，以此类推翻倍。
G1X is 1 DPU, G2X is 2, and so on doubling.

422
00:37:16,686 --> 00:37:19,684
R 系列是大家容易忽略的，因为它们比较新。
The R types are the ones people miss because they are newer.

423
00:37:20,494 --> 00:37:23,588
在虚拟 CPU 数量相同的情况下，它们提供双倍的内存。
They give you double the memory for the same virtual CPU count.

424
00:37:24,462 --> 00:37:27,364
对于内存密集型任务，这就是你需要的。
That is what you want for memory intensive.

425
00:37:27,760 --> 00:37:32,676
Spark 的工作包括缓存、洗牌和倾斜聚合。
Spark work like caching, shuffling, and skewed aggregations.

426
00:37:33,646 --> 00:37:39,172
所以一个描述在大规模连接过程中出现内存不足错误的题目有两个合理的答案。
So a question describing out of memory errors during a large join has two plausible answers.

427
00:37:39,758 --> 00:37:43,716
要么提高 G 系列级别，要么横向切换到 R 系列。
Move up the G scale or move sideways to an R type.

428
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:51,396
这一页值得记住，因为 Glue cost 相关问题很常见，只要掌握规则，逻辑就很简单。
This slide is worth memorizing because blue cost questions are common and mechanical once you know the rules.

429
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:59,360
默认分配是 10 DPU，无论任务是否需要这么多，而 Spark 作业的最小值是 2。
The default allocation is 10 dP, as whether the job needs them or not, and the minimum for a spark job is 2.

430
00:37:59,918 --> 00:38:07,076
现实中很大一部分 Glue 超支情况，仅仅是因为一直沿用那个默认设置。
A large share of real-world blue overspend is nothing more sophisticated than that default being left untouched for a year.

431
00:38:07,630 --> 00:38:12,676
注意这里有两个不同的最低计费时长，题目会利用这一点来考你。
Notice there are two different minimum billing durations, and questions do exploit this.

432
00:38:13,134 --> 00:38:16,228
作业和交互式会话从 1 分钟起计费。
Jobs and interactive sessions bill from 1 minute.

433
00:38:17,294 --> 00:38:20,452
爬虫和开发端点从 10 分钟起计费。
Crawlers and development endpoints bill from 10.

434
00:38:20,910 --> 00:38:27,716
所以一个关于每 5 分钟运行一次的轻量级爬虫的问题，就是在考那个 10 分钟的底线。
So a question about a lightweight crawler scheduled every 5 minutes is pointing straight at that 10 minute floor.

435
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:32,676
即使它只运行 30 秒，你也要支付 10 分钟的费用。
You pay for 10 minutes each time it runs for 30 seconds.

436
00:38:34,414 --> 00:38:38,820
这个区别是 Glue 特有的，并且经常出现在题目中。
This distinction is blue specific and it appears in questions regularly.

437
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:44,420
Spark 数据帧要求每一条记录都符合预先确定的一个模式。
A spark data frame requires every record to fit one schema decided up front.

438
00:38:45,422 --> 00:38:48,240
实际摄入的数据往往不符合这个要求。
Real ingested data often does not oblige.

439
00:38:49,166 --> 00:38:55,396
如果一个字段在大多数记录中是数字，而在少数记录中是字符串，就会导致数据帧读取直接失败。
A field that arrives as a number in most records and a string in a few will break a data frame read outright.

440
00:38:56,398 --> 00:39:04,004
动态帧可以容忍这种情况，它会保留两种可能性，直到你通过 解析选择 明确去解析它们。
A dynamic frame tolerates that, keeping both possibilities alive until you resolve them deliberately using resolve choice.

441
00:39:04,878 --> 00:39:11,172
代价是动态帧运行较慢且仅存在于 Glue 中，所以代码不具备可移植性。
The cost is that dynamic frames are slower and exist only inside glue, so the code is not portable.

442
00:39:11,470 --> 00:39:12,228
Spark。
Spark.

443
00:39:13,134 --> 00:39:18,180
常见的实际应用模式是先作为动态帧读取，并在早期解决混乱问题。
The common real-world pattern is to read as a dynamic frame and resolve the mess early.

444
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:22,852
然后使用 2DF 将其转换为数据帧，再在其中进行繁重的工作。
Then convert to a data frame with 2DF and do the heavy work there.

445
00:39:23,662 --> 00:39:26,308
这是考试中被视为正确答案的逻辑。
That is the shape the exam treats as correct.

446
00:39:27,918 --> 00:39:30,788
其中有两个选项出现的频率明显高于其他选项。
Two of these come up considerably more than the others.

447
00:39:31,246 --> 00:39:39,524
当题目描述需要将深度嵌套的 JSON 存入 Redshift 或其他关系型目标时，关系化是标准答案。
Relationalize is the standard answer when a question describes deeply nested JSON that needs to land in redshift or another relational target.

448
00:39:40,462 --> 00:39:48,000
它会将结构展开成一组由生成键连接的标记表，这正是数据仓库所需要的格式。
It unnests the structure into a set of flag tables joined by generated keys, which is exactly the shape a warehouse wants.

449
00:39:48,270 --> 00:39:51,972
手动操作这些非常麻烦，这就是为什么考试喜欢考这个点。
Doing that by hand is painful, which is why the exam likes it.

450
00:39:52,494 --> 00:39:58,692
当题目描述去重那些相似但并非完全相同的记录时，查找匹配 就是答案。
Find matches is the answer when a question describes deduplicating records that are similar but not identical.

451
00:39:59,534 --> 00:40:04,484
包含拼写错误、缩写街道名称或数字颠倒的客户记录。
Customer records with typos, abbreviated street names, transpose digits.

452
00:40:05,326 --> 00:40:12,560
这是一种基于标注样本训练的机器学习转换，仅靠精确匹配或 SQL 是做不到的。
It is a machine learning transform you train on labeled examples, and no amount of exact matching or SQL will do that job.

453
00:40:14,318 --> 00:40:19,140
书签可以回答一类问题，但有一个陷阱值得注意。
Bookmarks answer a whole family of questions, and there is one trap worth knowing about.

454
00:40:20,046 --> 00:40:23,908
它们依赖于作业脚本在开始时调用 作业初始化
They depend on the job script calling job.init at the start

455
00:40:24,622 --> 00:40:26,404
并在结束时调用 job.commit。
and job.comic at the end.

456
00:40:27,280 --> 00:40:36,772
如果作业缺少这些调用，即使启用了书签也会正常运行，每次都重新处理所有内容，且不会报错。
A job missing those calls will run happily with bookmarks enabled, reprocess everything every single time, and report no error at all.

457
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:38,340
没有任何警告。
Nothing warns you.

458
00:40:39,214 --> 00:40:47,040
对于 JDBC 源，书签需要一个只增加的列，比如自增键或最后修改时间戳。
For JDBC sources, the bookmark needs a column that only ever increases, such as an auto-incrementing key or a last

459
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,580
最后修改时间戳。
modified timestamp.

460
00:40:49,518 --> 00:40:53,220
如果源表两者都没有，书签就无法在其上工作。
If the source table has neither, bookmarks cannot work on it.

461
00:40:53,870 --> 00:40:59,684
正确答案将变成另一种增量方法，通常是 DMS 的变更数据捕获。
The correct answer becomes a different incremental approach, usually change data capture to DMS.

462
00:41:01,358 --> 00:41:04,036
这三项中的任何一项单独都会出考题。
Three of these produce exam questions on their own.

463
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:06,480
超时默认为 48 小时。
The timeout defaults to 48 hours.

464
00:41:06,702 --> 00:41:13,280
一个卡住而不是失败的作业，在有人发现之前会持续计费两天的 DPU 小时。
A job that hangs rather than fails keeps billing DPU hours for two days before anyone notices.

465
00:41:14,606 --> 00:41:18,000
设置合理的超时是降低成本的标准答案。
Setting a realistic timeout is a standard cost answer.

466
00:41:18,574 --> 00:41:20,720
最大并发运行数默认为 1。
Max concurrent runs defaults to 1.

467
00:41:20,814 --> 00:41:22,084
而这是一个微妙的点。
And this is the subtle one.

468
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:28,772
如果作业是按文件触发的，且两个文件同时到达，第二个触发将被直接拒绝而不是进入队列。
If a job is triggered per file and two files land together, the second trigger is rejected outright rather than queued.

469
00:41:30,766 --> 00:41:35,364
题目描述在高负载下文件被静默跳过，就是在指向这个默认值。
A question describing files being silently skipped under load is pointing at that default.

470
00:41:36,174 --> 00:41:42,372
只有当重新运行产生相同结果时，重试才是安全的，这就是幂等性的含义。
And retrees are only safe when rerunning produces the same result, which is what idem potent means.

471
00:41:43,086 --> 00:41:44,676
我们稍后会回到这一点。
We come back to that shortly.

472
00:41:46,414 --> 00:41:55,076
Flex 是成本类问题中价值最高的知识点之一。它是一个带有大幅折扣且有明显触发词的单一设置。
Flex is one of the highest value things to know for cost questions. It is a single setting with a large discount and an obvious trigger phrase.

473
00:41:57,774 --> 00:42:03,520
作业在闲置容量上运行，因此可能会延迟开始，并且可能在运行过程中被回收资源。
Jobs run on spare capacity, so they may start late and may have resources reclaimed mid run.

474
00:42:04,558 --> 00:42:11,652
这使得它不适用于有截止日期的任务，但非常适合夜间的批处理回填和测试负载。
That makes it wrong for anything with a deadline and right for nightly batch backfills and test workloads.

475
00:42:12,366 --> 00:42:17,124
注意那些没有 SLA 的夜间作业，当题目询问如何降低成本时。
Watch for an overnight job with no SLA where the question asks how to cut cost.

476
00:42:18,094 --> 00:42:20,708
Flex 通常是考查的两个点之一。
Flex is usually one of the two things being tested.

477
00:42:21,358 --> 00:42:23,524
另一个是 DPU 的规格优化。
The other is right sizing the DPS.

478
00:42:25,198 --> 00:42:31,396
自动缩放将你面临的问题从“我需要多少个工作节点”变为“我最多想要多少个”。
Auto scaling changes the question you have to answer from how many workers do I need to what is the most I would ever want.

479
00:42:33,102 --> 00:42:40,480
View 会在作业进行过程中增加或减少执行器，并且你只为实际运行的部分付费，而不是为你设置的上限付费。
View then adds and removes executors as the job progresses, and you are billed only for what actually ran rather than for the ceiling you set.

480
00:42:41,390 --> 00:42:50,052
当某晚的文件比另一晚的大 10 倍时，这非常有用，这描述了许多真实的流水线。
That is genuinely useful when one night's file is 10 times larger than another's, which describes a lot of real pipelines.

481
00:42:52,240 --> 00:42:57,124
最后一点对排查故障类题目很重要，而且它有点反直觉。
The last point matters for troubleshooting questions and it is counterintuitive.

482
00:42:57,934 --> 00:43:05,360
如果一个作业变慢是因为所有工作都堆到了一个执行器上，那增加更多执行器根本没用。
If a job is slow because all of the work landed on one executor, adding more executors changes nothing at all.

483
00:43:05,600 --> 00:43:08,772
它们会闲置，而同一个任务仍在缓慢运行。
They will sit idle while the same single task grinds on.

484
00:43:08,960 --> 00:43:11,748
这就是倾斜，它需要通过解决倾斜来修复。
That is SKU and it needs a SKU fix.

485
00:43:13,166 --> 00:43:21,956
一家公司运行一个每晚的 AWS Glue 作业，用于转换 Amazon S3 中前一天的订单文件并写入 Parquet 输出。
A company runs a nightly AWS Glue job that transforms the previous day's order files in Amazon S3 and writes parquet output.

486
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:26,640
该作业创建于 18 个月前，从未重新配置过。
The job was created 18 months ago and has never been reconfigured.

487
00:43:26,862 --> 00:43:28,644
它使用的是默认设置。
It uses the default settings.

488
00:43:29,518 --> 00:43:34,052
现在这个作业需要 4 小时，而且每月的 Glue 账单在持续增长。
The job now takes 4 hours and the monthly glue bill has grown steadily.

489
00:43:34,734 --> 00:43:36,836
财务部门要求降低成本。
Finance has asked for a reduction.

490
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:43,396
该作业必须在早上 8 点业务日开始前完成，目前它从午夜开始运行。
The job must finish before the business day begins at 8 in the morning and it currently starts at midnight.

491
00:43:43,918 --> 00:43:46,884
数据量每月增长约 2%。
Data volume grows by about 2% a month.

492
00:43:47,840 --> 00:43:52,324
哪种组合能在最小风险的情况下降低成本？
Which combination will reduce cost with the least risk to the deadline?

493
00:43:52,974 --> 00:43:53,280
A。
A.

494
00:43:53,806 --> 00:43:58,180
将作业切换到弹性执行类并启用作业书签。
Switch the job to the flex execution class and enable job bookmarks.

495
00:43:59,150 --> 00:44:04,900
d. 将工作节点类型从 G1X 增加到 G8X，以便更快完成任务。
d. Increase the worker type from G1X to G8X so the job finishes sooner.

496
00:44:05,520 --> 00:44:05,760
C
C

497
00:44:07,118 --> 00:44:12,164
将 DPU 分配从默认的 10 减少到 2，并接受更长的运行时间。
Reduce the DPU allocation from the default of 10 to 2 and accept a longer runtime.

498
00:44:13,006 --> 00:44:13,280
D。
D.

499
00:44:14,190 --> 00:44:19,120
将作业迁移到使用竞价实例的 EC2 上的 Amazon EMR。
Migrate the job to Amazon EMR on EC2 with spot instances.

500
00:44:20,398 --> 00:44:21,508
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

501
00:44:28,174 --> 00:44:29,440
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

502
00:44:30,894 --> 00:44:34,080
这个场景中有两个细节在提示我们。
Two details in that scenario, were doing the work.

503
00:44:34,574 --> 00:44:38,116
从未重新配置过，并且使用默认设置。
Never been reconfigured and uses the default settings.

504
00:44:39,214 --> 00:44:42,756
这是考试在告诉你，10 DPU 的默认值仍然生效。
That is the exam telling you the 10 dPU default is still in place.

505
00:44:43,630 --> 00:44:50,660
而且在有 4 小时运行时间的情况下，8 小时的窗口提供了巨大的缓冲时间，这正是使用 Flex 安全的条件。
And the 8 hour window against a 4 hour runtime is enormous slack, which is exactly the condition under which Flex is safe.

506
00:44:51,086 --> 00:44:53,200
选项 C 是一个有趣的陷阱。
Option C is the interesting trap.

507
00:44:53,422 --> 00:44:54,692
减少 DP
Reducing DP

508
00:44:55,662 --> 00:45:01,412
量确实是降低 Glue 成本的一个有效手段。而且本课程在两张幻灯片前就告诉过你这一点。
us genuinely is a valid blue cost lever. And this course told you so two slides ago.

509
00:45:02,318 --> 00:45:09,476
对于一个有严格截止日期的作业，将其减少到最低限度而不做任何衡量，并不等同于进行规格优化。
Reducing to the absolute floor with no measurement on a job with a hard deadline is not the same as right sizing it.

510
00:45:10,894 --> 00:45:13,956
这个选择的影响远不止于方便程度而已。
This choice has consequences well beyond convenience.

511
00:45:14,318 --> 00:45:24,644
从目录中读取意味着 Glue 已经知道哪些分区存在。这是谓词下推发挥作用的前提条件，因为你无法裁剪一个你还没获取到的列表。
Reading from the catalog means Blue already knows which partitions exist. That is the precondition for pushdown predicates doing anything useful because you cannot prune a list you have not got.

512
00:45:25,710 --> 00:45:35,840
这也是唯一适用 AWS Lake Formation 权限的路径，因为 Lake Formation 是在目录表上授予权限，而不是在 S3 上
It is also the only path where AWS Lake Formation permissions apply, Since lake formation grants permissions on catalog tables rather than on S3

513
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:36,708
前缀上。
prefixes.

514
00:45:38,158 --> 00:45:42,160
直接从路径读取会绕过这两个机制。
Reading straight from a path bypasses both mechanisms.

515
00:45:43,118 --> 00:45:48,804
所以当题目要求在 Glue 作业上进行列或行级别的访问控制时，要留意读取路径。
So when a question requires column or row level access control on a blue job, watch the read path.

516
00:45:49,358 --> 00:45:55,748
其中一个选项是直接从 S3 位置读取，这在逻辑上与该要求不兼容。
An option, reading directly from an S3 location, is quietly incompatible with that requirement.

517
00:45:57,360 --> 00:46:00,772
第二点非常重要，但经常被忽略。
The second point is worth real marks and gets overlooked.

518
00:46:01,262 --> 00:46:08,836
传统的模式是：作业写入新数据，然后运行爬虫来发现并注册新分区。
The traditional pattern is that a job writes new data, then a crawler runs afterwards to discover the new partitions and register them.

519
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:15,364
这是两个移动部件，而且它们之间存在延迟，在此期间新数据无法查询。
That is two moving parts, plus a delay between them during which the new data is not queryable.

520
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:21,796
使用 Enable Update Catalog 时，作业在写入的同时就会注册自己的分区。
With Enable Update Catalog, the job registers its own partitions as it writes them.

521
00:46:22,480 --> 00:46:29,028
留意那些询问如何以最低运维开销让新数据立即可查询的题目。
Watch for a question asking how to make new data queryable immediately with the least operational overhead.

522
00:46:29,360 --> 00:46:33,444
如果某个选项完全去掉了爬虫，那通常就是正确答案。
If one option removes the crawler entirely, that is usually the answer.

523
00:46:35,726 --> 00:46:38,180
最后一点是模块 1 的重申。
The last point restates module 1.

524
00:46:39,086 --> 00:46:45,380
根据你过滤的条件进行分区，而这很少是源数据本身的组织方式。
Partition on what you filter by, which is rarely how the source happens to organize itself.

525
00:46:47,086 --> 00:46:54,756
这是新加入的考点之一，因此 2025 年 12 月之前编写的资料可能无法帮你应对这一题。
This is one of the newly examinable areas, so material written before December 2025 will not prepare you for it.

526
00:46:56,046 --> 00:47:03,076
这些格式解决的问题是：在 S3 中堆放的普通 Parquet 文件没有“事务”的概念。
The problem these formats solve is that a plain pile of Parquet files in S3 has no concept of a transaction.

527
00:47:03,694 --> 00:47:05,668
你无法更新单行数据。
You cannot update a single row.

528
00:47:06,478 --> 00:47:12,324
如果没有重写整个文件，你就无法为了隐私请求删除某个客户的记录。
You cannot delete one customer's records for a privacy request without rewriting whole files.

529
00:47:12,942 --> 00:47:15,716
而且读取者可能会看到处于半写入状态的数据。
And a reader can see a half-written state.

530
00:47:16,846 --> 00:47:21,604
Iceberg 添加了一个元数据层，使这些操作具有原子性。
Iceberg adds a metadata layer that makes those operations atomic.

531
00:47:22,446 --> 00:47:30,820
对于 Glue 作业来说，实际效果是你可以对数据湖执行合并语句，这改变了架构上可行性的范围。
For a blue job, the practical effect is that you can write merge statements against a data lake, which changes what is architecturally possible.

532
00:47:31,310 --> 00:47:33,444
模块 9 会全面涵盖这一点。
Module 9 covers this in full.

533
00:47:34,702 --> 00:47:40,432
现在，这是一个比其表面规模预示的要多出更多考题的主题。
Now, a topic that produces more exam questions than its apparent size suggests.

534
00:47:41,038 --> 00:47:48,740
Glue 在 AWS 管理的环境中运行，而不是在你的账户网络内，除非你为作业连接一个连接。
Dew runs in an AWS managed environment, not inside your account's network, until you attach a connection to the job.

535
00:47:49,518 --> 00:47:55,748
一旦作业必须访问私有资源，网络就会介入，故障点也会大幅增加。
The moment a job must reach something private, networking gets involved and the surface for failure grows sharply.

536
00:47:56,558 --> 00:48:00,388
这意味着位于 VPC 中的数据库或处于私有路由后的存储桶。
That means a database in a VPC or a bucket behind a private route.

537
00:48:01,006 --> 00:48:04,260
因为 Glue 是无服务器的，这些故障看起来会很神秘。
Because Blue is serverless, these failures look mysterious.

538
00:48:04,992 --> 00:48:09,796
没有实例可以登录，也没有明显的可以运行连通性测试的地方。
There is no instance to log into and no obvious place to run a connectivity test from.

539
00:48:10,192 --> 00:48:12,932
好消息是，原因很少且经常重复。
The good news is that the causes are few and repeat.

540
00:48:13,454 --> 00:48:18,596
掌握那三到四个标准原因，这就会变成拿分的捷径，而不是让你感到头疼的难题。
Learn the three or four standard ones and this becomes a source of quick marks rather than a source of dread.

541
00:48:20,302 --> 00:48:23,044
第三点第一次就坑到几乎所有人。
The third point catches almost everyone the first time.

542
00:48:23,232 --> 00:48:30,692
当 Glue 把网络接口放入你的子网时，工作节点之间会互相通信，这些流量受安全组控制。
When Glue puts network interfaces into your subnet, the workers talk to each other and that traffic is governed by the security group.

543
00:48:31,214 --> 00:48:37,572
因为源和目的地都在这个组内，该组必须允许来自自身的入站流量。
Because the source and destination are both inside that group, the group must allow inbound traffic from itself.

544
00:48:37,872 --> 00:48:43,108
如果没有这个自引用规则，任务就会卡住，然后报错提示信息不明确。
Without that self-referencing rule, the job hangs and then fails with something unhelpful.

545
00:48:43,982 --> 00:48:45,860
第四点是经典考点。
And the fourth point is the classic.

546
00:48:46,352 --> 00:48:49,892
Glue 从 S3 读取自己的脚本和库。
Glue reads its own script and its libraries from S3.

547
00:48:50,830 --> 00:48:56,420
如果你把任务放在一个没有通往 S3 路由的私有子网中，代码还没开始运行就会崩溃。
Put a job in a private subnet with no root to S3 and it dies before your code starts.

548
00:48:57,934 --> 00:49:03,204
容易让人困惑的是网络连接类型，因为它并不连接到任何东西。
The one that confuses people is the network connection type because it does not connect to anything.

549
00:49:03,566 --> 00:49:11,204
它的唯一用途是告诉 Glue 将任务的网络接口放在哪个 VPC、子网和安全组中。
Its only purpose is to tell Blue which VPC, subnet, and security group to place the job's network interfaces in.

550
00:49:12,942 --> 00:49:18,084
当你需要任务访问非 JDBC 数据库的私有资源时，就会用到它。
You use it when the job must reach something private that is not a JDBC database.

551
00:49:19,022 --> 00:49:25,412
常见情况是通过 VPC 端点访问 S3 bucket，或者访问 VPC 内的 API。
The common case is an S3 bucket reached through a VPC endpoint or an API inside the VPC.

552
00:49:26,126 --> 00:49:33,348
所以，一个描述在不涉及数据库的情况下必须在 VPC 内运行的 Glue 作业的问题，就是在考查网络连接。
So a question describing a blue job that must run inside a VPC with no database involved is describing a network connection.

553
00:49:33,902 --> 00:49:37,924
选项通常会提供 JDBC 作为看似合理的错误答案。
The options will usually offer JDBC as the plausible wrong answer.

554
00:49:39,182 --> 00:49:43,812
这个区别非常关键，而且在压力下很容易选错。
This distinction is worth real marks and it is easy to get wrong under pressure.

555
00:49:45,358 --> 00:49:49,988
网关端点不是设备，它是路由表中的一个条目。
A gateway endpoint is not a device, it is an entry added to a root table.

556
00:49:50,414 --> 00:49:57,188
这就是为什么关于“看起来已配置但无法工作的网关端点”的问题，几乎总是考查路由表。
That is why a question about a gateway endpoint that looks configured but does not work is almost always a root table question.

557
00:49:58,062 --> 00:50:05,828
接口端点是利用 AWS PrivateLink 在你的子网内拥有私有 IP 的真实网络接口。
An interface endpoint is a genuine network interface with a private address inside your subnet using AWS private link.

558
00:50:06,766 --> 00:50:13,552
网关端点仅用于 S3 和 DynamoDB。它们是免费的，且无法从 VPC 外部访问。
Gateway endpoints exist only for S3 and DynamoDB. They are free and they cannot be reached from outside the VPC.

559
00:50:13,902 --> 00:50:16,260
其他所有情况都需要接口端点。
Everything else needs an interface endpoint.

560
00:50:17,902 --> 00:50:23,140
一名数据工程师配置了一个 AWS Glue 作业来读取 Amazon S3 bucket。
A data engineer has configured an AWS Glue job to read from an Amazon S3 bucket.

561
00:50:23,312 --> 00:50:32,612
已经创建了包含正确 VPC、私有子网和安全组的 Glue 连接。附加到任务的 IAM 角色已授予对该存储桶的完全访问权限。
A glue connection has been created with the correct VPC, private subnet, and security group. The IAM role attached to the job grants full access to the bucket.

562
00:50:33,486 --> 00:50:40,112
任务每次运行都会失败，报错信息指向 Amazon S3 VPC 网关端点。
The job fails on every run with an error referring to the Amazon S3 VPC gateway endpoint.

563
00:50:40,430 --> 00:50:44,836
存储桶策略是宽松的，且 IAM 角色的正确性已得到验证。
The bucket policy is permissive and the IAM role has been verified as correct.

564
00:50:45,806 --> 00:50:47,396
最可能的原因是什么？
What is the most likely cause?

565
00:50:48,046 --> 00:50:48,272
A。
A.

566
00:50:49,294 --> 00:50:54,020
Glue 安全组不允许来自 S3 网关端点的入站流量。
The Blue Security Group does not allow inbound traffic from the S3 gateway endpoint.

567
00:50:54,478 --> 00:50:54,752
b。
b.

568
00:50:54,990 --> 00:50:58,628
存储桶策略没有明确列出 Glue 服务主体。
The bucket policy does not explicitly name the Blue service principle.

569
00:50:59,470 --> 00:51:03,232
C. Glue 连接缺少完整的域名
C. The Blue connection is missing a fully qualified domain

570
00:51:03,232 --> 00:51:04,432
名称。D。
name. D.

571
00:51:05,614 --> 00:51:09,924
子网的路由表没有通往 S3 网关端点的路由。
The Subnet's root table has no root to the S3 gateway endpoint.

572
00:51:10,574 --> 00:51:11,844
停下来思考一下并做决定。
Pause and decide.

573
00:51:18,606 --> 00:51:22,468
答案是 D，原因就是上一页幻灯片直接套用的逻辑。
The answer is D, and the reasoning is the previous slide applied directly.

574
00:51:22,926 --> 00:51:25,156
网关端点是路由表中的一项条目。
A gateway endpoint is a root table entry.

575
00:51:25,550 --> 00:51:32,644
如果不存在该路由，通往 S3 的流量将走默认路径，而在私有子网中，这会导致流量无法到达任何地方。
If the root is not there, traffic to S3 leaves by the default path, which in a private subnet goes nowhere.

576
00:51:33,102 --> 00:51:39,428
选项 A 是为了误导那些只记得安全组对 Glue 很重要的人。
Option A is designed to catch anyone who half remembers that security groups matter for blue.

577
00:51:39,822 --> 00:51:40,272
它们确实很重要。
They do.

578
00:51:40,590 --> 00:51:46,628
对于工作节点之间的自引用规则，但网关端点并不是负责传输流量的东西。
For the self-referencing rule between workers, but a gateway endpoint is not a thing that sends you traffic.

579
00:51:47,982 --> 00:51:50,244
注意 B 是如何被排除的。
And notice how B was disposed of.

580
00:51:51,150 --> 00:51:55,460
题目明确验证了 IAM 和存储桶策略。
The question explicitly verified IAM and the bucket policy.

581
00:51:56,046 --> 00:52:02,084
当问题提供一个已确认的事实时，它是在排除一个选项，而不是在描述场景。
When a question hands you a verified fact, it is eliminating an option, not decorating the scenario.

582
00:52:03,790 --> 00:52:08,132
这两个概念经常被混淆，一旦掌握了区分点就非常简单。
These two get confused constantly, and the separator is simple once you have it.

583
00:52:08,718 --> 00:52:14,596
Amazon Macie 会检查已经存在于 S3 中的数据，并告诉你其中包含哪些敏感信息。
Amazon Macy looks at data already sitting in S3 and tells you what sensitive information is in there.

584
00:52:15,438 --> 00:52:21,380
它是一个按计划在各个存储桶中运行的发现和监控工具，并报告其发现结果。
It is a discovery and monitoring tool that runs on a schedule across buckets and it reports findings.

585
00:52:22,318 --> 00:52:28,100
Glue 的敏感数据检测是在作业过程中、记录流经时运行的。
Blue Sensitive data detection runs inside the job as records pass through.

586
00:52:28,526 --> 00:52:33,476
它可以对发现的内容采取行动，在数据写入之前进行脱敏或遮盖。
It can act on what it finds, masking or redacting before the data is ever written down.

587
00:52:34,062 --> 00:52:39,140
因此，关于“发现现有资产中存在哪些个人数据”的问题属于 Macie。
So a question about discovering what personal data already exists across an estate is messy.

588
00:52:39,792 --> 00:52:46,404
而关于“防止个人数据进入精炼层”的问题则是 Glue。
A question about preventing personal data from reaching the curated layer in the first place is blue.

589
00:52:47,632 --> 00:52:55,940
无服务器意味着没有可以登录的机器，因此考试要求你了解哪种可观测性开关能解决哪类问题。
Serverless means there is no machine to log into, so the exam expects you to know which observability switch answers which complaint.

590
00:52:56,432 --> 00:52:59,204
最后一点是出题点。
The last point is the one that generates questions.

591
00:52:59,632 --> 00:53:02,756
默认情况下，日志是在作业完成后才写入的。
By default, logs are written when the job completes.

592
00:53:03,534 --> 00:53:07,556
对于耗时较长的任务，这意味着要等几个小时才能查出失败原因。
For a long job, that means waiting hours to discover why it failed.

593
00:53:07,982 --> 00:53:12,420
对于卡住并最终被强制终止的任务，可能根本就没有有用的日志。
For a job that hangs and is eventually killed, it can mean no useful logs at all.

594
00:53:13,038 --> 00:53:15,460
持续日志会将它们流式传输到 CloudWatch。
Continuous logging streams them to CloudWatch.

595
00:53:16,206 --> 00:53:17,604
在任务运行过程中实时记录日志。
Logs as the job runs.

596
00:53:18,446 --> 00:53:20,804
Spark UI 回答的是另一个问题。
The Spark UI answers a different question.

597
00:53:21,552 --> 00:53:28,708
它显示哪个阶段消耗了时间，这在你需要分析“任务成功但耗时远超预期”的情况时非常有用。
It shows which stage consumed the time, which is what you need when a job succeeded but took far longer than expected.

598
00:53:30,352 --> 00:53:40,004
考试指南明确提到了 Databrew，所以它是考点；而且从 1.1 版本起，它还同时提到了 Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio。
The exam guide names Databrew explicitly, so it is examinable and it also names Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio alongside it as of version 1.1.

599
00:53:40,672 --> 00:53:42,756
这是它们之间的实际关系。
Here is the practical relationship.

600
00:53:43,232 --> 00:53:50,148
Data Brew 是为分析师提供的较旧的独立工具，包含超过 250 种预设转换。
Data Brew is the older standalone tool for analysts with over 250 pre-built transformations.

601
00:53:50,894 --> 00:53:56,068
Glue Studio 现在拥有自己的无代码数据准备体验。
Blue Studio now has its own no-code data preparation experience.

602
00:53:56,494 --> 00:54:02,596
它的功能基本相同，运行在 Glue Spark 上，并且可以导入现有的 Data Brew 脚本。
It does much the same thing, runs on Blue Spark, and can import existing Data Brew recipes.

603
00:54:03,918 --> 00:54:11,552
当题目描述一名无法编写代码、需要清洗数据的业务分析师时，这两个选项中的任何一个都可能是正确答案。
When a question describes a business analyst who cannot write code needing to clean data, either answer can be correct.

604
00:54:12,046 --> 00:54:14,084
要根据题目具体提到的名称来判断选择哪一个。
Read for which one the question names.

605
00:54:15,342 --> 00:54:18,980
Python shell 作业目前利用率不高，它们常出现在成本相关的题目中。
Python shell jobs are underused and they show up in cost questions.

606
00:54:19,232 --> 00:54:24,420
考虑一个仅调用 API、移动文件或执行一条 SQL 语句的作业。
Consider a job that just calls an API, moves a file, or issues one SQL statement.

607
00:54:24,974 --> 00:54:27,364
为了这类任务去启动一个 Spark 集群是浪费。
Spinning up a Spark cluster for that is waste.

608
00:54:27,758 --> 00:54:32,868
在 1/6 DPU 上运行 Python shell 作业是合适的规模，且成本极低。
A Python shell job at 116th of a DPU is the right shape and a fraction of the price.

609
00:54:37,552 --> 00:54:42,192
它在 2026 年 4 月底停止面向新客户提供服务。
It closed to new customers at the end of April 2026.

610
00:54:43,566 --> 00:54:49,860
现有客户可以继续使用，而 AWS 将新的 Ray 工作负载指向 Amazon EKS。
Existing customers carry on and AWS points new ray workloads at Amazon EKS.

611
00:54:50,606 --> 00:54:54,980
它仍保留在旧的题库中，所以要认出它并了解它的现状。
It remains in older question banks, so recognize it and know its status.

612
00:54:55,886 --> 00:55:01,188
现有客户可以继续使用，而 AWS 将新的 Ray 工作负载指向 Amazon EKS。
Existing customers carry on and AWS points new Ray workloads at Amazon EKS.

613
00:55:01,646 --> 00:55:05,764
它仍保留在旧的题库中，所以要认出它并了解它的现状。
It remains in older question banks, so recognize it and know its status.

614
00:55:07,054 --> 00:55:12,900
Glue 有自己的小型编排系统，了解它的边界在哪里是考试的考点。
Glue has its own small orchestration system and knowing where its boundary sits is the exam point.

615
00:55:13,720 --> 00:55:20,292
Glue 工作流可以将爬虫、作业和触发器结合在一起，并根据成功或失败提供条件逻辑。
Glue workflows can chain crawlers, jobs, and triggers together with conditional logic on success or failure.

616
00:55:21,230 --> 00:55:29,316
对于一个完全由 Glue 组件构成的流水线，这已经足够了，不需要额外服务，因此它是开销最低的选项。
For a pipeline made entirely of blue components, that is genuinely enough and it needs no additional service, which makes it the lowest overhead answer.

617
00:55:30,126 --> 00:55:38,272
一旦流水线包含非 Glue 的内容，比如 Lambda 函数、Redshift 语句或人工审批步骤，
The moment the pipeline includes something that is not blue, a lambda function, a redshift statement, a human approval step,

618
00:55:38,542 --> 00:55:40,452
Glue 工作流就无法再继续处理了。
blue workflows run out of road.

619
00:55:41,102 --> 00:55:45,712
此时的答案就变成了 AWS Step Functions 或 Amazon MWAA。
The answer then becomes AWS Step Functions or Amazon MWAA.

620
00:55:47,150 --> 00:55:49,732
模块 6 正确涵盖了这一对比。
Module 6 covers that comparison properly.

621
00:55:51,438 --> 00:55:56,452
这把模块 1 中的可靠性词汇与具体的技术应用联系了起来。
This connects the reliability vocabulary from module 1 to something concrete.

622
00:55:56,974 --> 00:56:04,420
最大重试次数看起来像是免费的弹性，但并非如此，因为一个在半途中失败的作业可能已经写入了一半的输出。
Max retrees looks like free resilience, and it is not because a job that failed halfway may already have written half of its output.

623
00:56:05,006 --> 00:56:07,876
重新执行它时，那一半的内容就会被再次写入。
Retree it and that half gets written a second time.

624
00:56:08,878 --> 00:56:11,236
有三种机制可以让重试变得安全。
Three mechanisms make reruns safe.

625
00:56:12,142 --> 00:56:13,860
覆盖整个分区。
Overwriting a whole partition.

626
00:56:14,222 --> 00:56:18,788
这样第二次运行就会替换掉第一次运行的工作，而不是叠加在上面。
So the second run replaces the first run's work rather than adding to it.

627
00:56:19,502 --> 00:56:20,324
书签（Bookmarks）。
Bookmarks.

628
00:56:20,910 --> 00:56:24,580
这样第二次运行就不会重新读取相同的源记录。
So the second run does not reread the same source records.

629
00:56:25,326 --> 00:56:32,932
或者基于标识符的 Iceberg 合并，这样重复的记录会原地更新而不是产生重复。
Or an iceberg merge keyed on an identifier, so a repeated record updates in place rather than duplicating.

630
00:56:33,902 --> 00:56:41,732
如果没有其中任何一种机制，开启重试会将明显的失败转变为隐蔽的数据质量问题，这要糟糕得多。
Without one of those, turning on retrees converts a visible failure into an invisible data quality problem, which is much worse.

631
00:56:43,374 --> 00:56:50,212
故障排除类问题是领域 1 和领域 3 的核心内容，并且它们遵循一种可识别的模式。
Troubleshooting questions are a reliable part of both domain 1 and domain 3, and they follow a recognizable pattern.

632
00:56:50,672 --> 00:56:59,524
任务运行缓慢或失败，提供 4 个合理的修复方案，而正确的选项完全取决于症状所反映出的底层问题。
A job is slow or failing, 4 plausible fixes are offered, and the right one depends entirely on which underlying problem the symptoms describe.

633
00:57:00,334 --> 00:57:09,348
基本上有四种原因：并行度不足、读取数据过多、跨键的数据倾斜，以及小文件问题。
There are essentially four causes not enough parallelism, too much data being read, data skew, across keys, and the small file problem.

634
00:57:09,632 --> 00:57:12,260
增加工作节点仅能解决第一种情况。
Adding workers only helps the first of those.

635
00:57:12,974 --> 00:57:20,004
养成在查看选项前先判断属于这四种情况之一的习惯，可以在两个领域中为你赢得分数。
Getting into the habit of asking which of the four this is before you look at the options will earn you marks across two domains.

636
00:57:20,398 --> 00:57:26,148
这也能防止你选择那个听起来最全面的选项，而这正是这类题目误导人的地方。
It also stops you picking the option that sounds most thorough, which is how these questions catch people.

637
00:57:27,854 --> 00:57:29,444
把这张表当作查询表来学习。
Learn this table as a lookup.

638
00:57:30,126 --> 00:57:35,140
需要仔细区分的前两行是前两项，因为它们都描述了任务运行缓慢的情况。
The two rows to separate carefully are the first two because both describe a slow job.

639
00:57:35,918 --> 00:57:42,432
如果每个执行器都在工作但任务只是变慢了，说明你缺乏容量，增加更多工作节点会有帮助。
If every executor is working and the job is simply slow, you are short of capacity and more workers help.

640
00:57:42,926 --> 00:57:49,412
如果一个任务运行一小时而其他任务在几分钟内就完成了，那就是数据倾斜，此时增加的工作节点只会闲置。
If one task runs for an hour while the others finished in minutes, that is skewed, and more workers will sit idle watching.

641
00:57:49,806 --> 00:57:52,912
解决倾斜的方法是改变数据的分布方式。
The fix for skew is to change how the data is distributed.

642
00:57:53,232 --> 00:58:00,036
基于更好的键进行重分区，添加随机盐值来分散热键，或者通过 R 类型给每个工作节点分配更多内存。
Repartition on a better key, add a random salt to spread a hotkey, or give each worker more memory with an R type.

643
00:58:01,294 --> 00:58:08,356
这是模块 1 分区课程中的 Glue 表达式，考试中它被作为成本问题而非性能问题来考查。
This is the glue expression of the partitioning lesson from module 1, and the exam tests it as a cost question rather than a performance one.

644
00:58:08,752 --> 00:58:17,312
如果没有下推谓词，一个请求一天数据的任务会将整个表读入执行器内存，然后丢弃掉几乎所有的内容。
Without a pushdown predicate, a job asked for one day of data, reads the entire table into executor memory and then discards almost all of it.

645
00:58:17,870 --> 00:58:22,308
你为每一个字节、每个工作节点的每一秒钟都付了费，但结果却是一样的。
You paid for every byte, every second of every worker, and the result is identical.

646
00:58:24,430 --> 00:58:32,032
有了下推谓词，Glue 会先根据分区元数据评估过滤条件，根本不会打开不需要的文件夹。
With a pushdown predicate, Blue evaluates the filter against partition metadata first and simply never opens the folders it does not need.

647
00:58:32,192 --> 00:58:35,460
目录分区谓词变体更进一步。
The catalog partition predicate variant goes one better.

648
00:58:35,886 --> 00:58:39,460
它在数据目录本身内部就进行过滤评估。
It evaluates the filter inside the data catalog itself.

649
00:58:39,758 --> 00:58:42,628
这样 Glue 就甚至不需要列出这些分区了。
So Blue never even lists the partitions.

650
00:58:44,174 --> 00:58:49,668
小文件是导致数据湖莫名变慢最常见的原因，考试也知道这一点。
Small files are the most common real cause of an inexplicably slow lake, and the exam knows it.

651
00:58:51,054 --> 00:58:53,028
有三个层级的修复方法和相关题目。
There are three levels of fix and questions.

652
00:58:53,358 --> 00:58:54,512
测试不同的方案。
Test different ones.

653
00:58:54,752 --> 00:59:00,868
在写入时，减少输出分区的数量，让 Glue 生成更少但更大的文件。
On write, reduce the number of output partitions so blue emits fewer larger files.

654
00:59:01,710 --> 00:59:05,872
在读取时，Glue 可以将小文件组合在一起，让一个任务处理
On read, blue can group small files together so one task handles

655
00:59:05,872 --> 00:59:13,316
多个文件。从结构上讲，运行一个合并作业或让 Apache Iceberg 为你完成，这在模块 9 中有涵盖。
many. Structurally, run a compaction job or let Apache IZBOG do it for you, which module 9 covers.

656
00:59:15,214 --> 00:59:17,552
最后一项是镜像情况。
The last bullet is the mirror image.

657
00:59:18,158 --> 00:59:24,772
一个巨大的 Gzip 文件无法拆分，因此无论你有多少工作节点，只有一个执行器会去读取它。
One enormous Gizip file cannot be split, so exactly one executor reads it, however many workers you have.

658
00:59:26,414 --> 00:59:36,228
一个视图任务读取 Amazon S3 中的分区 Parquet 数据集，其中包含按年和月划分的 5 年交易历史。
A view job reads a partitioned Parquet dataset in Amazon S3 containing 5 years of transaction history partitioned by year and month.

659
00:59:36,622 --> 00:59:40,324
该任务生成的报告仅涵盖最近的一个月。
The job produces a report covering the most recent month only.

660
00:59:40,782 --> 00:59:45,284
该任务在 20 个 G2X 工作节点上运行，耗时 90 分钟。
The job runs on 20 G2X workers and takes 90 minutes.

661
00:59:46,126 --> 00:59:51,972
监控显示所有执行器一直处于忙碌状态，且任务每次运行都要读取大约 4TB 数据。
Monitoring shows all executors are busy throughout and the job reads roughly 4TB on every run.

662
00:59:52,366 --> 00:59:56,804
团队被要求在不改变报告内容的情况下，同时降低运行时间和成本。
The team has been asked to reduce both runtime and cost without changing the report.

663
00:59:57,358 --> 00:59:59,396
数据工程师应该首先做什么？
What should the data engineer do first?

664
01:00:01,454 --> 01:00:06,180
a. 将工作节点数量从 20 个增加到 60 个，以缩短运行时间。
a Increase the number of workers from 20 to 60 to shorten the runtime.

665
01:00:06,702 --> 01:00:06,912
b.
b.

666
01:00:07,118 --> 01:00:11,428
添加下推谓词，使任务仅读取当前月份的分区。
Add a pushdown predicate so the job reads only the current month's partitions.

667
01:00:11,950 --> 01:00:16,752
c. 将工作节点从 G2X 切换到 R2X，为每个节点提供更多内存。
C. Switch the workers from G2X to R2X to provide more memory per worker.

668
01:00:17,102 --> 01:00:17,312
d.
D.

669
01:00:17,552 --> 01:00:20,548
启用自动扩缩容，最大限制为 20 个工作节点。
Enable autoscaling with a maximum of 20 workers.

670
01:00:22,912 --> 01:00:24,964
稍等一下，我们来做决定。
Pause and decide.

671
01:00:31,374 --> 01:00:32,612
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

672
01:00:33,070 --> 01:00:38,820
关键数字是 4TB，这是为了生成 5 年数据中仅 1 个月的数据量。
The decisive number is 4TB, read to produce 1 month of a 5-year dataset.

673
01:00:40,526 --> 01:00:44,260
这大约是报告所需数据的 60 倍。
That is roughly 60 times more data than the report needs.

674
01:00:44,910 --> 01:00:49,924
选项 A 是值得思考的，因为它在机制上并没有错。
Option A is the one worth dwelling on because it is not wrong about the mechanism.

675
01:00:50,862 --> 01:00:54,756
所有执行器忙碌确实意味着增加更多工作节点可以更快完成任务。
All executors busy really does mean more workers would finish faster.

676
01:00:55,054 --> 01:01:00,324
但它没能满足要求的另一半——成本，这就是典型的 Glue 陷阱题型。
It fails on the second half of the requirement, cost, and this is the standard shape of a glue trap.

677
01:01:02,414 --> 01:01:07,460
一个只满足其中一个目标而让另一个变差的选项就是干扰项。
An option that satisfies one stated goal while making the other worse is a distractor.

678
01:01:07,680 --> 01:01:09,572
不过，我们要纠正一下它的逻辑。
However, correct its reasoning.

679
01:01:10,894 --> 01:01:16,480
一个 AWS Glue 作业将每日提取的数据加载到精选的 Amazon S3 数据集中。
An AWS Glue job loads a nightly extract into a curated Amazon S3 dataset.

680
01:01:16,814 --> 01:01:21,476
由于源数据库偶尔会超时，最大重试次数被设置为 3。
Max retrease is set to 3 because the source database occasionally times out.

681
01:01:21,680 --> 01:01:24,836
该作业将其输出追加到当天的分区中。
The job appends its output to the current days partition.

682
01:01:25,390 --> 01:01:29,956
分析师报告称，在某些日子里，收入总额大约是财务部门预期值的两倍。
Analysts report that on some days the revenue totals are roughly double what finance expects.

683
01:01:30,734 --> 01:01:34,640
受影响的日期与源数据库运行缓慢的夜晚相吻合。
The affected days correlate with nights when the source database was slow.

684
01:01:34,800 --> 01:01:37,572
该作业在所有这些晚上都报告成功。
The job reports success on every one of those nights.

685
01:01:38,254 --> 01:01:40,452
发生了什么情况，正确的修复方法是什么？
What is happening and what is the correct fix?

686
01:01:41,198 --> 01:01:41,440
a.
A.

687
01:01:42,318 --> 01:01:44,836
源数据库正在发送重复的行。
The source database is sending duplicate rows.

688
01:01:45,040 --> 01:01:47,076
在提取查询中添加 distinct。
Add a distinct to the extract query.

689
01:01:47,600 --> 01:01:51,524
b. 重试会重新运行已经写入过输出的作业。
b Retriees rerun a job that had already written output.

690
01:01:52,014 --> 01:01:55,588
在分区上使用覆盖模式，而不是追加。
Write with overwrite on the partition instead of appending.

691
01:01:56,174 --> 01:01:56,400
C。
C.

692
01:01:57,040 --> 01:02:01,988
最大重试次数应设为零，以便将故障暴露给运维团队。
Max retrieve should be set to zero so that failures are surfaced to the operations team.

693
01:02:02,798 --> 01:02:03,040
D。
D.

694
01:02:04,238 --> 01:02:09,220
该任务需要更多的 DPS，以便在数据库超时前完成。
The job needs more DPS so that it completes before the database times out.

695
01:02:09,840 --> 01:02:11,076
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

696
01:02:17,454 --> 01:02:18,468
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

697
01:02:18,958 --> 01:02:20,868
有两个细节。它们同时揭示了答案。
Two details. Give it away together.

698
01:02:21,200 --> 01:02:24,612
任务报告成功，所以这根本不是一个关于故障的问题。
The job reports success, so this is not a failure question at all.

699
01:02:24,880 --> 01:02:29,280
而且糟糕的情况与缓慢的夜晚相关，而那时正是触发重试的时候。
And the bad days correlate with slow nights, which is when retrees fire.

700
01:02:29,840 --> 01:02:37,188
一个在写入一半输出后失败、然后从头开始重试并再次追加的任务，就会产生这种结果。
A job that failed after lighting half its output, then retried from the beginning and appended again, produces exactly this.

701
01:02:37,710 --> 01:02:41,252
选项 C 很诱人，因为它确实能停止重复。
Option C is the tempting one because it does stop the duplication.

702
01:02:41,998 --> 01:02:49,348
但它也丢弃了让流水线在不稳定的数据库中幸存的弹性，把一个隐性的数据问题变成了每天都要处理的运维问题。
It also throws away the resilience that made the pipeline survive a flaky database, converting a silent data problem into a nightly operational one.

703
01:02:50,094 --> 01:02:52,000
考试奖励的是修复写入过程。
The exam rewards fixing the write.

704
01:02:52,302 --> 01:02:56,612
所以是让重试变得安全，而不是取消重试导致写入保持不安全。
So retrees become safe rather than removing retrees so writes stay unsafe.

705
01:02:58,286 --> 01:03:01,988
这对选项经常出现，而且有一个明确的规则。
This pair appears constantly and there is a clean rule for it.

706
01:03:02,254 --> 01:03:05,412
Lambda 有严格的 15 分钟执行限制。
Lambda has a hard 15-minute execution limit.

707
01:03:05,870 --> 01:03:12,836
如果描述的工作可能超过这个限制，无论 Lambda 看起来多么方便，它都会被排除。
If the work described could ever exceed that, lambda is eliminated regardless of how convenient it otherwise looks.

708
01:03:13,358 --> 01:03:15,440
这是要检查的第一件事。
That is the first thing to check.

709
01:03:15,950 --> 01:03:21,092
在那个上限之下，Lambda 更便宜，且能在毫秒内启动，而不是几分钟。
Below that ceiling, lambda is cheaper and starts in milliseconds rather than minutes.

710
01:03:21,614 --> 01:03:26,948
对于处理单个上传文件并进行轻量级转换，它通常是首选。
For reacting to a single uploaded file with a light transform, it usually wins outright.

711
01:03:27,470 --> 01:03:30,980
第二个判断标准是工作是否真正属于分布式计算。
The second decider is whether the work is genuinely distributed.

712
01:03:31,822 --> 01:03:36,160
合并两个大型数据集需要 Spark，因此需要 Glue。
Joining two large datasets needs Spark and therefore Blue.

713
01:03:36,654 --> 01:03:40,880
在 8 MB 文件中重命名 3 个列则不需要。
Renaming 3 columns in an 8 MB file does not.

714
01:03:42,254 --> 01:03:48,356
模块 5 会深入探讨引擎选择，包括 Amazon EMR 在两者中的定位。
Module 5 goes deeper into engine choice, including where Amazon EMR fits alongside both.

715
01:03:49,902 --> 01:03:56,868
Glue 和 EMR 有大量重叠，题目依赖于你找到区分点，而不是进行通用的权衡。
Blue and EMR overlap heavily and questions rely on you finding the separator rather than weighing them generally.

716
01:03:57,582 --> 01:04:00,164
有两件事能可靠地指向 EMR。
Two things reliably point at EMR.

717
01:04:00,718 --> 01:04:03,524
第一，是 Glue 不提供的引擎。
First, an engine Glue does not offer.

718
01:04:04,000 --> 01:04:10,320
如果问题明确提到高权重的 HBase、Presto 或 Trino，那么 Glue 就立刻排除。
If the question mentions high weighted HBase, Presto or Trino by name, Blue is out immediately.

719
01:04:10,862 --> 01:04:19,760
第二，是正在迁移的现有 Hadoop 环境，在这种情况下，为 Glue 重写所有内容是昂贵的路径，而平移迁移则是廉价的路径。
Second, an existing Hadoop estate being migrated where rewriting everything for Blue is the expensive path and lift and shift is the cheap one.

720
01:04:20,206 --> 01:04:21,636
有两件事指向 Glue
Two things point at Blue

721
01:04:22,638 --> 01:04:29,124
运维开销最少，且是一个没有特殊要求的简单定时 ETL 作业。
Least operational overhead phasing and a straightforward scheduled ETL job with no exotic requirements.

722
01:04:29,934 --> 01:04:39,428
别忘了还有 EMR 无服务器，它大大削弱了关于运维开销的论点，而且这是人们经常忽略的选择项。
And remember that EMR serverless exists, which blunts the operational overhead argument considerably and is often the option people forget to consider.

723
01:04:40,878 --> 01:04:46,212
这是一个非常现代化的选项，并且出现在较新的题目中，所以值得深入了解。
This is a genuinely modern option and it appears in newer questions, so it is worth knowing well.

724
01:04:46,926 --> 01:04:55,364
Zero ETL 集成从受支持的源端持续复制到 Amazon Redshift，由 AWS 负责运行整个机制。
Zero ETL integrations replicate from a supported source into Amazon Redshift continuously with AWS operating the entire mechanism.

725
01:04:56,302 --> 01:05:00,548
不需要编写作业，无需安排计划，也不需要处理故障。
There is no job to write, nothing to schedule, and no failure to handle.

726
01:05:01,454 --> 01:05:04,740
正是这些限制条件让它成为考试中的正确答案。
The limits are what make it answerable in an exam.

727
01:05:05,838 --> 01:05:11,204
它仅在受支持的配对之间工作，且是移动数据而非转换数据。
It works only between supported pairs and it moves data rather than transforming it.

728
01:05:12,142 --> 01:05:21,316
所以要留意那些要求提供分析用的操作数据、追求最低运维开销且未提及任何转换要求的题目。
So watch for a question wanting operational data available for analytics with the least possible overhead where no transformation is mentioned.

729
01:05:22,286 --> 01:05:25,424
Zero ETL 的表现优于你可能构建的任何流水线。
Zero ETL beats any pipeline you could build.

730
01:05:25,806 --> 01:05:29,664
当数据在传输过程中必须重新建模时，它就不再适用。
When the data must be reshaped on the way, it does not apply at all.

731
01:05:31,086 --> 01:05:35,044
知道什么时候某个服务不合适，与知道它何时合适同样重要。
Knowing when a service is wrong is worth as much as knowing when it is right.

732
01:05:35,470 --> 01:05:41,540
考试中的干扰项是那些“几乎合适”的服务，而不是明显荒谬的选项。
The exam builds its distractors out of services that are nearly appropriate rather than obviously absurd.

733
01:05:42,064 --> 01:05:45,636
第四点值得作为一种独立的模式来专门强调。
The fourth point deserves naming as a pattern in its own right.

734
01:05:46,510 --> 01:05:54,756
如果数据已经存在于 Redshift 中并需要转换到另一个 Redshift 表，答案几乎总是在 Redshift 内部执行 SQL。
If data already sits in Redshift and needs transforming into another Redshift table, the answer is almost always SQL executed inside Redshift.

735
01:05:55,104 --> 01:05:59,876
而不是由 Glue 作业读取数据、进行转换然后再写回。
It is not a blue job that reads the data out, transforms it, and writes it back.

736
01:06:00,782 --> 01:06:08,580
将数据从仓库中移出进行转换然后再移回，这种模式在考试中始终被判定为错误。
Moving data out of a warehouse to transform it and then moving it back in is a shape the exam consistently marks wrong.

737
01:06:09,326 --> 01:06:13,540
这会增加成本、延迟并产生毫无收益的流水线。
It adds cost, latency, and a pipeline for no benefit.

738
01:06:14,798 --> 01:06:23,264
一家金融服务公司每晚从 40 家合作伙伴银行中的每一家接收一个 CSV 文件，每个文件大小在 2 到 8 MB 之间
A financial services company receives one CSV file from each of 40 partner banks every night between 2 and 8 MB

739
01:06:23,664 --> 01:06:23,972
每一个。
each.

740
01:06:24,398 --> 01:06:33,124
每个文件都需要相同的轻量级转换：重命名 3 个列、重新格式化 1 个日期，并将结果作为 Parquet 写入 Amazon S3。
Each file needs the same light transformation, 3 columns we named, 1 date reformatted, and the result written as parquet to Amazon S3.

741
01:06:33,838 --> 01:06:36,836
文件在夜间的任何时间到达，并不固定。
Files arrive at unpredictable times through the night.

742
01:06:37,358 --> 01:06:43,396
当前设计是在早上 6 点运行一个单一的 Glue Spark 作业来处理所有已到达的文件。
The current design runs a single blue spark job at 6 in the morning that processes whatever has arrived.

743
01:06:43,824 --> 01:06:48,932
团队希望每个文件落地后能立即获得结果，并希望降低成本。
The team wants results available as soon as each file lands and wants to reduce cost.

744
01:06:51,054 --> 01:06:53,476
哪种设计最符合这两个要求？
Which design best meets both requirements?

745
01:06:54,544 --> 01:06:54,864
A
A

746
01:06:56,174 --> 01:07:00,196
保留 Glue 作业，但将其从每天一次改为每小时执行一次。
Keep the GRU job but schedule it hourly instead of once at 6.

747
01:07:00,624 --> 01:07:08,356
b 通过 S3 事件通知触发 AWS Lambda 函数，在文件到达时进行转换。
b Trigger an AWS Lambda function from S3 event notifications to transform each file on arrival.

748
01:07:08,944 --> 01:07:09,264
C
C.

749
01:07:09,664 --> 01:07:14,980
为每个到达的文件从 S3 事件通知中触发一个 Glue Spark 作业。
Trigger a GNU Spar job from S3 event notifications for each file that arrives.

750
01:07:15,984 --> 01:07:16,224
D
D.

751
01:07:17,582 --> 01:07:23,364
将设计更改为在夜间持续运行的 Amazon EMR 集群。
Replace the design with an Amazon EMR cluster running continuously through the night.

752
01:07:24,366 --> 01:07:25,764
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

753
01:07:32,462 --> 01:07:39,236
答案是 B，而选项 C 是整个模块一直在铺垫的干扰项。
The answer is B and option C is the distractor the whole module has been building towards.

754
01:07:39,630 --> 01:07:41,572
C 选项在架构上是正确的。
C gets the architecture right.

755
01:07:41,904 --> 01:07:46,340
到达时触发是应对不可预测时间点的正确模式。
Event driven on arrival is exactly the correct pattern for unpredictable timing.

756
01:07:46,944 --> 01:07:48,676
但它随后选择了错误的引擎。
It then picks the wrong engine.

757
01:07:49,614 --> 01:07:59,076
40 个独立的 Spark 作业，每个都要支付 1 分钟的最低计费门槛，并且有以分钟计的启动延迟，仅仅是为了转换 8 MB 的数据。
40 separate spark jobs, each paying a 1 minute minimum billing floor and a startup delay measured in minutes to transform 8 megabytes.

758
01:07:59,584 --> 01:08:07,664
这就是为什么本模块花时间讲解计费最小值的原因。注意这是故意与场景 1 配对的。
This is why the module spent time on the billing minimums. Notice this pairs with scenario 1 deliberately.

759
01:08:07,904 --> 01:08:10,852
在那个案例中，Glue 是正确的，只是配置错误。
There Glue was right and only misconfigured.

760
01:08:11,598 --> 01:08:15,204
而在这个案例中，无论你怎么配置，Glue 都不是正确的工具。
Here glue is the wrong tool no matter how you configure it.

761
01:08:16,590 --> 01:08:22,783
一家医疗分析公司运行一个 Glue 作业，从 Amazon S3 读取患者记录。
A healthcare analytics company runs a Glue job that reads patient records from Amazon S3.

762
01:08:23,104 --> 01:08:28,356
它将这些记录与参考数据合并，并写入一个供三个分析团队使用的精选数据集。
It joins them with reference data and writes a curated dataset used by three analytics teams.

763
01:08:29,229 --> 01:08:36,036
合规性要求其中一个团队可以看到所有列，而另外两个团队不得看到患者身份标识列。
Compliance requires that one team can see all columns and the other two must not see the patient identifier column at all.

764
01:08:36,384 --> 01:08:42,340
该作业目前使用 Options 中的 Create Dynamic Frame 直接从 S3 路径读取。
The job currently reads directly from an S3 path using Create Dynamic Frame from Options.

765
01:08:43,278 --> 01:08:49,444
安全团队要求在不维护三份独立数据副本的情况下实现列级访问控制。
The security team has asked for column level access control without maintaining three separate copies of the data.

766
01:08:49,904 --> 01:08:52,068
数据工程师应该做出什么更改？
What should the data engineer change?

767
01:08:52,558 --> 01:08:59,652
a. 写入三个到不同 S3 前缀的输出数据集，并使用存储桶策略控制访问。
a Write three output datasets to different S3 prefixes and control access with bucket policies.

768
01:09:00,462 --> 01:09:00,703
b
b

769
01:09:01,966 --> 01:09:09,904
将数据集注册在视图数据目录中，从目录读取，并在 AWS Lake
Register the dataset in the view data catalog, read from the catalog, and grant column level permissions in AWS Lake

770
01:09:10,144 --> 01:09:10,468
Formation 中授予列级权限。
Formation.

771
01:09:12,142 --> 01:09:20,228
C. 使用 AWS KMS 加密患者身份标识列，并仅授予授权团队的密钥访问权限。
C Encrypt the patient identifier column with AWS KMS and grant key access only to the permitted team.

772
01:09:21,344 --> 01:09:21,504
D
D

773
01:09:22,926 --> 01:09:27,620
在作业上启用 Glue 敏感数据检测以脱敏患者身份标识。
Enable blue sensitive data detection on the job to redact the patient identifier.

774
01:09:28,464 --> 01:09:29,796
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

775
01:09:36,301 --> 01:09:41,060
答案是 B，这取决于本模块前面关于目录读取的那张幻灯片。
The answer is B, and it depends on the slide about catalog reads earlier in this module.

776
01:09:41,279 --> 01:09:44,644
Lake Formation 为数据目录表授予权限。
Lake Formation grants permissions on data catalog tables.

777
01:09:45,421 --> 01:09:51,812
直接从 S3 路径读取的作业永远不会涉及目录，因此任何 Lake Formation 授权都无法应用于它。
A job reading straight from an S3 path never concerns the catalog, so no lake formation grant can apply to it.

778
01:09:52,526 --> 01:09:57,444
因此，更改读取路径并不是次要问题，它就是答案所在。
Changing the read path is therefore not incidental to the answer, it is the answer.

779
01:09:57,920 --> 01:10:05,920
选项 D 是设计良好的干扰项，因为敏感数据检测确实是在 Glue
Option D is the well-designed destructor because sensitive data detection is genuinely the right tool for masking personal data in a GRU

780
01:10:06,080 --> 01:10:06,308
作业中对个人数据进行脱敏的正确工具。
job.

781
01:10:07,214 --> 01:10:09,572
它在需求中的一个词上就失败了。
It fails on one word in the requirement.

782
01:10:10,478 --> 01:10:15,204
一个团队仍需看到该列，而遮盖并不是由消费者选择性的。
One team must still see the column, and redaction is not selective by consumer.

783
01:10:16,878 --> 01:10:22,980
有五个问题适用于任何 Glue 场景，它们涵盖了考试中关于该服务的大部分内容。
Five questions to run on any GRU scenario, and between them they resolve most of what this exam asks about the service.

784
01:10:23,440 --> 01:10:25,892
最后两个是得分的关键点。
The last two are where the marks hide.

785
01:10:26,350 --> 01:10:33,156
两者都描述了一个正在运行而非失败的任务，并且都有具体的名称修复，而不是通用的修复。
Both describe a job that is working rather than failing, and both have a specific name fix rather than a general one.

786
01:10:34,080 --> 01:10:40,004
一个成本在增长而数据量保持不变的作业是重复处理，书签可以解决这个问题。
A job whose cost grows while volume is static is reprocessing, and bookmarks stop that.

787
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:44,196
一个读取量远超报告量的任务需要下推谓词。
A job reading far more than it reports on needs a push-down predicate.

788
01:10:44,640 --> 01:10:49,920
这两者都不是通过增加容量来解决的，而这正是那个诱人的干扰项会提供的方案。
Neither is solved by adding capacity, which is exactly what the tempting distractor will offer.

789
01:10:50,080 --> 01:10:52,420
因为增加容量听起来很有说服力。
Because adding capacity sounds decisive.

790
01:10:53,230 --> 01:11:00,836
下一个模块是流式摄入，这是领域一的另一半，这里的决定性约束从成本变成了延迟。
Next module is streaming ingestion, the other half of domain one, where the deciding constraint becomes latency instead of cost.

791
01:11:02,350 --> 01:11:04,240
模块 2 是关于成本的。
Module 2 was about cost.

792
01:11:04,750 --> 01:11:06,724
这个模块是关于延迟的。
This module is about latency.

793
01:11:07,182 --> 01:11:15,588
在为本课程分析的题库中，流式处理约占 7% 的考点，但这个数字低估了它的重要性。
Streaming accounted for roughly 7% of term hits in the bank analyzed for this course, and that number understates its importance.

794
01:11:16,526 --> 01:11:27,108
流式处理的问题是人们最容易做错的，因为这里的四个服务高度重叠，而考试正是利用这种重叠来设置干扰项的。
Streaming questions are disproportionately the ones people get wrong because four services here overlap heavily and the exam builds its distractors precisely out of that overlap.

795
01:11:28,718 --> 01:11:31,588
其中两个可以将数据存入 Amazon S3。
Two of them can land data in Amazon S3.

796
01:11:32,494 --> 01:11:34,404
其中两个可以被 Lambda 读取。
Two of them can be read by Lambda.

797
01:11:35,374 --> 01:11:37,476
其中三个可以承载相同的记录。
Three of them can carry the same records.

798
01:11:37,680 --> 01:11:46,180
到本模块结束时，你将能够用一句话区分这四个服务，并且你会知道决定吞吐量问题的具体数值。
By the end of this module, you will be able to separate all four in a sentence each, and you will know the specific numbers that decide the throughput questions.

799
01:11:46,990 --> 01:11:55,748
过程中有四个工作场景，以及一个可用性警告，它会使大多数现有题库中的正确答案失效。
Four work scenarios along the way and one availability warning that invalidates a correct answer in most existing question banks.

800
01:11:57,262 --> 01:12:02,720
从模块 1 中带到这里，因为这是整个领域中最常见的错误。
Carry this over from module 1 because it is the most common error in this whole area.

801
01:12:03,040 --> 01:12:07,268
数据持续到达并不就意味着它是一个流式问题。
Data arriving continuously does not make something a streaming problem.

802
01:12:07,680 --> 01:12:11,492
传感器每秒钟向一个仅读取一次的报告发送数据。
Sensors emitting every second into a report read once.

803
01:12:11,680 --> 01:12:15,300
早晨报表是一个具有活跃源头的批处理工作量。
A morning is a batch workload with a talkative source.

804
01:12:16,142 --> 01:12:22,500
让它成为流式处理的原因是，消费者在等待，且答案的价值会随着时间的推移而降低。
What makes it streaming is that a consumer is waiting and the value of the answer decays with time.

805
01:12:23,566 --> 01:12:25,444
一个阻塞支付的欺诈检查。
A fraud check blocking a payment.

806
01:12:26,510 --> 01:12:28,740
一个提醒流水线压力正在上升的警报。
An alert that a pipeline pressure is rising.

807
01:12:29,788 --> 01:12:31,168
交易员们正在查看的仪表板。
A dashboard traders are watching.

808
01:12:32,398 --> 01:12:39,588
如果没人受 12 小时延迟的影响，那么正确的答案几乎肯定不是流，无论源头是否是连续的。
If nobody suffers from a 12 hour delay, the correct answer is almost certainly not a stream, however continuous the source is.

809
01:12:39,982 --> 01:12:41,636
这在商业上也很重要。
This matters commercially too.

810
01:12:42,862 --> 01:12:48,480
流式处理基础设施每天每小时都要花钱，无论有没有人在读取。
Streaming infrastructure costs money every hour of every day, whether anyone is reading or not.

811
01:12:48,880 --> 01:12:54,628
这就是为什么考试中，不必要的流式处理会被视为错误答案，而不是无关紧要的选项。
That is why the exam treats an unnecessary stream as a wrong answer rather than a harmless one.

812
01:12:55,918 --> 01:13:02,756
考试中的每种流式架构都遵循这条逻辑，而第三个框才是最重要的。
Every streaming architecture on this exam is some version of this line, and the third box is the one that matters most.

813
01:13:04,750 --> 01:13:08,580
消费者按自己的节奏读取，并记住读到哪里了。
A consumer reads at its own pace and remembers where it got to.

814
01:13:10,542 --> 01:13:17,600
多个消费者可以独立读取相同的记录，每个都在日志中处于不同的位置。
Multiple consumers can read the same records independently, each sitting at a different position in the log.

815
01:13:18,542 --> 01:13:23,716
一个可能落后几秒，另一个可能落后一小时，且互不影响。
One might be seconds behind, another an hour behind, and neither affects the other.

816
01:13:24,240 --> 01:13:28,804
之所以能做到这一点，是因为流在被读取后仍保留数据，
That is possible only because the stream retains the data after it has been read,

817
01:13:29,454 --> 01:13:31,652
而不是在消费后就将其删除。
rather than deleting it on consumption.

818
01:13:32,558 --> 01:13:39,140
记住这个特性，因为下一张幻灯片会把它变成考试中经常出现的决策点。
Hold on to that property because the next slide turns it into an exam decision that comes up constantly.

819
01:13:39,680 --> 01:13:46,244
这也是让重放成为可能的原因，而在考试指南中，重放本身就是一项核心技能。
It is also the property that makes replay possible, with the exam guide names as a skill in its own right.

820
01:13:47,822 --> 01:13:54,308
这对特性出现的频率比大家预想的要高，而且有三个信号可以判断是该选流还是队列。
This pair appears more often than people expect, and there are three signals that force a stream rather than a queue.

821
01:13:55,054 --> 01:13:59,172
首先，多个系统需要出于不同目的获取相同的记录。
First, more than one system needs the same records for different purposes.

822
01:13:59,440 --> 01:14:03,716
队列做不到这一点，因为第一个获取消息的消费者就会将其删除。
A queue cannot do that because the first consumer to take a message removes it.

823
01:14:04,782 --> 01:14:05,956
其次，是重放。
Second, replay.

824
01:14:06,894 --> 01:14:13,156
如果周四发现 Bug 且必须重新处理周一的数据，而队列在几天前就把数据删了，那就没法处理了。
If a bug is discovered on Thursday and Monday's data must be reprocessed, a queue deleted it days ago.

825
01:14:15,662 --> 01:14:17,092
第三，是严格的顺序。
Third, strict ordering.

826
01:14:18,062 --> 01:14:25,216
Kinesis 保障分片内的顺序，而标准的 Amazon SQS 完全不提供任何顺序保证。
Kinesis guarantees order within a shard, and standard Amazon SQS makes no ordering guarantee at all.

827
01:14:25,742 --> 01:14:34,532
如果题目中没出现这三个信号中的任何一个，SQS 更简单、更便宜，也几乎肯定是预设的正确答案。
If none of those three signals appear in the question, SQS is simpler, cheaper, and almost certainly the intended answer.

828
01:14:35,758 --> 01:14:39,684
在只需要队列的情况下选择流式处理是错误的答案。
Reaching for a stream when a queue would do is a wrong answer.

829
01:14:40,096 --> 01:14:42,180
考试题目是故意这样设计的。
The exam sets deliberately.

830
01:14:43,936 --> 01:14:48,484
掌握这四句话，你就已经搞定了这个模块的大部分内容。
Learn these four sentences, and a large share of the module is already done.

831
01:14:48,896 --> 01:14:53,092
得分的关键在于区分「传输」和「交付」。
The distinction that earns marks is between transporting and delivering.

832
01:14:53,456 --> 01:15:00,996
Kinesis、DataStreams 和 Amazon MSK 保留数据，并允许你编写消费者对数据进行任何你想做的操作。
Kinesis, DataStreams, and Amazon MSK hold data and let you write a consumer that does whatever you want with it.

833
01:15:01,776 --> 01:15:05,252
这意味着灵活性，也意味着你可以掌控代码。
That means flexibility and it also means code you own.

834
01:15:05,536 --> 01:15:08,356
Amazon Data Firehose 完全没有所谓的“消费者”。
Amazon Data Firehose has no consumers at all.

835
01:15:08,576 --> 01:15:17,380
你只需指向一个目的地，它就会把数据放过去并处理中间的所有环节。托管的 Apache Flink 服务不具备这两项功能。
You point it at a destination and it puts the data there, managing everything in between. Managed service for Apache Flink does neither of those jobs.

836
01:15:17,966 --> 01:15:22,416
它处于中间位置并对流进行计算，这是另一个不同的动词。
It sits in the middle and computes over the stream, which is a different verb again.

837
01:15:22,656 --> 01:15:31,076
当你看到四个选项分别对应四个服务时，问问问题到底需要哪个动词，通常其中三个就会被排除掉。
When you see four options naming four services, ask which verb the question actually needs, and usually three of them drop away immediately.

838
01:15:32,462 --> 01:15:40,932
Kinesis DataStreams 是最可能出现在吞吐量计算中的服务，而这些计算最终都取决于分片。
Kinesis DataStreams is the service most likely to appear in a throughput calculation, and those calculations all come down to shards.

839
01:15:41,518 --> 01:15:43,300
一个分片同时具备两个属性。
A shard is two things at once.

840
01:15:45,518 --> 01:15:49,124
它既是容量单位，也是排序单位。
It is a unit of capacity and it is a unit of ordering.

841
01:15:50,094 --> 01:15:56,196
携带相同分区键的记录总是落在同一个分片上，并且在那个分片中按到达顺序排列。
Records carrying the same partition key always land on the same chart, and within that shard they stay in the order they arrived.

842
01:15:56,846 --> 01:15:58,692
增加分片就意味着增加吞吐量。
Add shards and you add throughput.

843
01:16:00,398 --> 01:16:06,724
增加分片还会让你的分区键分布得更开，而这正是这类考试题目开始出现的地方。
Add shards and you also spread your partition keys further apart, which is where a whole family of exam problems begins.

844
01:16:07,598 --> 01:16:11,524
因为只有在初始状态下键就分布良好时，分散才有意义。
Because spreading is only useful if the keys were well distributed to start with.

845
01:16:13,710 --> 01:16:18,180
下一张幻灯片上有这些数字，它们值得直接记住，而不是去推算。
The next slide has the numbers and they are worth memorizing rather than reasoning about.

846
01:16:19,214 --> 01:16:22,788
因为题目会把计算过程摆在你面前，并要求你跟着逻辑走。
Because questions do the arithmetic in front of you and expect you to follow.

847
01:16:24,416 --> 01:16:33,216
正确的限制实际上是两个限制，而标注出的部分就是考点：每秒 1 MB 或每秒 1000 条记录，
The right limit is really two limits and the callout is the exam point, 1 MB per second or 1000 records per second,

848
01:16:33,390 --> 01:16:34,916
以先达到哪一个为准。
whichever you reach first.

849
01:16:35,758 --> 01:16:45,284
如果生产者发送的是很小的记录，比如每条只有 200 字节的遥测数据，那么在每秒约 200 KB 时就会达到 1000 条记录的上限。
A producer sending tiny records, say 200 bytes of telemetry each, will hit the 1000 record ceiling at roughly 200 kilobytes per second.

850
01:16:45,934 --> 01:16:51,300
看起来它只用了分片带宽的五分之一，但依然被限流了。
It looks like it is using a fifth of the shard's bandwidth and it is being throttled anyway.

851
01:16:52,014 --> 01:17:00,420
这就是为什么标准建议是在发送前聚合小记录，而这正是 Kinesis Producer 库为你做的事情。
That is why the standard advice is to aggregate small records before sending, which is exactly what the kinesis producer library does for you.

852
01:17:01,102 --> 01:17:09,412
在读取端，请注意每秒 2 MB 是该分片上的所有标准消费者共享的，而不是分配给每个人的。
On the read side, note that the 2 MB per second is shared across every standard consumer on that shard, not granted to each.

853
01:17:10,158 --> 01:17:17,060
5 个消费者各分到每秒 400 KB，这就是问题所在。Fanout 存在的目的就是为了解决这个问题。
5 consumers get 400 kilobytes per second each, which is the problem enhanced. Fanode exists to solve.

854
01:17:18,734 --> 01:17:23,716
这对应了模块 1 中关于流式处理的无服务器论点。
This mirrors the serverless argument from Module 1 applied to streams.

855
01:17:26,126 --> 01:17:35,940
指向「按需模式」的词汇包括不可预测、多变、突发、爆发式，或者是一个还没有人测量过的新工作负载。
The words that point at on demand are unpredictable, variable, spiky, bursty, or a new workload nobody has measured yet.

856
01:17:36,590 --> 01:17:40,292
指向「预置型」的词语是稳定、一致。
The words that point at provisioned are steady, consistent.

857
01:17:41,038 --> 01:17:47,236
还有题目中给出的具体吞吐量数值，因为明确的数字意味着有人测量过它。
And a specific throughput figure the question actually hands you because a stated number means somebody measured it.

858
01:17:47,536 --> 01:17:50,052
这是题目中出现的一个很有用的细节。
One useful detail that appears in questions.

859
01:17:50,416 --> 01:17:54,052
你可以将现有的流在两种模式之间切换，且无需停机。
You can switch an existing stream between the two modes without downtime.

860
01:17:54,976 --> 01:17:59,268
不需要更改应用程序代码，不需要重新发布，数据也不会中断。
No application code changes, no republishing, no gap in the data.

861
01:17:59,616 --> 01:18:05,636
这使得「按需模式」成为一个合理的答案，即使是针对那些一直被限流的现有预置型流。
That makes on demand a reasonable answer even for an existing provisioned stream that keeps getting throttled.

862
01:18:06,478 --> 01:18:09,924
而且它排除了迁移会导致中断的顾虑。
And it removes the objection that migrating would be disruptive.

863
01:18:11,214 --> 01:18:15,780
这些数字最近更新过，很多备考资料还没跟上。
These numbers moved recently and a lot of preparation material has not caught up.

864
01:18:16,176 --> 01:18:21,892
按需模式以前上限是每秒 200 MB，然后是 1GB，接着是 2GB。
On demand used to cap at 200 MB per second, then 1GB, then 2.

865
01:18:22,606 --> 01:18:28,132
从 2024 年 11 月起，在三个区域它达到了每秒 10 GB。
Since November 2024, it reaches 10 GB per second right in three regions.

866
01:18:28,896 --> 01:18:35,652
预置型分片配额在 2025 年 4 月从每个账户的 500 个增加到了 20,000 个。
The provision shard quota went from 500 to 20,000 per account in April 2025.

867
01:18:36,176 --> 01:18:46,052
实际考试中的后果是，对于真正庞大的工作负载，按需模式现在是一个可信的答案，而旧的资料可能会迫使你选择预置型。
The practical exam consequence is that on demand is now a credible answer for genuinely large workloads where older material would have forced you to provisioned.

868
01:18:46,736 --> 01:18:52,964
不过最后一项依然重要：按需模式会扩展，但它不会瞬间完成扩展。
The last bullet still matters though, on demand scales, but it does not scale instantaneously.

869
01:18:54,574 --> 01:19:00,324
这是最可靠的流式处理故障排除问题，而且它的特征非常明显。
This is the single most reliable streaming troubleshooting question, and it has a memorable shape.

870
01:19:00,928 --> 01:19:03,108
症状是不均匀的限流。
The symptom is uneven throttling.

871
01:19:04,174 --> 01:19:11,396
有些分片处于极限负载，而其他分片几乎没被使用，整个流的总吞吐量远未达到容量上限。
Some shards sit at their limit while others are barely used, and the total throughput across the stream is nowhere near capacity.

872
01:19:12,334 --> 01:19:19,300
直觉是增加分片，考试知道这是你的直觉，所以它总是作为选项出现。
The instinct is to add shards, and the exam knows that is your instinct, which is why it is always offered.

873
01:19:22,638 --> 01:19:23,808
但这不起作用。
It does not work.

874
01:19:23,968 --> 01:19:32,288
无论有多少个分片，热键都会哈希到唯一的一个分片上。如果 90% 的流量都带有设备 ID1，
The hotkey hashes to exactly one shard, however many shards exist. If 90% of your traffic carries device, ID1,

875
01:19:33,198 --> 01:19:37,732
那么将流分成两个，只会让你得到一个负载为 90% 的分片和一个负载为 10% 的分片。
splitting the stream in two gives you one shard at 90% and one at 10.

876
01:19:38,350 --> 01:19:41,572
正确的解决方法始终是更改键，让流量分散开来。
The fix is always to change the key so traffic spreads.

877
01:19:42,126 --> 01:19:46,084
提高基数、使用复合键或添加随机后缀。
Higher cardinality, a composite key or a random suffix.

878
01:19:47,118 --> 01:19:49,968
如果不需要按原始键排序，
If ordering per original key is not required,

879
01:19:51,246 --> 01:19:53,828
那么“保留时间”就是这里一个非常重要但常被忽视的设置。
retention is the quietly important setting here.

880
01:19:54,542 --> 01:20:01,092
默认是 24 小时，这在消费端没有 Bug 的情况下没问题，但如果你想重新处理一周前的数据时就会出问题。
The default is 24 hours, which is fine until the day a consumer has a bug and you want to reprocess a week.

881
01:20:01,678 --> 01:20:06,368
扩展保留时间可以延长到 7 天，而长期保留可以达到整整一年。
Extended retention takes you to 7 days and long-term retention reaches a full

882
01:20:06,368 --> 01:20:16,996
因此，当题目描述在下游故障后需要重放几天的数据时，答案通常是延长保留时间。
year. So when a question describes needing to replay several days of data after a downstream failure, the answer usually involves extending retention.

883
01:20:17,568 --> 01:20:23,556
而提供从原始源重新构建的选项，则是在做远超必要的工作。
And an option that proposes rebuilding from the original source is doing far more work than necessary.

884
01:20:24,462 --> 01:20:28,836
保留时间也是有成本的，这就是为什么没人默认将其设置为一年。
Retention is also built, which is why nobody sets it to a year by default.

885
01:20:30,286 --> 01:20:33,828
考试通过症状而非名称来考查这一点。
The exam tests this through symptoms rather than by name.

886
01:20:34,510 --> 01:20:40,100
题目描述有五个应用程序在读取同一个流，而最新加入的一个让其他变慢了。
A question describes five applications reading the same stream and the newest one has made the other slow.

887
01:20:40,608 --> 01:20:44,292
这意味着有五个消费者在瓜分每秒 2 MB 的带宽。
That is five consumers dividing two MB per second between them.

888
01:20:45,198 --> 01:20:50,596
增强型扇出是解决方法，因为这样每个消费者都能获得属于自己的两兆字节。
An enhanced fan out is the fix because each consumer then gets its own two megabytes.

889
01:20:51,118 --> 01:20:52,900
第二个触发点是延迟。
The second trigger is latency.

890
01:20:54,766 --> 01:20:58,980
标准消费者采用轮询，这会导致它们落后约 200 毫秒。
Standard consumers poll, which puts them around 200 milliseconds behind.

891
01:20:59,726 --> 01:21:03,748
增强型扇出采用推送模式，能将延迟降低到大约 70 毫秒。
Enhanced fan out pushes, which brings that down to roughly 70.

892
01:21:04,718 --> 01:21:11,300
如果题目要求的延迟预算比 100 毫秒还要严格，标准轮询就无法满足要求。
If a question states a latency budget tighter than about 100 milliseconds, standard polling will not meet it.

893
01:21:12,718 --> 01:21:16,804
Kinesis 客户端库是值得在概念上理解的一个重点。
The kinesis client library is the one worth understanding conceptually.

894
01:21:17,168 --> 01:21:26,884
可靠地读取流意味着要追踪你处理了哪些记录，处理底层的分片拆分，并协调多个工作者共享负载时的情况。
Reading a stream reliably means tracking which records you have processed, handling a shard splitting underneath you, and coordinating when several workers share the load.

895
01:21:27,822 --> 01:21:34,756
KCL 处理了所有这些操作，并将检查点存储在它为你创建的 DynamoDB 表中。
The KCL does all of that, storing its checkpoints in a DynamoDB table it creates for you.

896
01:21:36,046 --> 01:21:45,188
那个 DynamoDB 表是一个很好的考试细节，因为如果 Kinesis 应用同时伴随出现神秘的 Dynamo DB 费用，就指向这个原因。
That DynamoDB table is a nice exam detail because a question about mysterious Dynamo DB costs alongside a kinesis application is pointing at it.

897
01:21:45,408 --> 01:21:48,164
注意最后一项中的停止支持日期。
Note the end of support dates on the last bullet.

898
01:21:48,910 --> 01:21:57,156
客户端库的第 1 版本和生产者库的第 0 版本都将在 2026 年 1 月停止支持。
Version 1 of the client library and version 0 of the producer library are both finished as of January 2026.

899
01:21:58,766 --> 01:22:02,308
这是考试中的一个常用场景，因为它的症状非常具有误导性。
This is a favorite exam scenario because the symptom is so misleading.

900
01:22:02,528 --> 01:22:08,768
读取 Kinesis 流的 Lambda 函数遇到一条记录时无法处理，可能是因为 JSON 格式错误。
A Lambda function reading a kinesi stream hits a record, it cannot process, perhaps malform JSON.

901
01:22:09,088 --> 01:22:10,848
Lambda 获取整个批处理。
Lambda retrieves the whole batch.

902
01:22:11,086 --> 01:22:11,972
它再次失败了。
It fails again.

903
01:22:12,848 --> 01:22:22,628
因为分片内的顺序必须保持，该批处理之后的任何内容都无法继续。因此，整个分片都会停滞，而迭代器年龄会持续上升。
Because ordering must be preserved within a shard, nothing behind that batch can proceed. So the entire shard stalls while iterator age climbs steadily.

904
01:22:23,088 --> 01:22:27,844
这看起来完全像是一个容量问题，增加并发性也没用。
It looks exactly like a capacity problem, and adding concurrency does nothing.

905
01:22:30,894 --> 01:22:32,132
有两个设置可以解决这个问题。
Two settings solve it.

906
01:22:33,070 --> 01:22:38,532
错误时拆分批次功能会不断拆分失败的批处理，从而隔离出那个唯一的错误记录。
Bisec batch on error splits the failing batch repeatedly to isolate the single bat record.

907
01:22:39,534 --> 01:22:44,964
并且一个失败后的目标位置会将该记录发送到队列或主题，以便处理继续进行。
And an on-failure destination sends that record to a queue or topic so processing continues.

908
01:22:45,966 --> 01:22:54,464
并行化因子是另一个值得知道的设置，因为它是获取多于
The parallelization factor is the other setting worth knowing because it is the one legitimate way to get more than

909
01:22:54,784 --> 01:22:57,700
每个分片一个并发调用的唯一合法方式。
one concurrent invocation per shard.

910
01:22:59,438 --> 01:23:04,996
一家网约车公司将车辆位置更新流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis 数据中。
A Ride hailing company streams vehicle location updates into Amazon Kinesis data.

911
01:23:06,606 --> 01:23:09,636
数据以预置模式在包含 12 个分片的流中流入。
Data streams in provision mode with 12 shards.

912
01:23:10,478 --> 01:23:15,908
记录使用城市名称作为分区键，且公司在 11 个城市运营。
Records use the city name as the partition key and the company operates in 11 cities.

913
01:23:16,654 --> 01:23:19,812
运维团队报告称出现了间歇性的行程限流。
The operations team reports intermittent ride throttling.

914
01:23:20,814 --> 01:23:27,172
CloudWatch 显示有两个分片始终处于限流状态，而其他 10 个分片的平均利用率低于 15%。
CloudWatch shows two shards consistently at their light limit, while the other 10 average under 15% utilization.

915
01:23:28,224 --> 01:23:32,068
整个流的总摄入量远低于每秒 12 MB。
Total ingest across the stream is well under 12 MB per second.

916
01:23:32,384 --> 01:23:34,084
数据工程师应该怎么做？
What should the data engineer do?

917
01:23:35,086 --> 01:23:38,084
a. 将分片数量从 12 增加到 24。
a increase the shard count from 12 to 24.

918
01:23:38,830 --> 01:23:43,076
b. 将流切换到按需容量模式。
b switch the stream to on-demand capacity mode.

919
01:23:43,504 --> 01:23:43,824
C。
C.

920
01:23:44,398 --> 01:23:48,740
将分区键更改为同时包含车辆标识符和城市。
Change the partition key to include the vehicle identifier as well as the city.

921
01:23:49,104 --> 01:23:49,424
D。
D.

922
01:23:49,838 --> 01:23:53,060
为消费端应用启用增强型扇出。
Enable enhanced fan out for the consumer applications.

923
01:23:53,582 --> 01:23:54,788
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

924
01:24:01,518 --> 01:24:02,944
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

925
01:24:03,264 --> 01:24:10,948
决定性的细节是，虽然两个分片已饱和，但总摄入量远低于每秒 12 MB。
The decisive detail is that total ingest is well under 12 MB per second while two shards are saturated.

926
01:24:12,142 --> 01:24:17,156
每个分片可以承载每秒 12 MB，所以根本不存在容量短缺。
Crunch shards can carry 12 MB per second, so there is no capacity shortage at all.

927
01:24:17,646 --> 01:24:20,260
只是容量分布到了错误的地方。
The capacity is simply in the wrong place.

928
01:24:21,230 --> 01:24:26,980
11 个分区键无法均匀分布在 12 个分片中，而两个最大的城市占据了大部分。
11 partition keys cannot spread across 12 shards evenly and the two largest cities dominate.

929
01:24:27,470 --> 01:24:34,180
选项 B 是一个很巧妙的干扰项，因为按需模式最终确实会拆分热点分片，所以它并非毫无用处。
Option B is a thoughtful distractor here because on-demand does eventually split hot shards, so it is not useless.

930
01:24:35,054 --> 01:24:39,104
它把一个设计问题转化成了账单，这就是这类题目典型的陷阱答案。
It converts a design problem into a bill, which is the kind of answer.

931
01:24:39,264 --> 01:24:42,308
考试中，修复根本原因的选项始终排在前面。
The exam consistently ranks below fixing the cause.

932
01:24:43,758 --> 01:24:50,532
Firehose 是本模块中被误解最多的服务，正确理解它能拿到不少分数。
Firehose is the most misunderstood service in this module, and understanding it properly is worth several marks.

933
01:24:51,022 --> 01:24:52,644
它不是一个你可以从中读取流的数据源。
It is not a stream you read from.

934
01:24:52,974 --> 01:24:59,396
它没有分片数量、没有消费者库、没有检查点，也没有可以追踪的位置。
There is no shard count, no consumer library, no checkpointing, and no position to track.

935
01:25:00,270 --> 01:25:08,516
你配置源、可选的转换和目的地，然后由 AWS 处理端到端的交付。
You configure a source, optionally a transformation, and a destination, and AWS runs the delivery end-to-end.

936
01:25:09,326 --> 01:25:17,092
这让它的运维开销比本模块中的任何其他服务都低，这也是它在许多“最低运维开销”题目中胜出的原因。
That gives it by far the lowest operational overhead of anything in this module, which is why it wins so many least overhead questions.

937
01:25:17,870 --> 01:25:20,516
这也意味着它只能做它能做到的事情。
It also means it can only do what it does.

938
01:25:21,422 --> 01:25:26,948
如果题目需要自定义的消费者逻辑，或者两个独立读取相同记录的程序，
If a question needs custom consumer logic or two independent readers of the same records,

939
01:25:27,664 --> 01:25:33,380
或者需要回溯并重新处理的能力，无论 Firehose 听起来多方便，它都不符合要求。
or the ability to rewind and reprocess, Firehose is out no matter how convenient it sounds.

940
01:25:34,190 --> 01:25:38,116
了解它不能做什么，和了解它能做什么一样重要。
Knowing what it cannot do is as valuable as knowing what it can.

941
01:25:39,886 --> 01:25:44,644
第三点和第五点结合在一起，就是 Firehose 在许多题目中胜过流水线的原因。
The third and fifth points together are the reason Firehose beats a pipeline in a lot of questions.

942
01:25:45,024 --> 01:25:50,144
模块 1 已经确定，Parquet 加分区是解决查询成本的标准方案。
Module 1 established that parquet plus partitioning is the standard fix for query cost.

943
01:25:50,624 --> 01:25:55,012
Firehose 通过配置而非代码，在数据进入时就完成了这两项操作。
Firehose does both of those on the way in with configuration rather than code.

944
01:25:55,854 --> 01:26:02,564
所以考虑这样一个问题：原始 JSON 数据落地到 S3，分析师抱怨 Athena 的成本太高。
So consider a question describing raw JSON landing in S3 with analysts complaining about Athena costs.

945
01:26:03,086 --> 01:26:05,604
答案中根本不需要 Glue作业。
The answer involves no glue job whatsoever.

946
01:26:05,998 --> 01:26:09,412
只需开启格式转换和动态分区即可。
Just turn on format conversion and dynamic partitioning.

947
01:26:10,224 --> 01:26:20,932
当某个选项提供一个计划的作业来转换文件，而 Firehose 本就可以在到达时完成转换时，那个选项就是在做多余的工作。
When an option offers a scheduled job to convert files that Firehose could have converted on arrival, that option is doing unnecessary work.

948
01:26:22,574 --> 01:26:24,388
这两行内容在这里非常重要。
Two rows earn their place here.

949
01:26:25,390 --> 01:26:29,828
Redshift 这一行解释了一个在题目中看起来很奇怪的行为。
The redshift row explains a behavior that otherwise looks odd in questions.

950
01:26:30,478 --> 01:26:34,372
Firehose 并不是像你想象的那样把行流式传输到 Redshift。
Firehose does not stream rows into Redshift the way you might imagine.

951
01:26:35,630 --> 01:26:40,004
它是将对象写入 S3 bucket，然后对这些对象执行复制命令。
It writes objects to an S3 bucket and then issues a copy command against them.

952
01:26:40,910 --> 01:26:45,892
这就是为什么 Redshift 目标仍然需要你配置一个 S3 bucket。
That is why a Redshift destination still requires you to configure an S3 bucket.

953
01:26:46,382 --> 01:26:52,388
这也是为什么只有 GZIP 压缩在那个路径上可行，以及为什么延迟比单纯的缓冲间隔预估的要高。
Why only GZIP compression works on that path and why the latency is higher than the buffer interval alone suggests.

954
01:26:53,326 --> 01:26:56,164
ICberg 这一行是新加入的考点，值得标注。
The ICBerg row is newly examinable and worth flagging.

955
01:26:57,056 --> 01:27:05,412
Firehose 交付到 Apache ICberg 表时可以执行更新和删除，而不仅仅是插入，
Firehose delivering into Apache ICBerg tables can express updates and deletes, not only inserts,

956
01:27:05,616 --> 01:27:10,052
这与将文件追加到前缀中的功能有着本质区别。
which is a genuinely different capability from appending files into a prefix.

957
01:27:10,576 --> 01:27:14,852
2024 年底之前编写的资料完全没有涵盖这一点。
Material written before late 2024 does not cover it at all.

958
01:27:16,496 --> 01:27:20,228
这是对模块 1 的更正，完整表述如下。
This is the correction from module 1, stated in full.

959
01:27:20,910 --> 01:27:26,308
Firehose 通常被描述为近实时，因为它在交付前会进行缓冲。
Firehose is conventionally described as near real time because it buffers before delivering.

960
01:27:26,830 --> 01:27:29,764
而且多年来，这个流程确实是 60 秒。
And for years the flow really was 60 seconds.

961
01:27:30,574 --> 01:27:36,708
自2023年12月起，您可以将缓冲间隔设置为零，从而在约5秒内完成交付。
Since December 2023, you can set the buffer interval to zero and get delivery in about 5 seconds.

962
01:27:37,198 --> 01:27:40,420
这从根本上改变了 Firehose 能回答哪些问题。
That materially changes which questions Firehose can answer.

963
01:27:41,136 --> 01:27:48,740
要求数据在10秒内可用不再排除它，而很多学习资料仍假设它会被排除。
A requirement for data available within 10 seconds no longer rules it out, and a lot of study material still assumes it does.

964
01:27:49,614 --> 01:27:53,060
有两个注意事项很重要，且两个都会出现在题目中。
Two caveats matter and both appear in questions.

965
01:27:53,998 --> 01:28:01,156
当启用动态分区时，无法提供零缓冲，因为 Firehose 会按每个分区分别进行缓冲。
Zero buffering is not available when dynamic partitioning is enabled because firehose buffers separately per partition.

966
01:28:01,936 --> 01:28:10,096
而且非常小的缓冲区会产生大量微小对象，这正是第二章警告过的
And very small buffers produce a flood of tiny objects, which is precisely the small file problem module too warned

967
01:28:10,256 --> 01:28:12,196
故意提到的“小文件问题”。
about created deliberately.

968
01:28:13,710 --> 01:28:19,428
这是流式处理问题中最常见的组合，陷阱在于将其视为二选一。
This is the most common pairing in streaming questions, and the trap is treating it as either or.

969
01:28:19,936 --> 01:28:22,596
一种非常标准的架构是同时使用两者。
A very standard architecture uses both.

970
01:28:24,494 --> 01:28:27,364
Kinesis 数据流接收记录。
Kinesis data streams receives the records.

971
01:28:27,536 --> 01:28:31,216
Flink 应用读取这些记录用于实时告警。
A Flink application reads them for real-time alerting.

972
01:28:31,694 --> 01:28:37,376
Firehose 流读取相同的记录并将其存入 S3 以供后续分析。
A Firehose stream reads the same records and lands them in S3 for later analysis.

973
01:28:37,616 --> 01:28:40,644
每个消费者从同一个源获取所需的资源。
Each consumer gets what it needs from one source.

974
01:28:41,166 --> 01:28:46,468
因此，要留意那些同时描述实时响应和存档要求的题目。
So watch for a question describing both a real-time reaction and an archival requirement.

975
01:28:46,896 --> 01:28:49,444
结合这两者的选项通常是正确的。
An option combining the two is often correct.

976
01:28:50,254 --> 01:28:53,668
强迫你只能选一个的选项就是干扰项。
An option forcing you to pick one is the distractor.

977
01:28:55,374 --> 01:28:57,700
第一个要点是出现在题目中的那个。
The first bullet is the one that appears in questions.

978
01:28:58,016 --> 01:29:04,656
Firehose 会对失败的目标持续重试长达24小时，然后永久丢弃这些记录。
Firehose will keep retrying a failing destination for up to 24 hours and then it discards those records permanently.

979
01:29:04,816 --> 01:29:09,056
默认情况下没有死信队列，也没有办法在之后恢复它们。
There is no dead letter queue by default and no way to recover them afterwards.

980
01:29:09,550 --> 01:29:13,316
这就是为什么配置 S3 备份如此重要。
That is why configuring S3 backup matters so much.

981
01:29:13,616 --> 01:29:19,908
这也是为什么关于长周末期间 OpenSearch 集群宕机的问题会有“数据丢失”这一答案。
And it is why a question about an open search cluster down over a long weekend has a data loss answer.

982
01:29:22,606 --> 01:29:25,412
除非启用了备份，否则这是正确的。
That is true unless backup was enabled.

983
01:29:26,606 --> 01:29:30,820
最后两个要点的交付语义值得作为一对内容来记忆。
The delivery semantics on the last two bullets are worth memorizing as a pair.

984
01:29:31,758 --> 01:29:37,892
“至少一次”意味着超时后的重试可能会产生重复数据，你的消费者必须能够容忍这种情况。
At least once means a retry after a timeout can produce a duplicate, which your consumer must tolerate.

985
01:29:38,446 --> 01:29:43,748
例外列表包括 Amazon S3、Apache Iceberg 表和 Snowflake
The exception list Amazon S3, Apache IZBerg tables, and Snowflake

986
01:29:44,622 --> 01:29:46,308
这个列表足够短，可以直接背下来。
is short enough to learn outright.

987
01:29:47,936 --> 01:29:56,452
这是在数据仓库问题中区分两个看似合理的选项的关键细节。将流导入 Redshift 有两种方式，它们的行为不同。
This is the detail that separates two plausible options in a warehouse question. There are two ways to get a stream into Redshift and they behave differently.

988
01:29:56,896 --> 01:30:03,332
以 Redshift 为目标的 Firehose 会先将对象写入 S3，然后执行复制命令。
Firehose with Redshift as the destination writes objects to S3 and then issues a copy command.

989
01:30:04,142 --> 01:30:07,876
因此，它总是有一个暂存步骤，并且始终存在 S3 的延迟。
So there is always a staging hop and always S3 latency.

990
01:30:08,256 --> 01:30:18,084
Redshift 流式摄入将数据仓库直接连接到 Kinesis 流或 MSK 主题，在完全不经过 S3 的情况下将记录体现为视图。
Redshift streaming ingestion connects the warehouse directly to a Kinesis stream or an MSK topic. Materializing records into a view without touching S3 at all.

991
01:30:18,542 --> 01:30:20,548
这样可以将处理时间从几分钟缩短到几秒钟。
That gets you seconds instead of minutes.

992
01:30:21,056 --> 01:30:28,356
所以，如果题目要求在 Redshift 中实现近乎实时的仪表板且尽可能减少移动部件，指向的就是流式摄入。
So a question asking for near real time dashboards in Redshift with the fewest moving parts is pointing at streaming ingestion.

993
01:30:28,590 --> 01:30:30,916
而 Firehose 就是设计精良的干扰项。
And Firehose is the well designed distractor.

994
01:30:32,462 --> 01:30:37,956
一家媒体公司将点击流事件流式传输到 Amazon S3 中，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行分析。
A media company streams clickstream events into Amazon S3 for analysis with Amazon Athena.

995
01:30:38,606 --> 01:30:44,836
事件以原始 JSON 格式到达，每 30 秒一个对象，进入一个没有任何分区的单一前缀中。
Events arrive as raw JSON, one object every 30 seconds, into a single prefix with no partitioning.

996
01:30:45,710 --> 01:30:47,716
该流水线是一个 Kinesis。
The pipeline is a kinesis.

997
01:30:48,910 --> 01:30:54,436
数据流由一个 AWS Lambda 函数引导，该函数将对象写入 S3。
Data stream stream led by an AWS Lambda function that writes objects to S3.

998
01:30:55,758 --> 01:31:02,084
分析师报告称，Athena 查询中过滤单日的数据时会扫描整个数据集，且成本变得很高。
Analysts report that Athena queries filtering on a single day scan the entire dataset and are becoming expensive.

999
01:31:02,368 --> 01:31:06,532
团队还负责维护 Lambda 函数，并希望降低运维负担。
The team also maintains the Lambda function and wants less to operate.

1000
01:31:07,374 --> 01:31:11,012
哪项更改能同时解决查询成本和运维负担？
Which change addresses both the query cost and the operational burden?

1001
01:31:11,694 --> 01:31:18,532
a. 添加一个计划的 AWS Glue job，将 JSON 转换为 Parquet 并按日期重新写入分区。
a add a scheduled AWS Glue job to convert the JSON to Parquet and rewrite it partition by date.

1002
01:31:19,054 --> 01:31:26,052
b. 用具有格式转换和动态分区的 Amazon Data Firehose 流替换 Lambda 消费者。
b. Replace the Lambda consumer with an Amazon data Firehose stream using format conversion and dynamic partitioning.

1003
01:31:26,688 --> 01:31:27,008
c。
C.

1004
01:31:27,822 --> 01:31:32,708
d. 增加 Lambda 函数的内存，以便它能写入更大、组织更好的对象。
Increase the Lambda function's memory so it can write larger, better organized objects.

1005
01:31:33,488 --> 01:31:33,808
e。
D.

1006
01:31:34,288 --> 01:31:38,756
f. 将数据移入 Amazon Redshift，让分析师在那里查询。
Move the data into Amazon Redshift and have analyst query it there instead.

1007
01:31:39,534 --> 01:31:40,644
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

1008
01:31:47,342 --> 01:31:57,408
答案是 B，而选项 A 是值得学习的干扰项。转换为 Parquet 并按日期分区正是正确的建议，而且本课程已经给过你两次这个建议了。
The answer is B, and option A is the distractor worth studying. Converting to parquet and partitioning by date is exactly the correct advice, and this course gave you that advice twice.

1009
01:31:57,648 --> 01:32:01,956
它在这里是错误的，因为题目要求两点，而 A 只满足其中一点。
It is wrong here because the question asks for two things, and A only delivers one.

1010
01:32:02,862 --> 01:32:08,132
它解决了查询成本问题，但为明确要求降低运维负担的团队增加了一个 Glue作业。
It fixes query cost while adding a Blue job to a team that explicitly asks for less to operate.

1011
01:32:10,094 --> 01:32:11,812
这是考试中常见的题型。
This is a recurring exam shape.

1012
01:32:13,166 --> 01:32:17,700
即提供在技术上正确的优化方案，但这种形式忽略了题目给出的约束条件。
The technically correct optimization offered in a form that ignores a stated constraint.

1013
01:32:18,606 --> 01:32:26,020
Firehose 通过配置而非代码来执行相同的转换，并在过程中删除了一个组件。
Firehose does the same transformation as configuration rather than as code and deletes a component while doing it.

1014
01:32:27,648 --> 01:32:33,728
Amazon MSK 是托管的 Apache Kafka，关键点在于它确实就是 Kafka。
Amazon MSK is managed apache Kafka, and the important thing is that it really is Kafka.

1015
01:32:34,128 --> 01:32:42,756
同样的 API、同样的客户端库、相同的连接器和监控工具生态系统。这就是该服务的全部意义所在。
The same APAs, the same client libraries, the same ecosystem of connectors and monitoring tools. That is the entire point of the service.

1016
01:32:43,342 --> 01:32:49,508
因此，题目很少考查 Kafka 的内部原理，因为 AWS 不会考核你对开源软件的底层细节。
Questions therefore rarely test Kafka internals because AWS is not examining you on open source software.

1017
01:32:50,446 --> 01:32:51,588
它们考查两点。
They test two things.

1018
01:32:52,270 --> 01:33:00,292
即 MSK 或 Kinesis 是否是描述情境下的正确选择，以及哪种 MSK 部署选项符合工作负载。
Whether MSK or Kinesis is the right choice for a described situation and which of the MSK deployment options fits the workload.

1019
01:33:01,102 --> 01:33:07,620
这两点都可以从题目文本中的少量信号中得出，接下来的几张幻灯片将提供这些信息。
Both are answerable from a handful of signals in the question text, which is what the next few slides give you.

1020
01:33:08,334 --> 01:33:14,724
将选项中任何深层次的 Kafka 配置细节视为噪音，而不是你必须掌握的内容。
Treat any deep Kafka configuration detail in an option as noise rather than as something you are expected to know.

1021
01:33:16,334 --> 01:33:23,172
这两者的对应关系非常接近，如果你理解 Kinesis 分片，你就已经理解了 Kafka 分区。
The mapping is close enough that if you understand kinesis shards, you already understand Kafka partitions.

1022
01:33:23,488 --> 01:33:29,796
排序是在分区内保证的，而不是跨分区，这与分片的逻辑完全一致。
Ordering is guaranteed within a partition and not across partitions, exactly as with shards.

1023
01:33:30,766 --> 01:33:37,220
Kafka 中的消费者组提供的功能大致与 Kinesis 客户端库相同，即协调哪个消费者处理哪个分区。
A consumer group in Kafka does roughly what the Kinesis client library does for you, coordinating which consumer handles which partition.

1024
01:33:37,582 --> 01:33:44,644
唯一的真正区别是代理节点（代理），Kinesis 没有对应的概念，因为在 Kinesis 中你根本不需要看到或规划服务器规模。
The one genuine difference is the broker, which has no Kinesis equivalent, because in kinesis you never see or size a server at all.

1025
01:33:45,230 --> 01:33:48,932
这一个区别就是 MSK 整个运维逻辑的核心。
That single difference is the entire operational story of MSK.

1026
01:33:49,262 --> 01:33:56,068
这就是为什么 MSK 的考题经常围绕容量和补丁展开，而 Kinesis 的考题则围绕分片和键展开。
And it is why MSK questions so often turn on capacity and patching while Kinesis questions turn on shards and keys.

1027
01:33:56,366 --> 01:33:57,476
注意这里的特别说明。
Note the call out too.

1028
01:33:58,286 --> 01:34:06,468
Kafka 已从 Zookeeper 转向 Kraft 来管理集群元数据，而 AWS 不额外收取这些元数据节点的费用。
Kafka has moved from Zookeeper to Kraft for cluster metadata, and AWS includes those metadata nodes at no extra charge.

1029
01:34:08,174 --> 01:34:13,540
这个提醒很重要，因为命名确实容易混淆，考试可能会利用这一点来设陷阱。
The call out matters because the naming genuinely is confusing and the exam can exploit it.

1030
01:34:14,478 --> 01:34:15,844
MSK Provision
MSK Provision

1031
01:34:16,526 --> 01:34:19,556
和 MSK Serverless 是两种集群类型。
and MSK Serverless are the two cluster types.

1032
01:34:20,110 --> 01:34:26,756
Express 是你在 provision 模式下选择的一种代理节点类型，它与标准型并列，而不是第三种集群类型。
Express is a broker type you choose inside provision, sitting alongside standard rather than being a third cluster type.

1033
01:34:27,598 --> 01:34:36,804
Express 代理节点在 2024 年推出，取消了配置存储的需求，同时提供了大约高出三倍的单代理吞吐量，
Express brokers arrived in 2024 and removed the need to provision storage at all while delivering roughly 3 times the throughput per broker,

1034
01:34:37,614 --> 01:34:42,468
扩展速度快约 20 倍，且从代理故障中恢复的速度也快得多。
scaling around 20 times faster and recovering from broker failure far more quickly.

1035
01:34:43,438 --> 01:34:49,936
因此，如果选项描述的是高吞吐量的 Kafka，且涉及更少的代理和存储管理，那么指向的就是 Express。
So an option describing high throughput Kafka with less broker and storage management is pointing at Express.

1036
01:34:51,214 --> 01:34:56,996
如果选项描述的是完全不需要容量规划、按使用量计费，那么指向的就是 Serverless。
An option describing no capacity planning whatsoever with billing by usage is pointing at serverless.

1037
01:34:57,998 --> 01:35:04,132
而强调精细化配置控制的选项则指向标准代理节点。
And an option emphasizing fine-grained configuration control is pointing at standard brokers.

1038
01:35:05,518 --> 01:35:11,940
这是整个考试中最清晰的判别点之一，题目会直接体现出来而不是隐藏起来。
This is one of the cleanest tiebreakers in the whole exam and questions signal it plainly rather than hiding it.

1039
01:35:12,782 --> 01:35:20,736
如果场景提到现有的 Kafka 部署、Kafka 客户端库、Kafka Connect 或具备 Kafka 专业知识的团队，
If the scenario mentions an existing Kafka deployment, Kafka client libraries, Kafka Connect, or a team with Kafka expertise,

1040
01:35:20,896 --> 01:35:23,268
那么答案就是 Amazon MSK。
the answer is Amazon MSK.

1041
01:35:24,046 --> 01:35:29,616
重写现有的 Kafka 生产者和消费者以使用 Kinesis。
Rewriting working Kafka producers and consumers to use Kinesis A B.

1042
01:35:31,438 --> 01:35:34,468
这正是那种不必要的迁移
Is this exactly the kind of unnecessary migration

1043
01:35:36,206 --> 01:35:36,496
成本吗？
cost?

1044
01:35:39,214 --> 01:35:41,636
考试会一致判定此类选项为错误。
The exam consistently marks wrong.

1045
01:35:43,118 --> 01:35:49,604
如果场景是一个全新的流水线，且在任何地方都没有 Kafka 背景，那么 Kinesis 更简单，
If the scenario is a new pipeline with no Kafka history anywhere in it, Kinesis is simpler,

1046
01:35:50,286 --> 01:35:55,332
它涉及的组件更少，并且能与更多的 AWS 服务开箱即用。
has fewer moving parts and integrates with more AWS services out of the box.

1047
01:35:56,206 --> 01:36:04,576
如果没有其他明确信号，从运维开销的角度考虑，应倾向于选择 Kinesis，因为它没有代理、不需要规划分区
Absent IDA signal lean towards kinesis on operational overhead grounds because there are no brokers, no partitions to plan

1048
01:36:04,750 --> 01:36:06,180
也不需要计算集群规模。
and no cluster to size.

1049
01:36:07,918 --> 01:36:08,932
这三类情况都会出现。
Three of these come up.

1050
01:36:09,376 --> 01:36:10,084
MSK。
MSK.

1051
01:36:12,334 --> 01:36:22,436
Connect 是运行 Kafka Connect 连接器的托管方式。这是在不编写消费者的情况下，让 Kafka 与数据库和对象存储之间传输数据的方法。
Connect is the managed way to run Kafka Connect connectors. That is how Kafka moves data to and from databases and object stores without you writing consumers.

1052
01:36:23,246 --> 01:36:26,436
MSK Replicator 处理跨区域复制。
MSK Replicator handles cross-region replication.

1053
01:36:27,056 --> 01:36:31,236
它是解决 Kafka 容灾问题的低开销方案。
It is the low overhead answer to Kafka disaster recovery questions.

1054
01:36:31,886 --> 01:36:35,936
这里的干扰项是自己在 EC2 上运行 MirrorMaker。
The distractor there is running MirrorMaker yourself on EC2.

1055
01:36:38,030 --> 01:36:43,296
而且 Glue Schema Registry 也值得了解，因为它也支持 Kinesis 和 Flink。
And the Blue Schema Registry is worth knowing because it also works with Kinesis and Flink.

1056
01:36:43,918 --> 01:36:52,804
它能验证生产者发送的内容是否符合消费者的预期，这是一种在流式处理中而非落地后进行的质量控制。
It validates that producers are sending what consumers expect, which is a data quality control applied at the stream rather than after landing.

1057
01:36:54,094 --> 01:36:58,148
这个重点是值得带入考试的架构差异。
The callout is the architectural difference worth carrying into the exam.

1058
01:36:58,542 --> 01:37:02,692
Amazon MSK 集群部署在你自己的 VPC 中
An Amazon MSK cluster is deployed into your own VPC

1059
01:37:04,334 --> 01:37:07,536
其中的代理节点在你的子网中拥有私有地址。
with brokers holding private addresses in your subnets.

1060
01:37:07,696 --> 01:37:12,356
所以网络隔离是默认状态，而不是需要你配置的选项。
So network isolation is the default state rather than something you configure.

1061
01:37:13,262 --> 01:37:19,108
Kinesis Data Streams 是一个区域性服务，通过公共服务端点访问。
Kinesis Data Streams is a regional service reached through a public service endpoint.

1062
01:37:19,936 --> 01:37:20,256
所以，
So,

1063
01:37:21,294 --> 01:37:29,296
源自私有子网的流量需要一个接口、VPC 端点，并使用 AWS PrivateLink，
traffic originating in a private subnet needs an interface, VBC endpoint, using AWS private link,

1064
01:37:29,456 --> 01:37:33,252
正如第 2 模块中描述的关于 Glue 的内容一样。
exactly as module 2 described for AWS Blue.

1065
01:37:34,094 --> 01:37:40,644
这意味着关于让流式处理流量不经过公共互联网的问题，根据涉及的服务不同，答案确实完全不同。
That means a question about keeping streaming traffic off the public internet has genuinely different answers depending on which service is involved.

1066
01:37:40,816 --> 01:37:44,164
而且选项中会故意提供错误的对应服务。
And the options will offer you the wrong services answered deliberately.

1067
01:37:44,736 --> 01:37:49,572
在身份验证方面，MSK 是更灵活的，支持 IAM。
On authentication, MSK is the flexible one, supporting IAM.

1068
01:37:50,510 --> 01:37:54,628
支持带有 SCRAM 和双向 TLS 的 SASN。
SASN with S C R A M and Mutual T L S.

1069
01:37:55,984 --> 01:38:02,212
一家零售商在一个区域的 Amazon EC2 上运行自管理的 Apache Kafka 集群。
A retailer runs a self-managed Apache Kafka cluster on Amazon EC2 in one region.

1070
01:38:02,624 --> 01:38:12,836
大约有 40 个生产者和消费者应用使用标准的 Kafka 客户端库，还有几个使用 Kafka Connect 连接器将数据移动到 Amazon S3。
Around 40 producer and consumer applications use the standard Kafka client libraries, and several use Kafka Connect connectors to move data into Amazon S3.

1071
01:38:13,742 --> 01:38:20,464
平台团队花费大量时间去修复代理节点、重新平衡分区以及从代理节点故障中恢复。
The platform team spends significant time patching brokers, rebalancing partitions, and recovering from broker failures.

1072
01:38:20,704 --> 01:38:27,524
他们希望减少这些工作，保持所有现有应用运行不变，并增加跨区域容灾。
They want to reduce that work, keep all existing applications running unchanged, and add cross-region disaster recovery.

1073
01:38:28,686 --> 01:38:30,052
公司应该怎么做？
What should the company do?

1074
01:38:31,790 --> 01:38:38,084
A. 迁移到按需模式的 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 并重写客户端应用。
Migrate to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams in on-demand mode and rewrite the client applications.

1075
01:38:38,958 --> 01:38:48,772
B. 迁移到配备 Express Brokers 的预置型 Amazon MSK，使用 MSK Connect 并添加 MSK Replicator。
b Migrate to Amazon MSK provisioned with Express Brokers, use MSK Connect and add MSK Replicator.

1076
01:38:49,264 --> 01:38:49,504
C。
C.

1077
01:38:50,254 --> 01:38:56,580
保留 EC2 上的 Kafka，但增加一个自动扩展组和带 Mirror Maker 的第二个集群。
Keep Kafka on EC2 but add an auto-scaling group and a second cluster with Mirror Maker.

1078
01:38:58,766 --> 01:39:04,100
D. 迁移到以 Amazon S3 为目的地的 Amazon Data Firehose。
Migrate to Amazon Data Firehose with Amazon S3 as the destination.

1079
01:39:05,070 --> 01:39:06,500
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1080
01:39:13,102 --> 01:39:18,308
答案是 B，而且应该很快就能做出来，因为题目已经把所有工作都做好了。
The answer is B, and it should have been quick, because OnePlus did all the work.

1081
01:39:18,926 --> 01:39:21,668
保持所有现有应用在不改变的情况下继续运行。
Keep all existing applications running unchanged.

1082
01:39:22,062 --> 01:39:29,476
在一个完全围绕 Kafka 客户端和 Kafka Connect 构建的场景中，只有兼容 Kafka 的选项才能满足要求。
In a scenario built entirely around Kafka clients and Kafka Connect is a requirement only Kafka compatible options can satisfy.

1083
01:39:30,414 --> 01:39:37,956
这可以在你权衡任何技术优劣之前，就排除掉 A 和 D，因为这两项都需要放弃 Kafka APIs。
That eliminates A and D before you weigh a single technical merit because both require abandoning the Kafka APEs.

1084
01:39:38,894 --> 01:39:47,524
然后，C 因为它增加了第二个需要打补丁的集群，而不是移除第一个，所以无法满足减少运维工作的目标。
Then, C fails on the stated goal of reducing operational work since it adds a second cluster to patch rather than removing the first.

1085
01:39:48,366 --> 01:39:54,692
剩下的就是 B，它的三个组成部分分别对应三个明确的要求。
What remains is B and each of its three components maps to one of the three stated requirements.

1086
01:39:55,854 --> 01:39:59,652
Express Brokers、减少 Broker 以及存储管理。
Express Brokers, Reduce Broker, and Storage Management.

1087
01:40:01,518 --> 01:40:02,384
MSK
MSK

1088
01:40:03,278 --> 01:40:05,156
Connect 接管连接器。
Connect takes over the connectors.

1089
01:40:06,478 --> 01:40:09,860
MSK Replicator 提供跨区域恢复。
MSK Replicator provides the cross-region recovery.

1090
01:40:10,784 --> 01:40:16,420
这就是模块 1 中的四个问题，大约在 15 秒内就能全部做完。
This is the four questions from module 1 running to completion in about 15 seconds.

1091
01:40:17,742 --> 01:40:20,932
到目前为止的所有内容都是将记录从一个地方移动到另一个地方。
Everything so far moves records from one place to another.

1092
01:40:21,424 --> 01:40:26,116
Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink 做的是完全不同的事情。
Amazon Managed Service for Apache, Flink does something categorically different.

1093
01:40:26,638 --> 01:40:31,300
它在流上进行持续计算，并在过程中保留状态，
It computes over a stream continuously, holding state as it goes,

1094
01:40:31,982 --> 01:40:33,636
统计每分钟的事件数量。
counting events per minute.

1095
01:40:36,142 --> 01:40:38,788
基于共享键连接两个流。
Joining two streams on a shared key.

1096
01:40:39,344 --> 01:40:44,292
检测某个值在五分钟内是否超过了阈值三次。
Detecting that a value has exceeded a threshold three times within five minutes.

1097
01:40:44,544 --> 01:40:51,428
仅靠传输是无法实现这些功能的，因为所有这些操作都需要记住当前记录到达之前发生的情况。
None of that is possible with delivery alone because all of it requires remembering what happened before the current record arrived.

1098
01:40:52,174 --> 01:40:58,660
识别一个问题是否需要状态是本节教授的技能，而且这是一个非常有用的通用技能。
Recognizing when a question needs state is the skill this section teaches and it is a genuinely transferable one.

1099
01:40:59,278 --> 01:41:09,380
一旦你能识别出来，一整类问题就能在几秒钟内解决，因为四个选项中只有一个能保持状态，其他三个无需思考即可排除。
Once you can spot it, a whole class of question resolves in seconds because only one of the four options can hold state and the other three are eliminated without further thought.

1100
01:41:10,670 --> 01:41:16,516
这个提示是实战测试，值得在每一个流式处理问题上有意识地运用。
The callout is the practical test and it is worth applying deliberately on every streaming question.

1101
01:41:17,390 --> 01:41:22,084
询问处理这条记录是否需要了解任何其他记录的信息。
Ask whether handling this record requires knowing anything about any other record.

1102
01:41:22,702 --> 01:41:25,156
转换时间戳格式不需要。
Converting a timestamp format does not.

1103
01:41:25,614 --> 01:41:27,588
所以 Lambda 函数就足够了。
So a lambda function is enough.

1104
01:41:28,046 --> 01:41:30,340
而使用 Flink 就会造成昂贵的过度设计。
And flink would be expensive overkill.

1105
01:41:31,184 --> 01:41:36,612
统计该用户在过去 5 分钟内产生了多少个事件，这绝对需要状态。
Counting how many events this user has produced in the last 5 minutes absolutely does.

1106
01:41:36,784 --> 01:41:43,684
检测温度是否连续三次读数上升，或者将订单流与支付流连接起来，也同样需要状态。
So does detecting that a temperature has risen for three consecutive readings or joining an order stream to a payment stream.

1107
01:41:44,494 --> 01:41:52,100
如果没有流处理器，你就需要一个外部状态存储，再加上处理过期、乱序到达和并发访问的逻辑。
Without a stream processor, you would need an external state store, plus logic for expiry, out of order arrival, and concurrent access.

1108
01:41:53,550 --> 01:42:03,588
无状态和有状态之间的这种区别在考试指南中明确说明了，这告诉你 AWS 认为这是你需要在考场上识别出的内容。
That distinction between stateless and stateful is named explicitly in the exam guide, which tells you AWS considers it something you should identify on site.

1109
01:42:04,910 --> 01:42:11,300
窗口类型是可考查的词汇，一旦用正确的术语表达出来，其中的区别就很容易分辨。
Window types are testable vocabulary and the distinction is easy once you hear it in the right words.

1110
01:42:12,816 --> 01:42:17,284
滚动窗口就像一份针对覆盖范围 R 的报告。
Tumbling windows are like a report that runs on the R covering that R.

1111
01:42:17,966 --> 01:42:22,736
每条记录仅属于一个窗口，且窗口之间互不重叠。
Each record belongs to exactly one window and windows never overlap.

1112
01:42:23,662 --> 01:42:32,132
滑动窗口会重叠，因此一条记录可以被计入多个窗口，这正是实现持续更新的滚动平均值所需要的。
Sliding windows do overlap, so a single record can be counted in several of them, which is what you want for a continuously updating rolling average.

1113
01:42:33,518 --> 01:42:35,748
会话窗口没有任何固定的长度。
Session windows have no fixed length at all.

1114
01:42:36,142 --> 01:42:39,856
它们按活动分组，并在一段定义的静默期后关闭。
They group activity and close after a defined period of silence.

1115
01:42:40,430 --> 01:42:46,500
这正是你在不预先决定访问时长的情况下衡量网站访问量的方法。
That is exactly how you measure a visit to a website without deciding in advance how long a visit lasts.

1116
01:42:47,406 --> 01:42:56,324
需要留意的词是「滚动」，这几乎总是指滑动窗口；而「每 n 分钟」这个短语，几乎总是指翻滚窗口。
The phrase to listen for is rolling, which almost always means sliding, and the phrase every n minutes, which almost always means tumbling.

1117
01:42:58,016 --> 01:43:04,740
检查点和保存点的区别是那种能区分两个看似完全相同的选项的细节。
The checkpoint and save point distinction is the kind of detail that separates two otherwise identical options.

1118
01:43:05,296 --> 01:43:13,860
检查点按计划自动生成，它们的存在是为了让崩溃的应用程序能够从之前的位置恢复，而不是从零开始。
Checkpoints happen automatically on a schedule and they exist so that an application which crashes resumes from where it was rather than from nothing.

1119
01:43:15,278 --> 01:43:16,516
你不需要去管理它们。
You do not manage them.

1120
01:43:17,518 --> 01:43:23,716
保存点是你主动创建的，因为你即将部署新代码或更改应用程序的并行度，
Save points you take deliberately because you are about to deploy new code or change the parallelism of the application,

1121
01:43:23,936 --> 01:43:29,316
并且你希望新版本能接续旧版本积累的状态，而不是从空状态开始。
and you want the new version to pick up the old version's accumulated state rather than starting empty.

1122
01:43:30,254 --> 01:43:37,252
所以，关于在不丢失运行聚合数据的情况下升级 Flink 应用的问题，就是考查保存点。
So a question about upgrading a flink application without losing its running aggregations is a save point question.

1123
01:43:38,062 --> 01:43:41,764
关于在节点故障时幸存的问题，则是考查检查点。
A question about surviving a node failure is a checkpoint question.

1124
01:43:42,176 --> 01:43:45,092
最后一项是真正的生产环境中的考量。
The last bullet is a real production concern.

1125
01:43:45,806 --> 01:43:53,636
基于无界内容（如永不重复的会话标识符）建立的状态，会一直增长直到应用程序崩溃。
State keyed on something unbounded, like a session identifier that never repeats, grows until the application falls over.

1126
01:43:55,150 --> 01:44:00,068
这是本模块关于可用性的警告，也是整个课程中最严厉的一个。
This is the availability warning for this module, and it is the sharpest one in the whole course.

1127
01:44:00,590 --> 01:44:03,940
有两个不同的产品共享 Kinesis 数据。
There were two distinct products sharing the kinesis data.

1128
01:44:04,814 --> 01:44:08,004
Analytics 这个名称是导致混淆的根源。
Analytics name, which is the root of the confusion.

1129
01:44:08,494 --> 01:44:17,156
Flink 1 在 2023 年更名为 Managed Service for Apache Flink，它仍然活跃、现行，且是高频考点。
The Flink 1 was renamed to Manage Service for Apache Flink in 2023 and is alive, current, and heavily examinable.

1130
01:44:18,094 --> 01:44:25,220
SQL 1 允许你直接对流编写 SQL，它已经被完全停止服务了。
The SQL 1, which let you write SQL directly against a stream, has been discontinued entirely.

1131
01:44:26,126 --> 01:44:35,172
AWS 从 2025 年 10 月起不再允许创建新应用，并于 2026 年 1 月 27 日删除了剩余的应用程序。
AWS stopped allowing new applications from October 2025 and deleted remaining applications from the 27th of January 2026.

1132
01:44:35,616 --> 01:44:41,924
它在本次课程分析的题库中出现了 9 次，有时作为标注正确的答案。
It appears 9 times in the bank analyzed for this course, sometimes as the marked correct answer.

1133
01:44:42,702 --> 01:44:48,164
认出这个名字，知道它已经不存在了，然后选择 Managed Service for Apache 作为答案。
Recognize the name, know that it is gone, and answer with Managed Service for Apache.

1134
01:44:49,870 --> 01:44:51,172
也就是 Flink。
Flink instead.

1135
01:44:52,942 --> 01:45:00,576
Lambda 读取流是一个真正好的模式且经常是正确答案，所以不要假设流式处理就意味着必须用 Flink。
Lambda reading from a stream is a genuinely good pattern and often the right answer, so do not assume that streaming implies FLINK.

1136
01:45:01,056 --> 01:45:05,668
Lambda 接收一批记录，对每一条执行操作，然后退出。
Lambda receives a batch of records, does something to each of them, and exits.

1137
01:45:06,958 --> 01:45:09,252
它在不同调用之间不保留任何记忆。
It remembers nothing between invocations.

1138
01:45:09,870 --> 01:45:12,496
这涵盖了大量实际的工作内容。
That covers a surprising amount of real work.

1139
01:45:13,358 --> 01:45:21,376
过滤掉无关事件、重新格式化费用、将根记录分发到不同目的地，或者为每一条记录调用外部 API。
Filter out irrelevant events, reformat fees, root records to different destinations, call an external API for each one.

1140
01:45:21,536 --> 01:45:26,980
它成本低廉，在没有数据流时没有任何东西在运行，而且不需要专门的应用程序来维护。
It is cheap, there is nothing running when no data flows and there is no application to operate.

1141
01:45:27,696 --> 01:45:34,736
一旦需求涉及时间窗口、累计总和或来自两个不同流的匹配记录。
The moment the requirement involves a time window, a running total or matching records arriving on two different streams.

1142
01:45:35,150 --> 01:45:39,258
Lambda 就需要外部状态存储以及谨慎的并发处理。
Lambda would need an external state store and careful concurrency handling.

1143
01:45:40,430 --> 01:45:44,516
到那个时候，你就是在手动构建 Flink，而正确答案就是 Flink。
At that point, you are building FLINK by hand and the answer becomes FLINK.

1144
01:45:46,254 --> 01:45:51,652
一家在线支付公司将交易事件流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流中。
An online payments company streams transaction events into Amazon Kinesis data streams.

1145
01:45:52,302 --> 01:46:02,656
新需求是：标记任何在滚动 1 分钟内进行超过 5 次交易的账户，并在第五次交易发生后 2 秒内发出警报。
A new requirement is to flag any account that makes more than 5 transactions in any rolling 1 minute period and to raise an alert within 2 seconds of the fifth transaction.

1146
01:46:03,296 --> 01:46:10,816
现有的 AWS Lambda 函数已经正在读取该流并将每笔交易写入 Amazon S3。
An existing AWS Lambda function already reads the stream and writes each transaction to Amazon S3.

1147
01:46:11,296 --> 01:46:18,532
提议是扩展该函数，通过在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中存储计数来实现新逻辑。
A proposal is to extend that function with the new logic storing counts in an Amazon DynamoDB table.

1148
01:46:20,430 --> 01:46:22,532
哪种设计最合适？
What is the most appropriate design?

1149
01:46:25,102 --> 01:46:30,308
A. 扩展现有的 Lambda 函数，在 Dynamo DB 中维护每个账户的计数。
Extend the existing Lambda function to maintain per account counts in Dynamo DB.

1150
01:46:30,702 --> 01:46:36,832
B. 添加一个带有跨度为一分钟滑动窗口的 Apache Flink 管理式服务。C。
B Add a managed service for Apache Flink application with a sliding window over one minute. C.

1151
01:46:37,072 --> 01:46:42,992
C. 使用 Data Firehose 将流传输到 Amazon S3，并每分钟运行一次 Athena 查询。
Deliver the stream to Amazon S3 with Data Firehose and run an Athena query every minute.

1152
01:46:43,312 --> 01:46:43,552
D
D

1153
01:46:44,526 --> 01:46:51,876
D. 将交易加载到 Amazon Redshift，并使用每分钟刷新一次的物化视图。
Load the transactions into Amazon Redshift and use a materialized view refreshed each minute.

1154
01:46:52,686 --> 01:46:53,956
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1155
01:47:00,814 --> 01:47:02,112
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1156
01:47:02,992 --> 01:47:04,740
两个短语决定了结果。
Two phrases decided it.

1157
01:47:05,230 --> 01:47:12,548
“滚动 1 分钟周期”是滑动窗口的标准描述，而“2 秒”排除了任何在计算前进行缓冲的设计。
Rolling 1 minute period is the textbook description of a sliding window, and 2 seconds eliminates any design that buffers before computing.

1158
01:47:14,446 --> 01:47:19,332
选项 A 值得关注，因为它并不荒谬，而且团队确实会这样构建。
Option A deserves attention because it is not absurd and teams really do build it.

1159
01:47:20,046 --> 01:47:22,916
难点在于描述中省略掉的所有细节。
The difficulty is everything the description leaves out.

1160
01:47:23,438 --> 01:47:32,356
随着窗口移动而过期计数、处理乱序到达的记录，以及处理同一个账户被两个并发调用同时处理的情况。
Expiring counts as the window moves, handling records that arrive out of order, and coping when the same account is processed by two concurrent invocations.

1161
01:47:32,910 --> 01:47:35,300
Flink 会自动解决这三个问题。
Flink solves all three as a matter of course.

1162
01:47:36,174 --> 01:47:42,180
任何通过手动重新实现管理功能的选项，都是这次考试中经常出现的错误答案。
An option that re-implements a managed capability by hand is a recurring wrong answer on this exam.

1163
01:47:43,790 --> 01:47:48,768
这一对组合经常出现，区分点在于保留时间和扇出。
This pairing shows up regularly, and the separator is retention and fanout.

1164
01:47:50,388 --> 01:47:58,852
DynamoDB Streams 是内置的，不需要额外服务，并保留 24 小时的条目级变更供 Lambda 函数响应。
DynamoDB Streams is built-in, needs no extra service, and keeps 24 hours of item level changes that a Lambda function can react to.

1165
01:47:59,662 --> 01:48:07,876
对于更新内容的常见情况，当记录发生变化时，这完全足够，且是开销更低的答案。
For the common case of updating something, when a record changes, that is entirely sufficient and it is the lower overhead answer.

1166
01:48:09,358 --> 01:48:18,468
当你需要超过 24 小时的回放，或者有多个独立的消费者处理同一更改并用于不同目的时。
When you need more than 24 hours of replay or several independent consumers leading the same change, freed for different purposes.

1167
01:48:19,312 --> 01:48:21,604
将变更路由到 Kinesis 数据中。
Routing changes into Kinesis data.

1168
01:48:22,032 --> 01:48:26,180
Streams 提供这两者，但代价是设计中需要引入另一个服务。
Streams gives you both at the cost of another service in the design.

1169
01:48:27,152 --> 01:48:32,324
24 小时的限制无法延长，这通常是决定这些问题的关键点。
The 24 hour limit is not extendable, which is usually what decides these questions.

1170
01:48:32,878 --> 01:48:35,556
最后一项是较新的内容，且经常被忽略。
The last bullet is newer and often overlooked.

1171
01:48:36,302 --> 01:48:46,884
为了保持搜索索引同步，Dynamo DB 和 Amazon OpenSearch 之间的零 ETL 集成完全去除了设计中的变更流水线。
For keeping a search index synchronized, the zero ETL integration between Dynamo DB and Amazon OpenSear removes the change pipeline from the design entirely.

1172
01:48:48,590 --> 01:48:53,316
Pipes 很容易被忽略，但它能回答特定类型的题目。
Pipes is easy to overlook and it answers a specific shape of question.

1173
01:48:54,158 --> 01:48:59,876
大量的实际流水线包含一个 Lambda 函数，其全部工作就是读取流。
A large number of real pipelines contain a lambda function whose entire job is to read a stream.

1174
01:49:00,622 --> 01:49:06,244
丢弃不重要的记录，对剩下的内容进行微调，然后交给其他组件处理。
Throw away the records that do not matter, reshape the rest slightly and hand them to something else.

1175
01:49:07,182 --> 01:49:11,588
那是需要编写、部署、监控并支付费用的代码。
That is code to write, deploy, monitor, and pay for.

1176
01:49:12,782 --> 01:49:13,636
EventBridge。
Event bridge.

1177
01:49:14,414 --> 01:49:22,340
Pipes 通过配置来实现，并在调用目标之前应用过滤，这样你就不会处理掉弃用的事件。
Pipes does it as configuration with filtering applied before the target is invoked so you are not beyond events you discard.

1178
01:49:23,022 --> 01:49:25,092
最后一项让它保持在自己的范畴内。
The last bullet keeps it in its lane.

1179
01:49:26,032 --> 01:49:28,836
它一次移动并过滤一条记录。
It moves and filters records one at a time.

1180
01:49:29,072 --> 01:49:32,672
所以任何需要记忆其他记录的操作仍需使用 Flink。
So anything needing memory of other records is still flink.

1181
01:49:34,414 --> 01:49:39,652
考试指南将管理扇入和扇出列为一项技能，所以要留意它。
The exam guide names managing fan in and fan out as a skill, so expect it.

1182
01:49:40,270 --> 01:49:41,956
最后一项是陷阱。
The last bullet is the trap.

1183
01:49:42,638 --> 01:49:48,516
当多个团队想要相同的数据时，直观的答案是给每个团队提供自己的流。
When several teams want the same data, the intuitive answer is to give each team its own stream.

1184
01:49:49,006 --> 01:49:53,028
但这在成本、一致性和运维开销上都是错误的。
And it is wrong on cost, on consistency, and on operational overhead.

1185
01:49:53,952 --> 01:50:01,252
如果他们竞争读取容量，使用增强型扇出的单流多消费者就是正确的架构。
One stream with multiple consumers is the design using enhanced fan out if they contend for read capacity.

1186
01:50:02,222 --> 01:50:05,156
SNS 变体值得单独拿出来讨论。
The SNS variant is worth separating.

1187
01:50:06,062 --> 01:50:12,432
如果分发的内容是发生了某事的通知，而不是持续的数据流。
If what is being distributed is a notification that something happened rather than a continuous data feed.

1188
01:50:13,868 --> 01:50:18,588
具有多个订阅者的 SNS 比任何流都要简单。
SNS with multiple subscribers is simpler than any stream.

1189
01:50:21,070 --> 01:50:24,260
这张表可以回答一种经常出现的题目类型。
This table answers a question shape that appears reliably.

1190
01:50:24,624 --> 01:50:30,084
下游系统故障了几天，现在 Bug 已修复，数据必须重新处理。
A downstream system was broken for several days, the bug is fixed, and the data must be reprocessed.

1191
01:50:30,304 --> 01:50:34,304
你能做什么完全取决于数据在通过时保存在哪里。
What you can do depends entirely on where the data was held while it passed through.

1192
01:50:34,544 --> 01:50:37,092
Kinesis 和 MSK 会保留数据并允许你回溯。
Kinesis and MSK keep it and let you rewind.

1193
01:50:37,838 --> 01:50:42,660
Firehose 不会，因为它是一种交付机制而不是存储。
Firehose does not because it is a delivery mechanism rather than a store.

1194
01:50:42,784 --> 01:50:47,268
所以在那里的恢复意味着回到任何提供给 Firehose 流的源头。
So recovering there means going back to whatever fed the firehose stream.

1195
01:50:48,078 --> 01:50:55,044
这就是在 Firehose 前面使用 Kinesis Data Streams 而不是直接写入 Firehose 的一个好理由。
That is a good reason to have kinesis data streams in front of firehose rather than writing to firehose directly.

1196
01:50:56,784 --> 01:51:01,348
应用模块 1 中的计费单位规则，成本相关的题目就迎刃而解了。
Apply the billing unit rule from module 1 and the cost answers fallout.

1197
01:51:01,664 --> 01:51:04,580
任何持续计费的项目都会惩罚闲置时间。
Anything charged continuously punishes idle time.

1198
01:51:05,264 --> 01:51:11,364
无论记录是否流动，配置分片和 MSK 代理节点都会按时计费。
Provision shards and MSK brokers both bill around the clock whether records flow or not.

1199
01:51:12,142 --> 01:51:17,892
对于多可用区的生产集群，MSK Provision 包含三个代理节点的底线。
An MSK provision carries a three-broker floor for a multi-availability zone production cluster.

1200
01:51:18,414 --> 01:51:23,108
这使得它在处理低流量工作负载时成本很高，这也是考题的切入点。
That makes it expensive for a low volume workload in a way that supplies people.

1201
01:51:23,904 --> 01:51:32,932
Firehose 和按需模式，Kinesis 按数据量计费，所以它们在闲置时几乎不花钱，只有在高持续流量下才会变贵。
Firehose and on demand, kinesis charge for data, so they cost almost nothing when idle and become expensive at sustained high volume.

1202
01:51:34,784 --> 01:51:41,028
关于 MSK 集群上低吞吐量流的问题，直接指向的就是那个代理器底线。
A question about a low throughput stream on an MSK cluster is pointing straight at that broker floor.

1203
01:51:42,734 --> 01:51:48,740
迭代器年龄值得单独用一句话来解释，因为它是 CloudWatch 问题构建的核心指标。
Iterator age deserves its own sentence because it is the metric CloudWatch questions are built around.

1204
01:51:49,184 --> 01:51:56,544
它报告当前正在处理的记录有多旧。换句话说，就是你的消费者落后于实时时间多少。
It reports how old the record currently being processed is. In other words, how far behind real time your consumer has fallen.

1205
01:51:57,166 --> 01:52:01,764
迭代器年龄持续上升意味着消费速度低于生产速度。
A steadily rising iterator age means consumption is lower than production.

1206
01:52:02,542 --> 01:52:08,996
它会一直上升，直到消费者提速或者超过保留窗口导致数据丢失为止。
And it will keep rising until either the consumer speeds up or the retention window is exceeded and data is lost.

1207
01:52:09,902 --> 01:52:22,116
平稳且较低的迭代器年龄意味着你跟得上进度。如果题目给出一个不断攀升的迭代器年龄图表，它在考查的是消费能力，而不是生产能力。
A flat, low iterator age means you are keeping up. If a question hands you a graph description of a climbing iterator age, it is asking about consumer capacity, not producer capacity.

1208
01:52:23,566 --> 01:52:29,252
这 5 个问题涵盖了考试中几乎所有的流式处理场景。
5 questions and between them they resolve nearly every streaming scenario on this exam.

1209
01:52:29,744 --> 01:52:35,524
按这个顺序来做，因为每一个问题都能直接排除掉错误选项，而不仅仅是排序。
Run them in that order because each one eliminates options rather than merely ranking them.

1210
01:52:36,784 --> 01:52:40,004
第二个是整个模块中最快能拿分的题。
The second is the fastest win in the whole module.

1211
01:52:42,542 --> 01:52:45,444
“现有的 Kafka”实际上就是一个词就能得出答案的题目。
Existing Kafka is effectively a one-word answer,

1212
01:52:46,382 --> 01:52:52,900
而考生往往还在浪费时间去权衡 Kinesis 和 MSK，尽管题目已经把答案告诉他们了。
and candidates still spend the minute carefully weighing kinesis against MSK when the question already told them.

1213
01:52:53,424 --> 01:52:55,588
第五个是大家最容易忽略的。
The fifth is the one people forget.

1214
01:52:55,904 --> 01:53:03,076
因为当提供四个服务且其中三个听起来更强大、更有趣时，Firehose 很容易被忽视。
Because Firehose is easy to overlook when four services are offered and three of them sound more powerful and more interesting.

1215
01:53:03,790 --> 01:53:11,748
无需自定义逻辑的托管传输到目标端是一个常见的需求，而 Firehose 通常是这类问题的标准答案。
Managed delivery to a destination with no custom logic is a common requirement and firehose is usually the intended answer for it.

1216
01:53:13,358 --> 01:53:20,516
下一个模块是迁移与连接，涵盖所有非流式数据如何进入 AWS。
Next module is migration and connectivity, covering how everything that is not a stream gets into AWS.

1217
01:53:22,158 --> 01:53:27,024
模块 2 和 3 涵盖了数据进入 AWS 后会发生什么。
Modules 2 and 3 covered what happens to data once it is in AWS.

1218
01:53:27,278 --> 01:53:29,344
这个模块涵盖的是它们如何到达。
This one covers how it arrives.

1219
01:53:29,584 --> 01:53:37,264
在为本课程分析的题库中，AWS DMS 出现了 72 次，比 Amazon Athena 还要多。
AWS DMS appeared 72 times in the bank analyzed for this course, which puts it ahead of Amazon Athena.

1220
01:53:38,126 --> 01:53:44,196
这里的其他服务虽然单个出现的频率较低，但合在一起涵盖了大量的题目。
The other services here appear less often individually, but collectively they carry a lot of questions.

1221
01:53:44,384 --> 01:53:48,932
这些题目的得分非常容易，因为每一个服务都有明确且定义清晰的任务。
They are unusually easy marks because each one has a narrow, well defined job.

1222
01:53:50,894 --> 01:53:56,144
只要搞对源类型到服务的对应关系，这些问题只需 15 秒就能做完。
Get the mapping from source type to service right, and these questions take 15 seconds.

1223
01:53:56,654 --> 01:54:00,836
这个模块还包含全课程中最大的可用性警示。
This module also carries the largest availability warning in the whole course.

1224
01:54:01,358 --> 01:54:07,588
这是因为一个作为标准正确答案长达十年的服务正在被关停。
That is because a service that has been a standard, correct answer for a decade is being switched off.

1225
01:54:09,230 --> 01:54:15,012
这个模块中的几乎每道题都会给出一个源，并询问如何将其导入 AWS。
Almost every question in this module names a source and asks how to get it into AWS.

1226
01:54:15,344 --> 01:54:20,932
目标端几乎总是 Amazon S3 或数据库，这部分很少决定最终答案。
The destination is nearly always Amazon S3 or a database and it rarely decides anything.

1227
01:54:21,424 --> 01:54:23,812
真正起决定作用的是源是什么：
What decides it is what the source is:

1228
01:54:24,462 --> 01:54:32,676
是关系型数据库、文件共享、SaaS 应用、通过互联网上传的合作伙伴数据，还是别人拥有的数据集。
a relational database, a file share, a SaaS application, a partner uploading over the internet or a dataset somebody else owns.

1229
01:54:33,262 --> 01:54:39,236
每一个情况都有一个明显的对应服务和三个看似合理的错误选项。所以阅读技巧很简单。
Each of those has one obvious service and three plausible wrong ones. So the reading technique is simple.

1230
01:54:40,174 --> 01:54:49,028
找到描述源的那句话，对其进行分类，在你思考任何技术细节之前，大部分选项就会被排除掉。
Find the sentence describing the source, classify it, and most of the options fall away before you have thought about anything technical.

1231
01:54:49,934 --> 01:54:55,620
下一张幻灯片是把这些分类汇总成一个表格，非常值得直接背下来。
The next slide is that classification in one table and it is worth memorizing outright.

1232
01:54:56,878 --> 01:54:59,556
这个表格能解决大部分模块的问题。
This table resolves most of the module.

1233
01:54:59,982 --> 01:55:03,428
特别标注的内容是大家最容易搞混的区别。
The call-out is the distinction people get wrong most often.

1234
01:55:03,694 --> 01:55:04,676
所以从这里开始。
So start there.

1235
01:55:05,870 --> 01:55:12,324
AWS DataSync 是你用来按照设定的计划，从你控制的地点获取数据的服务。
AWS DataSync is something you run to go and fetch data from a location you control on a schedule you set.

1236
01:55:13,104 --> 01:55:19,460
AWS Transfer Family 是你建立的一个端点，让其他人可以将数据发送给你。
AWS Transfer Family is an endpoint you stand up so that other people can send data to you.

1237
01:55:19,984 --> 01:55:24,388
他们按照自己的时间表，使用他们系统自带的协议来操作。
They do it on their schedule using protocols their systems already speak.

1238
01:55:25,024 --> 01:55:29,220
两者的核心任务都是移动文件，只是发起方向相反。
Same broad job of moving files, opposite direction of initiation.

1239
01:55:30,190 --> 01:55:36,996
所以，如果题目提到合作伙伴、供应商或外部客户上传数据，那就是 传输系列 的问题。
So a question mentioning partners, suppliers, or external customers uploading is a transfer family question.

1240
01:55:38,318 --> 01:55:42,180
如果题目关于你自己的文件服务器，那就是 DataSync 的问题。
A question about your own file servers is a data sync question.

1241
01:55:43,790 --> 01:55:46,500
这里的特别标注是你要带入考试的排序逻辑。
The call out is the ranking to carry into the exam.

1242
01:55:48,974 --> 01:55:54,052
优先选择管理连接器，因为它纯粹是配置，且由他人维护。
Manage connector first because it is pure configuration and somebody else maintains it.

1243
01:55:54,926 --> 01:55:57,796
其次是 Glue 市场或自定义连接器。
Then a blue marketplace or custom connector.

1244
01:55:58,606 --> 01:56:06,436
连接器本身仍由他人负责，而任务编排、重试和日志记录都由 Glue 提供，而不是由你来处理。
The connector itself is still somebody else's problem and the job orchestration, retrees, and logging all come from Blue rather than from you.

1245
01:56:06,784 --> 01:56:14,436
最后才考虑作为真正最后的手段的定制代码。这类方案的所有维护成本都归你负责，包括供应商后续的任何破坏性更新。
Then bespoke code as a genuine last resort. Everything about it becomes yours to maintain forever, including the vendor's next breaking.

1246
01:56:15,024 --> 01:56:16,324
API 变更。
API change.

1247
01:56:17,166 --> 01:56:23,460
这个领域的题目几乎总是包含每个层级的一个选项，这就是它们之所以能被答出来的原因。
Questions in this area almost always include one option from each tier, which is what makes them answerable.

1248
01:56:24,144 --> 01:56:27,108
限定词会告诉你想要哪一个层级的答案。
The qualifier tells you which tier is wanted.

1249
01:56:27,664 --> 01:56:31,172
“开发工作量最少”会让你往列表上方的 App Flow 靠拢。
Least development effort pushes you up the list towards App Flow.

1250
01:56:31,824 --> 01:56:34,660
“没人支持的源头”则会将你推向列表下方。
A source that nobody supports pushes you down it.

1251
01:56:36,270 --> 01:56:40,804
理解这个顺序可以解释 DMS 的大部分功能及其原因。
Understanding this sequence explains most of what DMS does and why.

1252
01:56:41,184 --> 01:56:49,956
单靠全量加载需要冻结源数据库直到复制完成，对于大型生产系统来说，这意味着无法接受的停机时间。
A full load alone would require freezing the source database for however long the copy takes, which for a large production system means an unacceptable outage.

1253
01:56:50,304 --> 01:56:52,196
变更数据捕获解决了这个问题。
Change data capture solves that.

1254
01:56:52,959 --> 01:57:01,039
全量加载在运行的同时，源端发生的每一次更改都会被捕获，并在之后应用到目标端。
The full load runs against a live database, and while it runs, every change happening on the source is captured and applied to the target afterwards.

1255
01:57:01,039 --> 01:57:07,339
目标端会与源端同步，切换窗口从几小时缩短到几分钟。
The target converges on the source and the cut-over window shrinks from hours to minutes.

1256
01:57:08,599 --> 01:57:14,699
当题目提到“最小停机时间”或“迁移过程中数据库必须保持可用”时，
When a question mentions minimal downtime or the database must remain available during migration,

1257
01:57:15,539 --> 01:57:18,039
它描述的就是全量加载加上变更数据捕获。
it is describing full load plus CD.

1258
01:57:18,990 --> 01:57:21,476
这个短语本身就是答案。
That phrase is effectively the answer.

1259
01:57:23,182 --> 01:57:26,692
它的名字容易误导人，而考试正是利用这一点。
The name misleads people and the exam exploits it.

1260
01:57:27,184 --> 01:57:35,716
数据库迁移服务听起来像是用一次就关掉的东西，但它在考试中出现的大部分情况并非如此。
Database migration service sounds like something you use once and switch off, and a large share of its exam appearances are nothing of the kind.

1261
01:57:37,344 --> 01:57:44,068
DMS 是保持分析型存储与运营数据库同步时的常用答案。
DMS is very commonly the answer for keeping an analytic store in sync with an operational database.

1262
01:57:44,944 --> 01:57:48,624
它会一直运行，并不涉及所谓的“迁移”。
It runs indefinitely with no migration in sight.

1263
01:57:48,784 --> 01:57:56,036
它可以写入到 Amazon S3、Kinesis DataStreams、Amazon MSK 以及 Amazon Redshift。
It can write to Amazon S3, to Kinesis DataStreams, to Amazon MSK, and to Amazon Redshift.

1264
01:57:56,974 --> 01:58:00,580
这些都不是传统意义上你会迁移到的数据库。
None of those is a database you would migrate to in the traditional sense.

1265
01:58:01,486 --> 01:58:12,548
所以当题目描述在不触碰源应用的情况下，希望获取可用于分析的运营数据时，即便没人真的在做“迁移”，也要想到 DMS。
So when a question describes wanting operational data available for analytics without touching the source application, think DMS even though nobody is migrating anything.

1266
01:58:13,774 --> 01:58:20,132
这包含四个组件，考试主要考查它们之间的关系，而不是每个组件的细节。
Four components and the exam mostly tests the relationships between them rather than the details of each.

1267
01:58:20,304 --> 01:58:23,844
这个提示说明了一个经常出现的模式。
The call out describes a pattern that comes up regularly.

1268
01:58:24,224 --> 01:58:31,588
将多个源数据库整合到一个目标仓库中，是使用指向同一个目标端点的多个任务。
Consolidating several source databases into one target warehouse uses several tasks pointing at the same target endpoint.

1269
01:58:32,366 --> 01:58:40,260
它不需要部署多个独立的 DMS，而且表映射值得一提，因为它是迁移子集的方法。
It does not need several separate DMS deployments, and the table mappings deserve a mention because they are how you migrate a subset.

1270
01:58:41,038 --> 01:58:45,348
比如只选择某些模式、过滤行或在传输过程中重命名表。
Selecting only some schemas, filtering rows, or renaming a table on the way.

1271
01:58:45,966 --> 01:58:51,556
注意那些询问如何仅迁移特定表或如何在过程中重命名对象的题目。
Watch for a question asking how to migrate only certain tables or how to rename objects on the way.

1272
01:58:51,904 --> 01:58:56,612
答案是表映射，而不是后续的独立转换步骤。
The answer is table mappings, not a separate transformation step afterwards.

1273
01:58:58,158 --> 01:59:00,100
这个提示正是得分点所在。
The callout is where the marks are.

1274
01:59:00,512 --> 01:59:02,532
变更数据捕获不是某种“东西”。
Change data capture is not something.

1275
01:59:03,054 --> 01:59:05,828
DMS 可以从外部直接开启。
DMS can simply switch on from outside.

1276
01:59:06,990 --> 01:59:13,060
它读取源数据库自身的事务日志，而该日志必须产生正确的信息。
It reads the source database's own transaction log, and that log has to be producing the right information.

1277
01:59:14,032 --> 01:59:18,116
在 Oracle 上，这意味着归档日志模式和补充日志。
On Oracle, that means archive log mode and supplemental logging.

1278
01:59:19,086 --> 01:59:22,272
在 MySQL 上，意味着行格式下的二进制日志。
On MySQL, it means binary logging in row format.

1279
01:59:22,638 --> 01:59:33,860
在 SQL Server 上，意味着变更数据捕获或应用启用。因此，如果看到一个 DMS 任务完成了全量加载但完全没能捕捉到后续变化，要注意这种情况。
On SQL Server, it means change data capture or application enabled. So watch for a DMS task that completes the full load and then captures no ongoing changes at all.

1280
01:59:34,734 --> 01:59:37,860
这几乎总是源配置问题。
That is almost always a source configuration problem.

1281
01:59:38,912 --> 01:59:43,236
修复方案是在数据库端，而不是在 DMS 中。
The fix is on the database rather than in DMS.

1282
01:59:44,814 --> 01:59:48,996
这和课程中其他地方提到的无服务器论点是一样的。
This is the same serverless argument as everywhere else in the course.

1283
01:59:50,062 --> 01:59:56,676
DMS 无服务器自 2023 年起已进入通用可用阶段，所以它是合理的考试答案，而不是什么新奇玩意。
DMS serverless has been generally available since 2023, so it is a fair exam answer rather than a novelty.

1284
01:59:57,454 --> 02:00:01,828
它经常出现的原因是，当……时，准确估算复制实例的规模确实很难。
The reason it appears often is that sizing a replication instance is genuinely hard to do when.

1285
02:00:30,319 --> 02:00:33,316
工作负载是长期运行且负载已知的情况。
the workload is long running and its load is genuinely known.

1286
02:00:35,159 --> 02:00:40,619
第三点值得记住，因为它能实现一种意想不到的架构。
The third bullet is the one worth remembering because it enables an architecture people do not expect.

1287
02:00:41,899 --> 02:00:48,619
将 DMS 连接到 Kinesis 数据流，可以将任何支持的关系型数据库转换为变更事件流。
Pointing DMS at Kinesis data streams turns any supported relational database into a change event stream.

1288
02:00:49,518 --> 02:00:52,679
源端不需要任何应用更改，也不需要触发器。
There are no application changes and no triggers on the source.

1289
02:00:53,838 --> 02:00:58,919
每一次插入、更新和删除都会变成流中的一条记录，任何东西都可以消费它。
Every insert, update, and delete becomes a record on a stream that anything can consume.

1290
02:00:59,839 --> 02:01:06,179
对于在无法修改应用程序的情况下响应数据库变化的问题，这是一个非常强力的答案。
That is a genuinely powerful answer to questions about reacting to database changes when you cannot modify the application.

1291
02:01:07,579 --> 02:01:15,199
干扰项通常会提供数据库触发器或轮询，这两者都会给源端带来负载，因此会被判定为错误选项。
The distractors will usually offer database triggers or polling, both of which put load on the source and are marked wrong for that reason.

1292
02:01:16,750 --> 02:01:22,199
这个细节能区分出一个可行设计和一个后期会让大家措手不及的设计。
This is the detail that separates a working design from one that surprises people later.

1293
02:01:24,399 --> 02:01:32,679
当 DMS 将变更数据捕获输出写入 Amazon S3 时，它不会在原位更新行，因为 S3 对象是不可变的。
When DMS writes change data capture output to Amazon S3, it does not update rows in place because S3 objects are immutable.

1294
02:01:33,919 --> 02:01:40,299
它会追加描述变更内容的记录，每条记录都标明是插入、更新还是删除。
It appends records describing what changed, each tagged with whether it was an insert, an update or a delete.

1295
02:01:40,974 --> 02:01:46,532
查询这些原始输出时，你得到的是每一行历史版本，而不是当前状态。
Query that raw output and you get every historical version of every row rather than the current state.

1296
02:01:47,086 --> 02:01:52,676
必须有东西来应用这些变更，而这正是 OpenTable Format 解决的问题。
Something has to apply those changes, and this is exactly the problem OpenTable Format solve.

1297
02:01:53,152 --> 02:02:01,956
将 DMS 输出落地到 Apache Iceberg 或 Hoodie 可以让合并操作将变更日志合并到当前表中。
Landing DMS output into Apache Iseberg or Hoodie lets a merge operation collapse. The change log into a current table.

1298
02:02:03,552 --> 02:02:08,516
异构迁移的两步式特性是考试中的考点。
The two-step nature of a heterogeneous migration is the examinable point.

1299
02:02:09,006 --> 02:02:16,068
数据类型、存储过程、触发器和函数不会在不同引擎之间自动转换。
Data types, stored procedures, triggers and functions do not translate between engines automatically.

1300
02:02:16,654 --> 02:02:20,804
因此，在 DMS 移动任何一行之前，必须先对它们进行转换。
So something has to convert them before DMS moves a single row.

1301
02:02:21,550 --> 02:02:26,352
那个转换器以前是一个名为 AWS Schema Conversion Tool 的独立下载工具。
That converter used to be a separate download called the AWS Schema Conversion Tool.

1302
02:02:26,512 --> 02:02:31,268
现在它已集成到 DMS 控制台中，称为 DMS Schema Conversion。
It is now built into the DMS console as DMS Schema Conversion.

1303
02:02:32,334 --> 02:02:34,628
注意当前考试指南中的一个奇怪之处。
Note something odd in the current exam guide.

1304
02:02:35,310 --> 02:02:40,356
它在 2025 年 12 月从范围内服务的列表中删除了 AWS SCT。
It removed AWSS CT from the InScope service list in December 2025.

1305
02:02:41,294 --> 02:02:44,324
与此同时，一个任务陈述仍将其作为一个示例。
Meanwhile, a task statement still names it as an example.

1306
02:02:44,814 --> 02:02:49,700
当指南前后矛盾时，要掌握核心概念并准备好两种名称中的任何一种。
When the guide contradicts itself, learn the concept and expect either name.

1307
02:02:51,342 --> 02:02:56,992
这三个选项经常同时出现，区分它们可以拿到实实在在的分数。
These three appear together constantly, and separating them is worth real marks.

1308
02:02:58,702 --> 02:03:03,332
从 0 EDL 开始，因为当它适用时，它在降低开销方面具有绝对优势。
Start with 0 EDL because when it applies, it wins on overhead outright.

1309
02:03:03,950 --> 02:03:13,092
它需要支持的源和目标对，目前包括 Aurora、Amazon、RDS 和 DynamoDB 到 Redshift
It requires a supported source and target pair, currently Aurora, Amazon, RDS, and DynamoDB into Redshift

1310
02:03:13,390 --> 02:03:15,812
并且它在移动数据时不进行转换。
and it moves data without transforming it.

1311
02:03:16,750 --> 02:03:21,604
假设该对不被支持，或者目标是数据湖而非 Redshift。
Suppose the pair is not supported or the target is a data lake rather than Redshift.

1312
02:03:22,478 --> 02:03:26,148
那么带有变更数据捕获的 DMS 就是持续同步的选择。
Then DMS with change data capture is the continuous option.

1313
02:03:27,150 --> 02:03:35,620
而对于在传输过程中应用真实转换的计划提取，通过 JDBC 连接运行 Glue作业比两者都简单。
And for a scheduled extract with real transformation applied on the way, a blue job over a JDBC connection is simpler than either.

1314
02:03:35,904 --> 02:03:41,316
要避免的错误是仅仅因为源端是数据库就自动选择 DMS。
The mistake to avoid is reaching for DMS automatically because the source is a database.

1315
02:03:42,958 --> 02:03:46,596
第二个要点在实际项目和考试中经常误导考生。
The second bullet catches people in real projects and in exams.

1316
02:03:47,118 --> 02:03:53,508
DMS 处理大对象，即存储在列中的文档或图像等内容，有三种模式。
DMS handles large objects, things like documents or images stored in a column in one of three modes.

1317
02:03:54,446 --> 02:04:02,948
受限大对象模式速度很快，因为它为每个值分配固定数量的内存，任何超过该限制的内容都会被静默截断。
Limited LOB mode is fast because it allocates a fixed amount of memory per value, and anything larger than that limit is silently truncated.

1318
02:04:03,264 --> 02:04:07,300
全量大对象模式能正确移动所有内容，但速度明显较慢。
Full LOB mode moves everything correctly and is considerably slower.

1319
02:04:08,142 --> 02:04:13,796
内联大对象模式是一种折中方案，它在行内处理小值，将大值分开处理。
Inline LOB mode is the compromise, handling small values inline and large ones separately.

1320
02:04:14,064 --> 02:04:19,172
因此，要留意那些迁移成功但某些列的值被截断的情况。
So watch for a migration that completed successfully where some column values are cut short.

1321
02:04:19,664 --> 02:04:23,664
那是受限大对象模式，且设定的限制值太低了。
That is limited LOB mode with the limit set too low.

1322
02:04:25,006 --> 02:04:31,332
脱敏功能值得了解，因为它常作为其他脱敏选项的干扰项出现。
The masking capability is worth knowing because it appears as a distractor against other masking options.

1323
02:04:32,718 --> 02:04:38,980
DMS 可以在传输过程中转换列内容，确保敏感数据永远不会进入目标端。
DMS can transform column contents on the way through so sensitive values never land in the target at all.

1324
02:04:39,822 --> 02:04:47,396
这与在数据仓库中后期进行脱敏不同，也与第二模块涵盖的视图敏感数据检测不同。
That is different from masking in the warehouse afterwards and different again from view sensitive data detection, which module 2 covered.

1325
02:04:47,662 --> 02:04:50,276
注意这张幻灯片上的可用性警告。
And note the availability warning on this slide.

1326
02:05:05,904 --> 02:05:06,224
它
It

1327
02:05:06,254 --> 02:05:10,500
在旧教材中作为数据库发现问题的答案出现。
appears in older material as the answer to database discovery questions.

1328
02:05:12,206 --> 02:05:17,984
切换是迁移问题转变为运维问题的时刻，且一个指标起到了关键作用。
Cut over is where migration questions become operations questions and one metric does most of the work.

1329
02:05:18,304 --> 02:05:22,464
CDC 延迟衡量的是目标端落后了多少。
CD C latency measures how far behind the target is running.

1330
02:05:22,734 --> 02:05:26,852
在全量加载期间以及之后的一段时间内，该数值会很高。
While the full load is happening and for some time afterwards it will be high.

1331
02:05:27,310 --> 02:05:33,124
随着目标端追上进度，它会降向零。延迟接近于零意味着目标端实际上是实时的。
As the target catches up, it falls towards zero. And a latency near zero means the target is effectively current.

1332
02:05:33,504 --> 02:05:36,004
那是停止源端写入的时机。
That is the moment to stop writes at the source.

1333
02:05:36,398 --> 02:05:40,484
让最后几项更改流过，然后重新指向应用程序。
Let the last few changes drain through and repoint the applications.

1334
02:05:41,422 --> 02:05:47,396
询问如何判断迁移何时可以切换的问题，就是在问这个指标。
A question asking how to know when a migration is ready to cut over is asking about that metric.

1335
02:05:47,664 --> 02:05:52,388
干扰项会提供行数，而这些行数在数据仍是陈旧时也可能匹配。
The distractors will offer row counts which can match while data is still stale.

1336
02:05:53,710 --> 02:05:59,812
一家零售商在 Amazon EC2 上运行自管理的 Oracle 数据库，支持其订单系统。
A retailer runs a self-managed Oracle database on Amazon EC2, supporting its order system.

1337
02:06:00,302 --> 02:06:07,300
分析团队希望在 Amazon Redshift 中获取订单数据用于报告，并要求在几分钟内更新。
The analytics team wants order data available in Amazon Redshift for reporting refreshed within a few minutes.

1338
02:06:07,822 --> 02:06:12,900
应用团队拒绝对 Oracle 数据库或其应用程序代码进行任何更改。
The application team has refused any changes to the Oracle database or its application code.

1339
02:06:13,806 --> 02:06:21,380
一名数据工程师配置了一个 AWS DMS 任务，迁移类型设置为全量加载加 CDC。
A data engineer configures an AWS DMS task with the migration type set to full load plus CDC.

1340
02:06:21,664 --> 02:06:25,984
全量加载成功完成，所有现有行都出现在 Redshift 中。
The full load completes successfully and all existing rows appear in Redshift.

1341
02:06:26,304 --> 02:06:31,780
后续没有任何更改到达，且任务仍处于运行状态，未报告错误。
No subsequent changes ever arrive and the task remains in a running state without reporting an error.

1342
02:06:32,622 --> 02:06:34,244
最可能的原因是什么？
What is the most likely cause?

1343
02:06:34,830 --> 02:06:39,876
a. 复制实例规模不足，无法跟上变更量。
a The replication instance is undersized and cannot keep up with the change volume.

1344
02:06:40,384 --> 02:06:45,316
b. 源 Oracle 数据库未启用补充日志。
b supplemental logging is not enabled on the source Oracle database.

1345
02:06:45,934 --> 02:06:46,144
C。
C.

1346
02:06:46,624 --> 02:06:51,652
目标 Redshift 集群需要清单文件来进行增量加载。
The target redshift cluster requires a manifest file for incremental loads.

1347
02:06:53,264 --> 02:06:59,264
任务本应只使用 CDC，而不是全量加载加 CDC。
The task should have used CDC only rather than full load plus cdc.

1348
02:07:01,024 --> 02:07:02,116
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1349
02:07:09,134 --> 02:07:10,384
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1350
02:07:10,624 --> 02:07:16,964
有三个细节共同指向它。全量加载成功了，所以连接、权限和目标端都没问题。
Three details point at it together. The full load worked. So connectivity, permissions, and the target are all fine.

1351
02:07:17,184 --> 02:07:23,972
没有报告错误，这排除了大部分故障模式，因为 DMS 在出问题时通常会报错很多。
No error is reported, which rules out most failure modes because DMS is quite noisy when something breaks.

1352
02:07:24,718 --> 02:07:31,620
而且数据完全没到达，而不是传输缓慢，这与容量问题不同。
And nothing arrives at all rather than arriving slowly, which distinguishes it from a capacity problem.

1353
02:07:32,590 --> 02:07:36,740
注意关于拒绝数据库变更的约束条件。
Notice the constraint about no changes to the database being refused.

1354
02:07:37,424 --> 02:07:43,584
这是为了让你犹豫，因为启用补充日志属于数据库变更。
That is there to make you hesitate because enabling supplemental logging is a database change.

1355
02:07:44,142 --> 02:07:53,956
它属于配置更改，而不是模式或应用更改，而且它是唯一能满足要求的选项。
It is a configuration change rather than a schema or application change, and it is the only thing that makes the requirement achievable.

1356
02:07:55,214 --> 02:08:00,868
文件传输问题可以从两个维度来划分，这两个维度通常在题干中表述得很清楚。
File movement questions split on two axes, and both are usually stated plainly in the question text.

1357
02:08:01,742 --> 02:08:05,860
第一个是发起方向，前面的表格已经介绍过了。
The first is the direction of initiation, which the earlier table introduced.

1358
02:08:06,350 --> 02:08:09,860
是你去获取数据，还是由其他人把数据发给你？
Do you go and fetch the data or do other people send it to you?

1359
02:08:10,944 --> 02:08:14,500
第二个是网络带宽是否足以支撑数据量。
The second is whether the network is adequate for the volume.

1360
02:08:14,704 --> 02:08:18,628
题目可能会同时给出数据量和连接速度。
A question may hand you a data volume and a connection speed together.

1361
02:08:19,024 --> 02:08:22,820
它想让你注意到在给定的时间内，计算结果并不成立。
It wants you to notice the arithmetic does not work in the time available.

1362
02:08:23,694 --> 02:08:27,268
从历史上看，这指向的是通过物理设备运输。
Historically, that pointed at physically shipping a device.

1363
02:08:28,064 --> 02:08:34,624
接下来的几页幻灯片将讲解为什么这个答案在现实中已经消失，但仍保留在考试中。
The next few slides cover why that answer is now disappearing from reality while remaining in the exam.

1364
02:08:34,864 --> 02:08:39,844
这两个维度可以解决你遇到的几乎所有文件传输问题。
Between them, these two axes resolve almost every file transfer question you will meet.

1365
02:08:41,358 --> 02:08:47,236
DataSync 是专门为传输设计的服务，考试通常将其与编写脚本进行对比。
DataSync is a purpose-built transfer service and the exam usually contrasts it with writing a script.

1366
02:08:47,504 --> 02:08:56,164
第四个要点是题目判定的关键。使用 CLI 复制文件会移动字节但会丢失文件系统的元数据。
The fourth bullet is the differentiator that questions turn on. Copying files with the CLI moves the bytes and loses the file system metadata.

1367
02:08:57,104 --> 02:09:02,820
这意味着 Windows 或 Unix 文件共享所携带的权限、所有权和时间戳。
That means the permissions, ownership, and timestamps a Windows or Unix file share carries.

1368
02:09:03,264 --> 02:09:05,028
DataSync 可以保留这些信息。
DataSync preserves them.

1369
02:09:05,904 --> 02:09:13,348
因此，关于迁移必须保留权限的文件共享问题，可以直接排除脚本复制。
So a question about migrating a file share where permissions must be retained rules out a scripted copy immediately.

1370
02:09:13,984 --> 02:09:17,188
提示框中的增量行为也很重要。
The incremental behavior in the callout matters too.

1371
02:09:18,094 --> 02:09:24,452
在第一次运行后，计划的 DataSync 任务会对比源和目标，仅移动差异部分。
After the first run, a scheduled data sync task compares source and destination and moves only differences.

1372
02:09:25,294 --> 02:09:29,636
这使得它成为一种持续同步的可行方案，而不仅仅是一次性的迁移。
That makes it viable as an ongoing sync rather than only a one-off migration.

1373
02:09:31,278 --> 02:09:35,012
传输系列是为了处理特定且非常常见的场景而存在的。
Transfer family exists for a specific and very common situation.

1374
02:09:35,264 --> 02:09:42,544
你有合作伙伴、供应商或客户给你发送文件。他们已经通过 SFTP 操作了 15 年。
You have partners, suppliers, or customers who send you files. They have been doing it over SFTP for 15 years.

1375
02:09:42,784 --> 02:09:46,532
没人会去重写他们的系统来调用 AWS API。
Nobody is going to rewrite their systems to call an AWS API.

1376
02:09:47,214 --> 02:09:54,084
从历史上看，这意味着在实例上运行一个 SFTP 服务器，并对其进行补丁、监控和备份。
Historically, that meant running an SFTP server on an instance, patching it, monitoring it, and backing it up.

1377
02:09:54,766 --> 02:09:58,468
传输系列去掉了服务器，但保留了协议。
Transfer Family removes the server while keeping the protocol.

1378
02:09:59,374 --> 02:10:06,944
文件通过 SFTP 到达并直接进入 S3 bucket，然后事件通知可以立即启动流水线。
Files arrive over SFTP and land directly in an S3 bucket where an event notification can start a pipeline immediately.

1379
02:10:07,264 --> 02:10:12,676
当题目提到合作伙伴上传以及需要维护的 SFTP 服务器时，这就是正确答案。
When a question mentions partners uploading and an SFTP server to maintain, this is the answer.

1380
02:10:14,224 --> 02:10:21,028
这是本模块中最快的判别题之一，因为措辞本身就暴露了答案，而不是隐藏它。
This is one of the fastest tiebreakers in the module because the wording gives it away rather than hiding it.

1381
02:10:21,584 --> 02:10:30,020
像合作伙伴、供应商、厂商、客户或第三方这样的词，都意味着在你的控制范围之外的人正在发起传输。
Words like partner, supplier, vendor, customer, or third party all mean somebody outside your control is initiating the transfer.

1382
02:10:30,734 --> 02:10:32,676
这就是传输系列。
That is transfer family.

1383
02:10:33,582 --> 02:10:42,436
而文件服务器、本地存储或数据中心等词语则意味着是你自己在发起。那是 DataSync。
Words like a file servers or on premises storage or a data center mean you are initiating. That is data sync.

1384
02:10:44,942 --> 02:10:51,812
唯一的模糊地带是合作伙伴可以接受任何一种方案，但即便如此，协议通常也能解决问题。
The only genuine ambiguity is a partner who would accept either arrangement, and even then the protocol usually settles it.

1385
02:10:52,624 --> 02:11:01,124
如果题目中任何地方提到了 SFTP，答案就是传输系列，因为 DataSync 完全不支持 SFTP。
If the question mentions SFPP anywhere, the answer is transfer family because datasync does not speak SFTP at all.

1386
02:11:01,824 --> 02:11:10,372
如果题目提到保留文件权限，那就是 DataSync，因为传输系列是交付到对象存储中。
And if the question mentions preserving file permissions, that is data sync, because transfer family is delivering into object storage.

1387
02:11:12,078 --> 02:11:19,876
这是本课程中最大的可用性警示，需要特别注意，因为考试内容和现实情况现在不一致了。
This is the largest availability warning in the course and it needs care because the exam and reality now disagree.

1388
02:11:20,622 --> 02:11:26,084
十年来，PB级数据加上慢速网络一直是 Snowball 的考题点。
For a decade, petabytes of data plus a slow network has been a snowball question.

1389
02:11:26,702 --> 02:11:31,424
这在目前的考试材料和每一个题库中依然是这样出现的。
That is still how it appears in exam material and in every question bank.

1390
02:11:31,982 --> 02:11:41,344
与此同时，AWS 将在 2025 年 11 月向新客户推销 Snowball，并将在 2026 年底完全停止支持。
Meanwhile, AWS plows snowball to new customers in November 2025 and will end support entirely at the end of 2026.

1391
02:11:41,614 --> 02:11:43,236
所以这里的指导非常明确。
So the guidance is explicit.

1392
02:11:43,584 --> 02:11:50,628
如果题目描述的是带宽不足的超大规模离线传输，Snowball 仍然是预设的答案。
If a question describes an enormous offline transfer with inadequate bandwidth, Snowball is still the intended answer.

1393
02:11:52,718 --> 02:11:53,444
选它。
Choose it.

1394
02:11:54,414 --> 02:12:04,004
然后你要知道，实际项目会使用带测试链接的 DataSync、用于实物交付的数据传输终端或者用于边缘计算的 Outposts。
Then know that a real project would use datasync over a beta link, the data transfer terminal for physical delivery or outposts for edge compute.

1395
02:12:05,518 --> 02:12:07,396
存储网关是另一种选择。
Storage gateway is the option.

1396
02:12:07,758 --> 02:12:11,460
考生往往会忘记，而它与 DataSync 的区别非常明确。
Candidates forget and the distinction from datasync is clean.

1397
02:12:12,686 --> 02:12:15,876
DataSync 是将数据从 A 点移动到 B 点，任务完成后就结束了。
Data sync moves data from A to B and the job ends.

1398
02:12:16,864 --> 02:12:18,564
文件网关是持久性的。
File gateway is permanent.

1399
02:12:19,278 --> 02:12:28,224
它提供一个文件共享，让本地应用程序像以前一样挂载并使用，而实际的字节数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。
It presents a file share that on premises applications mount and use exactly as before while the actual bytes live in Amazon S3.

1400
02:12:28,590 --> 02:12:32,464
没有任何东西被迁移，因为文件接口永远不会消失。
Nothing is migrated because the file interface never goes away.

1401
02:12:32,974 --> 02:12:38,724
所以，如果题目描述的是一个无法修改且必须继续读写文件的遗留应用。
So a question describing a legacy application that cannot be modified, which must keep reading and writing files.

1402
02:12:39,024 --> 02:12:44,068
同时，组织希望将数据存入 S3 进行分析，这就是文件网关问题。
Meanwhile, the organization wants the data in S3 for analytics is a file gateway question.

1403
02:12:44,782 --> 02:12:48,068
关于废弃文件服务器的问题则是 DataSync 问题。
A question about decommissioning a file server is a data sync question.

1404
02:12:49,774 --> 02:13:00,624
一家制造商每天从 30 家外部供应商处接收生产文件。每个供应商系统都将文件上传到运行在 Amazon EC2 实例上的公司管理的 SFTP 服务器。
A manufacturer receives daily production files from 30 external suppliers. Each supplier system uploads to a company-managed SFTP server running on an Amazon EC2 instance.

1405
02:13:00,784 --> 02:13:06,116
然后一个定时任务将这些文件复制到 Amazon S3，由 Glue作业进行处理。
A cron job then copies the files into Amazon S3 where a blue job processes them.

1406
02:13:06,862 --> 02:13:12,900
运维团队负责修补和监控 EC2 实例，并且已经因为磁盘满导致过两次停机。
The operations team patches and monitors the EC2 instance and has had two outages from full disks.

1407
02:13:13,264 --> 02:13:15,652
供应商无法更改他们发送文件的方式。
Suppliers cannot change how they send files.

1408
02:13:16,078 --> 02:13:21,476
公司希望移除该服务器，同时确保在文件落地后立即开始处理。
The company wants to remove the server while keeping processing starting as soon as a file lands.

1409
02:13:21,904 --> 02:13:23,844
公司应该采用什么方案？
What should the company implement?

1410
02:13:27,344 --> 02:13:35,504
用 AWS 替换 EC2 实例。使用传输系列将 SFTP 直接写入 Amazon S3。
Replace the EC2 instance with AWS. Transfer family for SFTP writing directly to Amazon S3.

1411
02:13:35,904 --> 02:13:36,144
B选项。
b.

1412
02:13:36,494 --> 02:13:42,852
在每个供应商现场部署 AWS DataSync 代理程序，将文件拉取到 Amazon S3。
Deploy AWS datasync agents at each supplier site to pull the files into Amazon S3.

1413
02:13:43,344 --> 02:13:43,664
C选项。
C.

1414
02:13:44,142 --> 02:13:50,564
将 SFTP 服务器迁移到自动扩展组中更大容量的 EC2 实例上。
Move the SFTP server to a larger EC2 instance in an auto-scaling group with a bigger volume.

1415
02:13:51,264 --> 02:13:51,504
D选项。
D.

1416
02:13:52,462 --> 02:13:58,116
要求供应商使用预签名 URL 直接上传到 Amazon S3。
Ask suppliers to upload directly to Amazon S3 using presigned URLs.

1417
02:13:58,574 --> 02:13:59,588
停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1418
02:14:06,299 --> 02:14:10,179
答案是 A，而且其中一句话就排除了一半的选项。
The answer is A, and one sentence eliminated half the options.

1419
02:14:10,766 --> 02:14:16,516
“供应商无法更改他们发送文件的方式”意味着 SFTP 协议是固定的。
Suppliers cannot change how they send files means the SFTP protocol is fixed.

1420
02:14:17,070 --> 02:14:19,812
这直接就把 D 排除掉，并让 B 变得不合理。
That kills D outright and makes B absurd.

1421
02:14:20,302 --> 02:14:24,784
因为在另外 30 家公司内部安装代理程序仍然属于较大的变动。
Since installing agents inside 30 other companies is a bigger change still.

1422
02:14:25,326 --> 02:14:29,380
注意 A 的第二个优点，虽然题目没直接问到这一点。
Notice the second benefit of A that the question does not ask about directly.

1423
02:14:29,664 --> 02:14:35,812
因为传输系列可以写入 S3，所以用于复制文件的定时任务也就消失了。
Because transfer family writes into S3, the cron job that copied files across disappears as well.

1424
02:14:36,366 --> 02:14:39,504
S3 事件通知可以触发 Glue作业。
An S3 event notification can start the blue job.

1425
02:14:39,694 --> 02:14:46,756
文件到达的一瞬间，仅需一次更改就能移除服务器、定时脚本和延迟。
The moment a file arrives, one change removes a server, a scheduled script, and a delay.

1426
02:14:48,046 --> 02:14:50,468
这个强调点就是选择 AppFlow 的全部理由。
The callout is the whole argument for AppFlow.

1427
02:14:50,784 --> 02:15:00,356
手动从 SaaS 应用程序拉取数据意味着要处理身份验证令牌、刷新它们、分页处理结果，并遵守供应商的速率限制，
Pulling data from a SaaS application by hand means handling authentication tokens and refreshing them, paginating two results, respecting the vendor's rate limits,

1428
02:15:00,624 --> 02:15:03,972
而且当供应商更改 API 时还要重写所有内容。
rewriting all of it when the vendor changes their API.

1429
02:15:05,006 --> 02:15:06,820
那是持续不断的繁琐工作。
That is real ongoing work.

1430
02:15:07,630 --> 02:15:09,664
而 AppFlow 是通过配置来完成这些的。
App Flow does it as configuration.

1431
02:15:09,824 --> 02:15:17,700
所以当题目描述需要将 Salesforce 或 ServiceNow 数据放入数据湖时，答案就是 AppFlow。
So when a question describes needing Salesforce or ServiceNow data in a data lake, the answer is AppFlow.

1432
02:15:18,478 --> 02:15:23,024
干扰项会提供一个按计划调用 API 的 Lambda 函数。
The distractors will offer a lambda function calling the API on a schedule.

1433
02:15:24,064 --> 02:15:29,476
那个干扰项虽然可行，但需要更多的开发工作和更高的运维开销，
That distractor works and it is more development effort and more operational overhead,

1434
02:15:30,126 --> 02:15:33,124
而这正是题目中的限定词所衡量的标准。
which is exactly what the qualifier in the question is measuring.

1435
02:15:34,830 --> 02:15:41,828
数据交换是 2025 年 12 月修订版中加入考试的服务之一，所以旧的资料不涵盖它。
Data exchange is one of the services added to the exam in the December 2025 revision, so older material does not cover it.

1436
02:15:42,350 --> 02:15:43,620
这个概念很简单。
The concept is simple.

1437
02:15:44,782 --> 02:15:51,108
与数据供应商谈判意味着要安排文件传输并建立一个收集他们每月更新的流程。
Negotiating with a data vendor means arranging file transfers and building a process to collect their monthly updates.

1438
02:15:51,904 --> 02:15:56,900
相反，你通过市场平台订阅，数据就会进入你的账户。
Instead, you subscribe through the marketplace and the data arrives in your account.

1439
02:15:57,710 --> 02:16:00,100
新的修订内容可以自动流转过来。
New revisions can flow through automatically.

1440
02:16:00,590 --> 02:16:07,908
所以当题目描述在自己的数据基础上需要第三方市场数据、天气数据或人口统计数据时。
So a question describing needing third-party market data, weather data or demographic data alongside your own.

1441
02:16:08,846 --> 02:16:12,452
现在要求「运维开销最低」时，答案就很明显了。
Asking for the least operational overhead now has an obvious answer.

1442
02:16:13,230 --> 02:16:19,396
在这次修订之前，预期的答案可能是传输系列端点或手动处理过程。
Before this revision, the expected answer would have been a transfer family endpoint or a manual process.

1443
02:16:20,974 --> 02:16:26,500
有时没有托管连接器，你确实得自己调用 API。
Sometimes no managed connector exists and you genuinely do have to call the API yourself.

1444
02:16:26,990 --> 02:16:32,772
第二点是值得内化的，因为这是考试区分两个可行答案的地方。
The second bullet is the one worth internalizing because it is where the exam separates two working answers.

1445
02:16:33,183 --> 02:16:37,986
当拉取数据涉及翻页大量结果，或者需要应对供应商限流时。
When a pull involves paging through many results, coping with a vendor that thorts you.

1446
02:16:38,924 --> 02:16:44,356
在不丢失当前位置的情况下重试失败操作，单个 Lambda 函数就会变得脆弱。
Retrying failures without losing your place, a single lambda function becomes fragile.

1447
02:16:45,022 --> 02:16:50,788
而且它也会变得很难调试，因为所有逻辑都隐藏在一个调用中。
It also becomes very hard to debug because all that logic hides inside one invocation.

1448
02:16:52,013 --> 02:16:59,940
Step Functions 处理循环、等待和重试策略，作为一个你可以监控运行的显式状态机。
Step functions handles the looping, the waiting, and the retry policy as an explicit state machine you can watch running.

1449
02:17:00,878 --> 02:17:09,124
这就是为什么在那些简单 Lambda 会在中途超时或静默丢失记录的问题中，它被视为正确答案。
That is why it appears as the correct answer in questions where a naive lambda would time out partway through or silently lose records.

1450
02:17:09,966 --> 02:17:12,964
模块 6 正确地涵盖了 Step Functions。
Module 6 covers step functions properly.

1451
02:17:14,544 --> 02:17:18,624
一家媒体公司将客户记录存储在 Salesforce 中。
A media company stores customer records in Salesforce.

1452
02:17:18,784 --> 02:17:28,740
分析团队希望这些记录每天进入 Amazon S3，且在入库前对邮件地址进行脱敏，并完全排除一个区域的记录。
The analytics team wants those records in Amazon S3 daily with email addresses masked before they land and with records for one region excluded entirely.

1453
02:17:31,022 --> 02:17:36,484
一名数据工程师提议使用基于 EventBridge 计划的 AWS Lambda 函数。
A data engineer has proposed an AWS Lambda function on an event bridge schedule.

1454
02:17:37,165 --> 02:17:45,188
它验证 Salesforce API 的身份，翻页获取结果，执行过滤和脱敏，然后写入 S3。
It authenticates to the Salesforce API, pages through results, applies the filtering and masking, then writes to S3.

1455
02:17:47,918 --> 02:17:51,343
团队在持续维护方面的能力有限。
The team has limited capacity for ongoing maintenance.

1456
02:17:52,654 --> 02:17:54,980
数据工程师应该改用什么方法？
What should the data engineer do instead?

1457
02:17:57,388 --> 02:18:03,843
A. 按提议构建 Lambda 函数，将 Salesforce 凭证存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。
Build the Lambda function as proposed, storing the Salesforce credentials in AWS Secrets Manager.

1458
02:18:05,486 --> 02:18:05,769
B。
B.

1459
02:18:06,704 --> 02:18:13,058
使用带有计划流的 Amazon App Flow，在流配置中应用过滤和脱敏。
Use Amazon App Flow with a scheduled flow, applying the filter and mask in the flow configuration.

1460
02:18:14,304 --> 02:18:22,020
C 使用 AWS DMS，以 Salesforce 为源端点，Amazon S3 为目标端点。
C Use AWS DMS with Salesforce as a source endpoint and Amazon S3 as the target.

1461
02:18:25,343 --> 02:18:29,700
通过 AWS Data Exchange 订阅 Salesforce 数据集。
subscribe to the Salesforce dataset through AWS Data Exchange.

1462
02:18:29,998 --> 02:18:31,012
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1463
02:18:37,454 --> 02:18:40,544
答案是 B。注意这道题是怎么构建的。
The answer is B. Notice how the question was built.

1464
02:18:40,864 --> 02:18:46,404
两个额外的要求，即字段脱敏和排除区域，并不是无关的细节。
The two extra requirements, masking a field and excluding a region, are not incidental color.

1465
02:18:46,798 --> 02:18:55,138
它们都是故意列出的 App Flow 原生功能，目的是让那个无需代码即可完成这些操作的服务成为最强答案。
They are both native app flow capabilities listed deliberately so that the service which does them without code becomes the strongest answer.

1466
02:18:55,629 --> 02:19:03,183
选项 A 值得尊重，因为它并不错，而且关于 机密管理器 的细节确实是良好的实践。
Option A is worth respecting because it is not wrong and the detail about secrets manager is genuinely good practice.

1467
02:19:03,424 --> 02:19:07,299
但它在「维护能力有限」这一约束条件下输掉了。
It loses on the stated constraint of limited maintenance capacity.

1468
02:19:08,142 --> 02:19:16,900
选项 C 和 B 是类别错误，只要你掌握了每个服务的核心定义，就能立刻排除掉这些选项。
Options C and B are category errors, and they are the kind you can eliminate instantly once you hold the one sentence definition of each service.

1469
02:19:18,544 --> 02:19:21,602
其中大部分内容属于解决方案架构师的范畴。
Most of this is solutions architect territory.

1470
02:19:21,838 --> 02:19:26,596
考试大纲将创建 IP 地址白名单列为一项技能。
The exam guide names creating allow lists for IP addresses as a skill.

1471
02:19:26,784 --> 02:19:28,708
所以这里有一点很重要。
So a little of it matters here.

1472
02:19:31,566 --> 02:19:34,531
要仔细阅读 直接连接 这一行。
The direct connect row is the one to read carefully.

1473
02:19:35,374 --> 02:19:43,652
每当题目提到大量数据时，考生就会想到 直接连接，而真正的区别在于一致性而非原始速度。
Candidates reach for direct connect whenever a question mentions large volumes, and the real differentiator is consistency rather than raw speed.

1474
02:19:44,430 --> 02:19:51,908
通过公共互联网的 虚拟专用网络 可能很快，但其延迟会随着当天互联网上的其他情况而变化。
A VPN over the public internet can be fast and its latency varies with whatever else is happening on the internet that day.

1475
02:19:52,622 --> 02:19:56,708
直接连接 是具有可预测性能的专用线路。
Direct Connect is a dedicated circuit with predictable performance.

1476
02:19:56,912 --> 02:20:05,988
因此，强调一致或可预测吞吐量的题目指向 直接连接，而仅提到安全性的题目则指向 虚拟专用网络。
So a question emphasizing consistent or predictable throughput points at Direct Connect and one merely mentioning security points at a VPN.

1477
02:20:07,726 --> 02:20:10,404
这是一个包含一个好记故障模式的小知识点。
This is a small topic with a memorable failure mode.

1478
02:20:10,766 --> 02:20:17,604
考虑在 VPC 内部的 Lambda 函数或视图作业调用外部 API 的情况。
Consider a Lambda function or a view job calling an external API from inside a VPC.

1479
02:20:18,254 --> 02:20:22,276
流量将通过子网路由表定义的路径流出。
Traffic leaves by whatever path the subnet's root table defines.

1480
02:20:23,086 --> 02:20:34,372
如果没有带固定弹性 IP 的 NAT gateway，合作伙伴看到的源地址可能会变化。执行 IP 白名单的合作伙伴会拒绝某些调用并接受其他调用。
Without a NAT gateway carrying a fixed elastic IP, the source address the partner sees can change. A partner enforcing an IP allow list will reject some calls and accept others.

1481
02:20:34,592 --> 02:20:36,164
这种故障现象让人抓狂。
The symptom is maddening.

1482
02:20:36,352 --> 02:20:41,476
它大部分时间都能正常工作，但在代码中没有任何规律的情况下不可预测地失败。
It works most of the time and fails unpredictably with no pattern in the code.

1483
02:20:41,952 --> 02:20:49,188
解决方法是将出站流量路由到 NAT gateway，这样每次调用都会显示相同的地址。
The fix is to route outbound traffic through a NAT gateway so that every call presents the same address.

1484
02:20:50,638 --> 02:21:00,644
一家物流公司必须将 400 TB 的历史存档文件从本地的 SMB 文件共享迁移到 Amazon S3。
A logistics company must migrate 400 terabytes of historical archive files from an on-premises SMB file share into Amazon S3.

1485
02:21:01,390 --> 02:21:09,732
连接到 Amazon S3 的是 1 GB 每秒的链路，且在工作时间内已承载生产流量。
The connection to Amazon S3 there is a 1 GB per second link that is already carrying production traffic during business hours.

1486
02:21:10,606 --> 02:21:14,352
文件必须保留原始权限和时间戳。
The files must retain their original permissions and timestamps.

1487
02:21:14,512 --> 02:21:20,932
迁移后，必须持续进行每天约 200 GB 新文件的夜间传输。
After the migration, a nightly transfer of roughly 200 GB of new files must continue indefinitely.

1488
02:21:22,062 --> 02:21:24,516
哪种方法最符合要求？
Which approach best meets the requirements?

1489
02:21:25,614 --> 02:21:33,892
a 使用 AWS Datasync 处理批量迁移和持续的夜间传输，并安排在非工作时间进行。
Use AWS datasync for both the bulk migration and the ongoing nightly transfer, scheduling it outside business hours.

1490
02:21:34,672 --> 02:21:41,668
b 使用 AWS CLI 通过多部分上传和并行同步脚本复制文件。
b Copy the files with the AWS CLI using multi-part upload and a parallel sync script.

1491
02:21:42,574 --> 02:21:42,832
C。
C.

1492
02:21:43,630 --> 02:21:49,412
部署 AWS 存储网关 文件网关，让缓存随时间推移填充。
Deploy AWS storage gateway file gateway and let the cache populate over time.

1493
02:21:50,222 --> 02:21:50,512
D
D

1494
02:21:51,726 --> 02:21:58,436
使用带有 SFTP 端点的 AWS Transfer Family 并编写上传脚本。
Use AWS transfer family with an SFTP endpoint and script the uploads.

1495
02:22:00,462 --> 02:22:01,712
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1496
02:22:08,110 --> 02:22:10,752
答案是 A，且有两个要求非常严格。
The answer is A and two requirements for strict.

1497
02:22:11,246 --> 02:22:19,396
保留权限和时间戳排除了任何简单的复制，这就是为什么选项 B 虽然是工程师直觉上的答案但却失败了。
Retaining permissions and timestamps eliminates any plain copy, which is why option B fails despite being the intuitive engineer's answer.

1498
02:22:20,302 --> 02:22:30,084
而且持续的夜间传输意味着解决方案在迁移后必须继续工作，而 Datasync 通过增量传输和调度可以实现这一点。
And the ongoing nightly transfer means the solution must keep working after the migration, which datasync does through incremental transfers and scheduling.

1499
02:22:30,592 --> 02:22:32,900
注意题目没有要求什么。
Note what the question did not ask.

1500
02:22:33,582 --> 02:22:40,260
通过共享的 1GB 链路传输 400TB 很慢，而且提供的选项中没有 Snowball。
400TB over a shared 1GB link is slow and there is no snowball option offered.

1501
02:22:41,134 --> 02:22:50,660
考虑到之前提到的退役时间线，预计该选项出现的频率会降低，且需仔细阅读题目是否真的需要它。
Given the retirement timeline covered earlier, expect that option to appear less often over time and read carefully for whether a question actually needs it.

1502
02:22:51,918 --> 02:22:56,388
这一页值得停下来看一下，你可以用手遮住右侧那一列。
Worth pausing on this slide and covering the right-hand column with your hand.

1503
02:22:56,910 --> 02:23:05,476
如果你能根据服务名称推导出每一句描述，更重要的是，能从每句描述中推断出对应的服务名称，那么这个模块的任务就完成了。
If you can produce each sentence from the service name and more importantly, produce the service name from each sentence, this module has done its job.

1504
02:23:06,254 --> 02:23:10,020
最容易混淆的两行是数据同步和传输系列。
The two rows that get confused are data sync and transfer family.

1505
02:23:11,022 --> 02:23:14,468
发起方向每次都能把它们区分开来。
The direction of initiation separates them every single time.

1506
02:23:14,672 --> 02:23:18,500
所以，你应该先问这个问题，而不是去比较功能。
So make that your first question rather than comparing features.

1507
02:23:19,182 --> 02:23:26,052
另外两行容易被忽略的是存储网关，因为候选人往往会忘记持续的混合访问也是一种选项。
The two rows that get overlooked are storage gateway because candidates forget that ongoing hybrid access is an option at all.

1508
02:23:27,022 --> 02:23:31,204
还有数据交换，因为它是在考试大纲中新增的内容。
Data exchange because it is new to the exam guide.

1509
02:23:32,142 --> 02:23:40,836
最后一项是考试内容与商业现实的分歧点，这部分在可用性警告中已经详细说明了。
And the last row is where the exam and commercial reality now part company, which the availability warning covered in detail.

1510
02:23:42,542 --> 02:23:47,552
又是五个问题，而第五个问题在这个模块中的重要性超过大多数题目。
Five questions again, and the fifth earns its place in this module more than most.

1511
02:23:48,192 --> 02:23:51,072
迁移场景中充满了明确的拒绝条件。
Migration scenarios are full of stated refusals.

1512
02:23:51,312 --> 02:23:53,220
供应商无法更改他们的系统。
Suppliers cannot change their systems.

1513
02:23:53,632 --> 02:23:56,324
应用团队不会修改数据库。
The application team will not modify the database.

1514
02:23:57,326 --> 02:24:00,100
团队没有能力去维护自定义代码。
The team has no capacity to maintain custom code.

1515
02:24:00,910 --> 02:24:08,356
每一个这样的条件都是为了排除特定选项，识别出这些条件能把四选一的对比简化为二选一。
Each of those is placed to eliminate a specific option, and spotting them turns a 4-way comparison into a 2-way one.

1516
02:24:09,678 --> 02:24:20,132
下一个模块从数据摄入转向数据转换，比较 Glue、EMR、Lambda 和 Redshift 作为处理引擎。
Next module moves from getting data in to transforming it, comparing Blue, EMR, Lambda, and Redshift as processing engines.

1517
02:24:21,070 --> 02:24:28,036
涵盖大语言模型作为数据处理工具在考试大纲中的出现情况。
Covering how large language models now appear in the exam guide as a data processing tool.

1518
02:24:29,582 --> 02:24:35,780
这个模块涵盖了考试大纲中多达 11 项不同的技能，比课程中任何其他模块都要多。
This module covers 11 separate skills from the exam guide, more than any other in the course.

1519
02:24:36,974 --> 02:24:40,644
这是因为转换环节是服务重叠最多的地方。
That is because transformation is where the most services overlap.

1520
02:24:41,582 --> 02:24:51,744
有六种引擎可以处理你的数据，其中许多都能处理任何给定的数据集，而考试的干扰项几乎完全建立在这些重叠点上。
Six engines can process your data, several of them can process any given dataset, and the exam builds its distractors almost entirely out of that overlap.

1521
02:24:52,064 --> 02:24:55,204
正在测试的技能是“选择”，而不是单纯的“知识”。
The skill being tested is selection rather than knowledge.

1522
02:24:56,142 --> 02:25:04,228
因此，这个模块包含八个实战案例，而非通常的四个，而且其中大多数是关于如何选择，而不是关于某项技术如何运作。
So this module carries eight worked scenarios instead of the usual four, and most of them are about choosing rather than about how something works.

1523
02:25:04,544 --> 02:25:07,588
它还涵盖了作为处理工具的大语言模型。
It also covers large language models as a processing tool.

1524
02:25:08,366 --> 02:25:13,668
这在 2025 年 12 月才加入考试大纲，在更早的资料中并不出现。
That arrived in the exam guide in December 2025 and appears in no older material.

1525
02:25:15,374 --> 02:25:18,244
有一种习惯在任何其他事情之前都需要纠正。
There is a habit worth breaking before anything else.

1526
02:25:18,894 --> 02:25:23,748
候选人通常学习服务，然后试图将场景匹配到他们熟悉的某个服务上。
Candidates learn services and then try to match a scenario to a service they know.

1527
02:25:24,384 --> 02:25:26,628
更可靠的方法是反过来操作。
The reliable direction is the opposite.

1528
02:25:27,118 --> 02:25:29,284
先用通俗易懂的语言描述工作内容。
Describe the work in plain terms first.

1529
02:25:29,904 --> 02:25:34,144
这是一个小文件，还是跨越数 TB 的分布式连接？
Is it one small file or a distributed join across terabytes?

1530
02:25:34,702 --> 02:25:37,572
它需要 Spark，还是用 SQL 就够了？
Does it need Spark or would SQL do?

1531
02:25:37,966 --> 02:25:40,292
是运行 30 秒还是 3 小时？
Does it run for 30 seconds or 3 hours?

1532
02:25:41,582 --> 02:25:48,740
任务描述清楚后，通常只有一两个引擎能胜任，而题目中的限定词就是用来区分这些选项的。
Once the work is described, usually only one or two engines can even do it, and the qualifier in the question separates those.

1533
02:25:49,184 --> 02:25:53,668
如果反过来思考，就会导致四个选项看起来都像合理的答案。
Doing it the other way around is how four options all end up looking plausible.

1534
02:25:55,406 --> 02:26:00,068
这 6 个引擎和底部的 2 个是大家在压力下容易忽略的选项。
6 engines and the 2 at the bottom are the ones people overlook under pressure.

1535
02:26:00,558 --> 02:26:04,932
Athena 和 Redshift 是转换引擎，而不只是查询引擎。
Athena and Redshift are transformation engines, not only query engines.

1536
02:26:05,264 --> 02:26:10,020
选择其中一个通常意味着你即将构建的流水线根本不需要存在。
Choosing one of them often means the pipeline you are about to build does not need to exist.

1537
02:26:10,862 --> 02:26:17,860
Bedrock 是考试中较新的内容，它出现在这个列表里是因为有一类真正的转换并不是算术运算。
Bedrock is newer to this exam and belongs on this list because a real class of transformation is not arithmetic at all.

1538
02:26:18,894 --> 02:26:24,036
分类支持工单、从扫描的发票中提取费用、总结评论。
Classifying a support ticket, pulling fees out of a scanned invoice, summarizing a review.

1539
02:26:24,590 --> 02:26:26,340
这些都不是 Spark 能做到的。
No amount of spark does that.

1540
02:26:27,278 --> 02:26:35,108
阅读题目时要记住这六个选项，因为正确的答案往往是那个不是最显而易见的引擎。
Keep all six in mind when you read a question because a strong answer is frequently the engine that was not the obvious one.

1541
02:26:36,622 --> 02:26:43,824
这三个词在考试大纲中作为一项特定技能出现，所以它们的价值高于它们通常吸引的营销噱头。
These three words appear in the exam guide as a named skill, so they are worth more than the marketing they usually attract.

1542
02:26:44,078 --> 02:26:45,732
把它们当作清单来对待。
Treat them as a checklist.

1543
02:26:46,254 --> 02:26:49,104
数量决定了一个机器是否能完成这项工作。
Volume tells you whether one machine can do the job.

1544
02:26:49,344 --> 02:26:54,468
速度决定了这是批处理还是流式处理，这在模块 3 中讲到过。
Velocity tells you whether this is batch or streaming, which module 3 covered.

1545
02:26:55,406 --> 02:26:58,180
多样性才是真正发生变化的一项。
Variety is the one that has genuinely moved.

1546
02:26:58,862 --> 02:27:04,548
结构化数据交给 SQL 引擎，像 JSON 这样的半结构化数据交给 Spark 或动态帧。
Structured data goes to SQL engines, semi-structured like JSON goes to Spark or a dynamic frame.

1547
02:27:05,166 --> 02:27:08,036
非结构化内容过去意味着需要构建自定义的东西。
Unstructured content used to mean building something custom.

1548
02:27:08,814 --> 02:27:14,980
自从考试大纲修订后，它有了托管答案，本模块的最后一部分会涵盖这个内容。
Since the exam guide revision, it has a managed answer, which the last section of this module covers.

1549
02:27:16,590 --> 02:27:22,628
模块 2 将此项标记为一个考点。考试中如果选错，就会扣分，所以这里需要详细讲解。
Module 2 flagged this as a shape. The exam marks wrong and it deserves the full treatment here.

1550
02:27:26,414 --> 02:27:34,144
将数据从仓库移出进行转换然后再移回，会增加流水线、延迟、成本以及运维负担。
Moving data out of a warehouse to transform it and then moving it back in adds a pipeline, latency, cost, and a thing to operate.

1551
02:27:34,464 --> 02:27:37,604
而这些操作都是为了完成原本就在仓库内就能处理的工作。
All of that to do work the warehouse could have done in place.

1552
02:27:38,542 --> 02:27:47,396
当题目描述的数据已经存在于 Redshift 中，且只需要简单转换到另一个 Redshift 表时，答案是 Redshift 内的 SQL。
When a question disguises data already sitting in Redshift needing lee shaping into another Redshift table, the answer is SQL inside Redshift.

1553
02:27:47,664 --> 02:27:51,396
干扰项会是一个 Glue 作业，它看起来像是正确的工程做法。
The distractor will be a glue job and it will look like proper engineering.

1554
02:27:52,270 --> 02:27:59,108
当数据在入库前必须清洗，或者目标系统无法执行转换时，选择 ETL 是正确的。
ETL is right when data must be cleaned before it lands or when the target cannot do the transformation.

1555
02:28:00,622 --> 02:28:07,140
Glue 和 EMR 的重叠非常严重，所以同时提供这两个选项的题目实际上是在考你是否知道两者的界限。
Glue and EMR overlap so heavily that questions offering both are really asking whether you know the boundary.

1556
02:28:07,662 --> 02:28:12,356
两者都运行 Apache Spark，都从 S3 读取数据，且都是托管服务。
Both run Apache Spark, both read from S3, both are managed.

1557
02:28:12,942 --> 02:28:19,492
如果一个问题可以用其中任何一个来回答，那么限定词就会起决定作用，而“运维开销最小”几乎总是指向 Glue。
If a question could be answered by either, the qualifier decides and least operational overhead points at Blue almost every time.

1558
02:28:20,142 --> 02:28:25,124
所以有用的知识是：哪些特定情况是 Glue 真正无法胜任的。
So the useful knowledge is the set of situations where Blue genuinely cannot do the job.

1559
02:28:25,806 --> 02:28:29,380
有三种情况，它们很具体，下一页列出了这些情况。
There are three, they are specific, and the next slide lists them.

1560
02:28:30,350 --> 02:28:37,284
当这三项都不符合且题目提到运维开销时，停止对比，直接选择 Glue。
When none of the three is present and the question mentions overhead, stop comparing and choose blue.

1561
02:28:38,926 --> 02:28:42,948
把这些作为排除项来学习，而不是做对比。
Learn these as an elimination test rather than as a comparison.

1562
02:28:43,918 --> 02:28:45,248
第一个是 Hive。
The first is the keynest.

1563
02:28:46,350 --> 02:28:49,380
Glue 只运行 Spark 和 Python，不运行其他任何东西。
Glue runs Spark and Python and nothing else.

1564
02:28:49,968 --> 02:28:56,932
所以一旦题目提到 Hive、HBase、Presto 或 Trino，就可以排除 Glue，几秒钟内就能找到答案。
So the moment a question names Hive HBase, Presto, or Trino, Glue is out and you have your answer in seconds.

1565
02:28:57,648 --> 02:29:01,156
第二个是关于迁移成本而非技术问题。
The second is about migration economics rather than technology.

1566
02:29:01,582 --> 02:29:09,540
拥有多年 Hive 脚本的组织可以几乎原封不动地将它们迁移到 EMR，而转向 Glue 则意味着要重写所有内容。
An organization with years of hive scripts can lift them onto EMR almost unchanged, where moving to Glue means rewriting everything.

1567
02:29:10,368 --> 02:29:12,996
第四个原因是大家最容易忽略的一点。
The fourth reason is the one people forget.

1568
02:29:13,870 --> 02:29:20,164
竞价实例可以大幅降低计算成本，而 Glue 没有对应的功能。
Spot instances can cut compute costs dramatically, and Blue offers no equivalent.

1569
02:29:20,448 --> 02:29:27,300
因此，在面临成本压力且有持续高负载的情况下，即使仅用 Spark 也能搞定，答案也可能指向 EMR。
So a sustained heavy workload under cost pressure can point at EMR even when Spark alone would do.

1570
02:29:28,942 --> 02:29:36,036
这个提示很重要，因为很多考试备考资料仍将 EMR 视为自动的高运维开销选项。
The callout matters because a lot of exam preparation still treats EMR as automatically the high overhead option.

1571
02:29:36,462 --> 02:29:38,820
EMR 无服务器 改变了这一点。
EMR serverless changed that.

1572
02:29:39,438 --> 02:29:42,468
它不需要对集群进行容量规划、打补丁或扩缩容。
There is no cluster to size, patch, or scale.

1573
02:29:43,054 --> 02:29:46,276
计费按秒计算，每个工作节点的最小计费时间为一分钟。
Billing is per second with a one minute minimum per worker.

1574
02:29:47,182 --> 02:29:50,436
你仍然拥有 Glue 所缺乏的完整框架选择。
You still get the full framework choice that GRU lacks.

1575
02:29:50,608 --> 02:29:58,276
因此，对于需要 Hive 且运维开销最低的问题，有一个明确的答案，而旧的资料可能会认为这在逻辑上是矛盾的。
So a question needing hive with the least operational overhead has a clean answer that older material would have called contradictory.

1576
02:29:58,638 --> 02:30:01,220
EMR on EKS 的适用范围更窄。
EMR on EKS is narrower.

1577
02:30:02,158 --> 02:30:11,204
它是为那些已经在运行 Kubernetes、并希望其分析任务与所有其他内容共享相同集群和工具的组织准备的。
It is for organizations already running Kubernetes who want their analytics jobs sharing the same cluster and the same tooling as everything else.

1578
02:30:12,654 --> 02:30:18,660
这三种节点类型很重要，因为它们决定了在哪些位置使用竞价实例是安全的，下一页将涵盖这一点。
The three node types matter because they decide where spot instances are safe, which the next slide covers.

1579
02:30:19,054 --> 02:30:21,444
不过底层的存储点更重要。
The storage point underneath is bigger though.

1580
02:30:22,638 --> 02:30:29,252
传统的 Hadoop 将数据保存在集群的 HDFS 中，这意味着集群必须与数据共存。
Traditional Hadoop kept data on the cluster in HDFS, which meant the cluster had to live as long as the data.

1581
02:30:36,768 --> 02:30:38,724
现在集群是可抛弃的。
Now the cluster is disposable.

1582
02:30:39,168 --> 02:30:40,644
为一项任务启动它。
Spin it up for a job.

1583
02:30:41,259 --> 02:30:42,959
处理存储在 S3 中的数据，
process data that lives in S3,

1584
02:30:44,039 --> 02:30:46,884
将结果写回 S3，然后终止。
write results back to S3, Terminate.

1585
02:30:47,982 --> 02:30:50,148
这种模式被称为瞬时集群。
That pattern is called a transient cluster.

1586
02:30:51,088 --> 02:30:58,884
当题目描述一个在每晚运行之间处于闲置状态的 EMR 集群时，这通常是正确答案。
It is usually the correct answer when a question describes an EMR cluster sitting idle between nightly runs.

1587
02:31:00,494 --> 02:31:05,924
这一页是大多数关于 EMR 成本问题的答案，而且它有清晰的结构。
This slide is the answer to most EMR cost questions and it has a clear structure.

1588
02:31:09,390 --> 02:31:15,268
竞价实例属于任务节点，因为当执行器消失时，Spark 只会重试该任务。
Spot belongs on task nodes because Spark simply retries a task whose executor disappeared.

1589
02:31:16,718 --> 02:31:18,852
竞价实例不属于主节点。
Spot does not belong on the primary node.

1590
02:31:19,726 --> 02:31:27,876
这是因为丢失主节点会导致整个集群崩溃，或者在核心节点上是因为它们持有 HDFS 数据块。
That is because losing it kills the whole cluster or on core nodes because they hold HDFS blocks.

1591
02:31:30,222 --> 02:31:34,208
注意框中提到的实例群组和实例集群的区别，这值得记住。
The fleets and groups distinction in the call-out is worth memorizing.

1592
02:31:34,638 --> 02:31:41,636
实例组是单一类型的固定资源池。如果该类型没有竞价实例容量，你就拿不到任何资源。
Instance groups are a fixed pool of one instance type. So if that type has no spot capacity, you get nothing.

1593
02:31:42,606 --> 02:31:47,888
实例集群允许 EMR 在多种类型之间进行替换，以满足请求需求。
Instance fleets let EMR substitute among several types to fill the request.

1594
02:31:48,048 --> 02:31:54,084
这就是为什么每当题目提到竞价中断或容量问题时，它们就是正确答案。
That is why they are the answer whenever a question mentions spot interruptions or capacity.

1595
02:31:55,854 --> 02:32:07,748
一家媒体公司在 EC2 上 24 小时运行 Amazon EMR 集群。该集群每天运行一个耗时约 3 小时的 Apache Hive 作业，除此之外不跑任何内容。
A media company runs an Amazon EMR cluster on EC2 24 hours a day. The cluster runs a nightly Apache hive job that takes about 3 hours and nothing else.

1596
02:32:08,128 --> 02:32:14,340
它使用 15 个按需核心节点，并将中间数据存储在这些节点的 HDFS 中。
It uses 15 on-demand core nodes and stores intermediate data in HDFS on those nodes.

1597
02:32:14,768 --> 02:32:16,580
财务部门已经对成本提出了警告。
Finance has flagged the cost.

1598
02:32:17,488 --> 02:32:24,644
该作业必须在夜间完成，而且团队有一大堆现有的 Hive 脚本，他们不想重写。
The job must still complete overnight and the team has a large body of existing hive scripts they do not want to rewrite.

1599
02:32:25,168 --> 02:32:30,052
哪种组合能在满足要求的同时最大限度降低成本？
Which combination will reduce cost the most while meeting the requirements?

1600
02:32:30,608 --> 02:32:36,740
a. 将 Hive 脚本迁移到 AWS Glue，并作为计划的 Spark 作业运行。
a migrate the hive scripts to AWS Glue and run them as scheduled Spark jobs.

1601
02:32:37,518 --> 02:32:37,808
b
b

1602
02:32:38,766 --> 02:32:42,208
使用 EMRFS 将数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。
store data in Amazon S3 with EMRFS.

1603
02:32:43,054 --> 02:32:48,132
c. 每晚运行一个临时集群，并为任务节点使用竞价实例。
Run a transient cluster nightly and use spot instances for task nodes.

1604
02:32:49,648 --> 02:32:49,888
C。
C.

1605
02:32:50,368 --> 02:32:54,628
d. 将所有 15 个核心节点切换为竞价实例，并保持集群运行。
Switch all 15 core nodes to spot instances and keep the cluster running.

1606
02:32:55,982 --> 02:33:00,804
e. 将集群从 15 个节点减少到 5 个，并接受更长的运行时间。
D reduce the cluster from 15 nodes to 5 and accept a longer runtime.

1607
02:33:01,358 --> 02:33:02,500
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1608
02:33:09,200 --> 02:33:14,788
答案是 B，决定性的逻辑就在前两句话里。
The answer is B, and the deciding arithmetic is in the first two sentences.

1609
02:33:15,200 --> 02:33:20,804
一个为了跑 3 小时任务而全天候运行的集群，有七分之八的时间都在闲置。
A cluster running all day for a three hour job is ideal for seven eighths of its life.

1610
02:33:21,840 --> 02:33:25,892
无论怎么调整规模都无法解决这个问题，这就是为什么 D 是个陷阱。
No amount of resizing fixes that, which is why D is a trap.

1611
02:33:26,320 --> 02:33:30,276
它看起来很负责，但它优化的是错误的维度。
It looks responsible and it is optimizing the wrong dimension.

1612
02:33:31,118 --> 02:33:33,636
选项 A 因为一个词就失败了。
Option A fails on a single word.

1613
02:33:35,246 --> 02:33:40,324
5. Glue 不运行它，所以迁移意味着重写，而题目明确表示不接受重写。
5. Glue does not run it, so migrating means rewriting, which the question refused.

1614
02:33:41,134 --> 02:33:43,684
而且选项 C 展示了为什么节点类型很重要。
And option C shows why the node types matter.

1615
02:33:44,654 --> 02:33:50,884
在核心节点上使用竞价实例，会让 HDFS 数据放在 AWS 可以提前 2 分钟通知就收回的机器上。
Spot on code nodes puts HDFS data on machines AWS can reclaim with 2 minutes notice.

1616
02:33:52,526 --> 02:33:59,012
容器是考试大纲中明确列出的技能，但它们出现的频率比其重要性暗示的要低。
Containers are a named skill in the exam guide and they appear less often than their prominence there suggests.

1617
02:34:00,174 --> 02:34:06,560
需要识别的模式是：容器在组织架构层面胜出，而不是技术层面。
The pattern to recognize is that containers win on organizational grounds rather than technical ones.

1618
02:34:07,086 --> 02:34:14,180
考虑一个已经在 Kubernetes 上运行所有内容，并围绕它构建了监控、部署和访问控制的团队。
Consider a team already running everything on Kubernetes with monitoring, deployment and access control built around it.

1619
02:34:14,862 --> 02:34:18,148
让分析任务运行在同一个地方具有真正的价值。
Analytics jobs living in the same place is real value.

1620
02:34:18,606 --> 02:34:21,060
这就是 EMR on EKS 的用途。
That is what EMR on EKS is for.

1621
02:34:21,646 --> 02:34:30,148
容器通常不会在计划的 ETL 的直接对比中胜出，因为 Glue 根本不需要集群就能完成这项工作。
What containers do not usually win is a straight comparison for Scheduled ETL, because Blue does that with no cluster at all.

1622
02:34:31,310 --> 02:34:36,800
所以要读题，看题目描述的是现有的平台标准还是一个新的选择。
So read for whether the question describes an existing platform standard or a fresh choice.

1623
02:34:38,126 --> 02:34:43,684
这里的每个引擎都有交互式前端，考试会考查关于它们的两个方面。
Every engine here has an interactive front end and the exam tests two things about them.

1624
02:34:44,302 --> 02:34:48,612
第一个是探索和生产是两种不同的模式。
The first is that exploration and production are different modes.

1625
02:34:49,358 --> 02:34:55,840
你在提供即时反馈的笔记本中进行开发，然后将完成的代码作为作业进行计划。
You develop against a notebook where feedback is immediate, then schedule the finished code as a job.

1626
02:34:56,334 --> 02:35:00,320
任何建议让笔记本本身成为生产流水线的选项都是
An option proposing that the notebook itself becomes the production pipeline is

1627
02:35:00,320 --> 02:35:03,680
错误的。第二个是提到的成本点。
wrong. The second is the cost point in the call out.

1628
02:35:04,782 --> 02:35:09,988
交互式会话只要保持开启就会计费，而不是根据你实际运行的查询来计费。
Interactive sessions build for as long as they stay open, not for the queries you actually run.

1629
02:35:10,926 --> 02:35:14,852
一个被遗忘的笔记本会在整晚甚至整个周末持续产生费用。
A forgotten notebook accrues charges through the night and through the weekend.

1630
02:35:15,120 --> 02:35:21,572
Glue 的交互式会话在启动那一刻就会声明 5 DPU，这通常是让人感到意外的地方。
Blue interactive sessions claim 5 dP as the moment they start, which is where the surprise usually comes from.

1631
02:35:22,990 --> 02:35:29,924
一家公司每小时处理一个存放在 Amazon S3 中的压缩 CSV 文件。
A company processes a single compressed CSV file that lands in Amazon S3 once an hour.

1632
02:35:30,542 --> 02:35:32,800
该文件大小在 4 到 9 MB 之间。
The file is between 4 and 9 MB.

1633
02:35:33,902 --> 02:35:39,620
处理过程包括重命名 6 个列，转换 2 个日期字段，并将结果写入为 Parquet。
Processing means renaming 6 columns, casting 2 date fields, and writing the result as parquet.

1634
02:35:40,494 --> 02:35:45,604
目前的实现是一个由 S3 事件触发的 AWS Glue Spark 作业。
The current implementation is an AWS Glue Spark job triggered by an S3 event.

1635
02:35:46,000 --> 02:35:51,300
财务团队询问为什么处理 9 MB 的作业会产生这么多费用。
The finance team has asked why a job that handles 9 MB costs what it does.

1636
02:35:51,680 --> 02:35:53,732
数据工程师应该做些什么更改？
What should the data engineer change?

1637
02:35:54,160 --> 02:35:54,480
A
a

1638
02:35:55,470 --> 02:35:58,692
将 Glue 作业从 10 DPU 减少到最低的 2 个。
reduce the glue job from 10 DPUs to the minimum of 2.

1639
02:36:00,654 --> 02:36:05,348
用同样的事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数替换 Glue Spark 作业。
Replace the Glue Spark job with an AWS Lambda function triggered by the same event.

1640
02:36:05,840 --> 02:36:06,160
C。
C.

1641
02:36:06,574 --> 02:36:09,572
用 Glue Python shell 作业替换 Glue Spark 作业。
Replace the Glue Spark job with a Blue Python shell job.

1642
02:36:10,160 --> 02:36:10,480
D。
D.

1643
02:36:10,894 --> 02:36:15,012
对文件进行批处理，每天运行一次 Glue 作业，而不是每小时运行一次。
Batch the files and run one glue job daily instead of hourly.

1644
02:36:15,822 --> 02:36:16,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1645
02:36:23,662 --> 02:36:29,316
答案是 B。而选项 C 是值得研究的干扰项，因为它非常接近正确答案。
The answer is B. And option C is the distractor worth studying because it is nearly right.

1646
02:36:29,760 --> 02:36:35,876
使用 Glue Python shell 作业是正确的直觉。对于不需要分布式处理的工作，应避开 Spark。
A blue Python share job is the correct instinct. Moving away from Spark for work that is not distributed.

1647
02:36:36,160 --> 02:36:41,188
它仍然包含 Glue 的启动时间和一分钟的最低计费标准，每天运行 24 次。
It still carries blue startup time and its one minute billing minimum, 24 times a day.

1648
02:36:42,094 --> 02:36:44,996
Lambda 处理那个文件不到一秒钟。
Lambda processes that file in under a second.

1649
02:36:45,294 --> 02:36:47,524
注意它与前一个场景的对比。
Notice the pairing with the previous scenario.

1650
02:36:49,742 --> 02:36:56,516
在那个案例中，引擎是对的但配置是浪费的。而在这里，由于选错了类别，配置就无关紧要了。
There, the engine was right and the configuration was wasteful. Here, the configuration is irrelevant because the engine is the wrong category.

1651
02:36:57,422 --> 02:37:02,372
区分这两种情况是本模块教学的核心内容。
Distinguishing those two situations is most of what this module teaches.

1652
02:37:03,758 --> 02:37:07,344
这一部分是能稳拿分数的题目。
This section is where marks are quietly available.

1653
02:37:07,534 --> 02:37:15,184
这是因为考生往往把 Athena 和 Redshift 仅仅看作查询数据的场所，而不是转换数据的引擎。
That is because candidates think of Athena and Redshift as places to query data rather than as engines that transform it.

1654
02:37:15,424 --> 02:37:23,076
两者都可以通过一条语句从查询结果中创建新表，无需作业、集群或编排。
Both can create new tables from the results of a query in one statement with no job, no cluster, and no orchestration.

1655
02:37:23,534 --> 02:37:27,172
当数据已经存在于其中一个工具可以触达的地方时，
When data already lives where one of them can reach it,

1656
02:37:29,358 --> 02:37:32,516
这通常是开销最低的选项。
that is frequently the lowest overhead answer available.

1657
02:37:33,358 --> 02:37:40,612
而提供视图作业来完成同样工作的选项更符合真实的数据工程逻辑，这也是它被提供的原因。
And an option offering a view job to do the same work will look more like real data engineering, which is exactly why it is offered.

1658
02:37:42,286 --> 02:37:47,716
关于 Spectrum 的点值得强调，因为它能消除人们在做题时带入的固有假设。
The spectrum point deserves emphasis because it removes an assumption people carry into questions.

1659
02:37:48,462 --> 02:37:51,492
数据存在于湖中并不意味着 Redshift 就不能用了。
Data sitting in the lake does not mean redshift is out.

1660
02:37:52,462 --> 02:37:58,948
Spectrum 让 Redshift 查询可以直接读取 S3，并在同一条语句中将其与仓库表进行关联。
Spectrum lets a redshift query read S3 directly and join it to warehouse tables in the same statement.

1661
02:37:59,854 --> 02:38:06,532
因此，一条 SQL 语句就可以将精选的仓库数据与原始的湖数据结合起来。
So, a single SQL statement can combine curated warehouse data with raw lake data.

1662
02:38:06,926 --> 02:38:11,364
这通常比建立任何移动数据的流水线都要简单。
That is often simpler than any pipeline that would move one to the other.

1663
02:38:11,950 --> 02:38:14,084
注意这里的可用性警告。
And note the availability warning.

1664
02:38:15,758 --> 02:38:21,956
Redshift 的 Python 用户自定义函数将在 2026 年 6 月底停止支持。
Redshift Python user defined functions reach end of support at the end of June 2026.

1665
02:38:22,894 --> 02:38:30,692
所以，如果题目提供 Python UDF 作为实现自定义逻辑的方法，它描述的是一个即将淘汰的功能。
So a question offering a Python UDF as the way to implement custom logic is describing something on its way out.

1666
02:38:32,622 --> 02:38:37,988
Athena CTAS 是这门考试中被利用率最低的答案。
Athena C T A S is the single most underused answer on this exam.

1667
02:38:40,944 --> 02:38:48,068
一条 SQL 语句就能处理一堆 JSON 文件，并生成一个分区压缩的 Parquet 表。
One SQL statement takes a pile of JSON files and produces a partitioned compressed parquet table.

1668
02:38:49,070 --> 02:38:53,956
这就是在没有作业和集群的情况下，通过优化模块实现的方案。
That is the optimization module one recommended achieved with no job and no cluster.

1669
02:38:54,958 --> 02:38:57,828
不过，提示中的限制条件才是决定题目答案的关键。
The limits in the call out are what decide the questions though.

1670
02:38:58,224 --> 02:39:05,476
单条语句最多只能写入 100 个分区，超过这个数量会报错，提示有太多打开的写入器。
A single statement can write at most 100 partitions, and exceeding it produces an error about too many open writers.

1671
02:39:07,950 --> 02:39:10,884
五年的每日分区大约是 1800 个。
Five years of daily partitions is around 1800.

1672
02:39:11,854 --> 02:39:20,708
因此，对大型历史数据集进行一次性转换，需要使用一系列插入语句或 Glue作业。
So a one-shot conversion of a large historical dataset needs either a chain of insert statements or a blue job instead.

1673
02:39:21,934 --> 02:39:24,356
频率和复杂程度将这两者区分开来。
Frequency and complexity separate these two.

1674
02:39:24,718 --> 02:39:31,876
将数据集一次性转换为 Parquet 是用 CTAS 语句，而为此建立一个 Glue作业则显得过头了。
A one-off conversion of a dataset to parquet is a CTAS statement, and building a blue job for it is disproportionate.

1675
02:39:32,302 --> 02:39:36,804
每晚运行、仅处理新数据的流水线，需要使用书签。
A pipeline running every night, processing only what is new, needs bookmarks.

1676
02:39:37,294 --> 02:39:40,356
它可能需要一些 SQL 处理起来比较别扭的逻辑。
It probably needs logic that SQL expresses awkwardly.

1677
02:39:41,326 --> 02:39:42,468
这就是 Glue作业的用武之地。
That is a blue job.

1678
02:39:42,926 --> 02:39:45,124
折中方案也会出现在题目中。
The middle ground appears in questions too.

1679
02:39:45,518 --> 02:39:56,068
一个周期性但简单的转换，可以用由 Step Functions 定时调用的 CTAS 语句来实现，这样既保留了简单性又增加了重复执行。
A recurring but simple conversion can be a CTAS statement invoked on a schedule by step functions that keeps the simplicity while adding the repetition.

1680
02:39:56,942 --> 02:40:03,140
当你看到这个选项时，要认真对待它，而不是默认“周期性”就意味着要用 Glue。
When you see that option, take it seriously rather than assuming recurring means glue.

1681
02:40:04,784 --> 02:40:11,024
一个分析团队在 Amazon S3 中有三年的应用日志，格式为 gzip.json。
An analytics team has three years of application logs in Amazon S3 as gzip.json.

1682
02:40:11,598 --> 02:40:15,824
这些日志都在一个单一前缀下，没有进行分区，总共约 2TB。
They sit in a single prefix with no partitioning, totaling about 2TB.

1683
02:40:16,624 --> 02:40:21,604
分析师使用 Amazon Athena 查询它们，而且每次查询都会扫描整个数据集。
Analysts query them with Amazon Athena and every query scans the whole dataset.

1684
02:40:22,254 --> 02:40:25,956
团队想要进行一次性转换，将其转换为按天分区的 Parquet 格式。
The team wants a one-off conversion to parquet partitioned by day.

1685
02:40:26,286 --> 02:40:28,548
大约有 1100 天的数据。
There are roughly 1100 days of data.

1686
02:40:29,838 --> 02:40:35,300
转换后，每天仍会有新的文件到达，并且必须以相同的格式进行追加。
After the conversion, a new daily file will continue to arrive and must be appended in the same format.

1687
02:40:36,174 --> 02:40:38,116
最合适的方法是什么？
What is the most appropriate approach?

1688
02:40:40,782 --> 02:40:46,148
a. 运行一个按天分区的 Athena CTAS 语句来创建整个表。
Run a single Athena CT AS statement partition by day to create the whole table.

1689
02:40:46,766 --> 02:40:53,572
b. 运行一个 AWS Glue job 进行历史数据转换，然后用带有书签的计划的 Glue 条目处理每日文件。
b. Run an AWS blue job for the historical conversion, then a scheduled blue job with bookmarks for the daily file.

1690
02:40:54,478 --> 02:41:02,624
c. 对前 100 天运行 Athena CTAS 语句，然后对剩余部分执行 insert into，并进行每日插入
Run an Athena CTAS statement for the first 100 days, then insert into for the rest and a daily insert into

1691
02:41:02,784 --> 02:41:03,588
后续操作。
afterwards.

1692
02:41:04,334 --> 02:41:06,064
d. 在该前缀上启用 S3。
D. Enable S3.

1693
02:41:06,544 --> 02:41:10,436
智能分层，以降低扫描成本。
Intelligent tiering on the prefix to reduce the cost of scanning.

1694
02:41:11,246 --> 02:41:12,704
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1695
02:41:19,118 --> 02:41:25,092
答案是 B，这个场景故意惩罚了两个幻灯片前给出的建议。
The answer is B, and this scenario deliberately punishes the advice from two slides ago.

1696
02:41:25,808 --> 02:41:32,516
对于一次性转换，Athena 的 CTAS 确实是正确的工具，之前的幻灯片也这么说。
Athena, C TAS is genuinely the right tool for a one-off conversion, and the previous slide said so.

1697
02:41:32,974 --> 02:41:38,308
但这里的题目涉及 1100 天的数据，而上限是 100 个分区，所以排除掉这个选项。
Here the question plans 1100 days against a 100 partition ceiling, which rules it out.

1698
02:41:39,182 --> 02:41:45,408
选项 C 是官方文档中的一种变通方法，它并不错。只是比其他替代方案更费事。
Option C is a documented workaround and it is not wrong. It is simply more work than the alternative.

1699
02:41:45,648 --> 02:41:48,208
尤其是当你还需要处理每日重复的追加操作时。
Once you also need the recurring daily append.

1700
02:41:50,638 --> 02:41:52,708
选项 D 是纯粹的陷阱。
Option D is the pure trap.

1701
02:41:53,550 --> 02:42:03,108
存储类别和扫描字节数无关，但如果考生只记得智能分层能省钱，就会选它。
Storage class and bytes scanned are unrelated, and a candidate who half remembers that intelligent tiering saves money will reach for it.

1702
02:42:04,814 --> 02:42:10,276
格式转换是一个特定的技能点，根据你获取数据的时间点不同，有四个对应的答案。
Format conversion is a named skill and it has four answers depending on when you catch the data.

1703
02:42:11,630 --> 02:42:14,276
第一行是最容易被忽略的。
The first row is the most commonly missed.

1704
02:42:15,150 --> 02:42:23,972
如果记录仍在通过 Firehose 流传输，格式转换就是一个配置项，数据到达时就已经是按分区好的 Parquet 了。
If records are still flowing through a fire hose stream, format conversion is a configuration setting and the data arrives in parquet already partitioned.

1705
02:42:24,846 --> 02:42:27,428
这种情况下根本不需要任何转换作业。
No conversion job ever needs to exist.

1706
02:42:27,950 --> 02:42:31,204
模块 3 讲到过这个内容，值得重复强调一下。
Module 3 covered this and it is worth repeating.

1707
02:42:32,078 --> 02:42:39,428
这是因为描述在数据湖中堆积原始 JSON 的题目，通常是在上游而非下游进行修复。
That is because a question describing raw JSON piling up in a lake often has a fix upstream rather than downstream.

1708
02:42:40,238 --> 02:42:48,740
总原则是尽可能早地在流水线中修复格式，因为之后的每一个阶段都会继承这个问题。
The general principle is to fix the format as early in the pipeline as you can, because every stage after it inherits the problem.

1709
02:42:50,478 --> 02:42:57,124
整合多个来源是另一个技能点，考试考查的是判断力而非具体操作。
Integrating multiple sources is another named skill and the exam test judgment rather than mechanics.

1710
02:42:57,678 --> 02:43:05,284
Athena 联邦查询看起来最优雅，因为它可以在原位查询运营数据库，不需要任何流水线。
Athena federated query is the option that looks most elegant because it queries an operational database in place with no pipeline.

1711
02:43:05,966 --> 02:43:08,164
之所以强调这一点，是因为它经常是错误选项的原因。
The call out is why it is often wrong.

1712
02:43:08,974 --> 02:43:15,172
每一次联邦查询都会对一个用于支撑应用程序的生产系统产生负载。
Every federated query runs load against a production system that exists to serve an application.

1713
02:43:15,728 --> 02:43:21,248
分析师在上面运行即时查询，会导致结账页面的速度变慢。
Analysts running ad hoc queries against it is how you slow down a checkout page.

1714
02:43:21,568 --> 02:43:25,728
先将数据落地到数据湖中，可以将分析与源系统隔离开来。
Landing data in the lake first isolates the analytics from the source.

1715
02:43:26,126 --> 02:43:32,964
因此，联邦查询适用于偶尔查询参考数据，而不适合常规的分析工作负载。
So federated query suits occasional lookups of reference data, not a regular analytical workload.

1716
02:43:34,382 --> 02:43:38,052
零售商需要一份每日报告，该报告需要关联出 Amazon Redshift 中的数据。
A retailer needs a daily report joining out a data in Amazon Redshift.

1717
02:43:38,448 --> 02:43:44,740
Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 中的产品参考数据，以及 Amazon S3 中的点击流文件。
Product reference data in Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL. Clickstream files in Amazon S3.

1718
02:43:45,998 --> 02:43:49,796
这个 RDS 数据库同时还在为实时的结账应用提供服务。
The RDS database also serves the live checkout application.

1719
02:43:50,768 --> 02:43:57,540
一名数据工程师建议在生成报告时，使用 Amazon Athena Federated Query 来关联这三个数据源。
A data engineer proposes using Amazon Athena Federated Query to join all three sources at report time.

1720
02:43:57,934 --> 02:44:01,348
该报表查询非常耗费资源，且每天早上 8 点运行一次。
The reporting query is heavy and runs each morning at 8.

1721
02:44:01,808 --> 02:44:04,900
主要问题是什么？应该采取什么措施？
What is the main problem and what should be done instead?

1722
02:44:05,518 --> 02:44:07,748
a. Athena 无法查询 Redshift。
a Athena cannot query Redshift.

1723
02:44:08,590 --> 02:44:11,492
将所有数据迁移到 Redshift 中并在那里进行查询。
Move all data into Redshift and query it there.

1724
02:44:11,982 --> 02:44:15,844
b. 联邦查询会给实时的结账数据库增加负载。
b The Federated Query loads the live checkout database.

1725
02:44:16,048 --> 02:44:20,644
先将 RDS 参考数据复制到数据湖或数据仓库中。
Replicate the RDS reference data into the lake or warehouse first.

1726
02:44:21,248 --> 02:44:21,488
C。
C.

1727
02:44:22,318 --> 02:44:23,908
联邦查询太慢了。
Federated query is too slow.

1728
02:44:24,398 --> 02:44:27,108
增加 Athena 工作组的并发限制。
Increase the Athena workgroup concurrency limit.

1729
02:44:27,728 --> 02:44:28,048
D。
D.

1730
02:44:28,686 --> 02:44:29,728
没有问题。
There is no problem.

1731
02:44:30,446 --> 02:44:34,208
联邦查询正是为这种模式设计的。
Federated query is designed for exactly this pattern.

1732
02:44:34,734 --> 02:44:36,100
停下来思考一下再做决定。
Pause and decide.

1733
02:44:42,542 --> 02:44:45,252
答案是 B，其中一个条款决定了它就是正确选项。
The answer is B, and one clause carries it.

1734
02:44:45,968 --> 02:44:50,148
这个 RDS 数据库还在为实时的结账应用提供服务。
The RDS database also serves the live checkout application.

1735
02:44:50,688 --> 02:44:56,004
如果没有那句话，联邦查询会是一个合理的方案，D 也可以作为辩护项。
Without that sentence, federated query would be a reasonable design and D would be defensible.

1736
02:44:57,486 --> 02:45:02,820
有了这句话，你就是在对一个可用性直接关系到收入的系统运行繁重的分析关联查询。
With it, you are running a heavy analytical joint against a system whose availability is revenue.

1737
02:45:03,728 --> 02:45:08,068
注意这个解决方法与模块 4 的内容相呼应。
Notice that the fix connects back to module 4.

1738
02:45:08,622 --> 02:45:17,124
持续复制这些参考数据是 DMS 任务或零 ETL 集成，这些工具正是为了处理这种情况而设计的。
Replicating that reference data continuously is a DMS task or a zero ETL integration, which are the tools for exactly this.

1739
02:45:18,094 --> 02:45:19,140
并且注意选项。
And note option.

1740
02:45:20,078 --> 02:45:20,288
A
A

1741
02:45:21,518 --> 02:45:25,124
当某个选项断言某事不可能，但实际上并非如此时，
When an option asserts that something is impossible and it is not,

1742
02:45:25,966 --> 02:45:29,252
这通常是能提供的最快的排除法。
that is usually the fastest elimination available.

1743
02:45:30,990 --> 02:45:38,052
这种区别存在于每一个 Spark 排错问题中，理解它比死记硬背更有价值。
This distinction sits underneath every spark troubleshooting question, and it is worth understanding rather than memorizing.

1744
02:45:38,926 --> 02:45:42,916
窄转换在每个分区上独立运行。
A narrow transformation works on each partition independently.

1745
02:45:44,430 --> 02:45:49,092
十个执行器分担十分之一的工作。每一项都在各自处理，彼此之间不移动数据。
Ten executors do a tenth of the work. Each and nothing moves between them.

1746
02:45:50,126 --> 02:45:55,012
宽转换需要行共享同一个键，从而最终进入同一个执行器。
A wide transformation needs rows, sharing a key to end up on the same executor.

1747
02:45:56,782 --> 02:46:02,020
这意味着要写出数据，通过网络发送，然后再读回来。
That means writing data out, sending it across the network, and reading it back.

1748
02:46:02,638 --> 02:46:03,652
这就是洗牌。
That is a shuffle.

1749
02:46:04,334 --> 02:46:08,164
一旦你理解了这一点，排错表就不再是需要背诵的列表了。
Once you see this, the troubleshooting table stops being a list to memorize.

1750
02:46:09,102 --> 02:46:13,124
倾斜是由于某个目标接收了过多数据的洗牌。
SKU is a shuffle where one destination receives too much.

1751
02:46:13,582 --> 02:46:17,444
内存压力是因洗牌后的分区过大而无法容纳的情况。
Memory pressure is a shuffled partition too large to hold.

1752
02:46:18,350 --> 02:46:22,724
缓慢的阶段是你本可以通过重构任务来避免的洗牌。
Slow stages are shuffles you could have avoided by restructuring the job.

1753
02:46:24,302 --> 02:46:29,092
惰性可能会让人们感到意外，并且它会产生一种特定的考试场景。
Laziness surprises people and it produces a specific exam scenario.

1754
02:46:29,614 --> 02:46:36,644
Spark 构建计划而不是边运行边执行，只有在有东西请求输出时才会运行。
Spark builds a plan rather than executing as it goes and only runs when something asks for output.

1755
02:46:37,518 --> 02:46:44,516
考虑一个过滤并连接成中间结果，然后将该结果写入两个目标的任务。
Consider a job that filters and joins into an intermediate result, then writes that result to two destinations.

1756
02:46:45,454 --> 02:46:50,372
Spark 会执行两次过滤和连接，分别对应每一次输出。
Spark performs the filter and the join twice, once for each output.

1757
02:46:50,798 --> 02:46:54,564
捕捉到那个中间步骤会让第二次使用几乎不消耗资源。
Catching that intermediate step makes the second use nearly free.

1758
02:46:55,726 --> 02:46:59,172
最后一项之所以被列出，是因为它属于判断题而非规则。
The last bullet is why this is judgment rather than a rule.

1759
02:47:00,398 --> 02:47:04,772
缓存数据会占用执行器内存，而洗牌也需要这些内存。
Catch data occupies executor memory that shuffles also need.

1760
02:47:05,710 --> 02:47:12,484
不加区分地缓存会导致溢出到磁盘，而这正是你最初想要避免的减速原因。
Catching indiscriminately causes spilling to disk, which is the slowdown you were trying to prevent in the first place.

1761
02:47:13,966 --> 02:47:19,204
排查转换失败是一项专门的技能，而这个表格就是查询表。
Troubleshooting transformation failures is a named skill, and the table is the lookup.

1762
02:47:19,950 --> 02:47:25,060
最后一行值得关注，因为它与其他类别不同。
The last row deserves the attention because it is a different category from the rest.

1763
02:47:26,094 --> 02:47:29,604
其他每一行描述的都是配置不当的任务。
Every other row describes a job that is badly configured.

1764
02:47:30,510 --> 02:47:36,004
那一行描述的是一个配置正常但遇到了非预期数据的任务。
That row describes a job that is fine and has met data it did not expect.

1765
02:47:36,368 --> 02:47:41,988
原本一直是整数的字段变成了字符串，或者出现了一个新的嵌套字段。
A field that has always been an integer arises as a string or a new nested field appears.

1766
02:47:44,046 --> 02:47:46,368
Spark 数据帧在这种情况下会直接报错。
Spark data frames fail hard on that.

1767
02:47:47,086 --> 02:47:53,956
Glue 动态帧可以处理这种情况并让你有意识地解决冲突，这正是动态帧存在的意义。
Glue dynamic frames survive it and let you resolve the conflict deliberately, which is precisely why dynamic frames exist.

1768
02:47:54,830 --> 02:48:01,316
所以关于与源数据变化相关的间歇性故障问题，答案是模式问题，而不是容量问题。
So a question about intermittent failures correlated with source changes has a schema answer, not a capacity answer.

1769
02:48:03,109 --> 02:48:10,180
倾斜有专门的幻灯片，因为它是一个通过增加资源证明无效的性能问题。
SKU earns its own slide because it is the one performance problem where adding resources is provably useless.

1770
02:48:10,608 --> 02:48:14,788
考试知道，增加资源是所有人的本能反应。
The exam knows that adding resources is everyone's instinct.

1771
02:48:15,342 --> 02:48:17,124
这个机制很简单。
The mechanism is simple.

1772
02:48:18,926 --> 02:48:21,092
Spark 按键来划分工作。
Spark divides work by key.

1773
02:48:22,030 --> 02:48:30,128
如果一个键包含了 40% 的行，那么无论有多少个执行器，都有一个任务要承担 40% 的工作量。
If one key holds 40% of the rows, one task does 40% of the work, no matter how many executors exist.

1774
02:48:30,990 --> 02:48:37,092
排序通过在两个阶段的聚合过程中添加随机数，人为地分散这些键。
Sorting spreads that key artificially by appending a random number during the aggregation in two stages.

1775
02:48:37,888 --> 02:48:44,932
当连接的一侧足够小，可以复制到每个执行器时，广播就起作用了，这消除了倾斜所依赖的洗牌。
Broadcasting works when one side of a join is small enough to copy to every executor, which removes the shuffle that SKU depends on.

1776
02:48:46,638 --> 02:48:52,324
一个 AWS Glue 作业将事务表与客户表进行连接，并按客户进行聚合。
An AWS Glue job joins a transactions table to a customer table and aggregates by customer.

1777
02:48:52,750 --> 02:48:55,140
它运行在 20 个 G2X 工作节点上。
It runs on 20 G2X workers.

1778
02:48:56,494 --> 02:48:59,556
95% 的任务在 4 分钟内完成。
95% of tasks finish within 4 minutes.

1779
02:49:00,208 --> 02:49:05,924
有两个任务运行了一个多小时，而且整个作业的总运行时间主要由它们占据。
Two tasks run for over an hour, and the job's total runtime is dominated by them.

1780
02:49:06,830 --> 02:49:14,564
调查显示，由于两个客户标识符是内部测试账号，它们占到了所有交易的很大一部分。
Investigation shows that two customer identifiers account for a large share of all transactions because they are internal test accounts.

1781
02:49:14,928 --> 02:49:18,532
客户表本身很小，大约只有 40 MB。
The customer table itself is small, around 40 megabytes.

1782
02:49:19,086 --> 02:49:21,156
哪种更改最能改善运行时间？
Which change will most improve the runtime?

1783
02:49:23,310 --> 02:49:25,828
将工作节点数量从 20 个增加到 60 个。
Increase the worker count from 20 to 60.

1784
02:49:27,918 --> 02:49:33,380
过滤掉那两个内部测试账号，并在连接时对较小的客户表进行广播。
filter out the two internal test accounts and broadcast the small customer table in the join.

1785
02:49:33,902 --> 02:49:34,208
C。
C.

1786
02:49:34,638 --> 02:49:37,828
将工作节点类型从 G2X 更改为 G8X。
Change the worker type from G2X to G8X.

1787
02:49:39,534 --> 02:49:39,808
D。
D.

1788
02:49:40,622 --> 02:49:44,288
启用 Glue 自动缩放，最大支持 60 个工作节点。
Enable blue auto scaling with a maximum of 60 workers.

1789
02:49:45,358 --> 02:49:46,468
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1790
02:49:52,974 --> 02:49:54,276
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1791
02:49:54,638 --> 02:50:02,852
题目中描述的分布正是倾斜的定义，而四个选项中有三个都是在稍微变换措辞的情况下提供更多容量。
The distribution described in the question is the definition of skew, and three of the four options offer more capacity in slightly different clothing.

1792
02:50:04,974 --> 02:50:06,980
这种重复是有意为之的。
That repetition is deliberate.

1793
02:50:08,206 --> 02:50:12,064
考试在检查你是否会反射性地去寻求增加容量。
The exam is checking whether you reach for capacity reflexively.

1794
02:50:12,590 --> 02:50:22,308
选项 B 有两个独立的强力理由。测试账号不是真实数据，所以过滤它们是从源头消除倾斜，而不是绕过它。
Option B is strong for two independent reasons. The test accounts are not real data, so filtering them removes the skew at source rather than working around it.

1795
02:50:22,702 --> 02:50:30,340
而且一个 40 MB 的表足够小可以进行广播，这消除了最初导致连接变昂贵的洗牌。
And a 40 MB table is small enough to broadcast, which eliminates the shuffle that made the join expensive in the first place.

1796
02:50:32,078 --> 02:50:33,796
创建并消耗数据。
Creating and consuming data.

1797
02:50:34,158 --> 02:50:39,620
在两个不同的任务陈述中，APIs 是一个明确的技能点，所以这一页很有价值。
APs is a named skill in two separate task statements, so it is worth the slide.

1798
02:50:41,806 --> 02:50:42,948
Redshift Data
The Redshift Data.

1799
02:50:44,334 --> 02:50:47,300
API 是最值得理解的部分。
API is the piece most worth understanding.

1800
02:50:48,046 --> 02:50:52,772
传统的数据库连接是长连接，而 Lambda 函数不是。
A traditional database connection is long-lived and a lambda function is not.

1801
02:50:53,678 --> 02:50:59,748
所以，用常规方式连接 Redshift 的函数会耗尽连接限制，并浪费重新连接的时间。
So functions connecting to Redshift the normal way exhaust connection limits and waste time reconnecting.

1802
02:51:00,430 --> 02:51:01,124
数据
The data.

1803
02:51:03,406 --> 02:51:06,084
API 则完全去除了连接。
API removes connections entirely.

1804
02:51:06,384 --> 02:51:12,900
你通过 HTTPS 提交语句，获取一个标识符，并在结果准备好时进行采集。
You submit a statement over HTTPS, get an identifier, and collect the result when it is ready.

1805
02:51:13,742 --> 02:51:16,036
现在来看一个关于无服务器应用的题目。
So a question about a serverless application.

1806
02:51:16,304 --> 02:51:18,916
查询 Redshift 有一个特定的正确答案。
Querying Redshift has a specific right answer.

1807
02:51:19,598 --> 02:51:23,344
来自 Lambda 的 JDBC 连接是那个看似合理但错误的选项。
A JDBC connection from Lambda is the plausible wrong one.

1808
02:51:24,624 --> 02:51:34,244
创建数据 API 是一项技能，而维护它被单独列为一项技能。所以两者都会出现。限流出现的频率最高，原因是它能防止故障发生。
Creating a data API is one skill and maintaining it is named separately. So expect both. Throttling shows up most often and the reason is the failure it prevents.

1809
02:51:35,086 --> 02:51:36,100
还有分析。
And analytics.

1810
02:51:36,942 --> 02:51:40,544
API 位于一个容量有限的数据仓库前端。
API sits in front of a warehouse with finite capacity.

1811
02:51:41,230 --> 02:51:47,044
如果一个团队写了一个每秒运行一千次的循环，可能会导致该数据仓库对其他所有人造成性能下降。
One team writing a loop that caused it a thousand times a second can degrade that warehouse for everybody else.

1812
02:51:47,504 --> 02:51:53,316
使用计划会独立限制每个消费者的上限，因此行为不当的调用者只会损害到它自己。
Usage plans cap each consumer independently, so a badly behaved caller damages only itself.

1813
02:51:55,566 --> 02:51:57,604
缓存是另一个高价值项。
Catching is the other high value item.

1814
02:51:58,574 --> 02:52:08,484
针对缓慢变化的数据进行重复相同的查询非常普遍，从缓存中获取答案可以完全消除负载，而不仅仅是限制它。
Repeated identical queries against slowly changing data are extremely common, and answering them from a cache removes the load entirely rather than merely limiting it.

1815
02:52:10,062 --> 02:52:16,516
一家公司提供了一个内部 API，允许其他团队请求汇总的销售数据。
A company exposes an internal API that lets other teams request aggregated sales figures.

1816
02:52:16,942 --> 02:52:29,732
该 API 由查询 Amazon Redshift 的 AWS Lambda 函数支持。每次调用在开始时都会建立一个 JDBC 连接。在高负载下，各团队报告出现间歇性故障和响应缓慢。
The API is backed by AWS Lambda functions that query Amazon Redshift. Each invocation opens a JDBC connection at the start. Under load, teams report intermittent failures and slow responses.

1817
02:52:30,350 --> 02:52:38,596
CloudWatch 显示 Lambda 在等待连接时超时，而 Redshift 报告已达到连接限制。
CloudWatch shows Lambda invocations timing out while waiting to connect and Redshift reporting that the connection limit has been reached.

1818
02:52:39,118 --> 02:52:41,252
数据工程师应该做哪些更改？
What should the data engineer change?

1819
02:52:41,584 --> 02:52:46,788
A. 增加 Lambda 函数的超时时间，并添加带有指数退避的重试。
a increase the lambda function timeout and add retrees with exponential backoff.

1820
02:52:49,294 --> 02:52:55,184
B. 将 JDBC 连接替换为对 Amazon Redshift 数据 API 的调用。
Replace the JDBC connections with calls to the Amazon Redshift data API.

1821
02:52:55,504 --> 02:52:55,824
C。
C.

1822
02:52:56,384 --> 02:53:00,224
增加 Redshift 集群节点数量以提高连接限制。
Increase the Redshift cluster node count to raise the connection limit.

1823
02:53:00,544 --> 02:53:00,864
D。
D.

1824
02:53:01,264 --> 02:53:05,104
将 API 从 Lambda 迁移到 Amazon 的容器上。
Move the API from Lambda to containers on Amazon.

1825
02:53:05,454 --> 02:53:08,144
即 ECS，这样就可以进行连接池处理。
ECS so connections can be pulled.

1826
02:53:08,814 --> 02:53:10,052
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1827
02:53:16,718 --> 02:53:17,796
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1828
02:53:18,158 --> 02:53:29,316
选项 B 很耐人寻味，因为它是一个真实的工程解决方案，并且出现在生产系统中。连接池正是容器提供的、而 Lambda 不具备的功能。
Option B is the interesting one because it is a real engineering solution and it appears in production systems. Connection pooling is exactly what containers give you that Lambda does not.

1829
02:53:30,094 --> 02:53:37,984
它在这里被排除，是因为当存在专门为这种情况设计的托管 API 时，它改变架构去适配驱动程序是不合适的。
It loses here because it changes the architecture to suit a driver when a managed API designed for this situation exists.

1830
02:53:38,224 --> 02:53:46,948
注意这个场景和上一个场景中的规律。在这两个案例中，都有三个选项提供更多的东西：时间、容量或基础设施。
Notice the pattern across this scenario and the last one. In both, three options offer more of something, time, capacity, or infrastructure.

1831
02:53:47,824 --> 02:53:52,388
有一个选项解决了工具与问题形态之间的不匹配。
One option addresses a mismatch between the tool and the shape of the problem.

1832
02:53:52,784 --> 02:53:56,196
这是值得注意的一种重复出现的结构。
That is a recurring structure worth recognizing.

1833
02:53:57,358 --> 02:54:05,504
技能 1.2.10 是集成大语言模型进行数据处理，它在 2025 年 12 月之前并不存在。
Skill 1.2.10 is integrating large language models for data processing, and it did not exist before December 2025.

1834
02:54:05,742 --> 02:54:09,444
旧的题库里没有涵盖它，大多数课程也没有。
No older question bank covers it, and most courses do not either.

1835
02:54:09,870 --> 02:54:12,452
一旦框架建立正确，这个概念就很简单。
The concept is straightforward once framed correctly.

1836
02:54:13,264 --> 02:54:17,732
到目前为止，本模块中的每个引擎都能执行算术运算和集合操作。
Every engine so far in this module does arithmetic and set operations.

1837
02:54:17,998 --> 02:54:23,204
但它们都无法处理客户投诉并判断是计费问题还是交付问题。
None of them can lead a customer complaint and decide whether it is about billing or delivery.

1838
02:54:23,504 --> 02:54:28,068
它们也无法从每家供应商格式各异的账单中提取总额。
None can pull a total from an invoice laid out differently by every supplier.

1839
02:54:28,846 --> 02:54:34,564
这些属于对含义的判断，而在不久前，数据流水线必须将这些交给人工处理。
Those are judgments about meaning, and until recently, a data pipeline had to send them to a human.

1840
02:54:36,110 --> 02:54:40,164
这里的重点是这种框架让它变得可考，而不是模糊不清。
The callout is the framing that makes this examinable rather than vague.

1841
02:54:40,368 --> 02:54:44,292
在数据流水线中，语言模型几乎总是作为转换器使用。
A language model in a data pipeline is almost always a converter.

1842
02:54:45,070 --> 02:54:54,244
它位于前端，处理任何 SQL 引擎无法处理的内容，并生成结构化输出，供流水线的其余部分作为普通数据处理。
It sits at the front, takes something no SQL engine can handle, produces structured output that the rest of the pipeline treats as ordinary data.

1843
02:54:55,182 --> 02:55:01,572
一旦评论变成了情感得分和三个主题标签，Redshift 就可以像处理其他列一样对它进行聚合。
Once a review has become a sentiment score and three topic tags, Redshift can aggregate it like any other column.

1844
02:55:03,118 --> 02:55:06,404
所以，考试题目很少是关于模型本身的。
So, the exam question is rarely about the model.

1845
02:55:07,086 --> 02:55:12,964
而是在于识别出需要一个阶段来结构化输入，并知道哪个服务能提供这个功能。
It is about recognizing that a stage is needed to structure the input and knowing which service provides it.

1846
02:55:14,638 --> 02:55:17,604
有六种服务，而且它们的界限比看起来要清晰。
Six services and the boundaries are clearer than they look.

1847
02:55:18,094 --> 02:55:23,140
Textract 进行光学字符识别和结构检测，所以它可以读取页面内容。
Texttrand does optical character recognition and structure detection, so it reads the page.

1848
02:55:25,710 --> 02:55:32,580
Comprehend 执行固定的类别语言分析、实体、情感以及个人身份信息。
Comprehend does fixed categories of language analysis, entities, sentiment, and personally identifiable information.

1849
02:55:33,582 --> 02:55:39,408
Bedrock 是通用型的，你可以编写提示词来描述你想提取的内容。
Bedrock is general purpose where you write a prompt describing what you want extracted.

1850
02:55:39,822 --> 02:55:45,188
Bedrock 数据自动化是最新且与考试最相关的。
Bedrock data automation is the newest and most exam relevant.

1851
02:55:45,678 --> 02:55:52,900
这是因为它通过一个 API 在四种模式下完成了整个智能文档处理工作。
That is because it does the whole intelligent document processing job through one API across four modalities.

1852
02:55:53,678 --> 02:56:01,252
将 Textract 链入 Bedrock 提示词的模式仍然有效，而数据自动化是取代它的托管答案。
The pattern of chaining Textract into a bedrock prompt still works, and data automation is the managed answer that replaces it.

1853
02:56:02,894 --> 02:56:07,300
这个区别决定了两个看似合理的选项中哪一个是正确的。
This distinction decides which of two plausible options is right.

1854
02:56:07,726 --> 02:56:15,044
Comprehend 从预定义类别中识别实体，如人、地点、组织和日期。
Comprehend detects entities from predefined categories people, places, organizations, dates.

1855
02:56:15,950 --> 02:56:20,740
如果这是题目要求的，那么 Comprehend 更便宜、更快且可重复。
If that is what the question needs, comprehend is cheaper, faster, and repeatable.

1856
02:56:21,678 --> 02:56:24,740
而如果需求涉及特定的业务字段。
Then the requirement names field specific to the business.

1857
02:56:25,358 --> 02:56:28,868
比如保修期、保单号、交付承诺。
Warranty period, policy number, delivery promise.

1858
02:56:30,286 --> 02:56:34,916
没有预定义类别能涵盖这些，所以生成式模型是正确答案。
No predefined category covers those, so a generative model is the answer.

1859
02:56:35,694 --> 02:56:37,860
确定性这一点也很重要。
The determinism point matters too.

1860
02:56:38,574 --> 02:56:42,340
Comprehend 对同一份文档进行两次处理时，会返回相同的答案。
Comprehend given the same document twice returns the same answer.

1861
02:56:43,246 --> 02:56:48,388
生成式模型可能无法做到这一点，而这对于必须协调一致的流水线来说是一个真实的考量因素。
A generative model may not, which is a genuine consideration for a pipeline that must reconcile.

1862
02:56:49,774 --> 02:56:56,004
这就是第一模块中关于流式处理的课程以新形式出现的点：问谁在等待。
This is where the streaming lesson from module 1 returns in a new form. Ask who is waiting.

1863
02:56:56,302 --> 02:57:01,604
实时应用中的模型调用必须是交互式的，这样它才会按需计费。
A model call inside a live application must be interactive so it pays the on-demand rate.

1864
02:57:02,446 --> 02:57:11,748
每晚对昨日支持工单进行分类的作业没有人在等待，这正是批处理推理的用途，成本大约只有一半。
A nightly job classifying yesterday's support tickets has nobody waiting, which makes it exactly what batch inference is for, at roughly half the cost.

1865
02:57:12,622 --> 02:57:17,648
最后一点是一个简单的效率论证，题目中确实会考到这一点。
The last point is a straightforward efficiency argument that questions do test.

1866
02:57:18,208 --> 02:57:20,900
模型调用的计费是按文档计算的。
Model invocation is priced per document.

1867
02:57:21,774 --> 02:57:30,788
因此，在调用模型之前对数据集进行过滤，比对所有内容调用模型后再丢弃结果要便宜得多。
So filtering the dataset down before invoking the model is far cheaper than invoking it on everything and discarding results afterwards.

1868
02:57:32,462 --> 02:57:39,748
之所以有这一页幻灯片，是因为考试中会出现一些不需要语言模型的地方，但那个选项听起来很现代且令人印象深刻。
This slide exists because the exam will offer a language model where one is not needed and the option will sound modern and impressive.

1869
02:57:40,622 --> 02:57:44,516
处理格式一致的日志行不需要模型。
Passing a consistently formatted log line does not need a model.

1870
02:57:45,070 --> 02:57:48,516
从固定字段中提取日期也不需要模型。
Extracting a date from a fixed field does not need a model.

1871
02:57:49,486 --> 02:57:57,124
这些是模式匹配问题，相比于正则表达式，模型在这些方面更慢、更贵且可靠性更低。
Those are pattern matching problems and a model is slower, more expensive, and less reliable at them than a regular expression.

1872
02:57:57,488 --> 02:58:01,540
确定性问题是具有真实工程后果的那个点。
The determinism point is the one with real engineering consequences.

1873
02:58:03,822 --> 02:58:13,328
如果一个流水线在重新运行时必须产生相同的答案，那么任何可审计的流水线输出非确定性的结果都是一个设计问题
If a pipeline must produce the same answer on a rerun, that any auditable pipeline must non-deterministic output is a design problem

1874
02:58:13,488 --> 02:58:15,332
你必须有意识地去解决它。
you have to solve deliberately.

1875
02:58:16,942 --> 02:58:22,820
一家保险公司每晚接收大约 12,000 份扫描的索赔文件，格式为 PDF。
An insurance company receives around 12,000 scanned claim documents each night as PDFs.

1876
02:58:23,008 --> 02:58:24,848
不同代理的布局各不相同。
Layouts differ by broker.

1877
02:58:25,088 --> 02:58:34,244
公司需要从每份文件中提取六个字段，包括保单号、事故日期和索赔金额，并在早上 8 点前加载到 Amazon Redshift 中。
The company needs six fields from each document, including the policy number, incident date, and claim amount loaded into Amazon Redshift by 8 in the morning.

1878
02:58:35,054 --> 02:58:42,020
之前尝试使用基于规则的解析器，准确率仅达到约 60%，因为布局变化太大。
A previous attempt using a rules-based parser reached about 60% accuracy because the layouts vary too much.

1879
02:58:42,606 --> 02:58:44,356
结果需要在早上前提供。
Results are needed by morning.

1880
02:58:45,198 --> 02:58:47,620
没有人等待单份文件的处理。
Nobody is waiting on an individual document.

1881
02:58:48,302 --> 02:58:50,660
哪种方法最符合要求？
Which approach best meets the requirements?

1882
02:58:53,806 --> 02:58:58,404
A. 为每个代理的布局定制正则表达式的 AWS Glue job。
An AWS Blue Job with regular expressions tuned for each broker's layout.

1883
02:58:59,182 --> 02:59:06,692
B. 在夜间流水线中使用批处理进行 Amazon Bedrock 数据自动化，并将结果加载到 Redshift。
b Amazon Bedrock data automation in a nightly pipeline using batch processing, loading results into Redshift.

1884
02:59:07,534 --> 02:59:11,556
C. 使用 Amazon Comprehend 检测提取文本中的实体。
C. Amazon comprehend to detect entities in the extracted text.

1885
02:59:12,368 --> 02:59:12,688
D
D

1886
02:59:13,870 --> 02:59:18,884
每当有一份文件到达时，实时调用 Amazon Bedrock 进行处理。
Real time Amazon bedrock invocation per document as each one arrives.

1887
02:59:19,630 --> 02:59:20,932
停下来思考一下再做决定。
Pause and decide.

1888
02:59:27,630 --> 02:59:32,352
答案是 B，而每个错误选项都在三个预设的细节中其中一个上失败了。
The answer is B, and each wrong option fails on a different one of the three planted details.

1889
02:59:32,512 --> 02:59:37,412
选项 A 在变动的布局上失败，而题目明确说明这是之前尝试失败的原因。
Option A fails on varying layouts, which is stated as the reason the previous attempt failed.

1890
02:59:37,712 --> 02:59:43,850
选项 C 在特定业务字段上失败，因为保单号不是一个类别。Comprehend 不知道这些。
Option C fails on business specific fields because policy number is not a category. Comprehend knows.

1891
02:59:45,038 --> 02:59:51,460
选项 D 在经济性上不成立，因为没人需要等待，而且批处理推理的成本大约只有一半。
Option D fails on economics because nobody is waiting and batch inference costs roughly half.

1892
02:59:52,334 --> 02:59:58,212
这种结构中，每个干扰项都被不同的句子排除掉，这是高质量题目常见的做法。
That structure, where each distractor is killed by a different sentence, is common on well-written questions.

1893
02:59:59,406 --> 03:00:03,012
它奖励那些在看选项之前仔细阅读情况的人。
It rewards reading the situation carefully before looking at the options.

1894
03:00:04,718 --> 03:00:16,580
核心原则是贯穿所有五行的逻辑。在这场考试中，任何真正的成本优化都是减少不必要的工作量，而不是为同样的工作去谈更低的价格。
The call out is the principle underneath all five rows. Every genuine cost optimization on this exam reduces the amount of work performed rather than negotiating a lower price for the same work.

1895
03:00:16,942 --> 03:00:18,788
书签可以防止重复处理。
Bookmarks stop reprocessing.

1896
03:00:19,072 --> 03:00:21,392
谓词下推可以减少读取量。
Push down predicates stop reading.

1897
03:00:21,678 --> 03:00:23,428
分区可以减少扫描量。
Partitioning, stop scanning.

1898
03:00:24,334 --> 03:00:26,884
瞬时集群可以避免支付闲置时间的费用。
Transient clusters stop paying for idle time.

1899
03:00:27,886 --> 03:00:31,716
在调用模型前进行过滤，可以避免为被丢弃的文档付费。
Filtering before a model call stops paying for documents you discard.

1900
03:00:32,718 --> 03:00:37,572
当你看到成本问题时，要问：哪些是没必要做的多余工作？
When you see a cost question, ask what work is being done that does not need to be.

1901
03:00:38,350 --> 03:00:41,636
在你查看实例类型或计费模式之前先做这个判断。
Do that before you look at instance types or pricing modes.

1902
03:00:43,342 --> 03:00:46,404
一个数据平台团队运行四个工作负载。
A data platform team runs four workloads.

1903
03:00:47,118 --> 03:00:50,244
一个没有截止日期的每晚 Spark ETL 作业。
A nightly Spark ETL job with no deadline.

1904
03:00:51,118 --> 03:00:53,732
一个每小时转换一个小文件的任务。
An hourly conversion of one small file.

1905
03:00:54,112 --> 03:00:57,444
一个每天合并三个精选的 Redshift 表的报告。
A daily report joining three curated LEDshift tables.

1906
03:00:58,510 --> 03:01:03,396
一个每月将 20,000 条免费技术调查回复分类到六个主题的任务。
A monthly classification of 20,000 free tech survey responses into six themes.

1907
03:01:04,270 --> 03:01:11,076
团队被要求在不减少范围、且不推迟任何当前窗口任务的情况下，降低这四个方面的成本。
The team has been asked to reduce cost across all four without reducing scope or delaying anything beyond its current window.

1908
03:01:11,472 --> 03:01:13,892
哪一组更改最合适？
Which set of changes is most appropriate.

1909
03:01:15,918 --> 03:01:24,964
A. 将所有四个工作负载迁移到 Amazon EMR 在 EC2 上运行并使用竞价实例，以获得一个统一的平台。
A. Move all four workloads to Amazon, EMR on EC2 with spot instances to get one consistent platform.

1910
03:01:27,438 --> 03:01:32,644
Glue 使用 flex、一个 Lambda 函数、Redshift 内部的 SQL，
Glue with flex, a lambda function, SQL inside Redshift,

1911
03:01:33,326 --> 03:01:35,428
以及 Bedrock 批处理推理。
and Bedrock Batch Inference.

1912
03:01:35,872 --> 03:01:36,192
C。
C.

1913
03:01:36,750 --> 03:01:41,540
四个都用 Glue，并进行规格调整，因为单一服务操作起来最简单。
Glue for all four, right sized since a single service is simplest to operate.

1914
03:01:41,872 --> 03:01:42,192
D。
D.

1915
03:01:42,638 --> 03:01:43,072
Athena。
Athena.

1916
03:01:43,632 --> 03:01:49,700
四个都用 CTAS，因为无服务器 SQL 是可用的最便宜选项。
C T AS for all four since serverless SQL is the cheapest option available.

1917
03:01:50,510 --> 03:01:51,556
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1918
03:01:58,286 --> 03:02:03,076
答案是 B，这个案例是刻意用来结束本模块的。
The answer is B, and this scenario closes the module deliberately.

1919
03:02:05,262 --> 03:02:09,860
四个选项中的三个都是同一种直觉的变体，即标准化。
Three of the four options are versions of the same instinct, which is to standardize.

1920
03:02:10,382 --> 03:02:15,300
标准化是真正的工程美德，考试并不反对它。
Standardization is a genuine engineering virtue, and the exam is not against it.

1921
03:02:16,206 --> 03:02:20,196
它反对在工作负载特征明显不同的地方应用。
It is against applying it where the workloads have materially different shapes.

1922
03:02:20,494 --> 03:02:24,772
这四个选项中的每一个都有指向不同引擎的明确特征。
Each of these four has a stated characteristic pointing at a different engine.

1923
03:02:25,262 --> 03:02:26,052
没有截止日期。
No deadline.

1924
03:02:29,390 --> 03:02:30,276
小文件。
Small file.

1925
03:02:31,630 --> 03:02:33,232
数据已就位。
Data already in place.

1926
03:02:33,552 --> 03:02:35,204
没有等待读取者的文本。
Text with no waiting reader.

1927
03:02:36,078 --> 03:02:41,732
对每个工作负载分别运行模块 1 中的四个问题，这个问题就能迎刃而解。
Run the four questions from module 1 on each workload separately, and this question answers itself.

1928
03:02:43,312 --> 03:02:48,772
共有 5 个问题，其中第二个是投入最少但能拿最高分的题目。
5 questions, and the second is the one that gains the most marks for the least effort.

1929
03:02:49,152 --> 03:02:58,052
这是因为它排除掉的是整个流水线，而不是在它们之间做选择。已经在数据仓库中的数据通常应该就在那里进行转换。
That is because it eliminates entire pipelines rather than choosing between them. Data already in the warehouse should usually be transformed there.

1930
03:02:58,926 --> 03:03:03,364
第四个问题是本次考试的新题，值得加入你的备考习惯中。
The fourth question is new to this exam and worth adding to your habits.

1931
03:03:03,950 --> 03:03:10,660
这是因为非结构化输入现在有了托管答案，而不是一个研究项目。
That is because unstructured input now has a managed answer rather than being a research project.

1932
03:03:11,552 --> 03:03:19,428
下一个模块是编排，也就是如何将所有这些引擎串联在一起。如果其中一个在凌晨 3 点失败了会发生什么？
Next module is orchestration, which is how all of these engines get chained together. What happens when one of them fails at 3 in the morning?

1933
03:03:20,078 --> 03:03:23,108
为什么考试在两个不同的领域测试这个主题？
Why the exam tests that topic in two separate domains?

1934
03:03:24,832 --> 03:03:30,660
编排是核心主题。大多数学习计划都低估了它，原因是考试大纲的一个特殊之处。
Orchestration is the topic. Most study plans underrate, and the reason is a quirk of the exam guide.

1935
03:03:31,022 --> 03:03:32,228
它出现了两次。
It appears twice.

1936
03:03:32,672 --> 03:03:38,660
一次在领域 1 中作为构建工作流，另一次在领域 3 中作为自动化和故障排除。
Once in domain 1 as building workflows, and again in domain 3 as automating and troubleshooting them.

1937
03:03:39,150 --> 03:03:43,716
这使得它成为极少数能在两个不同领域得分的主题之一。
That makes it one of very few subjects earning marks in two separate domains.

1938
03:03:44,430 --> 03:03:51,172
在本次课程的分析中，EventBridge 和 Step Functions 出现的频率比 Amazon Athena 还要高。
In the bank analyze for this course, event bridge and step functions together appeared more often than Amazon Athena.

1939
03:03:51,822 --> 03:03:56,004
大多数考生给 Athena 分配的学习时间远多于这两者加起来的时间。
Most candidates give Athena considerably more study time than both combined.

1940
03:03:56,910 --> 03:04:01,508
本模块涵盖了四种编排工具以及如何在它们之间做出选择。
This module covers the four orchestration tools and how to choose between them.

1941
03:04:02,030 --> 03:04:03,524
工作是如何被触发的。
How work gets triggered.

1942
03:04:04,078 --> 03:04:07,332
当一个步骤失败时，一个高可用的流水线究竟能做什么。
What a resilient pipeline actually does when a step fails.

1943
03:04:08,782 --> 03:04:16,096
5 个工作场景，以及一个在 2025 年末发生变化、从而改变了标准考试答案的服务。
5 work scenarios and one service that changed in late 2025 in a way that alters a standard exam answer.

1944
03:04:17,422 --> 03:04:19,268
任何东西都可以按顺序执行步骤。
Anything can run steps in order.

1945
03:04:19,886 --> 03:04:21,380
Shell 脚本也能做到这一点。
A shell script can do that.

1946
03:04:21,696 --> 03:04:25,924
编排器为你提供的是围绕异常路径的所有处理。
What an orchestrator gives you is everything around the unhappy path.

1947
03:04:26,446 --> 03:04:30,468
当步骤 3 失败或步骤 4 超时时会发生什么？
What happens when step 3 fails or when step 4 times out?

1948
03:04:31,374 --> 03:04:39,204
当一个步骤等待一个永远不会到达的文件长达 4 小时，或者同一个工作流被意外触发两次时会发生什么？
What happens when a step waits 4 hours for a file that never arrives or when the same workflow is triggered twice by accident?

1949
03:04:40,238 --> 03:04:46,896
这些正是考试提出的问题，因为它们是那些在凌晨 3 点没人看守时真正重要的问题。
Those are the questions the exam asks, because they are the questions that matter at 3 in the morning when nobody is watching.

1950
03:04:47,438 --> 03:04:56,356
所以当你读到编排场景时，首先寻找其中描述的故障。通常是故障决定了答案，而不是步骤的顺序。
So when you read an orchestration scenario, look first for the failure described in it. The failure usually decides the answer, not the sequence of steps.

1951
03:04:56,896 --> 03:05:03,972
还要注意，本模块中大多数场景描述的是正在运行的流水线，而不是已经停止的。
Notice too that most of the scenarios in this module describe a pipeline that is running, not one that has stopped.

1952
03:05:04,718 --> 03:05:07,044
这种“无声的错误”就是一种故障模式。
Silent wrongness is the failure mode.

1953
03:05:07,278 --> 03:05:09,028
考试更看重大部分情况。
The exam cares about most.

1954
03:05:10,574 --> 03:05:14,788
这个提示区分了两个题目刻意制造冲突的任务。
The callout separates two jobs that questions deliberately conflict.

1955
03:05:15,790 --> 03:05:17,380
EventBridge 是一个触发器。
Event bridge is a trigger.

1956
03:05:17,776 --> 03:05:22,340
它能察觉到文件已到达，或者现在是凌晨两点，然后启动某些操作。
It notices that a file landed or that it is 2 in the morning and it starts something.

1957
03:05:23,278 --> 03:05:31,332
它不知道这些操作是否成功，无法获取第三步，也没有关于包含多个阶段的流程的概念。
It does not know whether that something succeeded, cannot retrieve step 3, and has no concept of a workflow with stages.

1958
03:05:32,590 --> 03:05:36,996
Step Functions、MWAA 和 Glue 工作流负责协调。
Step functions MWAA and Glue Workflows Coordinate.

1959
03:05:37,390 --> 03:05:43,136
它们了解整个流水线的结构，追踪当前进度，并决定在某个阶段失败时该如何处理。
They know the shape of the whole pipeline, track where it is, and decide what to do when a stage fails.

1960
03:05:43,694 --> 03:05:54,336
一种非常常见的架构是使用 EventBridge 来启动 Step Functions 状态机，而对于多步骤流水线，仅提供 EventBridge 的选项通常是错误的。
A very common architecture uses EventBridge to start a step function state machine, and options offering EventBridge alone for a multi-step pipeline are usually wrong.

1961
03:05:55,214 --> 03:05:58,052
第三点是解题的关键。
The third point is the one that wins questions.

1962
03:05:58,336 --> 03:06:06,980
如果没有编排器，重试逻辑就存在于每个任务内部，每次编写方式略有不同，且在出现问题时难以察觉。
Without an orchestrator, retry logic lives inside each job, written slightly differently every time and invisible when it misbehaves.

1963
03:06:07,790 --> 03:06:17,060
Step Functions 将其作为每个状态的配置，包含退避和最大尝试次数，并能在执行历史中显示每一次尝试。
Step functions declares it as configuration on each state with back-off and a maximum attempt count and shows you every attempt in the execution history.

1964
03:06:17,696 --> 03:06:22,532
分布式映射也值得一提，因为它很好地解决了特定问题。
Distributed map deserves a mention too, because it solves the specific problem well.

1965
03:06:23,278 --> 03:06:30,244
以前要用 Lambda 函数处理一百万个独立的 S3 对象时，需要自定义扇出。
Processing a million individual S3 objects with a lambda function each would previously have needed custom fan out.

1966
03:06:30,656 --> 03:06:38,340
分布式映射原生支持高并发来完成此操作，这使其成为处理大规模逐个对象处理问题的标准答案。
Distributed map does it natively with high concurrency, which makes it the answer to large-scale per object processing questions.

1967
03:06:39,918 --> 03:06:46,628
值得记住“分布式映射”这个名称，因为它能回答那些过去需要自定义扇出设计的问题。
Distributed map is worth knowing by name because it answers a question that used to require a custom fan out design.

1968
03:06:47,150 --> 03:06:56,420
以前要独立处理一百万个 S3 对象，得通过将队列和函数串联起来并由自己管理并发性。
Processing a million individual S3 objects, each independently, was previously a matter of chaining queues and functions together and managing the concurrency yourself.

1969
03:06:57,262 --> 03:07:05,668
分布式映射直接从 S3 读取对象列表，并在高并发下启动跨这些对象的子执行。
Distributed map reads the list of objects straight from S3 and launches child executions across them at high concurrency.

1970
03:07:07,406 --> 03:07:10,948
这两个配置点是考试考查的内容。
The two configuration points are what the exam tests.

1971
03:07:11,566 --> 03:07:19,684
之所以有最大并发性限制，是因为所有子任务都要写入某个地方，而十万个并发写入者会压垮大多数目标。
Maximum concurrency exists because the children all write somewhere and a hundred thousand concurrent writers will overwhelm most targets.

1972
03:07:20,398 --> 03:07:27,556
之所以有批处理，是因为为了处理一个 2KB 的对象而启动一个子执行大部分是浪费开销。
Batching exists because launching one child execution to process a 2KB object is mostly overhead.

1973
03:07:28,782 --> 03:07:34,976
你不会被要求去编写状态机，但识别出每种状态类型的功能能让你快速读懂题目。
You will not be asked to write a state machine, but recognizing what each state type does lets you read an auction quickly.

1974
03:07:35,216 --> 03:07:40,292
其中两个点解释了为什么考试更青睐 Step Functions 而不是按顺序调用各项任务的脚本。
Two of them explain why the exam favors step functions over a script that calls things in order.

1975
03:07:41,166 --> 03:07:49,444
选择状态根据实际流经的数据进行分支。因此，当文件为空和内容充足时，流水线的行为可以不同。
A choice state branches on the actual data flowing through. So a pipeline can behave differently when a file is empty than when it is full.

1976
03:07:49,998 --> 03:07:53,188
等待状态会在不消耗计算资源的情况下暂停。
A wait state pauses without consuming compute.

1977
03:07:53,934 --> 03:07:57,380
等待四小时的 EMR 集群不会产生额外费用。
Waiting four hours for an EMR cluster costs nothing.

1978
03:07:58,254 --> 03:08:03,780
Lambda 函数无法等待 4 小时，而 EC2 实例在等待时纯属浪费成本。
A lambda function waiting 4 hours is impossible, and an EC2 instance waiting is pure expense.

1979
03:08:05,422 --> 03:08:09,540
Map 是与集合中的逐项处理相关联的选项。
Map is the one to associate with per item processing over a collection.

1980
03:08:11,232 --> 03:08:16,164
这是 Step Functions 中最常考的细节，且它会导致经典的 Bug。
This is the most examinable detail in step functions and it produces a classic bug.

1981
03:08:16,622 --> 03:08:25,220
使用默认的请求响应模式调用 Glue作业，会立即启动任务并报告成功，因为 API 调用本身已经成功了。
Calling a blue job with the default request response pattern starts the job and reports success straight away because the API call itself succeeded.

1982
03:08:26,094 --> 03:08:30,192
随后状态机会在 Glue作业仍在运行的情况下进入下一步。
The state machine then moves to the next step while the blue job is still running.

1983
03:08:30,352 --> 03:08:32,868
所以下一步读取到的是不完整的数据。
So the next step reads incomplete data.

1984
03:08:33,454 --> 03:08:37,444
在数据流水线中，你几乎总是想要同步模式。
The dotsync pattern is what you almost always want in a data pipeline.

1985
03:08:37,712 --> 03:08:41,732
它会等待任务完成，如果任务失败，状态也会报错。
It waits for the job to finish and fails the state if the job failed.

1986
03:08:42,606 --> 03:08:49,764
回调模式适用于需要 AWS 外部响应的情况，包括人工审批某个步骤。
The callback pattern covers cases where something outside AWS must respond, including a human approving a step.

1987
03:08:51,438 --> 03:08:55,140
第四点是一个常出现在考试答案中的设计规则。
The fourth point is a design rule that appears as an exam answer.

1988
03:08:55,598 --> 03:09:00,132
状态机的有效负载有以千字节为单位的大小限制。
State machine payloads carry a size limit measured in kilobytes.

1989
03:09:00,672 --> 03:09:08,324
如果流水线试图在不同状态之间传递数据帧或文件的内容，一旦数据量超过限制就会失败。
A pipeline attempting to pass a data frame or a file's contents between states will fail once the data grows beyond it.

1990
03:09:09,262 --> 03:09:16,836
正确的做法是传递引用，比如 S3 键或任务标识符，让下一步自行读取数据。
The correct pattern is to pass a reference instead, an S3 key or a job identifier, and let the next step read the data itself.

1991
03:09:18,350 --> 03:09:21,892
这听起来显而易见，但经常会让构建第一个流水线的人掉进坑里。
That sounds obvious and it catches people building their first pipeline.

1992
03:09:22,752 --> 03:09:31,812
同样的原则也适用于 Glue 工作流，其中的运行属性是为分区日期等小数值设计的，而不是用来传输数据的。
The same principle applies in glue Workflows, where run properties are meant for small values like a partition date rather than for data.

1993
03:09:33,358 --> 03:09:37,072
这张表将编排与模块 5 的引擎重新联系起来。
This table connects orchestration back to module 5's engines.

1994
03:09:37,454 --> 03:09:39,332
有两行值得注意。
Two rows are worth attention.

1995
03:09:40,238 --> 03:09:44,516
EMR 这一行解释了瞬时集群模式实际上是如何运作的。
The EMR row explains how the transient cluster pattern actually operates.

1996
03:09:45,614 --> 03:09:54,820
这是因为状态机负责创建集群、添加步骤、等待执行并将其终止。因此在每晚的运行之间，没有任何东西在空转。
That is because the state machine creates the cluster, adds the steps, waits for them, and terminates it. So nothing is running between nightly executions.

1997
03:09:55,982 --> 03:10:00,452
Redshift 这一行重新关联到模块 5 的数据 API。
The redshift row reconnects to the data API from module 5.

1998
03:10:01,358 --> 03:10:05,732
状态机无法保持数据库连接，就像 Lambda 函数一样做不到。
A state machine cannot hold a database connection any more than a Lambda function can.

1999
03:10:06,192 --> 03:10:10,020
所以数据 API 是作为一种机制存在的，而不是为了优化。
So the data API is the mechanism rather than an optimization.

2000
03:10:10,766 --> 03:10:17,952
最后一项是审批步骤的工作原理，它出现在关于在发布前需要签核的流水线问题中。
And the last row is how approval steps work, which appears in questions about pipelines that need sign-off before publishing.

2001
03:10:19,182 --> 03:10:26,244
对于数据工程考试，答案通常是标准化的，了解背后的原因比死记硬背表格更重要。
For a data engineering exam, the answer is usually standard and knowing why matters more than memorizing the table.

2002
03:10:26,830 --> 03:10:34,980
运行 Glue作业的流水线至少需要几分钟，一旦在后面添加任何内容，就会超过 Express 的 5 分钟上限。
A pipeline that runs a glue job takes minutes at least, which already exceeds the 5-minute express ceiling once you add anything after it.

2003
03:10:35,470 --> 03:10:41,860
标准模式还会保留完整的执行历史，你可以几天后去检查，这让故障排除成为可能。
Standard also keeps a full execution history, you can inspect days later, which is what makes troubleshooting possible.

2004
03:10:42,382 --> 03:10:46,020
Express 是为了处理极高吞吐量、极短时间的事件处理而存在的。
Express exists for very high volume, very short event processing.

2005
03:10:46,574 --> 03:10:52,100
当你每秒处理 10 万次执行，且单个历史记录并不重要时。
You are handling 100,000 executions a second and the individual history does not matter.

2006
03:10:52,832 --> 03:10:58,340
如果题目描述的是逐个摄取点击流事件，那么 Express 是合理的选择。
If a question describes ingesting clickstream events one at a time, Express is plausible.

2007
03:10:59,726 --> 03:11:02,788
如果它描述的是 ETL 流水线，那就不是。
If it describes an ETL pipeline, it is not.

2008
03:11:04,032 --> 03:11:07,140
这是标准考试答案的一个真实变化。
This is a genuine change to a standard exam answer.

2009
03:11:07,566 --> 03:11:13,380
多年来，对比点一直是 Step Functions 是无服务器的，而 MWAA 不是。
For years the comparison ran that step functions is serverless while MWAA is not.

2010
03:11:13,774 --> 03:11:20,868
MWAA 意味着无论工作流是否运行，都要为调度器和元数据数据库支付全天候费用。
MWAA meant paying for a scheduler and metadata database around the clock, whether any workflow ran or not.

2011
03:11:21,294 --> 03:11:23,940
这是很多题目中的决定性论据。
That was the deciding argument in a lot of questions.

2012
03:11:24,846 --> 03:11:30,500
2025年11月发布的 MWAA 无服务器功能取消了这一区别。
MWAA serverless announced in November 2025 removes it.

2013
03:11:30,990 --> 03:11:38,404
每个任务都在隔离的容器中运行，你只需为消耗的秒数付费，且没有闲置的环境。
Each task runs in an isolated container, you pay for the seconds it consumes, and there is no environment sitting idle.

2014
03:11:39,342 --> 03:11:44,196
工作流是用 YAML 定义的，或者从 Python DAGs 转换而来。
Workflows are defined in YAML or converted from Python DAGs.

2015
03:11:45,134 --> 03:11:50,884
旧的资料没提到这一点，所以单纯从成本角度出发的论据现在不如以前强力了。
Older material does not mention it, so treat cost alone as a weaker argument than it used to be.

2016
03:11:52,174 --> 03:12:00,672
考试不是考 Airflow 本身，但这些词汇会出现在题目表述中，且最后两行涉及真实案例。
You are not being examined on Airflow itself, but this vocabulary appears in question wording and the last two rows produce real incidents.

2017
03:12:01,006 --> 03:12:03,152
回填确实很有用。
Backfill is genuinely useful.

2018
03:12:03,392 --> 03:12:10,340
它是指在修复 Bug 后重新处理历史数据，将过去每个时间段的工作流运行一遍，就像它们当时运行过一样。
It is how you reprocess history after fixing a bug, running the workflow for each past interval as though it had run at the time.

2019
03:12:11,310 --> 03:12:14,564
追赶是自动化的版本，但也是危险的。
Catchup is the automatic version and it is the dangerous one.

2020
03:12:14,958 --> 03:12:22,820
如果你开启一个起始日期在两年前且开启了“追赶”功能的 DAG，Airflow 会立即排期 700 次运行。
Enable a DAG whose start date is two years ago with catch up switched on and Airflow immediately schedules 700 runs.

2021
03:12:23,552 --> 03:12:30,436
传感器值得了解，因为它们表达了对文件模式的等待，这也是本模块场景 3 所涉及的内容。
Sensors are worth knowing because they express the wait for a file pattern that scenario 3 in this module is about.

2022
03:12:31,918 --> 03:12:36,676
流水线大部分时间都在等待，而你如何进行等待是一个真实的成本决策。
Pipelines spend a lot of their life waiting, and how you wait is a real cost decision.

2023
03:12:37,006 --> 03:12:38,212
考试会考到这些。
The exam tests.

2024
03:12:38,766 --> 03:12:42,884
最糟糕的版本是带 sleep 函数的 Lambda 函数在循环中运行。
The worst version is a lambda function pulling in a loop with a sleep.

2025
03:12:43,182 --> 03:12:47,952
你得为每一秒无所事事的等待付费，而且反正它也限制在 15 分钟以内。
You pay for every second of doing nothing and you are capped at 15 minutes anyway.

2026
03:12:48,494 --> 03:12:56,032
经典的 Airflow 传感器更好一些但仍占用工作节点，因此如果有 100 个 DAG 都在等待，可能会耗尽环境资源。
A classic airflow sensor is better and still holds a worker slot, so 100D AGs all waiting can exhaust the environment.

2027
03:12:56,580 --> 03:13:00,804
可推迟算子通过在等待时释放工作节点来解决这个问题。
Deferrable operators solve that by releasing the worker while waiting.

2028
03:13:02,542 --> 03:13:03,872
Step Functions。
Step functions.

2029
03:13:04,302 --> 03:13:08,708
等待状态是免费的，而且最后一点在任何地方都适用。
Wait states are free and the last point matters everywhere.

2030
03:13:09,582 --> 03:13:13,572
没有超时限制的等待会导致流水线永远静默挂起。
A wait with no timeout becomes a pipeline that hangs silently forever.

2031
03:13:15,086 --> 03:13:24,112
模块 2 和 4 都承诺提供这个对比，所以这里完整展示一下。它的信号特征与模块 3 中 Kinesis 对比 MSK 的情况一致。
Modules 2 and 4 both promise this comparison, so here it is in full. The signal is the same shape as kinesis against MSK in module 3.

2032
03:13:24,302 --> 03:13:30,752
留意现有的 Airflow DAGs、拥有 Airflow 专业知识的团队或需要跨出 AWS 的流水线。
Watch for existing Airflow DAGs, a team with Airflow expertise or a pipeline reaching outside AWS.

2033
03:13:31,022 --> 03:13:32,912
这些任何一个都意味着 MWAA？
Any of those means MWAA?

2034
03:13:33,966 --> 03:13:40,388
这是因为重写现有的 DAGs 是不必要的迁移，会导致考试得分错误。
That is because rewriting working DAGs is the unnecessary migration caused the exam marks wrong.

2035
03:13:41,070 --> 03:13:49,412
如果场景是仅协调 AWS 服务的新流水线，Step Functions 更简单且具有原生集成。
If the scenario is a new pipeline coordinating AWS services only, step functions is simpler and integrates natively.

2036
03:13:50,192 --> 03:14:00,100
选择 MWAA 的第二个原因是可移植性，这对不愿将编排层绑定在单一云平台的组织来说很重要。
The second reason for MWAA is portability, which matters to organizations that will not commit their orchestration layer to one cloud.

2037
03:14:01,774 --> 03:14:09,312
Glue 工作流是可用性最高的选项，因为它们根本不会给架构增加额外的服务。
Glue workflows are the lowest overhead option available when they apply because they add no service to the architecture at all. The

2038
03:14:09,312 --> 03:14:11,588
它的上限很明确且容易测试。
ceiling is sharp and easy to test for.

2039
03:14:12,494 --> 03:14:18,372
一旦流水线包含任何非 Glue 工作、爬虫或触发器的内容，它们就到头了。
The moment a pipeline includes anything that is not a blue job, crawler or trigger, they run out of road.

2040
03:14:19,310 --> 03:14:28,164
发送通知的 Lambda 函数、Redshift 存储过程、等待人工审批、或者是一个 EMR 步骤。
A Lambda function that sends a notification, a red shift stored procedure, a wait for a human to approve something, an EMR step.

2041
03:14:28,718 --> 03:14:32,912
这些中的任何一项都会迫使你使用 Step Functions 或 MWAA。
Any one of those forces you up to step functions or MWAA.

2042
03:14:34,926 --> 03:14:39,524
所以阅读测试的方法就是数一下描述的流水线中有多少个非 Glue 步骤。
So the reading test is simply to count the non-glue steps in the described pipeline.

2043
03:14:40,430 --> 03:14:44,420
如果数量为零，说明 Glue 工作流是可行的，通常也是正确的选项。
Zero means blue workflows are viable and probably correct.

2044
03:14:46,094 --> 03:14:54,244
这是较新的内容，很容易被忽略，因为它包含在一个大多数人认为属于机器学习的服务中。
This is one of the newer items and it is easy to overlook because it sits inside a service most people think of as machine learning.

2045
03:14:56,078 --> 03:14:57,412
Amazon SageMaker
Amazon SageMaker

2046
03:14:58,862 --> 03:15:03,204
Unified Studio 包含了基于 Apache Airflow 的工作流功能。
Unified Studio includes workflow capability built on Apache Airflow.

2047
03:15:04,078 --> 03:15:12,272
因此，项目团队可以在与数据目录、笔记本和查询相同的地点定义其流水线。
So a project team can define its pipelines in the same place as its data catalog, its notebooks, and its queries.

2048
03:15:15,406 --> 03:15:18,084
对考试来说，关键的框架是范围。
The framing that matters for the exam is scope.

2049
03:15:18,512 --> 03:15:25,232
它适用于由单一项目负责的工作，即编写查询的人员同时也负责调度。
It suits work owned within a single project, where the people writing the queries also own the schedule.

2050
03:15:25,838 --> 03:15:33,700
它并不是被定位为像 Step Functions 或独立的 MWAA 环境那样提供全平台范围的编排器。
It is not positioned as the platform-wide orchestrator that step functions or a standalone MWAA environment provides.

2051
03:15:34,510 --> 03:15:37,636
模块 20 正确涵盖了 Unified Studio。
Module 20 covers Unified Studio properly.

2052
03:15:38,862 --> 03:15:42,980
模块 1 介绍了这项工作，这里值得详细讲解。
Module 1 introduced this work and it is worth the detail here.

2053
03:15:43,392 --> 03:15:50,468
这是因为考试大纲将设置调度器和设置事件触发器列为不同的技能。
That is because the exam guide names both setting up schedulers and setting up event triggers as separate skills.

2054
03:15:50,912 --> 03:15:53,700
措辞几乎每次都能暴露答案。
The wording gives it away nearly every time.

2055
03:15:54,638 --> 03:16:00,036
每天一次、每小时一次、每月 1 号凌晨 2 点，这些都属于调度。
Every night, hourly, on the 1st of the month at 2 in the morning are all schedules.

2056
03:16:00,846 --> 03:16:06,404
文件到达时、上传后立即执行、出现新记录时，这些都是事件。
As soon as the file arrives, immediately after upload, when a new record appears, are all events.

2057
03:16:07,022 --> 03:16:11,204
有趣的问题是那些存在调度且导致问题的题目。
The interesting questions are the ones where a schedule exists and is causing a problem.

2058
03:16:12,142 --> 03:16:19,780
这是因为解决方法通常是转为事件驱动，而问题会描述症状而不是直接说明对策。
That is because the fix is usually to become event-driven and the question will describe the symptom rather than naming the cure.

2059
03:16:21,392 --> 03:16:25,380
前两行容易混淆，但这种区别值得记住。
The first two rows get confused and the distinction is worth holding.

2060
03:16:25,712 --> 03:16:33,380
EventBridge 规则匹配流经事件总线的事件中的模式，并且出于历史原因也可以包含调度。
Event bridge rules match a pattern against events flowing through an event bus and can also carry a schedule for historical reasons.

2061
03:16:34,190 --> 03:16:42,032
EventBridge scheduler 是一个专门为调度而建立的、较新的独立功能，支持一次性调度，
Event bridge scheduler is a separate, newer capability built specifically for scheduling, supporting one-time schedules,

2062
03:16:42,192 --> 03:16:45,412
时区以及大量的独立调度任务。
time zones, and very large numbers of individual schedules.

2063
03:16:46,382 --> 03:16:54,372
因此，关于在固定时间运行某项任务的问题指向 scheduler，而关于对已发生的事情做出反应的问题指向 rules。
So a question about running something at a fixed time points at scheduler and a question about reacting to something that happened points at rules.

2064
03:16:55,662 --> 03:17:01,988
S3 这一行很重要，因为从 S3 上传到有两条路径：直接通知和 EventBridge。
The S3 row matters because there are two paths from an S3 upload, direct notifications and event bridge,

2065
03:17:02,830 --> 03:17:04,452
下一张幻灯片将它们区分开来。
and the next slide separates them.

2066
03:17:06,272 --> 03:17:11,812
两者都在对象落地时开始工作，且题目会同时提供这两个选项。
Both start work when an object lands, and questions offer both as options.

2067
03:17:12,366 --> 03:17:20,580
S3 事件通知是在存储桶本身上配置的。它针对一小组目标，并且仅根据前缀和后缀进行过滤。
S3 event notifications are configured on the bucket itself. Go to a small set of targets and filter only on prefix and suffix.

2068
03:17:21,072 --> 03:17:25,792
这涵盖了大量的实际案例，且只要适用，就是更简单的答案。
That covers a great many real cases and is a simpler answer whenever it fits.

2069
03:17:26,606 --> 03:17:33,636
EventBridge 将相同的事件接收到事件总线上，其中任何数量的规则都可以独立匹配这些事件。
EventBridge accepts the same events onto an event bus where any number of rules can match them independently of each other.

2070
03:17:34,112 --> 03:17:41,988
目标包括直接连接 Step Functions，这很重要，因为 S3 通知无法自行启动状态机。
Targets include step functions directly, which matters because S3 notifications cannot start a state machine on their own.

2071
03:17:42,734 --> 03:17:46,884
过滤时不仅可以检查键，还可以检查事件中的任何字段。
The filtering can also examine any field in the event rather than just the key.

2072
03:17:48,494 --> 03:17:57,540
EventBridge 还支持归档事件并在稍后重放，这在下游消费者出现故障且你需要重新处理某段时间的数据时非常有用。
Event Bridge additionally supports archiving events and replaying them later, which is genuinely useful when a downstream consumer was broken and you need to reprocess a period.

2073
03:17:59,182 --> 03:18:08,260
一家公司运行一个包含四个 AWS 视图作业的夜间流水线，这些作业必须按顺序执行，第二个作业后接一个 Glue 爬虫，
A company runs a nightly pipeline consisting of four AWS, view jobs that must run in order, a blue crawler after the second job,

2074
03:18:08,846 --> 03:18:13,252
最后是一个将摘要发布到 Slack 频道的 AWS Lambda 函数。
a final AWS Lambda function that posts a summary to a Slack channel.

2075
03:18:13,966 --> 03:18:17,380
该流水线目前是由每个作业上的 Cron计划启动的。
The pipeline is currently started by a crone schedule on each job.

2076
03:18:18,318 --> 03:18:22,788
每个调度的时间间隔足够大，以确保前一个作业应该已经完成。
Each schedule is set far enough apart that the previous job should have finished.

2077
03:18:23,072 --> 03:18:30,564
偶尔前面的作业运行时间过长，导致后面的作业在数据不完整的情况下启动，且不会报错。
Occasionally an early job runs long and a later job starts against incomplete data without any error being raised.

2078
03:18:31,406 --> 03:18:36,112
团队希望流水线能够是依赖驱动的，并且在失败时发出警报。
The team wants the pipeline to be dependency driven and to alert on failure.

2079
03:18:36,654 --> 03:18:38,532
数据工程师应该实现什么？
What should the data engineer implement?

2080
03:18:39,054 --> 03:18:44,708
a 将所有五个步骤放入带有条件触发的 AWS Glue workflow 中。
a move all five steps into an AWS Glue workflow with conditional triggers.

2081
03:18:45,166 --> 03:18:52,516
b 构建一个 AWS step function 状态机，由 EventBridge scheduler 启动并按顺序调用每个步骤。
b Build an AWS step function state machine invoking each step in sequence started by event bridge scheduler.

2082
03:18:53,552 --> 03:18:53,712
C。
C.

2083
03:18:54,702 --> 03:18:58,404
增加 Cron计划之间的间隔，以提供更多缓冲时间。
Increase the gaps between the cron schedules to allow more headroom.

2084
03:18:59,470 --> 03:18:59,712
D。
D.

2085
03:19:00,622 --> 03:19:05,232
将每个 Glue作业的最大并发运行数设置为 1。
Set the maximum concurrent runs on each glue job to one.

2086
03:19:06,094 --> 03:19:07,620
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2087
03:19:14,350 --> 03:19:18,052
答案是 B，而选项 A 是干扰项。
The answer is B, and option A is the distractor.

2088
03:19:18,958 --> 03:19:20,996
这个模块的设计目的就是为了让你去辨析。
This module was built to make you check.

2089
03:19:23,182 --> 03:19:30,276
对于仅包含 Glue 的流水线来说，Glue workflow 确实是更低开销的选择，而四个作业加上一个爬虫符合这一条件。
Blue workflows really are the lower overhead choice for a glue-only pipeline, and four jobs plus a crawler qualifies.

2090
03:19:31,214 --> 03:19:36,036
最后的 Lambda 函数不符合这个条件，而且只要有一个非 Glue 步骤就足够了。
The lambda function at the end does not, and one non-blue step is enough.

2091
03:19:36,942 --> 03:19:46,180
选项 C 值得注意，因为扩大间隔是团队实际在做的做法，但这属于基于时间的协调，只是在伪装成基于依赖的逻辑。
Option C deserves attention to because widening the gaps is what teams actually do, and it is timing-based coordination, pretending to be dependency-based.

2092
03:19:47,630 --> 03:19:53,124
一旦有任何东西运行时间比你预想的长，它就会失败，而这正是题目描述中发生的情况。
It fails the moment something runs longer than you guessed, which is exactly what the question describes happening.

2093
03:19:54,862 --> 03:20:03,332
考试大纲将构建具有高性能、可用性、可扩展性、弹性和容错性的流水线列为一项单一技能。
The exam guide names building pipelines for performance, availability, scalability, resiliency, and fault tolerance as a single skill.

2094
03:20:04,432 --> 03:20:06,596
这些词汇其实都在表达同一个核心概念。
That is a lot of words for one idea.

2095
03:20:06,958 --> 03:20:08,036
故障总会发生。
Failures will happen.

2096
03:20:08,558 --> 03:20:13,412
网络掉线、源头宕机、数据格式错误、达到配额限制。
Networks drop, sources go down, data arrives malformed, quotas are hit.

2097
03:20:14,350 --> 03:20:17,700
区分好流水线和坏流水线的标准在于故障发生时系统的反应。
What separates a good pipeline from a bad one is what the failure does.

2098
03:20:17,952 --> 03:20:27,460
好的流水线会停止运行而不是破坏下游数据，它会通知相关人员保留异常任务以便检查，并且可以在不产生重复内容的情况下重新运行。
A good one stops rather than corrupting downstream data, tells somebody keeps the fair work so it can be examined, can be rerun without duplicating anything.

2099
03:20:27,950 --> 03:20:36,676
坏的流水线会带着部分数据静默继续运行，这是最糟糕的结果，因为直到报告出错时才有人发现。
A bad one carries on quietly with partial data, which is the worst outcome available because nobody finds out until a report is wrong.

2100
03:20:38,286 --> 03:20:40,672
这就是题目在考查的区别点。
The callout is the distinction questions test.

2101
03:20:44,014 --> 03:20:48,100
网络超时可能会在第二次尝试时成功，所以应该进行重试。
A network timeout might succeed on the second attempt, so it should be retried.

2102
03:20:48,782 --> 03:20:57,668
日期格式错误的记录每次都会失败，因此一直重试是纯粹的浪费，甚至更糟的是，它会阻塞后续的所有内容。
A record with a malformed date will fail identically every time, so retrying it forever is pure waste and worse, it blocks everything behind it.

2103
03:20:58,478 --> 03:21:04,804
这类记录应该放入死信队列中，在保留供调查的同时，让流水线继续运行。
That record belongs in a dead letter queue where it is preserved for investigation while the pipeline continues.

2104
03:21:05,646 --> 03:21:10,916
识别出场景描述的是哪种类型的故障，就能知道它需要哪种机制。
Recognizing which kind of failure a scenario describes tells you which mechanism it needs.

2105
03:21:11,534 --> 03:21:13,988
最后一点又回到了第二章的内容。
And the last point connects back to module 2.

2106
03:21:14,894 --> 03:21:21,700
在不覆盖而是追加内容的任务上进行重试，会将明显的失败变成隐蔽的重复数据。
Retreeze on a job that appends without overwriting turn one visible failure into silent duplicate data.

2107
03:21:23,278 --> 03:21:28,708
这出现在多个领域的限流问题中，而错误的选项总是很有诱惑力的。
This appears in throttling questions across several domains, and the wrong answer is always tempting.

2108
03:21:29,166 --> 03:21:35,844
当服务返回限流错误时，直觉是更积极地重试，以确保工作能完成。
When a service returns a throttling error, the instinct is to retry more aggressively so the work still gets done.

2109
03:21:36,782 --> 03:21:40,740
但这会增加一个已经告诉你负载过重的服务的负担。
That adds load to a service already telling you it has too much.

2110
03:21:41,070 --> 03:21:44,836
而且在拥有大量客户端的系统中，这会导致同步的重试风暴。
And in a system with many clients, it produces a synchronized retry storm.

2111
03:21:48,014 --> 03:21:50,660
退避会让每次尝试之间的间隔越来越长。
Backoff spaces attempts further apart each time.

2112
03:21:51,406 --> 03:21:57,668
抖动增加随机性，这样即使一千个客户端同时失败，也不会在同一瞬间同时重试。
Jitter adds randomness so that a thousand clients failing simultaneously do not all retry at the same instant.

2113
03:21:58,176 --> 03:22:03,780
如果题目提供“增加重试次数”和“添加退避”两个选项，那么答案就是退避。
If a question offers increasing the retry count against adding back-off, back off is the answer.

2114
03:22:05,390 --> 03:22:10,788
考试指南提到使用通知服务发送警报，所以这两个选项经常出现。
The exam guide names using notification services to send alerts, so both of these appear regularly.

2115
03:22:11,406 --> 03:22:13,604
区别在于它们各自承载的内容不同。
The distinction is what each one is carrying.

2116
03:22:14,222 --> 03:22:18,468
Amazon SNS 承载的是多个方可能都想知道的消息。
Amazon SNS carries news that several parties might want to know about.

2117
03:22:18,656 --> 03:22:23,012
它会同时推送给所有这些方，且不记录后续发生了什么。
It pushes to all of them at once with no memory of what happened afterwards.

2118
03:22:23,630 --> 03:22:26,916
如果订阅者不可用，它就会错过那条消息。
If a subscriber was unavailable, it missed that message.

2119
03:22:28,974 --> 03:22:36,292
Amazon SQS 承载的是只有一个消费者应该执行的工作，并持久保存直到有人真正去处理它。
Amazon SQS carries work that exactly one consumer should perform held durably until somebody actually does it.

2120
03:22:36,736 --> 03:22:41,796
这种组合模式在实际架构中经常出现。
The pattern in the call out combines them and appears constantly in real architectures.

2121
03:22:42,766 --> 03:22:48,676
一个 SNS 主题发布一个事件，多个 SQS 队列订阅这个主题。
One SNS topic publishes an event, several SQS queues subscribe to that topic.

2122
03:22:49,056 --> 03:22:56,068
每个下游系统按自己的节奏从自己的队列中消费，不会影响到其他任何系统。
Each downstream system consumes from its own queue at its own pace without affecting any of the others.

2123
03:22:57,518 --> 03:23:02,148
可见性超时是作为诊断问题最可能出现的机制。
The visibility timeout is the mechanic most likely to appear as a diagnosis question.

2124
03:23:02,766 --> 03:23:10,916
当消费者获取消息时，SQS 会隐藏它而不是删除它，这样如果消费者崩溃了，消息就会返回给其他人。
When a consumer takes a message, SQS hides it rather than deleting it so that if the consumer dies, the message returns for somebody else.

2125
03:23:11,534 --> 03:23:14,948
假设超时时间是 30 秒，而处理需要 45 秒。
Suppose the timeout is 30 seconds and processing takes 45.

2126
03:23:15,936 --> 03:23:20,900
在第一个消费者仍在处理时，消息就会重新出现。
The message reappears while the first consumer is still working on it.

2127
03:23:22,382 --> 03:23:26,020
第二个消费者会接手它，导致工作被执行两次。
A second consumer picks it up and the work happens twice.

2128
03:23:27,790 --> 03:23:29,028
没有任何报错。
Nothing errors.

2129
03:23:29,870 --> 03:23:37,508
解决方法是将可见性超时提高到高于实际处理时间，或者在处理过程中延长它。
The fix is to raise the visibility timeout above the realistic processing time or to extend it while processing.

2130
03:23:38,510 --> 03:23:43,716
描述间歇性重复处理的问题通常就是在描述这种情况。
Questions describing intermittent duplicate processing are usually describing this.

2131
03:23:45,486 --> 03:23:51,776
一个流水线通过调用合作伙伴 API 的 AWS Lambda 函数，从 Amazon SQS 队列中读取消息。
A pipeline reads messages from an Amazon SQS queue with an AWS Lambda function that calls a partner.

2132
03:23:52,430 --> 03:23:54,372
每条消息对应一个 API。
API for each message.

2133
03:23:54,816 --> 03:24:00,068
合作伙伴的 API 有速率限制，在繁忙时段会返回限流错误。
The partner API is rate limited and returns throttling errors during busy periods.

2134
03:24:00,416 --> 03:24:05,380
团队将 Lambda 函数配置为 10 次重试，且重试之间没有延迟。
The team has configured the Lambda function with 10 retrees and no delay between them.

2135
03:24:05,902 --> 03:24:10,308
在繁忙期间，队列堆积，限流错误急剧增加。
During busy periods, the queue backs up, throttling errors increase sharply.

2136
03:24:10,816 --> 03:24:17,700
由于未配置死信队列，一些消息最终超过最大接收次数并丢失。
Some messages eventually exceed the maximum receive count and are lost because no dead letter queue is configured.

2137
03:24:18,286 --> 03:24:21,092
哪种组合方案最能解决这个问题？
Which combination of changes best addresses the problem?

2138
03:24:23,758 --> 03:24:26,628
a. 将 Lambda 的重试次数从 10 次增加到 30 次。
Increase the lambda retry count from 10 to 30.

2139
03:24:26,976 --> 03:24:34,276
b. 对 API 调用添加带抖动的指数退避，并在 SQS 队列上配置死信队列。
b. Add exponential backoff with jitter to the AP i calls and configure a dead letter queue on the SQS queue.

2140
03:24:34,896 --> 03:24:35,216
C。
C.

2141
03:24:35,616 --> 03:24:40,868
c. 增加 Lambda 函数的预留并发量，以便并行处理更多消息。
Increase the lambda function's reserved concurrency so more messages are processed in parallel.

2142
03:24:41,230 --> 03:24:41,536
d。
D.

2143
03:24:42,542 --> 03:24:48,804
d. 将 SQS 从标准模式切换到 FIFO 模式以控制处理顺序。
Switch the SQSQ from standard to FIFO to control the processing order.

2144
03:24:49,550 --> 03:24:50,564
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2145
03:24:57,262 --> 03:24:59,716
答案是 B，注意一下题目结构。
The answer is B and notice the structure.

2146
03:25:00,176 --> 03:25:07,776
选项 A 和 C 都是通过增加流量来应对被限流的服务，只是手段不同。
Options A and C both respond to a throttled service by sending it more traffic, differing only in how.

2147
03:25:08,718 --> 03:25:14,468
这是考试在测试你是否把“限流”理解成了容量问题，而它并不是。
That is the exam testing whether throttling reads to you as a capacity problem, which it is not.

2148
03:25:14,926 --> 03:25:16,420
这是一个节奏控制问题。
It is a pacing problem.

2149
03:25:17,358 --> 03:25:20,004
B 的后半部分和前半部分同样重要。
The second half of B matters as much as the first.

2150
03:25:20,846 --> 03:25:30,532
退避机制能减少消息频繁失败的次数，而死信队列意味着即使仍然失败的消息也会被保留下来，而不是静默丢失。
Backoff stops the messages failing so often, and the dead letter queue means that a message which still fails is kept rather than silently lost.

2151
03:25:31,502 --> 03:25:39,428
题目明确告诉你消息正在丢失，这是一个隐藏在性能问题中的数据丢失问题。
The question told you explicitly that messages are being lost, which is a data loss problem hiding inside a performance question.

2152
03:25:41,102 --> 03:25:48,164
第四点值得深入思考，因为它能识破有经验和没经验的团队。
The fourth point is worth dwelling on because it catches experienced teams as well as inexperienced ones.

2153
03:25:48,750 --> 03:25:53,700
所有的监控设置都会对“失败”发出警报，但很少有警报能针对“缺失”发出。
Every monitoring setup alerts on failures, far fewer alert on absence.

2154
03:25:54,510 --> 03:26:02,576
如果一个计划任务根本没有触发，那是因为在部署期间某个触发器被禁用，或者上游依赖项
If a scheduled job simply never fires, that is because a trigger was disabled during a deployment or an upstream dependency

2155
03:26:02,766 --> 03:26:09,444
静默消失了。没有可捕获的错误，看不到失败的执行记录，也不会收到通知。
silently disappeared. There is no error to catch, there is no failed execution to see and no notification to receive.

2156
03:26:09,776 --> 03:26:15,268
数据不再更新，直到几天后有人发现某个数字不对时才被注意到。
The data just stops being fresh and somebody notices days later when a number looks wrong.

2157
03:26:16,078 --> 03:26:24,260
当任务在预期时间内未成功时发出警报可以捕捉到这种情况，模块 14 涵盖了如何在 CloudWatch 中实现它。
Alerting when a job has not succeeded within an expected window catches that, and module 14 covers how to implement it in CloudWatch.

2158
03:26:27,534 --> 03:26:29,700
第一点是关于理念的。
The first point is the philosophical one.

2159
03:26:30,190 --> 03:26:33,924
停止处理通常比在不完整的数据上继续运行要好。
Stopping is almost always better than continuing on partial data.

2160
03:26:35,566 --> 03:26:43,908
回填是那种没人去专门设计，但每个人最终都需要的东西，通常是在发现 Bug 后紧急进行的。
Backfilling is one of those things nobody designs for and everybody eventually needs, usually urgently after a bug is found.

2161
03:26:45,294 --> 03:26:47,300
前两点构成了整个设计逻辑。
The first two points are the whole design.

2162
03:26:48,238 --> 03:26:56,004
如果流水线在内部计算昨天的日期，那它只能处理昨天的数据，这意味着要修复一周的错误数据时，就得在压力下去修改代码。
A pipeline that computes yesterday's date internally can only ever process yesterday, so recovering a week of bad data means editing code under pressure.

2163
03:26:56,526 --> 03:27:00,420
而将日期作为参数传入的流水线可以指向任何一天。
A pipeline taking the date as a parameter can be pointed at any day.

2164
03:27:01,166 --> 03:27:07,236
结合模块 2 中提到的覆盖目标分区，重跑任务就会变得安全且可重复。
Combine that with overwriting the target partition from module 2 and reruns become safe and repeatable.

2165
03:27:08,014 --> 03:27:09,508
最后一点是实操层面的。
The last point is practical.

2166
03:27:10,126 --> 03:27:15,088
通过启动 90 个并发运行来回填 90 天的数据，会节流它们写入的任何目标。
Backfilling 90 days by launching 90 concurrent runs will throttle whatever they write to.

2167
03:27:16,462 --> 03:27:19,844
一个每日流水线将销售数据加载到 Amazon Redshift 中。
A daily pipeline loads sales data into Amazon Redshift.

2168
03:27:20,110 --> 03:27:26,928
如果源文件在早上 6 点前没到，目前的流水线仍会继续运行，处理现有的任何部分数据。
If the source file has not arrived by 6 in the morning, the pipeline currently proceeds anyway with whatever partial data is present.

2169
03:27:27,278 --> 03:27:30,180
生成的日报就是基于不完整的数据。
The daily report is produced from incomplete figures.

2170
03:27:30,990 --> 03:27:36,356
财务部门曾两次在不知数据不全的情况下，根据错误的数据做出决策。
Finance has twice made decisions on incorrect numbers without knowing they were incomplete.

2171
03:27:36,688 --> 03:27:41,124
团队希望流水线能正确处理延迟或缺失的文件。
The team wants the pipeline to handle a late or missing file correctly.

2172
03:27:42,208 --> 03:27:44,196
最合适的方案是什么？
What is the most appropriate design?

2173
03:27:44,814 --> 03:27:49,732
A. 在上午晚些时候运行流水线，这样文件更有可能已经送达。
a run the pipeline later in the morning so the file is more likely to have arrived.

2174
03:27:53,294 --> 03:28:00,388
B. 让流水线基于文件到达触发，配合 Step Functions 等待，并在截止日期前文件未到达时发出警报。
Make the pipeline event driven on file arrival with a step functions wait and an alert if the file has not arrived by a deadline.

2175
03:28:00,928 --> 03:28:06,148
C. 加载部分数据，但在报告中注明可能不完整。
C. Load the partial data but add a note to the report saying it may be incomplete.

2176
03:28:06,688 --> 03:28:06,928
D。
D.

2177
03:28:07,566 --> 03:28:11,844
在继续之前，采用指数退避重试加载三次。
Retry the load three times with exponential backoff before continuing.

2178
03:28:13,248 --> 03:28:14,372
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2179
03:28:20,782 --> 03:28:22,208
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2180
03:28:22,830 --> 03:28:25,700
这个场景是故意与前一个场景进行对比的。
And this scenario pairs with the previous one deliberately.

2181
03:28:26,478 --> 03:28:34,980
在那个例子中，指数退避是正确答案，因为合作伙伴 AP 是暂时拒绝请求并会恢复的。
There, exponential backoff was the correct answer because the partner AP, I was temporarily refusing requests and would recover.

2182
03:28:35,534 --> 03:28:37,348
而在这里，根本没有任何东西失败。
Here, nothing has failed at all.

2183
03:28:38,318 --> 03:28:45,444
文件只是还没出现，无论你重试多少次加载，都无法让上游系统更快产生它。
The file simply does not exist yet, and no amount of retrying a load causes an upstream system to produce it sooner.

2184
03:28:46,190 --> 03:28:49,252
识别出这种区别就是可以迁移的技能。
Recognizing that distinction is the transferable skill.

2185
03:28:50,062 --> 03:28:59,204
选项 A 是场景 1 中出现的模式再次出现，它是靠猜测时间而非根据现实做出反应，所以同样是错误的。
Option A is the pattern from scenario 1 appearing again, guessing at timing rather than reacting to reality, and it is wrong for the same reason.

2186
03:29:00,910 --> 03:29:05,892
第四点是既会导致生产事故、也会出现在考试题目中的内容。
The fourth point is the one that produces both production incidents and exam questions.

2187
03:29:06,606 --> 03:29:09,540
在系统层面，并行并不是免费的。
Parallelism is not free at the system level.

2188
03:29:09,838 --> 03:29:11,716
它只是改变了瓶颈所在的位置。
It just relocates the bottleneck.

2189
03:29:13,454 --> 03:29:20,448
将 Step Functions 的 map 扇出到一千个并发的 Lambda 函数，每个函数都建立数据库连接。
Fan out a step functions map to a thousand concurrent lambda functions, each opening a database connection.

2190
03:29:20,928 --> 03:29:25,956
在 Lambda 耗尽容量之前，你早就把数据库的连接限制撑爆了。
You will exhaust the database's connection limit long before lambda runs out of capacity.

2191
03:29:26,368 --> 03:29:28,608
Lambda 并不是约束条件。
Nothing about lambda was the constraint.

2192
03:29:28,910 --> 03:29:31,684
预置并发是正确的答案。
Reserve concurrency is the deliberate answer.

2193
03:29:32,558 --> 03:29:41,508
将函数的并发限制在比如 50 以内，可以在牺牲整体处理时间的前提下，保护其背后的数据库。
Capping a function at say 50 concurrent executions protects the database behind it at the cost of the work taking longer overall.

2194
03:29:41,968 --> 03:29:46,128
当依赖项与其他任何东西共享时，这种权衡通常是正确的。
That trade is usually correct when the dependency is shared with anything else.

2195
03:29:46,368 --> 03:29:50,436
这正是第 5 模块中 Redshift 连接场景的典型情况。
It is exactly the shape of the redshift connection scenario from module 5.

2196
03:29:52,014 --> 03:29:58,756
数据流水线的容灾与应用的容灾不同，这里的提示解释了原因。
Disaster recovery for data pipelines differs from disaster recovery for applications, and the callout explains why.

2197
03:29:59,246 --> 03:30:04,804
应用程序的数据库是核心真相，所以必须进行复制，否则就会丢失。
An application's database is the truth, so it must be replicated or you lose it.

2198
03:30:06,766 --> 03:30:09,892
精选的分析表是派生出来的。
A curated analytics table is derived.

2199
03:30:10,510 --> 03:30:16,740
因此，只要你保留原始输入和生成它们的代码，它根本不需要复制。
So it does not have to be replicated at all, provided you retain the raw inputs and the code that produced them.

2200
03:30:17,390 --> 03:30:19,012
这改变了你需要保护的对象。
That changes what you protect.

2201
03:30:19,248 --> 03:30:27,428
Amazon S3 中的原始落地区才真正需要跨区域复制，而下游的一切都可以重建。
The raw landing zone in Amazon S3 becomes the thing that genuinely needs cross-region replication, and everything downstream is something you rebuild.

2202
03:30:28,302 --> 03:30:35,172
定义代码化流水线（第 7 模块涵盖的内容）是让重建变得切实可行而非仅仅是理论的基础。
Defining pipelines as code, which module 7 covers, is what makes rebuilding realistic rather than theoretical.

2203
03:30:36,014 --> 03:30:38,528
前两点确定了你所负责的范围。
The first two bullets set the boundary of what you own.

2204
03:30:39,160 --> 03:30:42,148
托管服务已经跨越了可用性区域。
Managed services already span availability zones.

2205
03:30:43,054 --> 03:30:44,868
一个 EMR 集群
An EMR cluster

2206
03:30:45,614 --> 03:30:47,716
或者一个 MSK 集群
or an MSK cluster

2207
03:30:49,168 --> 03:30:53,188
都位于你的子网中，因此它的弹性取决于你的设计决策。
sits in your subnets, so its resilience is your design decision.

2208
03:30:54,894 --> 03:31:01,220
大型组织按团队或环境划分账户，考试内容也反映了这一点。
Larger organizations separate accounts by team or by environment and the exam reflects that.

2209
03:31:01,966 --> 03:31:06,180
可行的模式是集中协调与分布式执行。
The workable pattern is central coordination with distributed execution.

2210
03:31:06,574 --> 03:31:11,108
一个账户持有描述“在什么顺序发生什么事情”的状态机。
One account holds the state machines that describe what happens in what order.

2211
03:31:12,014 --> 03:31:16,996
每一步都在实际拥有数据和计算资源的账户中承担角色。
Each step assumes a role in whichever account actually owns the data and the compute.

2212
03:31:17,328 --> 03:31:22,020
这能让流水线定义集中在一个地方，这是平台团队所期望的。
That keeps the pipeline definition in one place, which is what a platform team wants.

2213
03:31:22,702 --> 03:31:27,588
与此同时，处理过程保留在数据旁边，这是性能和成本要求的。
Meanwhile, the processing stays next to the data, which is what performance and cost want.

2214
03:31:28,398 --> 03:31:37,284
EventBridge 是处理事件的等效机制，因为一个账户中的总线可以将匹配的事件转发到另一个账户中的总线。
Event bridge is the equivalent mechanism for events because a bus in one account can forward matching events to a bus in another.

2215
03:31:38,542 --> 03:31:42,980
应用第 1 模块中的计费单位规则，这里的模式就很清晰了。
Apply the billing unit rule from module 1 and the pattern here is clear.

2216
03:31:44,846 --> 03:31:45,956
Step Functions。
Step functions.

2217
03:31:47,598 --> 03:31:54,884
按状态转换标准收费，因此一个包含十几个步骤且每晚运行一次的流水线，成本极低。
Standard charges per state transition, so a pipeline with a dozen steps running once nightly costs a genuinely trivial amount.

2218
03:31:55,470 --> 03:32:01,168
这就是为什么在考试题目中，几乎从不以成本为由来反驳使用 Step Functions。
That is why cost is almost never the argument against step functions in an exam question.

2219
03:32:01,820 --> 03:32:09,924
预置型 MWAA 是表中的特例，无论是否运行任何 DAG，都会持续对环境计费。
Provisioned MWAA is the outlier on this table, billing continuously for an environment whether any DAG runs or not.

2220
03:32:10,734 --> 03:32:16,548
在 2025 年底无服务器技术出现之前，这是考试中反对它的标准论点。
That was the standard exam argument against it until serverless arrived in late 2025.

2221
03:32:16,928 --> 03:32:20,388
DU 工作流这一行值得单独记住。
The DU workflows row is worth remembering separately.

2222
03:32:22,190 --> 03:32:29,728
当流水线完全由 GU 组件组成时，增加一个完全不额外计费的编排层是一个巨大的优势。
Adding an orchestration layer that costs nothing extra at all is a real advantage when the pipeline happens to be entirely GU components.

2223
03:32:30,414 --> 03:32:32,996
这个选项很容易被忽略。
It is easy to forget as an option.

2224
03:32:34,702 --> 03:32:43,524
一个编排团队在 Amazon EC2 上基于自管理的 Airflow 部署运行约 40 个 Apache Airflow DAGs。
An orchestration team runs about 40 Apache Airflow DAGs on a self-managed Airflow deployment on Amazon EC2.

2225
03:32:45,006 --> 03:32:50,688
这些 DAGs 使用了混合的 AWS 算子和两个本地部署系统的算子。
The DAGs use a mix of AWS operators and operators for two on-premises systems.

2226
03:32:51,150 --> 03:32:53,668
大约一半的 DAGs 每周运行一次。
Roughly half the DAGs run once a week.

2227
03:32:54,414 --> 03:32:57,028
其余的每天运行，并在几分钟内完成。
The rest run daily and complete in minutes.

2228
03:32:57,966 --> 03:33:04,516
团队花费大量时间去修补 Airflow、升级元数据库以及恢复调度器。
The team spends significant time patching airflow, upgrading the metadata database, and recovering the scheduler.

2229
03:33:04,910 --> 03:33:09,636
他们希望减少这些工作量，并停止为大部分时间处于闲置状态的容量付费。
They want to reduce that work and stop paying for capacity that is idle most of the time.

2230
03:33:10,254 --> 03:33:12,036
DAGs 必须保持运行。
The DAGs must keep running.

2231
03:33:13,326 --> 03:33:14,564
团队应该怎么做？
What should the team do?

2232
03:33:16,654 --> 03:33:20,900
A. 将 DAGs 重写为 AWS Step Functions 状态机。
rewrite the DAGs as AWS Step Functions state machines.

2233
03:33:21,488 --> 03:33:28,100
B. 迁移到 Amazon MWAA 无服务器版本，保留现有的 Airflow 工作流。
b migrate to Amazon MWAA serverless, keeping the existing airflow workflows.

2234
03:33:28,768 --> 03:33:34,660
C. 迁移到为峰值负载设计的预置型 Amazon MWAA 环境。
C. Migrate to a provisioned Amazon MWAA environment sized for peak load.

2235
03:33:35,278 --> 03:33:42,208
D. 将 Airflow 部署迁移到具有集群自动扩缩容功能的 Amazon EKS 容器上。
D. Move the Airflow deployment to containers on Amazon EKSS with cluster autoscaling.

2236
03:33:43,648 --> 03:33:44,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2237
03:33:51,248 --> 03:33:57,156
答案是 B，而且这个问题不可能在 2025 年 11 月之前出现。
The answer is B, and this question could not have been asked before November 2025.

2238
03:33:57,568 --> 03:33:59,168
预置型 MWAA
Provision MWAA

2239
03:34:00,128 --> 03:34:02,180
原本会是最好的可选答案。
would have been the best available answer.

2240
03:34:02,688 --> 03:34:10,244
因为它只能满足两个要求中的一个，因为无论 DAGs 是否运行，环境都会持续计费。
It only satisfies one of the two stated requirements because the environment builds continuously whether DAGs run or not.

2241
03:34:11,054 --> 03:34:14,692
MWAA 无服务器版本能同时满足这两个要求。
MW AA serverless satisfies both.

2242
03:34:16,174 --> 03:34:28,196
注意关于本地部署算子的细节，这是在做一些隐形的任务。它强调了这部分必须保留为 Airflow。因为 Airflow 的算子生态系统可以连接到各种外部系统，而 Step Functions 不行。
Note the detail about on-premises operators, which is doing quiet work. It reinforces that this must stay airflow. Since the airflow operator ecosystem reaches systems, step functions cannot.

2243
03:34:29,070 --> 03:34:34,308
这和第三模块中现有 Kafka 指向 MSK 的逻辑是一样的。
That is the same signal as existing Kafka pointing at MSK in module 3.

2244
03:34:35,886 --> 03:34:39,460
这个特别标注是一个考试直接考查的设计点。
The callout is a design point that questions test directly.

2245
03:34:40,302 --> 03:34:47,684
将警报步骤作为工作流的最后一个状态来发送通知，在工作流正常完成时效果很好。
Putting the alerting step inside the workflow as a final state that sends a notification works perfectly when the workflow completes.

2246
03:34:48,238 --> 03:34:55,568
但如果工作流中途失败或根本没启动，这个操作就毫无作用，因为通知步骤根本没被触发。
It does nothing at all when the workflow fails halfway or never starts because the notification step is simply never reached.

2247
03:34:55,808 --> 03:34:58,500
从外部进行响应可以捕捉到这些情况。
Reacting from outside catches those cases.

2248
03:34:59,008 --> 03:35:05,956
一个 EventBridge 规则，监控执行状态变为失败的变化，无论流水线的哪个环节出问题都会触发。
An event bridge rule, watching for a failed execution state change, fires regardless of where in the pipeline things went wrong.

2249
03:35:06,448 --> 03:35:12,004
结合最后一点提到的“缺失警报”，你就能覆盖两类故障情况。
Combine that with the absence alarm on the last bullet, and you cover both categories of failure.

2250
03:35:12,368 --> 03:35:16,528
即：报错的流水线，以及悄无声息停止运行的流水线。
The pipeline that broke and the pipeline that quietly stopped existing.

2251
03:35:17,966 --> 03:35:19,044
Step Functions。
Step functions.

2252
03:35:19,648 --> 03:35:22,500
执行历史是另一个值得了解的内容。
Execution history is the other thing worth knowing.

2253
03:35:23,342 --> 03:35:29,924
这是因为它保留了每个状态的输入和输出，这让故障在几天后也能被诊断出来。
That is because it retains the input and output of every state, which is what makes a failure diagnosable days later.

2254
03:35:31,662 --> 03:35:39,812
一旦流水线包含几十个步骤，单一定义就会变得难以阅读，且每个编辑它的团队都会与其它团队产生冲突。
Once a pipeline passes a few dozen steps, a single definition becomes unreadable and every team editing it confits with every other team.

2255
03:35:40,430 --> 03:35:44,292
嵌套解决了函数在普通代码中解决的同样问题。
Nesting solves the same problem that functions solve in ordinary code.

2256
03:35:45,198 --> 03:35:53,956
父状态机协调整体序列，而每个阶段都是由负责该阶段的团队拥有的子状态机。
A parent state machine coordinates the overall sequence, and each stage is a child state machine owned by whichever team is responsible for that stage.

2257
03:35:54,288 --> 03:36:02,436
父级使用本模块前面提到的 run-a 作业模式等待每个子项，因此子项的故障能正确传递。
The parent waits for each child using the run-a job pattern from earlier in this module, so failure in a child propagates properly.

2258
03:36:03,328 --> 03:36:13,156
当题目描述有多个团队为同一个流水线贡献阶段时，通常采用组合式设计，而不是一个庞大的共享定义。
When a question describes several teams contributing stages to one pipeline, composition is usually the intended answer rather than one enormous shared definition.

2259
03:36:13,838 --> 03:36:16,196
最后一项的警告是真实的。
The warning on the last bullet is real.

2260
03:36:16,974 --> 03:36:23,876
两个互相等待的工作流都会永远等待下去，而且表现出来的症状像是卡死而非错误。
Two workflows that each wait for the other will both wait forever, and the symptom looks like a hang rather than an error.

2261
03:36:25,134 --> 03:36:33,028
这张表将本模块中的各种故障模式汇总到一个查询表中，最后一行值得回顾一下模块 2。
This table collects the failure modes from across the module into one lookup, and the last row is worth reconnecting to module 2.

2262
03:36:33,582 --> 03:36:37,028
Glue作业的最大并发运行次数默认是 1。
A glue jobs maximum concurrent runs defaults to 1.

2263
03:36:37,838 --> 03:36:46,788
每个文件触发一次，如果有两个文件在同一分钟内到达，第二个触发就会被直接拒绝，而不是排在第一个后面。
Trigger it once per file, have two files land within the same minute, and the second trigger is rejected outright rather than queued behind the first.

2264
03:36:47,566 --> 03:36:54,052
流水线中任何地方都不会出现错误，因为从触发器的角度来看，它完全按照要求执行了。
No error appears anywhere in the pipeline because from the trigger's point of view, it did exactly what it was asked to

2265
03:36:54,798 --> 03:36:58,020
文件只是从未被处理，而且没有任何提示。
do. The file is simply never processed and nothing says so.

2266
03:36:58,574 --> 03:37:06,564
这种事件驱动的触发与未更改的并发默认值的组合，是生产环境中非常常见的 Bug，也是一道合理的考试题。
That combination of event-driven triggering and an untouched concurrency default is a genuinely common production bug and a fair exam question.

2267
03:37:07,086 --> 03:37:11,428
第一行是本模块开始时提到的内容，也是最常见的一种。
The first row is the one this module opened with, and it is the most common of all.

2268
03:37:12,910 --> 03:37:18,660
Step Functions 的状态机通过为每个文件调用一个 Lambda 函数来处理文件。
A step function's state machine processes files by invoking a lambda function per file.

2269
03:37:19,022 --> 03:37:20,964
它已经稳定运行了一年。
It has run reliably for a year.

2270
03:37:21,582 --> 03:37:27,300
上周，上游系统开始发送少量带有错误头的报文。
Last week, the upstream system began sending a small number of files with a malformed header.

2271
03:37:27,854 --> 03:37:31,408
状态机现在会在遇到第一个错误头的文件时停止。
The state machine now stops on the first malformed file.

2272
03:37:31,918 --> 03:37:38,688
该执行过程中后续的所有有效文件都未被处理，团队直到第二天早上才发现问题。
Every valid file behind it in that execution is left unprocessed, and the team discovers the problem the following morning.

2273
03:37:38,928 --> 03:37:42,208
重试配置为三次尝试并带有退避机制。
Retrees are configured with three attempts and back off.

2274
03:37:42,830 --> 03:37:44,580
最合适的更改是什么？
What is the most appropriate change?

2275
03:37:44,942 --> 03:37:49,732
a. 将重试次数从 3 增加到 10，以便文件最终成功。
a Increase the retree attempts from 3 to 10 so the file eventually succeeds.

2276
03:37:50,608 --> 03:37:57,316
b. 在状态上添加 catch，将失败的文件路由到死信位置并继续处理其余内容。
b Add a catch on the state that routes failed files to a dead letter location and continues processing the rest.

2277
03:37:58,208 --> 03:37:58,528
c。
c.

2278
03:37:59,118 --> 03:38:02,532
d. 删除重试配置，让状态机更快报错。
Remove the retry configuration so the state machine fails faster.

2279
03:38:04,494 --> 03:38:08,292
e. 将状态机的模式从标准切换到 Express 工作流。
D switch the state machine from standard to express workflows.

2280
03:38:09,102 --> 03:38:10,180
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

2281
03:38:16,814 --> 03:38:21,188
答案是 B，决定这一项的词汇是“格式错误的标头”。
The answer is B and the phrase that decides it is malformed header.

2282
03:38:21,518 --> 03:38:27,908
那是文件的永久属性，不是瞬时故障，所以无论重试多少次结果都不会改变。
That is a permanent property of the file, not a transient condition, so no number of retrees changes the outcome.

2283
03:38:28,160 --> 03:38:33,508
之前的机制幻灯片就明确了这种区别，而这个场景就是在考查这一点。
The mechanism slide earlier made exactly this distinction and this scenario tests it.

2284
03:38:34,318 --> 03:38:36,100
注意题目中提到的第二个危害，
Notice the second harm in the question,

2285
03:38:37,006 --> 03:38:40,484
就是在错误文件之后的有效文件无法被处理。
which is that valid files behind the bad one go unprocessed.

2286
03:38:41,262 --> 03:38:46,980
捕获机制不只是处理坏文件，它还能防止一个错误的记录阻塞后续所有内容。
Catch does not just handle the bad file, it stops one bad record from holding up everything behind it.

2287
03:38:47,690 --> 03:38:52,996
这种阻塞行为与第三模块中的 Lambda 有毒记录问题性质相同。
That blocking behavior is the same shape as the Lambda Poison Record problem from module 3.

2288
03:38:54,720 --> 03:39:02,404
一共 5 道题，其中第四题是本模块中区分两个看似相同的选项最频繁的题目。
5 questions, and the fourth is the one that separates two otherwise identical options more often than any other in this module.

2289
03:39:02,800 --> 03:39:05,600
瞬时故障需要采用带退避机制的重试。
Transient failures want retry with back-off.

2290
03:39:06,160 --> 03:39:09,796
永久性故障需要路由到可以被检查的地方。
Permanent failures want routing to somewhere they can be inspected.

2291
03:39:10,670 --> 03:39:14,596
搞混这两者会导致无限浪费或数据丢失。
Getting that backwards produces either infinite waste or lost data.

2292
03:39:15,040 --> 03:39:18,212
第五题是考试最看重的判断力。
The fifth is the judgment the exam rewards most.

2293
03:39:18,510 --> 03:39:25,188
一个显式报错的流水线只是个麻烦，而一个仅处理部分数据就成功的流水线则是业务问题。
A pipeline that fails visibly is a nuisance, and a pipeline that succeeds on partial data is a business problem.

2294
03:39:26,126 --> 03:39:31,204
当某个选项以延迟为代价来保证正确性时，它通常就是预设的答案。
When an option preserves correctness at the cost of a delay, it is usually the intended answer.

2295
03:39:32,526 --> 03:39:39,076
下一个模块结束。领域 1 包括编程概念、Lambda 调优和基础设施即代码。
Next module closes. Domain 1 with programming concepts, lambda tuning, and infrastructure as code.

2296
03:39:40,654 --> 03:39:46,596
这个模块结束了领域 1，它涵盖的独立技能比课程中任何其他模块都要多。
This module closes domain 1 and it covers 13 separate skills more than any other in the course.

2297
03:39:48,718 --> 03:39:56,164
这听起来有点吓人，但并不是因为考试大纲中用“描述”而非“实现”来描述其中的几项。
That sounds alarming and it is not because several of them are described in the exam guide with the word describe rather than implement.

2298
03:39:57,134 --> 03:40:02,116
要求你识别分布式计算的含义，而不是去写一个调度器。
You are asked to recognize what distributed computing means, not to write a scheduler.

2299
03:40:02,830 --> 03:40:11,044
考试真正考核的是 Lambda 配置、基础设施即代码，以及流水线代码如何进入生产环境。
What the exam does test properly is Lambda configuration, infrastructure as code, and how pipeline code reaches production.

2300
03:40:11,406 --> 03:40:13,668
这三项占据了这里的绝大部分分数。
Those three carry most of the marks here.

2301
03:40:14,574 --> 03:40:20,356
四个实战场景和一项关于哪些开发工具在考核范围内的重要修正。
Four worked scenarios and one important correction about which developer tools are actually in scope.

2302
03:40:21,902 --> 03:40:26,404
值得记住的区别在于“编写代码”与“工程化实现”。
The distinction worth holding is between writing code and engineering it.

2303
03:40:26,800 --> 03:40:30,084
考试不会要求你写出 Python 代码。
Nobody will ask you to produce Python on this exam.

2304
03:40:30,560 --> 03:40:34,500
整个考试中没有任何代码编辑器，也没有任何语法问题。
There is no code editor and no syntax question anywhere in it.

2305
03:40:35,470 --> 03:40:43,076
你要回答的是流水线代码是否经过版本控制、测试、重复部署以及监控。
What you are asked is whether pipeline code is version controlled, tested, deployed repeatedly, and monitored.

2306
03:40:44,046 --> 03:40:50,756
即使是一个人下午写完的 300 行 PySpark，它也是生产级别的软件。
A pipeline is production software even when it is 300 lines of PySpark that one person wrote in an afternoon.

2307
03:40:51,886 --> 03:40:59,620
这个逻辑解释了为什么基础设施即代码和持续交付会出现在数据考试中，这往往会让一些人感到意外。
That framing explains why infrastructure as code and continuous delivery appear in a data exam at all, which surprises people.

2308
03:41:00,526 --> 03:41:05,572
一个仅仅因为有人在控制台上操作过一次才存在的转换过程就是一种隐患。
A transformation that exists only because somebody kicked through a console once is a liability.

2309
03:41:05,840 --> 03:41:11,840
它无法被审查，无法在另一个区域重建，而且在那个人离职后也无法解释。
It cannot be reviewed, cannot be rebuilt in another region, and cannot be explained after that person leaves.

2310
03:41:12,160 --> 03:41:16,516
考试将其视为一种隐患，并给那些能消除这种隐患的选项加分。
The exam treats it as a liability and marks the options that remove it.

2311
03:41:17,966 --> 03:41:21,764
这里的提醒是关于如何分配你时间的实用建议。
The call out is the practical advice for how to spend your time here.

2312
03:41:22,254 --> 03:41:28,004
特定语言的语法明确被列为超出范围，不要求考生掌握。
Language specific syntax is explicitly listed as out of scope for the target candidate.

2313
03:41:28,430 --> 03:41:32,868
所以没人会考你是否记得某个方法名或导入路径。
So nobody is testing whether you remember a method name or an import path.

2314
03:41:33,326 --> 03:41:36,964
SQL 是例外，它的处理方式不同。
SQL is the exception and it is treated differently.

2315
03:41:38,030 --> 03:41:43,120
考试用文字描述查询，并要求你推断其成本以及原因。
The exam describes queries in words and expects you to reason about what they cost and why.

2316
03:41:43,502 --> 03:41:51,332
连接、分组、用于计算滚动平均值的窗口函数、通用表表达式和透视，这些都在指南中明确列出了名称。
Joints, grouping, window functions for rolling averages, common table expressions, and pivoting are all named in the guide by name.

2317
03:41:52,174 --> 03:41:58,212
Scala 值得了解，因为它在创建视图和 EMR 作业时会作为选项出现。
Scala is worth recognizing because it appears as an option when creating view and EMR jobs.

2318
03:41:58,560 --> 03:42:04,612
当团队已经有 Scala Spark 代码时，选择它有时是正确的答案。
Choosing it over Python is occasionally the right answer when a team already has Scala Spark code.

2319
03:42:05,920 --> 03:42:11,076
考试指南要求你定义分布式计算，而不是去实现它。
The exam guide asks you to define distributed computing rather than implement one.

2320
03:42:11,310 --> 03:42:13,764
所以这属于词汇量范畴，而不是工程实践。
So this is vocabulary rather than engineering.

2321
03:42:14,862 --> 03:42:19,300
第二点和第三点非常重要，第五模块已经展示了原因。
The second and third points carry the weight, and module 5 already showed why.

2322
03:42:20,206 --> 03:42:28,868
不共享内存的机器在需要合并工作时必须互相发送数据，这种传输就是所谓的洗牌。
Machines that do not share memory must send data to each other whenever work needs to be combined, and that transfer is what a shuffle is.

2323
03:42:29,774 --> 03:42:35,560
分区决定了工作如何均匀分布，这就是为什么选择错误的键会导致倾斜。
Partitioning decides how evenly the work spreads, which is why a badly chosen key produces skew.

2324
03:42:36,622 --> 03:42:40,320
最后一点对于某一类特定问题非常重要。
The last point matters for a specific class of question.

2325
03:42:40,878 --> 03:42:48,868
依赖前一行的累计总和无法并行化，所以任何承诺通过增加工作节点来加速它的选项都是错误的。
A running total that depends on the previous row cannot be parallelized, so an option promising to speed it up with more workers is wrong.

2326
03:42:50,446 --> 03:42:58,020
考试指南明确提到了图和预数据结构，这在数据工程考试中可能会让一些人感到意外。
The exam guide names graph and pre-data structures explicitly which surprises people in a data engineering exam.

2327
03:42:59,118 --> 03:43:02,468
当你把它们与相关服务联系起来时，原因就变得清晰了。
The reason becomes clear when you connect them to services.

2328
03:43:03,118 --> 03:43:10,724
基于哈希的查找是 DynamoDB 能快速通过键获取单个项目的原因，但在范围查询方面则没用。
A hash-based lookup is what makes DynamoDB fast at fetching one item by key and useless at ranges.

2329
03:43:11,584 --> 03:43:18,212
排序结构是让范围查询成本低廉的关键，这就是为什么 Redshift 的排序键很重要。
A sorted structure is what makes a range query cheap, which is why Redshift sort keys matter.

2330
03:43:18,544 --> 03:43:23,812
图用于建模事物之间的关系，这也是 Amazon Neptune 的全部用途。
Graphs model relationships between things, which is Amazon Neptune's entire purpose.

2331
03:43:24,462 --> 03:43:34,436
而且第四个要点中的有向无环图是每个编排器使用的结构。所以从第六模块开始你就一直在处理这种结构。
And the directed acyclic graph in the fourth bullet is the shape every orchestrator uses. So you have already been working with one since module 6.

2332
03:43:35,982 --> 03:43:42,224
这是关于 Lambda 调优最有用的一点，而且它确实违背直觉。
This is the single most useful thing to understand about Lambda tuning, and it is genuinely counterintuitive.

2333
03:43:42,464 --> 03:43:45,184
你无法在任何地方配置 CPU。
You do not configure CPU anywhere.

2334
03:43:45,454 --> 03:43:50,596
你配置的是内存，Lambda 会按比例分配处理器能力给它。
You configure memory, and lambda allocates processor power proportionally to it.

2335
03:43:51,406 --> 03:43:57,444
所以考虑一个因为计算任务而运行缓慢、但仍有大量剩余内存的函数。
So consider a function that is slow because it is computing something with plenty of memory left spare.

2336
03:43:58,414 --> 03:44:03,588
提高内存设置仍然会让它变快，因为它会带来更多的处理器能力。
Raising the memory setting still makes it faster because more processor comes with it.

2337
03:44:04,014 --> 03:44:07,364
这会导致一个人们最难接受的结果。
That leads to the result people find hardest to accept.

2338
03:44:08,046 --> 03:44:18,404
增加内存频率会降低总成本，因为函数运行得快得多，缩短的持续时间足以抵消更高的每毫秒单价。
Increasing memory frequency reduces total cost because the function finishes so much sooner that the shorter duration more than offsets the higher per millisecond rate.

2339
03:44:19,118 --> 03:44:25,092
本模块中的第一个工作场景正是基于这一点构建的，而直觉上的答案是错误的。
The first work scenario in this module is built on exactly that, and the intuitive answer to it is wrong.

2340
03:44:26,544 --> 03:44:30,372
要区分硬限制和软限制，因为考试也会这么做。
Separate the hard limits from the soft ones because the exam does.

2341
03:44:30,704 --> 03:44:32,516
超时和内存是硬限制。
Timeout and memory are hard.

2342
03:44:32,864 --> 03:44:41,220
提交支持请求无法突破 15 分钟的上限，所以如果工作负载可能超过这个时间，就需要换用不同的引擎或者拆分成多个部分。
No support request raises the 15-minute ceiling, so a workload that might exceed it needs a different engine or needs breaking into pieces.

2343
03:44:43,950 --> 03:44:46,980
并发是软限制，可以根据需求调高。
Concurrency is soft and can be raised on request.

2344
03:44:47,824 --> 03:44:57,796
临时存储这一项值得注意，因为它变动了。以前固定是 512 MB，这迫使人们必须把所有内容都通过 S3 来传输。
The ephemeral storage row is worth noting because it moved. It used to be a fixed 512 MB, which forced people to route everything through S3.

2345
03:44:58,224 --> 03:45:07,108
现在它能达到 10GB。所以在本地处理大文件的函数是可行的，而旧的资料会说不可行。
It now reaches 10GB. So a function processing a large file locally is viable in a way older material says it is not.

2346
03:45:08,846 --> 03:45:14,784
考试指南将从 Lambda 内部挂载存储卷列为一项技能，所以这两个选项都会出现。
The exam guide names mounting storage volumes from within Lambda as a skill, so both options appear.

2347
03:45:15,310 --> 03:45:17,572
两者的区别在于共享和持久性。
The distinction is sharing and persistence.

2348
03:45:19,830 --> 03:45:28,470
斜杠 TMP 是属于单个执行环境的临时空间，所以第二个并发调用会得到一个不同的空间，且没有任何内容能可靠保留。
Slash TMP is scratch space belonging to one execution environment, so a second concurrent invocation gets a different one and nothing survives reliably.

2349
03:45:29,750 --> 03:45:36,350
Amazon EFS 是真正的共享文件系统，因此多个函数可以读写相同的文件，且数据是持久化的。
Amazon EFS is a real shared file system, so many functions can read and write the same files and the data persists.

2350
03:45:37,184 --> 03:45:43,012
这使得它成为处理大型共享参考数据集或包不下的模型文件的正确答案。
That makes it the answer for a large shared reference dataset or a model file too big to package.

2351
03:45:43,504 --> 03:45:46,916
成本方面对应第四个要点中的 VPC 要求。
The cost is the VPC requirement on the fourth bullet.

2352
03:45:48,590 --> 03:45:51,940
尺寸上限决定了这一点，而且判定非常明确。
The size ceiling decides this and it decides it sharply.

2353
03:45:52,384 --> 03:45:56,388
执行轻量级转换的函数可以轻松放入 zip 压缩包中。
A function doing light transformation fits comfortably in a zip archive.

2354
03:45:57,678 --> 03:46:03,908
层（Layers）可以让多个函数共享一份公共依赖项，而不是每个函数都携带自己的副本。
Layers let several functions share one copy of a common dependency rather than each carrying its own.

2355
03:46:04,814 --> 03:46:13,904
一旦函数需要大量的数值或机器学习库，250 MB 的解压限制就成了约束条件。
The moment a function needs a substantial numerical or machine learning library, the 250 MB unpack limit becomes the constraint.

2356
03:46:14,158 --> 03:46:16,864
容器镜像可以将这个上限提高到 10 GB。
A container image raises it to 10 GB.

2357
03:46:17,584 --> 03:46:20,388
最后一个要点中的权衡适用于这两者。
The trade in the last bullet applies to both.

2358
03:46:21,198 --> 03:46:25,988
在冷启动期间，包里的每一兆字节都要花费时间去下载和解压。
Every megabyte of package's time spent downloading and unpacking during a cold start.

2359
03:46:27,504 --> 03:46:31,620
这两个听起来很像，但解决的是相反的问题。
These two sound similar and solve opposite problems.

2360
03:46:32,224 --> 03:46:39,984
预留并发是你自己设定的上限，在第 6 模块中，它被用来保护数据库免受上千个并发写入者的冲击。
Reserved concurrency is a cap you impose on yourself, which module 6 used to protect a database from a thousand concurrent writers.

2361
03:46:40,144 --> 03:46:46,372
它不花额外费用，而且它还会预留账户配额中的那一块，确保其他函数不会挤占这个函数的资源。
It costs nothing and it also reserves that slice of the account limit so other functions cannot starve this one.

2362
03:46:47,480 --> 03:46:50,052
预置并发是针对冷启动的。
Provisioned concurrency is about cold starts.

2363
03:46:50,304 --> 03:46:56,676
它保持一定数量的环境处于初始化并待命状态，这样调用时就不需要消耗初始化时间。
It keeps a number of environments initialized and waiting, so an invocation does not pay initialization time.

2364
03:46:57,166 --> 03:46:58,660
它是持续构建的。
It is built continuously.

2365
03:47:01,422 --> 03:47:05,572
关于首次请求出现延迟峰值的题目指向预置并发。
A question about latency spikes on the first request points at provisioned.

2366
03:47:06,414 --> 03:47:10,596
关于压垮下游系统的题目指向预留并发。
A question about overwhelming something downstream points at reserved.

2367
03:47:11,968 --> 03:47:16,676
第三点是价值最高的习惯，它会出现在关于函数性能的题目中。
The third point is the highest value habit and it appears in questions about function performance.

2368
03:47:16,928 --> 03:47:22,756
在处理函数之外的代码在环境创建时运行一次，而内部的代码在每次调用时都会运行。
Code outside the handler runs once when the environment is created, and code inside runs on every invocation.

2369
03:47:23,374 --> 03:47:30,724
因此，在处理函数内创建 S3 客户端或数据库连接，每次都会支付这笔建立成本。
So creating an S3 client or a database connection inside the handler pays that setup cost every single time.

2370
03:47:31,008 --> 03:47:42,180
与此同时，在外部创建意味着后续的调用可以重复利用它。这就是为什么一个函数在第一次调用时很慢，而在第二次调用时很快。而第四点是一个真正的权衡。
Meanwhile, creating it outside means subsequent invocations reuse it. That is why a function can be slow on invocation 1 and fast on invocation 2. And the fourth point is a real trade.

2371
03:47:42,528 --> 03:47:47,492
将函数放入 VPC 是访问私有资源的必要条件，而且这并不免费。
Putting a function in a VPC is necessary to reach private resources and it is not free.

2372
03:47:47,808 --> 03:47:50,404
所以要根据需求去操作，而不是默认就这么做。
So do it deliberately rather than by default.

2373
03:47:51,694 --> 03:47:59,204
使用 Lambda 自动化数据处理是一项明确的技能，而事件源决定了失败时的行为，这也是考题考察的内容。
Automating data processing with Lambda is a named skill and the event source decides the failure behavior, which is what questions test.

2374
03:48:00,046 --> 03:48:09,572
来自 S3 或 EventBridge 的异步调用意味着 Lambda 在放弃之前会先自动重试两次，且没有任何程序在等待响应。
Asynchronous invocation from S3 or event bridge means Lambda itself retries a failed invocation twice before giving up and nothing is waiting for the answer.

2375
03:48:10,382 --> 03:48:14,276
基于队列的源如 SQS 和 Kinesis 的行为又有所不同。
Bold-based sources like SQS and Kinesis behave differently again.

2376
03:48:15,246 --> 03:48:23,396
这是因为 Lambda 处理的是批处理，只有在成功时才会删除它，这就是为什么第三模块提到的“毒丸记录”问题会导致分片阻塞。
That is because Lambda takes a batch and only deletes it on success, which is why module 3's poison record problem blocks a shard.

2377
03:48:24,014 --> 03:48:30,052
同步调用会将错误直接返回给调用者。因此，重试的决定权在调用方。
Synchronous invocation returns the error straight to whatever called it. So the retree decision belongs to the caller.

2378
03:48:31,726 --> 03:48:37,092
最后一项才是关键点，这也是本模块其余内容的共同主题。
The last bullet is the one that matters, and it is the same theme as the rest of this module.

2379
03:48:37,648 --> 03:48:42,404
一个触发了函数但失败三次的 S3 事件就直接消失了。
An S3 event that triggers a function which fails three times is simply gone.

2380
03:48:43,406 --> 03:48:51,428
错误不会在任何地方显现，对象永远不会被处理，唯一的迹象就是下游数据静默缺失。
No error surfaces anywhere, the object is never processed, and the only symptom is data that quietly does not exist downstream.

2381
03:48:54,318 --> 03:49:00,932
配置“失败后目的地”不花额外费用，且能将该问题转变为可见且可检查的事件。
Configuring an on-failure destination costs nothing and turns that into a visible inspectable event.

2382
03:49:01,550 --> 03:49:07,300
在这里，目的地取代了死信队列，因为它可以捕获包含错误信息的调用记录。
Destinations superseded dead letter queues here because they capture the invocation record, including the error.

2383
03:49:07,648 --> 03:49:11,716
死信队列仅捕获原始有效负载，让你只能靠猜。
A dead letter queue captures only the original payload and leaves you guessing.

2384
03:49:13,358 --> 03:49:19,588
一个 AWS Lambda 函数从 Amazon S3 获取 JSON 文件并写入 Parquet 格式。
An AWS Lambda function transforms JSON files from Amazon S3 and writes parquet.

2385
03:49:20,048 --> 03:49:25,764
它配置了 512 MB 内存，处理每个文件大约需要 40 秒。
It is configured with 512 MB of memory and takes about 40 seconds per file.

2386
03:49:26,368 --> 03:49:31,556
这段时间大部分消耗在 Parquet 转换上，这是 CPU 密集型任务。
That time is mostly spent in the parquet conversion, which is CPU bound.

2387
03:49:32,494 --> 03:49:37,860
团队每月处理约 8 万个文件，并希望降低 Lambda 的成本。
The team processes about 80,000 files a month and wants to reduce the lambda bin.

2388
03:49:39,054 --> 03:49:45,988
CloudWatch 报告的内存使用量峰值约为 180 MB，远低于配置的数值。
Memory user reported in CloudWatch peaks at around 180 MB, well under the configured amount.

2389
03:49:46,574 --> 03:49:48,484
数据工程师应该怎么做？
What should the data engineer do?

2390
03:49:50,734 --> 03:49:57,124
A. 将内存从 512 MB 降至 256 MB，因为只用了 180 MB。
reduce the memory from 512 MB to 256, since only 180 are used.

2391
03:49:57,648 --> 03:50:03,140
B. 增加内存，测量耗时的变化，并选择总成本最低的方案。
b Increase the memory, measure the change in duration, and settle on the cheapest total.

2392
03:50:03,568 --> 03:50:08,292
C. 启用预留并发，让函数不再承担冷启动时间。
C. Enable provisioned concurrency so the functions do not pay cold start time.

2393
03:50:09,008 --> 03:50:09,328
D。
D.

2394
03:50:09,838 --> 03:50:14,212
增加临时存储分配，以便转换时有更多空间。
Increase the ephemeral storage allocation so the conversion has more room.

2395
03:50:15,278 --> 03:50:16,612
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2396
03:50:23,118 --> 03:50:28,036
答案是 B，而选项 A 是整组幻灯片都在铺垫的陷阱。
The answer is B, and option A is the trap the whole slide sequence was building towards.

2397
03:50:28,448 --> 03:50:36,288
减少明显未使用的内存看起来像是标准的“规格优化”，如果函数是在等待某些资源，那这样做是对的。
Reducing memory that is visibly unused looks like textbook right sizing, and it would be correct if the function were waiting on something.

2398
03:50:36,528 --> 03:50:42,116
但它不是，它是 CPU 密集型任务，而增加内存是获取更多 CPU 能力的唯一方式。
It is not, it is CPU bound, and memory is the only way to buy CPU.

2399
03:50:42,990 --> 03:50:49,636
减半内存意味着处理器能力也减半，导致函数运行时间翻倍，而你为了一个更慢的流水线支付了几乎相同的费用。
Halving memory halves the processor, so the function takes about twice as long, and you pay roughly the same for a slower pipeline.

2400
03:50:50,126 --> 03:50:58,660
选项 B 中的“测量”一词也很重要，因为这种关系并非完全线性，必须通过实测来找到最便宜的设置。
The word measure in option B matters too because the relationship is not perfectly linear and the cheapest setting has to be found empirically.

2401
03:51:00,366 --> 03:51:08,868
AWS Batch 在官方考试范围的服务列表中，但几乎没人去研究它，所以这几行内容很有价值。
AWS batch is on the official in scope service list and almost nobody studies it, which makes it worth these few lines.

2402
03:51:09,742 --> 03:51:11,236
它填补了真正的空白。
It fills the genuine gap.

2403
03:51:11,758 --> 03:51:13,636
Lambda 的运行时间限制是 15 分钟。
Lambda stops at 15 minutes.

2404
03:51:14,446 --> 03:51:19,780
当任务必须在集群中分布，并涉及洗牌和连接时，Spark 是正确答案。
Spark is the answer when work must be distributed across a cluster which shuffles and joins.

2405
03:51:20,718 --> 03:51:27,568
Batch 涵盖了中间地带，即那些运行数小时、不需要 Spark，且可以打包成容器的任务。
Batch covers the space between, where a job runs for hours, does not need Spark, and can be packaged as a container.

2406
03:51:27,982 --> 03:51:33,668
比如转换 1 万张图片、运行模拟实验、或者用单线程工具处理大文件。
Converting 10,000 images, running a simulation, processing a large file with a single threaded tool.

2407
03:51:34,254 --> 03:51:40,196
它负责提供计算资源，将任务放入队列，并在队列清空时关闭。
It provisions the compute, queues the jobs, and shuts down when the queue empties.

2408
03:51:41,774 --> 03:51:50,180
基础设施即代码在考试指南中出现了两次，代表两个不同的技能点，这说明了 AWS 对这个职位的重视程度。
Infrastructure as code appears twice in the exam guide has two separate skills, which tells you how much weight AWS puts on it for this role.

2409
03:51:50,720 --> 03:51:56,068
关于灾难恢复的论点是模块 6 中提到的内容，表述得更通用一些。
The argument is the one module, six made about disaster recovery, stated more generally.

2410
03:51:56,942 --> 03:52:00,964
可以通过定义重新创建的流水线，可以在另一个区域重建。
A pipeline you can recreate from a definition can be rebuilt in another region.

2411
03:52:01,360 --> 03:52:07,268
它可以从测试环境提升到生产环境且不会产生漂移，在更改前可以进行审查，并在出错时回滚。
It can be promoted from test to production without drift, reviewed before it changes, and rolled back when it breaks.

2412
03:52:07,600 --> 03:52:11,204
而在控制台中手动组装的流水线无法做到这些。
A pipeline assembled by hand in the console can do none of those things.

2413
03:52:11,822 --> 03:52:14,116
它也没法在六个月后被解释清楚。
It also cannot be explained six months later.

2414
03:52:14,640 --> 03:52:20,388
构建它的人可能已经调到别的团队了，而且没人确定这 40 个任务中哪些还需要继续运行。
The person who built it has moved to another team, and nobody is sure which of the 40 jobs is still needed.

2415
03:52:20,910 --> 03:52:24,420
这是真实的组织成本，而不是理论上的成本。
That is a real organizational cost, not a theoretical one.

2416
03:52:26,222 --> 03:52:29,252
这里强调的是大多数人容易搞错的关系。
The call out is the relationship most people get wrong.

2417
03:52:29,966 --> 03:52:33,124
CDK 不是一种替代的部署引擎。
The CDK is not an alternative deployment engine.

2418
03:52:33,520 --> 03:52:42,532
它是一种使用编程语言来编写云构建的方法，它会生成一个云构建模板，然后由云构建去部署。
It is a way of writing cloud formation using a programming language, and it synthesizes a cloud formation template that cloud formation then deploys.

2419
03:52:43,246 --> 03:52:47,876
所以堆栈、变更集、漂移检测和回滚在这些情况下表现是一样的。
So stacks, change sets, drift detection, and rollback all behave identically.

2420
03:52:48,240 --> 03:52:50,916
选择 CDK 的原因是减少重复。
The reason to choose the CDK is repetition.

2421
03:52:51,280 --> 03:53:00,260
用 YAML 定义 40 个几乎相同的 Glue jobs，意味着要写 40 段几乎一样的 YAML 代码。而在 CDK 中，它就是一个循环。
Defining 40 near-identical blue jobs in YAM, L means 40 blocks of near-identical YAML. In the CDK, it is a loop.

2422
03:53:00,960 --> 03:53:08,548
当题目描述许多相似的资源或跨团队的可重用模式时，这就是 CDK 的信号。
When a question describes many similar resources or a reusable pattern across teams, that is the CDK signal.

2423
03:53:10,190 --> 03:53:18,020
变更集是考试中最值得了解的功能，因为它能解决题目中经常出现的特定问题。
Change sets are the feature most worth knowing for exam purposes because they answer a specific concern that appears in questions.

2424
03:53:19,520 --> 03:53:24,356
直接应用模板更改意味着你得在观察它发生的过程中去搞清楚它是做什么的。
Applying a template change directly means finding out what it does by watching it happen.

2425
03:53:25,262 --> 03:53:31,076
某些资源变更是替换而非更新，对于数据库来说，这意味着换成一个全新的空数据库。
Some resource changes are replacements rather than updates, which for a database means a new empty one.

2426
03:53:31,854 --> 03:53:38,020
变更集会先计算计划，并显示哪些资源将被创建、修改或替换。
A change set computes the plan first and shows which resources will be created, modified, or replaced.

2427
03:53:38,160 --> 03:53:41,444
这样在任何变动发生之前，破坏性的更改就能被看见。
So the destructive change is visible before anything moves.

2428
03:53:42,286 --> 03:53:51,652
堆栈集对于模块 6 中描述的多账户模式很重要，它能从一个地方把相同的基础设施部署到每个账户中。
Stack sets matter for the multi-account pattern module 6 described, deploying identical infrastructure into every account from one place.

2429
03:53:56,750 --> 03:53:58,084
它的价值在于压缩。
The value is compression.

2430
03:54:04,334 --> 03:54:12,240
在原始云构建中定义 Lambda 函数意味着要声明六个独立的东西：函数、角色、策略……
Defining a lambda function in raw cloud formation means declaring six separate things the function a role, a policy,

2431
03:54:12,462 --> 03:54:16,644
一个日志组、一个事件源映射和调用权限。
a log group, an event source mapping and invoke permissions.

2432
03:54:17,838 --> 03:54:20,132
这得写到一百多行。
That runs to well over a hundred lines.

2433
03:54:20,974 --> 03:54:23,844
对应的 SAM 资源只有几个。
The equivalent SAM resource is a handful.

2434
03:54:24,398 --> 03:54:27,460
它在底层展开后与云形成是一样的。
It expands into the same cloud formation underneath.

2435
03:54:27,982 --> 03:54:30,660
本地测试点是它出现的另一个原因。
The local testing point is the other reason it appears.

2436
03:54:31,200 --> 03:54:39,760
这是因为能够针对示例事件在本地调用函数，才让测试无服务器代码变得可行。
That is because being able to invoke a function locally against a sample event is what makes testing serverless code practical.

2437
03:54:41,070 --> 03:54:44,836
考试对这两者的区分比团队通常做的要更明确。
The exam distinguishes these two more sharply than teams often do.

2438
03:54:45,326 --> 03:54:50,180
两者都包含你的代码在运行时读取的值，且都可以用 KMS 加密。
Both hold values your code reads at runtime and both can encrypt with KMS.

2439
03:54:51,854 --> 03:54:54,468
决定题目答案的区别在于轮换。
The difference that decides questions is rotation.

2440
03:54:55,470 --> 03:55:00,900
机密管理器可以按计划轮换凭证，同时更新存储的值和数据库。
Secrets manager can rotate a credential on a schedule, updating the stored value and the database together.

2441
03:55:01,326 --> 03:55:05,380
这正是本模块中场景 4 所描述的问题。
That is exactly the problem scenario 4 in this module describes.

2442
03:55:06,126 --> 03:55:13,988
参数存储没有轮换功能，且对于标准参数是免费的，这使得它成为存储桶名称或阈值的理想选择。
Parameter store has no rotation and it is free for standard parameters, which makes it the sensible home for a bucket name or a threshold.

2443
03:55:14,606 --> 03:55:20,836
所以提到轮换凭证的问题只有一个答案，而关于配置值的问题则有另一个答案。
So a question mentioning rotating credentials has one answer and a question about configuration values has the other.

2444
03:55:22,510 --> 03:55:28,068
一个数据平台团队在三个环境中管理 60 个 AWS Glue jobs。
A data platform team manages 60 AWS Blue jobs across three environments.

2445
03:55:29,486 --> 03:55:35,364
每个环境的区别仅在于桶名称、数据库名称和工作节点数量。
Each environment differs only in bucket names, database names, and worker counts.

2446
03:55:37,486 --> 03:55:40,320
目前这些作业是手动在控制台中创建的。
Jobs are currently created by hand in the console.

2447
03:55:40,878 --> 03:55:47,108
环境之间的配置漂移已经两次导致生产故障，而这些故障在测试中并未出现。
Configuration drift between environments has twice caused a production failure that did not appear in test.

2448
03:55:47,520 --> 03:55:54,340
团队希望除了参数之外，各环境尽可能一致，并且要求在应用更改前进行审查。
The team wants environments to be probably identical apart from their parameters and wants changes reviewed before they are applied.

2449
03:55:54,734 --> 03:55:56,196
团队应该实施什么？
What should the team implement?

2450
03:55:59,342 --> 03:56:03,876
a. 详细记录控制台步骤，并让第二名工程师检查每项更改。
document the console steps thoroughly and have a second engineer check each change.

2451
03:56:04,366 --> 03:56:11,300
b. 使用带参数的 AWS CDK 定义每个环境的作业，并通过流水线进行部署。
b. Define the jobs with the AWS C DK parameterized per environment and deploy through a pipeline.

2452
03:56:11,920 --> 03:56:20,164
c. 在每次更改后，使用 AWS CLI 将生产环境的视图作业复制到其他环境中。
C. Copy the production view jobs into the other environments using the AWS C LI after each change.

2453
03:56:20,878 --> 03:56:21,120
d.
D.

2454
03:56:22,414 --> 03:56:26,628
使用 AWS Config 规则来检测环境何时出现偏差。
Use AWS config rules to detect when environments diverge.

2455
03:56:27,246 --> 03:56:28,484
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2456
03:56:35,200 --> 03:56:36,452
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2457
03:56:36,880 --> 03:56:44,900
选项 D 是一个很有迷惑性的干扰项，因为 AWS Config 确实能检测到配置漂移，并且是其他问题的正确答案。
Option D is the thoughtful distractor because AWS config genuinely does detect configuration drift and is a real answer to other questions.

2458
03:56:46,478 --> 03:56:52,068
它是检测而非预防。环境仍然会产生偏差，只是你能更早发现。
It is detection rather than prevention. The environments still diverge, you just find out sooner.

2459
03:56:53,070 --> 03:56:58,880
需求要求是可证明的完全一致，只有共享定义才能实现这一点。
The requirement asks for provably identical, which only a shared definition delivers.

2460
03:57:00,142 --> 03:57:07,108
60 个几乎相同的资源也是 CDK 优于纯云形成的一个特定条件。
60 near-identical resources is also the specific condition where the CDK beats plain cloud formation.

2461
03:57:07,840 --> 03:57:13,040
这是因为它变成了一个对列表的循环，而不是 60 个模板块。
That is because it becomes a loop over a list rather than 60 blocks of template.

2462
03:57:14,286 --> 03:57:16,640
这就是开头承诺过的修正内容。
This is the correction promised at the start.

2463
03:57:16,960 --> 03:57:19,652
AWS Code Commit 是 Git 托管服务。
AWS Code Commit was the Git hosting service.

2464
03:57:20,080 --> 03:57:27,332
它在 2024 年停止接受新客户，并在 2025 年 12 月的修订版中从考查范围服务列表中移除。
It closed to new customers during 2024 and it was removed from the in scope service list in the December 2025 revision.

2465
03:57:28,110 --> 03:57:33,092
旧的资料将其视为存放流水线代码的默认答案。
Older material treats it as the default answer for where pipeline code lives.

2466
03:57:33,390 --> 03:57:34,212
现在不是了。
It is not.

2467
03:57:57,040 --> 03:57:59,460
一次构建，多次部署。
Build once, deploy many times.

2468
03:58:02,222 --> 03:58:10,820
如果每个环境都从源码构建自己的制品，由于构建之间依赖版本的变化，它们可能会产生差异。
If each environment builds its own artifact from source, they can differ because a dependency version moved between builds.

2469
03:58:11,726 --> 03:58:16,420
推广相同的制品意味着你测试的内容就是你交付的内容。
Promoting the identical artifact means what you tested is what you shipped.

2470
03:58:17,134 --> 03:58:20,320
验证步骤是专门针对数据工作的。
The validate step is the one that is specific to data work.

2471
03:58:20,800 --> 03:58:23,812
对于应用程序，你要检查它是否能启动并做出响应。
For an application, you check that it starts and responds.

2472
03:58:24,654 --> 03:58:30,564
对于流水线，你需要用已知输入运行它，并确认输出符合预期。
For a pipeline, you run it against a known input and confirm the output matches what you expect.

2473
03:58:31,600 --> 03:58:37,124
这是因为一个流水线可能部署得非常完美，但仍然产出错误的数据。
That is because a pipeline can deploy perfectly and still produce wrong numbers.

2474
03:58:38,638 --> 03:58:42,820
最后一项是诚实的局限性，值得直白地说明一下。
The last bullet is the honest limitation and it is worth saying plainly.

2475
03:58:43,310 --> 03:58:47,108
金丝雀发布对于处理请求的函数非常有效。
Canary deployment works beautifully for a function serving requests.

2476
03:58:47,360 --> 03:58:54,852
因为你将 1% 的流量发送到新版本，观察错误率，然后决定增加更多流量或进行回滚。
That is because you send 1% of traffic to the new version, watch the error rate, and shift more or rollback.

2477
03:58:55,726 --> 03:58:59,972
一个批处理作业只有一次调用，所以没有可以拆分的流量。
A Nike batch job has one invocation, so there is no traffic to split.

2478
03:59:00,526 --> 03:59:08,932
数据流水线对应的做法是在测试环境中用已知数据运行新版本，并在推广前对比输出结果。
The equivalent discipline for data pipelines is running the new version against known data in a test environment and comparing the output before promoting.

2479
03:59:10,126 --> 03:59:13,124
这就是交付流水线中的验证步骤的作用。
That is what the validate step in the delivery pipeline is for.

2480
03:59:14,062 --> 03:59:19,364
识别出这种区别比死记硬背部署策略更有用。
Recognizing that difference is more useful than memorizing the deployment strategies.

2481
03:59:21,102 --> 03:59:25,732
最后两点是至关重要的区别，但很容易混淆。
The last two points are the distinction that matters and it is easy to blur.

2482
03:59:26,773 --> 03:59:32,004
测试是检查代码是否按照你预想的逻辑处理你在编写时考虑到的输入。
Tests check that the code does what you intended against inputs you thought of when you wrote them.

2483
03:59:33,070 --> 03:59:40,452
数据质量检查是在生产环境中针对真实数据运行，从而捕捉到那些你没考虑到的问题，而这些正是真正棘手的故障所在。
Data quality checks run in production against real data and catch what you did not think of, which is where the interesting failures live.

2484
03:59:41,294 --> 03:59:48,356
如果源系统开始在某一列发送空值，它会通过你写的每一个单元测试，因为你的测试数据中不包含空值。
A source system that starts sending nulls in a column will pass every unit test you wrote because your test data does not contain them.

2485
03:59:49,358 --> 03:59:52,196
模块 15 会妥善涵盖数据质量的内容。
Module 15 covers data quality properly.

2486
03:59:52,400 --> 03:59:56,484
目前，请记住「构建成功」和「输出正确」是两个不同的概念。
For now, hold that a green build and correct output are different claims.

2487
03:59:57,998 --> 04:00:05,284
一个团队通过将脚本上传到 Amazon S3 并手动更新作业定义来部署 AWS Glue job 脚本。
A team deploys AWS Blue job scripts by uploading them to Amazon S3 and updating the job definition manually.

2488
04:00:05,774 --> 04:00:14,212
一项最近的更改在未在测试中运行的情况下就应用到了生产环境，并在被发现前默默产出了两天的错误聚合数据。
A recent change was applied to production before it had been run in test and it silently produced incorrect aggregates for two days before anyone noticed.

2489
04:00:14,960 --> 04:00:22,436
团队希望在变更到达生产环境前进行测试，并希望检测出错误的输出，而不仅仅是失败的任务。
The team wants changes to be tested before reaching production and wants to detect incorrect output rather than only failed jobs.

2490
04:00:23,440 --> 04:00:26,372
哪种组合最能同时满足这两个要求？
Which combination best addresses both requirements?

2491
04:00:29,390 --> 04:00:38,692
A. 在测试环境中构建并测试的流水线将相同的制品推送到生产环境，并在作业中加入数据质量检查。
A code pipeline that builds and tests in a test environment promotes the same artifact to production plus data quality checks in the job.

2492
04:00:39,854 --> 04:00:40,153
B。
B.

2493
04:00:40,654 --> 04:00:46,596
C. 为 Glue作业添加重试和更长的超时时间，确保瞬时故障不会影响到生产环境。
Add retrees and a longer timeout to the glue job so transient failures do not reach production.

2494
04:00:47,758 --> 04:00:48,000
C
C

2495
04:00:49,294 --> 04:00:53,252
D。要求第二名工程师批准每次手动上传到 Amazon S3 的操作。
Require a second engineer to approve each manual upload to Amazon S3.

2496
04:00:54,800 --> 04:00:55,040
D。
D.

2497
04:00:55,726 --> 04:00:59,652
E。启用 Glue作业书签，确保错误数据不会被重新处理。
Enable blue job bookmarks so incorrect data is not reprocessed.

2498
04:01:00,206 --> 04:01:01,412
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2499
04:01:08,096 --> 04:01:11,620
答案是 A，而且这个结构值得注意。
The answer is A, and the structure is worth noticing.

2500
04:01:12,016 --> 04:01:16,260
题目给出了两个要求，只有一个选项能同时满足这两个要求。
The question states two requirements, and only one option addresses both.

2501
04:01:16,656 --> 04:01:18,916
一旦你开始寻找，这种题型就很常见了。
That is a common shape once you look for it.

2502
04:01:19,296 --> 04:01:21,476
另一个细节是「静默地」这个词。
The other detail is the word silently.

2503
04:01:21,902 --> 04:01:22,852
没有任何东西报错。
Nothing failed.

2504
04:01:23,696 --> 04:01:30,724
作业运行了，成功了，但写错了数据，这就是为什么所有关于故障处理的选项都不相关。
The job ran, succeeded, and wrote wrong numbers, which is why every option about failure handling is irrelevant.

2505
04:01:31,214 --> 04:01:34,980
这是第6模块提到的最糟糕的一种故障模式。
This is the same failure mode module 6 called the worst available outcome.

2506
04:01:35,726 --> 04:01:39,588
这也是为什么数据质量检查作为独立领域存在，而不仅仅是测试。
It is why data quality checks exist as a separate discipline from testing.

2507
04:01:41,262 --> 04:01:45,764
第四点描述的是在题目中作为症状出现的某种模式。
The fourth point describes a pattern that appears in questions as a symptom.

2508
04:01:46,254 --> 04:01:55,812
一个作业逐行遍历数据帧，为每条记录调用 API 或进行查询，但速度却莫名其妙地慢。
A job iterates over a data frame row by row, calling an API or doing a lookup for each record, and it is inexplicably slow.

2509
04:01:56,366 --> 04:01:59,056
解决方法几乎从来不是换更强大的机器。
The fix is almost never a bigger machine.

2510
04:01:59,630 --> 04:02:06,116
要么是把这些调用改为批处理，要么是将工作重构为针对数据集的连接，而不是对记录进行循环。
It is either to batch those calls or to restructure the work as a join against a dataset rather than a loop over records.

2511
04:02:06,896 --> 04:02:11,460
这和第5模块讨论的代码端洗牌逻辑是一样的道理。
That is the same lesson as Module 5 shuffle discussion approach from the code side.

2512
04:02:11,856 --> 04:02:15,876
这就是为什么考试要求数据工程师具备软件工程师的思维方式。
It is why the exam expects a data engineer to think like a software engineer.

2513
04:02:17,550 --> 04:02:25,124
通过代码调用 SDK 来访问 AWS 功能是一项明确的技能，这里的两点都会成为考题答案。
Calling SDKs to access AWS features from code is a named skill, and two points here become exam answers.

2514
04:02:25,456 --> 04:02:27,588
关于凭证的这一点是绝对的。
The credentials point is absolute.

2515
04:02:28,176 --> 04:02:35,716
任何在脚本、环境变量或配置文件中放入访问密钥和密钥的选项都是错误的。
Any option that puts an access key and secret in a script, an environment variable, or a configuration file is wrong.

2516
04:02:36,256 --> 04:02:41,604
正确的答案是给运行代码的实体关联一个 IAM 角色。
The correct answer is an IAM role attached to whatever is running the code.

2517
04:02:42,176 --> 04:02:45,060
第17模块详细讲解了原因。
Module 17 covers why in detail.

2518
04:02:47,566 --> 04:02:50,736
分页这一点在实际操作中经常坑到人。
The pagination point catches people in practice.

2519
04:02:51,310 --> 04:02:59,536
列表操作只返回第一页，所以如果不进行分页就列出存储桶的代码，只会静默地处理前一千个对象，
A list operation returns the first page only, so code that lists a bucket without paginating quietly, processes the first thousand objects,

2520
04:02:59,696 --> 04:03:00,868
而忽略剩下的部分。
and ignores the rest.

2521
04:03:02,446 --> 04:03:08,132
这个提示是本模块提到的所有关于“静默失败”内容的实际应用。
The callout is the practical version of everything this module has said about silent failure.

2522
04:03:10,126 --> 04:03:13,860
假设一个作业报告它读取了多少行，并写入了多少行。
Suppose a job reports how many rows it read and how many it wrote.

2523
04:03:14,862 --> 04:03:22,020
如果这两个数字出现意外偏差，即使从未抛出异常，也能立即发现。
A run where those numbers diverge unexpectedly becomes visible immediately, even though no exception was ever raised.

2524
04:03:22,990 --> 04:03:27,216
这就是自定义的 CloudWatch 指标和警报，而且成本几乎为零。
That is a custom CloudWatch metric and an alarm, and it costs almost nothing.

2525
04:03:27,456 --> 04:03:30,884
最后一点是平衡。日志记录并不是免费的。
The last point is the balance. Logging is not free.

2526
04:03:31,278 --> 04:03:35,428
考虑一个在 1 亿条记录中每条记录记录一行日志的作业。
Consider a job logging one line per record across 100 million records.

2527
04:03:35,616 --> 04:03:39,748
CloudWatch 日志账单可能会超过作业本身的计算成本。
The CloudWatch logs bill can exceed the compute cost of the job itself.

2528
04:03:40,430 --> 04:03:43,620
第 14 模块妥善涵盖了监控这一领域。
Module 14 covers the monitoring site properly.

2529
04:03:45,294 --> 04:03:48,256
一个每晚运行的 AWS Glue job 从合作伙伴那里读取数据。
A nightly AWS Blue job reads from a partner.

2530
04:03:48,736 --> 04:03:53,764
API 使用存储在作业脚本参数中的访问密钥和机密。
AP are using an access key and secrets stored in the job script parameters.

2531
04:03:56,142 --> 04:04:01,764
该作业列出 Amazon S3 bucket 中的对象，处理它们并写入结果。
The job lists objects in an Amazon S3 bucket, processes them, and writes results.

2532
04:04:02,510 --> 04:04:04,100
出现了两个问题。
Two problems have emerged.

2533
04:04:05,038 --> 04:04:10,500
合作伙伴更换了凭证，直到有人修改参数前，该作业一直失败。
The partner rotated the credentials and the job failed until someone edited the parameters.

2534
04:04:10,976 --> 04:04:19,364
另外，该作业一直在静默处理一个包含 4 万个对象、但它只读取前 1000 个对象的 bucket。
Separately, the job has been quietly processing only the first 1000 objects in a bucket that now holds 40,000.

2535
04:04:21,006 --> 04:04:23,620
哪种组合能同时解决这两个问题？
Which combination fixes both problems?

2536
04:04:25,838 --> 04:04:32,964
将合作伙伴的凭证存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中，并对 S3 列出操作进行分页。
store the partner credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and paginate the S3 list operation.

2537
04:04:33,582 --> 04:04:37,188
B 增加 Glue作业 超时时间并添加更多。
b Increase the glue job timeout and add more.

2538
04:04:48,496 --> 04:04:48,816
D
D

2539
04:04:49,678 --> 04:04:55,076
附加具有 S3 访问权限的 IAM 规则并启用作业书签。
Attach an IAM rule with S3 access and enable job bookmarks.

2540
04:04:56,846 --> 04:04:58,212
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2541
04:05:04,878 --> 04:05:07,684
答案是 A，题目中的数字是 2。
The answer is A and the number in the question is the 2.

2542
04:05:08,430 --> 04:05:11,748
一千是 S3 列出操作的默认分页大小。
A thousand is the default page size for an S3 list operation.

2543
04:05:12,176 --> 04:05:19,204
所以一个在 4 万个对象中只看到刚好 1000 个对象的作业并不是失败，它只是读取了一页就停止了。
So a job seeing exactly a thousand objects out of 40,000 is not failing. It is reading one page and stopping.

2544
04:05:19,950 --> 04:05:23,780
选项 D 值得关注，因为它在某种有趣的程度上对了一半。
Option D is worth attention because it is half right in an interesting way.

2545
04:05:24,016 --> 04:05:28,496
对于 AWS 凭证来说，IAM role 确实是正确的答案。
An IAAM role really is the correct answer for AWS credentials.

2546
04:05:28,816 --> 04:05:30,016
但这涉及的是合作伙伴。
This is a partner.

2547
04:05:31,342 --> 04:05:36,324
API 凭证，这是任何 IAM role 都无法代表的。
API credential, which no IAM role can represent.

2548
04:05:36,910 --> 04:05:43,972
这正是 机密管理器 存在的意义，它可以无需任何人修改作业就轮换值。
That is exactly what Secrets Manager exists for, and it can rotate the value without anyone editing a job.

2549
04:05:45,646 --> 04:05:52,676
Amazon Q 在 2025 年 12 月的修订版中与 Bedrock 和 Kendra 一起加入了 InScope 服务列表。
Amazon Q joined the InScope service list in the December 2025 revision alongside Bedrock and Kendra.

2550
04:05:53,518 --> 04:05:57,376
所以它是考试范围内的，且没有旧教材涵盖它。那个
So it is fair game and no older material covers it. The

2551
04:05:57,390 --> 04:06:02,084
区分两者的关键点在于，Q 是辅助工程师的，而不是用来处理数据的。
framing that keeps it straight is that Q assists the engineer rather than processing the data.

2552
04:06:02,894 --> 04:06:08,740
它能提供代码建议、解释他人编写的陌生任务，并帮助编写查询。
It suggests code, explains an unfamiliar job someone else wrote, and helps author a query.

2553
04:06:08,976 --> 04:06:14,372
与之相对的是第 5 模块中的 Bedrock，它位于流水线中并对记录进行转换。
Contrast that with Bedrock from module 5, which sits inside a pipeline and transforms records.

2554
04:06:17,838 --> 04:06:22,820
所以，如果选项是提供 Amazon Q 来对文档进行分类，那就混淆了两者。
So an option offering Amazon Q as the thing that classifies documents is confusing the two.

2555
04:06:23,470 --> 04:06:29,252
而如果选项是利用它帮助团队更快地编写 Glue jobs，这就是正确的用法。
An option offering it to help a team write blue jobs faster is using it correctly.

2556
04:06:30,862 --> 04:06:38,340
一共 5 道题，最后一题在连续三个模块中都出现过，这足以说明考试对它的重视程度。
5 questions and the last one has now appeared in three consecutive modules, which should tell you how much the exam cares about it.

2557
04:06:41,198 --> 04:06:46,693
任务失败是一个运维问题，对应的答案是重试、警报和死信队列。
A job that fails is an operations problem answered with retreats, alerts and dead letter queues.

2558
04:06:47,854 --> 04:06:56,068
任务成功但产出错误结果是完全不同的问题，对应的是验证、测试和数据质量检查。
A job that succeeds while producing wrong output is a completely different problem, answered with validation, testing, and data quality checks.

2559
04:06:56,974 --> 04:07:02,340
处理故障的选项永远不是针对「静默错误」类问题的正确答案。
Options that handle failure are never the answer to a question about silent wrongness.

2560
04:07:02,816 --> 04:07:07,332
而且考试每次都会给出这些选项，因为它们看起来很负责。
And the exam offers them every single time because they look responsible.

2561
04:07:08,814 --> 04:07:12,516
第三题是本模块中最快排除掉干扰项的一题。
The third question is the fastest elimination in the module.

2562
04:07:13,486 --> 04:07:15,492
在代码中包含凭证永远是错误的。
Credentials in code is always wrong.

2563
04:07:15,854 --> 04:07:21,284
IAM 角色适用于 AWS 访问，而机密管理器适用于其他任何情况。
An IAM role is right for AWS Access and Secrets Manager is right for anything else.

2564
04:07:22,190 --> 04:07:26,016
这完成了第 1 领域，占考试总分的 34%。
That completes domain 1, 34% of the exam.

2565
04:07:27,374 --> 04:07:31,652
从这里开始是第 2 领域，它占考试的 26%。
Domain 2 begins here and it is worth 26% of the exam.

2566
04:07:32,142 --> 04:07:39,940
在为本课程分析的题库中，Amazon S3 出现了 343 次，仅次于 AWS Glue。
Amazon S3 appeared 343 times in the bank analyzed for this course, second only to AWS Blue.

2567
04:07:40,718 --> 04:07:45,604
几乎所有其他模块中的流水线最终都会将数据存放在这里。
Almost every pipeline in every other module lands data here.

2568
04:07:46,016 --> 04:07:50,596
所以，这个模块是许多分散的参考点汇聚的地方。
So, this module is where a lot of scattered references get consolidated.

2569
04:07:51,246 --> 04:08:00,176
存储类别和生命周期规则、如何布局以保持查询成本低廉、保留和删除（包括法律要求的类型）
Storage classes and lifecycle rules, how to lay a layout, so queries stay cheap, retention and deletion, including the legal kind,

2570
04:08:00,416 --> 04:08:01,348
以及弹性。
and resilience.

2571
04:08:02,286 --> 04:08:10,976
有 4 个可行场景和 3 个可用性警告，因为一些旧题库中视为正确答案的 S3 功能
4 worked scenarios and 3 availability warnings because several S3 features that older question banks treat as correct answers

2572
04:08:11,182 --> 04:08:13,540
已经悄悄对新客户关闭了。
have quietly closed to new customers.

2573
04:08:15,136 --> 04:08:19,076
将对象放入 S3 并不是考试能有意义去考查的内容。
Putting an object into S3 is not something an exam can meaningfully test.

2574
04:08:19,534 --> 04:08:21,476
它考核的是后续的所有环节。
What it tests is everything that follows.

2575
04:08:22,030 --> 04:08:30,820
问题是：该对象属于哪个类别，何时移动到另一个类别，何时被删除，以及是否可以被删除。
The question is which class the object sits in, when it moves to another, when it is deleted, and whether it can be deleted at all.

2576
04:08:31,790 --> 04:08:35,588
这些操作在数年而非数天内的成本是多少。
What all of that costs across years rather than days.

2577
04:08:35,776 --> 04:08:45,540
这就是为什么生命周期配置在分析的题库中出现了 29 次，而那些更花哨的功能几乎没被提及。
That is why life cycle configuration appeared 29 times in the bank analyzed for this course, while more glamorous features barely registered at all.

2578
04:08:49,550 --> 04:08:52,976
所以，看到 S3 的题目时，要寻找其中的时间维度。
So, read an S3 question looking for the time dimension in it.

2579
04:08:53,136 --> 04:08:54,436
数据有多久了？
How old is the data?

2580
04:08:55,310 --> 04:08:58,596
与刚入库时相比，现在读取的频率是多少？
How often is it read now compared to when it landed?

2581
04:08:59,374 --> 04:09:01,348
法律规定必须保留多久？
How long must it legally be kept?

2582
04:09:01,696 --> 04:09:05,060
这三个问题能解决这个领域中很大一部分的题目。
Those three questions resolve a surprising proportion of this domain.

2583
04:09:06,638 --> 04:09:11,876
你要内化的是这张表中的规律，而不是具体的单价。
The pattern down this table is the thing to internalize rather than the individual prices.

2584
04:09:12,238 --> 04:09:19,332
追求更廉价存储的每一步，都会伴随更长的最小存储时长，并且通常包含检索费用。
Every step towards cheaper storage buys a longer minimum commitment and usually a retrieval charge.

2585
04:09:20,110 --> 04:09:26,340
深度归档的价格大约是标准存储的四分之一，但要求你保留对象至少 180 天。
Deep archive is roughly a 25th the price of standard and asks you to keep the object 180 days.

2586
04:09:26,656 --> 04:09:33,828
所以，一个在 7 天后将数据移至深度归档、并在 30 天后删除的生命周期规则根本没省钱。
So a lifecycle rule that moves data to deep archive after 7 days and deletes it after 30 is not saving money at all.

2587
04:09:34,574 --> 04:09:39,012
无论如何，你都会被收取全额的 180 天提前删除费用。
You pay the full 180 days regardless as an early deletion charge.

2588
04:09:39,598 --> 04:09:45,988
生命周期规则与最小存储时长之间的这种相互作用，是 S3 成本陷阱中最常见的一种。
That interaction between lifecycle rules and minimum durations is the single most common S3 cost trap.

2589
04:09:47,406 --> 04:09:51,780
这个考点是考试中设置的一个陷阱，一旦你发现它就会很有成就感。
The callout is a trap the exam does set and it is satisfying once you see it.

2590
04:09:52,176 --> 04:09:59,172
在频繁访问和 Glacier 类别中，无论对象实际包含多少内容，都会按每个对象至少 128 千字节计费。
In frequent access and glacier classes bill a minimum of 128 kilobytes per object, whatever the object actually contains.

2591
04:09:59,950 --> 04:10:07,296
所以一个包含 5000 万个、每个只有 4 千字节文件的湖，会被当作每个都是 128 千字节来计费。
So a lake holding 50 million four kilobyte files pays as though every one of them were 128 kilobytes.

2592
04:10:07,470 --> 04:10:09,860
这比实际的数据量高出了 32 倍。
That is 32 times the real data volume.

2593
04:10:11,310 --> 04:10:16,708
在这种情况下，切换到更便宜的存储类别会导致账单上涨而不是下降。
In that situation, moving to a cheaper storage class makes the bill go up rather than down.

2594
04:10:17,774 --> 04:10:24,868
这是模块 2 中提到的“小文件问题”以完全不同的形式再次出现，而答案也是一样的。
It is the small file problem from module 2 appearing again in a completely different guise, and the answer is the same one.

2595
04:10:25,136 --> 04:10:32,132
在进行任何其他优化之前先压缩文件，因为其他的优化都在对抗同一个底层问题。
Compact the files before you optimize anything else because every other optimization is fighting the same underlying problem.

2596
04:10:33,614 --> 04:10:40,100
S3 Express One Zone 反转了通常的定价逻辑，这正是它能成为考点的原因。
S3 Express One zone inverts the usual pricing shape, which is exactly what makes it examinable.

2597
04:10:40,416 --> 04:10:45,348
其他所有类别都是在“更便宜的存储”和“更快的检索速度”之间做权衡。
Every other class trays retrieval speed for cheaper storage in one direction or the other.

2598
04:10:45,998 --> 04:10:55,204
这个类别对存储收费更高，但对请求的费用要低得多，因为它专为产生海量小请求的工作负载而设计。
This one charges more for storage and far less per request because it is designed for workloads that make enormous numbers of small requests.

2599
04:10:55,790 --> 04:11:01,668
在洗牌密集阶段重复读取数千个文件的 Spark 作业就是典型案例。
A Spark job reading thousands of files repeatedly during a shuffle heavy stage is the archetype.

2600
04:11:02,158 --> 04:11:07,172
反复访问相同工作集的交互式查询引擎也是如此。
So is an interactive query engine hitting the same working set over and over.

2601
04:11:07,616 --> 04:11:14,436
单可用性区域的限制，原因和 One Zone 不频繁访问类是一样的。
The single availability zone point matters for the same reason it matters for one zone infrequent access.

2602
04:11:15,376 --> 04:11:23,492
它适用于中间数据或可重现的工作数据，而不适合任何无法从其他地方重建的数据。
It suits intermediate or reproducible working data, and it is the wrong home for anything you could not rebuild from somewhere else.

2603
04:11:25,070 --> 04:11:33,476
这个限制会让一些人感到意外，因为 S3 通常被描述为无限可扩展的，而在存储容量方面，它确实是这样的。
This limit surprises people because S3 is usually described as infinitely scalable and for storage volume it effectively is.

2604
04:11:34,862 --> 04:11:36,196
但请求速率不同。
Request rate is different

2605
04:11:36,846 --> 04:11:39,492
而且它是按前缀计算，而不是按存储桶计算。
and it applies per prefix rather than per bucket.

2606
04:11:40,462 --> 04:11:49,220
因此，将数百万个对象写入一个扁平前缀的任务可能会达到上限，而写入日期分区前缀的相同任务则永远不会接近这个限制。
So a job writing millions of objects into one flat prefix can hit a ceiling that the identical job writing into date partition prefixes never approaches.

2607
04:11:49,870 --> 04:11:53,028
这是你本来就想要的布局带来的一个不错的额外好处。
That is a nice side benefit of a layout you wanted anyway.

2608
04:11:53,456 --> 04:11:56,516
在实战中，识别出三位数的错误代码很有用。
The 3 digit error code is worth recognizing on site.

2609
04:11:57,358 --> 04:12:04,388
503 减速响应是 S3 要求客户端进行退避，而不是任何东西坏了的信号。
A 503 slowdown response is S3 asking the client to back off, not a sign that anything is broken.

2610
04:12:05,038 --> 04:12:12,164
正确的处理方式是第 6 章提到的指数退避模块，而不是提交支持工单或进入检索循环。
The correct response is the exponential back-off module, 6 covered, rather than a support ticket or a retrieval loop.

2611
04:12:13,774 --> 04:12:20,292
「智能分层」在题库中出现了 16 次，而且触发词非常一致。
Intelligent tiering appeared 16 times in the bank, and the trigger phrase is remarkably consistent.

2612
04:12:21,230 --> 04:12:26,180
注意那些描述为未知、不可预测或不断变化的访问模式。
Watch for access patterns described as unknown, unpredictable, or changing.

2613
04:12:26,830 --> 04:12:30,724
注意团队表示他们不知道数据被读取频率的表述。
Watch for a team saying they do not know how often data will be read.

2614
04:12:31,406 --> 04:12:32,516
这就是正确答案。
That is the answer.

2615
04:12:33,422 --> 04:12:40,068
它根据实际情况在不同层级之间移动对象，不收取检索费用，也不设最小存储时长。
It moves objects between tiers based on what actually happens, charges no retrieval fees, and imposes no minimum duration.

2616
04:12:40,416 --> 04:12:49,220
如果问题陈述的是已知模式，情况就不同了。例如数据在前 30 天被频繁读取，之后很少访问，这种情况下使用生命周期规则可以避免监控费用。
A question stating a known pattern is different. Data read heavily for 30 days and rarely afterwards suits a lifecycle rule which avoids the monitoring fee.

2617
04:12:50,094 --> 04:12:55,620
正是因为有监控费，它才不适合非常小的对象。
The monitoring fee is also why it is poor value for very small objects.

2618
04:12:57,166 --> 04:13:01,668
最后两点是真正涉及金钱的地方，且两者都会出现在题目中。
The last two bullets are where real money hides and both appear in questions.

2619
04:13:03,246 --> 04:13:06,724
当开启版本控制时，删除一个对象并不会将其移除。
When versioning is on, deleting an object does not remove it.

2620
04:13:07,214 --> 04:13:15,536
它会添加一个删除标记并保留所有之前的版本，除非生命周期规则将非当前版本过期，否则你将一直为这些版本付费。
It adds a delete marker and keeps every previous version, all of which you pay for indefinitely unless a lifecycle rule expires non current

2621
04:13:15,696 --> 04:13:16,132
版本。
versions.

2622
04:13:17,313 --> 04:13:26,020
中断的多部分上传会导致已上传的部分留在存储桶中，它们占用空间但不会显示在列出对象时。
And An interrupted multipart upload leaves the parts already uploaded sitting in the bucket built as storage but not shown when you list objects.

2623
04:13:27,662 --> 04:13:33,124
设置一个生命周期规则，在几天后终止未完成的多部分上传是标准做法。
A life cycle rule to abort incomplete multi-part uploads after a few days is standard practice.

2624
04:13:33,902 --> 04:13:39,300
如果题目描述的账单与可见数据不符，通常就是在指向这个问题。
A question describing a bill that does not match the visible data is often pointing at it.

2625
04:13:40,782 --> 04:13:44,512
一家公司将 IoT 遥测数据存储在 Amazon S3 中。
A company stores IoT telemetry in Amazon S3.

2626
04:13:44,878 --> 04:13:49,732
在前 14 天内，数据被频繁查询；接下来的 3 个月里，偶尔被查询。
Data is queried heavily for the first 14 days, occasionally for the next 3 months.

2627
04:13:50,670 --> 04:13:54,788
然后只有在监管机构要求时才会访问，大约一年才发生一次。
Then only if a regulator asks, which happens perhaps once a year.

2628
04:13:55,182 --> 04:13:58,276
法规要求数据保留 7 年。
Regulation requires the data to be kept for 7 years.

2629
04:13:58,832 --> 04:14:08,900
一名数据工程师提议采用一个生命周期规则：在 14 天后将对象转入 S3 Glacier Deep Archive，并在 7 年后将其过期。
A data engineer proposes a lifecycle rule that transitions objects to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 14 days and expires them after 7 years.

2630
04:14:09,232 --> 04:14:11,232
平均对象大小为 4 MB。
Average object size is 4 MB.

2631
04:14:11,712 --> 04:14:13,013
这个提议有什么问题？
What is wrong with the proposal?

2632
04:14:13,998 --> 04:14:15,300
A. 没有问题。
A. Nothing.

2633
04:14:16,206 --> 04:14:20,228
在 14 天后转入深度归档是可用的最便宜选项。
Deep archive after 14 days is the cheapest option available.

2634
04:14:20,750 --> 04:14:28,228
B. 从深度归档检索数据最多需要 48 小时，这无法满足第 1 到 3 个月所需的偶尔访问需求。
b Retrieval from Deep archive takes up to 48 hours, which does not meet the occasional access needed in months 1 to 3.

2635
04:14:28,942 --> 04:14:29,152
C。
C.

2636
04:14:30,286 --> 04:14:35,232
小于 128 KB 的对象无法转入深度归档。
Objects smaller than 128 kilobytes cannot be transitioned to deep archive.

2637
04:14:35,662 --> 04:14:35,872
D。
D.

2638
04:14:36,272 --> 04:14:40,004
生命周期规则不能让超过 5 年的物体过期。
Lifecycle rules cannot expire objects after more than 5 years.

2639
04:14:41,710 --> 04:14:42,980
停下来，做决定。
Pause and decide.

2640
04:14:49,678 --> 04:14:50,724
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2641
04:14:51,566 --> 04:14:56,644
题目描述了三个不同的阶段，而提议方案只涵盖了其中两个。
The question describes three distinct phases, and the proposal only accounts for two of them.

2642
04:14:58,190 --> 04:15:03,268
14天内高频访问，3个月内偶尔访问，然后几乎不再访问。
Heavy access for 14 days, occasional access for 3 months, then almost never.

2643
04:15:04,174 --> 04:15:14,212
深度归档非常适合第三个阶段，但完全不适用于第二个阶段，因为需要等待48小时的“偶尔访问”并不算真正的访问。
Deep archive serves the third phase beautifully and cannot serve the second at all because occasional access with a 48 hour wait is not access.

2644
04:15:15,982 --> 04:15:18,436
正确的结构应该是一个转换链。
The correct shape is a chain of transitions.

2645
04:15:19,552 --> 04:15:23,876
标准存储，接着是标准存储，然后是低频访问或 Glacier。
Standard, then standard, infrequent access or glacier.

2646
04:15:24,718 --> 04:15:28,708
中间阶段使用即时检索，长尾部分使用深度归档。
Instant retrieval for the middle period, then deep archive for the long tail.

2647
04:15:29,518 --> 04:15:36,932
注意选项 C，它把一个实数——128KB 的计费最小单位，变成了一个根本不存在的规则。
Notice option C, which takes a real number, the 128 kilobyte billing minimum, and turns it into a rule that does not exist.

2648
04:15:38,592 --> 04:15:44,912
模块 1 已经确定了分区和列式格式是从两个不同的维度来降低查询成本的。
Module 1 established that partitioning and columnar formats attack query cost from two different directions.

2649
04:15:45,232 --> 04:15:53,604
这一部分让这些概念变得具体，因为数据湖的布局是仅在早期由编写第一个摄入任务的人决定一次。
This section is where that becomes concrete because the layout of a lake is decided once, early, usually by whoever wrote the first ingestion job.

2650
04:15:54,192 --> 04:15:56,900
它随后会限制后续构建的所有内容。
It then constrains everything built afterwards.

2651
04:15:57,152 --> 04:16:05,348
后期更改它不是简单的配置更改，而是要重写每一个对象，对于大型数据湖来说，这是一个项目而非一个任务。
Changing it later is not a configuration change. It is rewriting every object, which for a large lake is a project rather than a task.

2652
04:16:05,632 --> 04:16:08,260
这就是为什么考试中不断强调布局的原因。
That is why the exam keeps returning to layout.

2653
04:16:08,912 --> 04:16:17,540
为什么描述查询变慢或成本变高的题目，几乎总是有关于“布局”的答案，而不是“计算”方面的答案。
Why a question describing a lake that has become slow or expensive to query almost always has a layout answer rather than a compute answer.

2654
04:16:17,872 --> 04:16:23,172
在布局糟糕的数据湖中增加工作节点，只会让它同时变得更快且更贵。
Adding workers to a badly laid out lake makes it faster and more expensive at the same time.

2655
04:16:24,912 --> 04:16:29,392
第四点是人们初学分区时常犯的错误。
The fourth point is a mistake people make when they first learn partitioning.

2656
04:16:29,582 --> 04:16:34,084
按客户进行分区感觉很自然，因为查询通常会根据客户进行过滤。
It feels natural to partition by customer because queries filter by customer.

2657
04:16:34,894 --> 04:16:45,476
如果有 50,000 个客户，就会产生 50,000 个文件夹，其中大多数只包含几个小文件，而引擎现在花费在寻找分区上的时间比读取数据还要长。
With 50,000 customers, that creates 50,000 folders, most holding a few small files, and the engine now spends longer discovering partitions than reading data.

2658
04:16:46,190 --> 04:16:53,252
日期通常是正确的选择，因为它具有低基数，且几乎所有的分析查询都有时间范围。
Date is usually right because it has low cardinality and almost every analytical query has a time range.

2659
04:16:54,158 --> 04:16:59,780
最后一点提到的分区投影值得了解，这是 Athena 特有的答案。
Partition projection on the last bullet is worth knowing as an Athena specific answer.

2660
04:17:00,462 --> 04:17:07,716
它通过模式计算分区位置而不是列出它们，从而完全去除了元数据查询。
It calculates partition locations from a pattern rather than listing them, which removes the metadata lookup entirely.

2661
04:17:09,358 --> 04:17:18,084
考试指南将索引与分区和压缩并列提及，而在湖中，它的含义与数据库索引不同。
The exam guide names indexing alongside partitioning and compression, and in a lake, it means something different from a database index.

2662
04:17:18,368 --> 04:17:23,236
Parquet 会记录每个块中每一列的最小值和最大值。
Parquet records the minimum and maximum value of each column within each block.

2663
04:17:23,982 --> 04:17:30,048
因此，过滤日期范围的查询可以跳过那些范围不重叠的整个块。
So a query filtering on a date range can skip entire blocks whose range does not overlap.

2664
04:17:30,528 --> 04:17:34,500
这只有在数据已排序的情况下才有效，也就是第二个要点。
That only works if the data is sorted, which is the second bullet.

2665
04:17:34,958 --> 04:17:40,036
随机顺序意味着每个块都跨越整个范围，任何内容都无法跳过。
Random order means every block spans the whole range and nothing can be skipped.

2666
04:17:40,846 --> 04:17:51,684
Glue 数据目录 中的分区索引解决的是另一个问题：即当一个表有数万个分区时，查找哪些分区存在所花费的时间。
Partition indexes in the blue data catalog solve a different problem. That is the time spent looking up which partitions exist when a table has tens of thousands of them.

2667
04:17:53,230 --> 04:17:57,728
Avro 是值得去理解的一个，因为它是一个人们往往搞不清楚的格式。
The Avruro is the one worth understanding because it is the format people cannot place.

2668
04:17:57,888 --> 04:18:02,404
它和 CSV 一样是基于行的，所以对于读取三个列的查询没有帮助。
It is row based like CSV, so it does not help a query that reads three columns.

2669
04:18:02,958 --> 04:18:08,932
它的优势在于随数据一起存储了正确的模式，并且强力支持该模式随时间变化。
What it does have is a proper schema stored with the data and strong support for that schema changing over time.

2670
04:18:09,728 --> 04:18:15,172
这使得它非常适合摄入层，因为记录是完整到达的，且结构会不断演变。
That makes it good for the ingestion layer where records arrive whole and structures evolve.

2671
04:18:15,854 --> 04:18:17,248
Parquet 则相反。
Parquet is the opposite.

2672
04:18:17,518 --> 04:18:23,172
列式存储非常适合从多行中读取少量列，是精炼层的标准答案。
Columna, excellent for reading a few columns from many rows, and the standard answer for the curated layer.

2673
04:18:23,918 --> 04:18:28,996
在流水线落地时，使用 Avro 并将其转为 Parquet 是完全合理的架构设计。
A pipeline landing, Avro and Curate into Parkate is a perfectly sensible design.

2674
04:18:30,448 --> 04:18:35,652
可分割性是区分深思熟虑的正确答案和瞎猜的关键点。
Splittability is the concept that separates a considered answer from a guess here.

2675
04:18:36,048 --> 04:18:41,572
分布式引擎通过让每个工作节点读取不同的字节范围，将文件分配给各个工作者。
A distributed engine divides a file among its workers by having each read a different byte range.

2676
04:18:43,470 --> 04:18:49,284
GZip 无法从中间开始解压，因此整个文件必须交给单个工作者处理。
GZip cannot be decompressed starting from the middle, so the entire file must go to a single worker.

2677
04:18:50,222 --> 04:18:51,812
一个 10GB 的 GZip 文件
A 10GB getzip

2678
04:18:53,422 --> 04:18:57,028
因此在 100 个工作者上运行的时间和在 1 个工作者上完全一样。
therefore takes exactly as long on 100 workers as it does on one.

2679
04:18:57,390 --> 04:18:59,524
增加容量根本没有任何变化。
Adding capacity changes nothing at all.

2680
04:19:00,078 --> 04:19:08,612
这就是为什么当题目描述一个任务在其他条件正常的情况下始终无法并行时，答案往往隐藏在压缩选项中。
That is why a question describing a job that stubbornly will not parallelize with everything else looking healthy often has a compression answer hiding in it.

2681
04:19:09,408 --> 04:19:18,148
在 Parquet 中，这个问题就消失了，因为 Parquet 对每个块独立进行压缩，且文件格式本身就是为了可分割而设计的。
Inside Parcate, the problem disappears because Part Kate compresses each block independently and the file format itself is designed to be split.

2682
04:19:19,694 --> 04:19:26,692
这三个层级可能有不同的名称，比如常见的青铜、白银、黄金，考试不会考查这些命名。
These three layers appear under several names, bronze, silver, gold being a common one, and the exam does not test the naming.

2683
04:19:27,118 --> 04:19:29,956
它考查的是这种划分带来的后果。
What it tests is the consequences of the separation.

2684
04:19:30,830 --> 04:19:39,168
原始数据是不可变的且从不重写，这使得下游所有内容都可复现，这就是容灾备份的论据
Raw data is immutable and never rewritten, which is what makes everything downstream reproducible, and that is the disaster recovery argument

2685
04:19:39,328 --> 04:19:40,612
模块 6 的重点。
module 6 made.

2686
04:19:41,358 --> 04:19:49,508
而且在最初几天后很少被读取，所以它是转入归档类别的积极生命周期转换的理想候选对象。
It is also read rarely after the first few days, so it is the natural candidate for aggressive life cycle transitions into archive classes.

2687
04:19:50,446 --> 04:19:52,688
精选数据则相反。
Curated data is the opposite.

2688
04:19:52,928 --> 04:19:59,172
它被仪表板和分析师不断读取，因此应保留在没有检索费用的标准存储中。
It is read constantly by dashboards and analysts, so it should stay in standard where there is no retrieval charge.

2689
04:19:59,726 --> 04:20:08,676
对整个存储桶应用单一生命周期规则会完全忽略这一区别，这正是为什么生命周期规则可以按前缀过滤的原因。
Applying one life cycle rule to a whole bucket misses that distinction entirely, which is precisely why life cycle rules can filter by prefix.

2690
04:20:10,190 --> 04:20:15,728
标签的作用比表面上看起来更重要，因为有三个独立的系统在读取并根据它们执行操作。
Tags are more useful than they first appear because three separate systems read them and act on them.

2691
04:20:16,110 --> 04:20:22,660
生命周期规则可以在不考虑它位于哪个前缀的情况下，让所有标记为临时的内容过期。
A lie cycle rule can expire everything tagged as temporary without caring which prefix it sits in.

2692
04:20:23,374 --> 04:20:31,808
身份和访问管理策略可以拒绝对任何标记为受限内容的访问，这在模块 18 中作为基于属性的访问控制进行讲解。
An IAM policy can deny access to anything tagged as restricted, which module 18 covers as attribute-based access control.

2693
04:20:32,494 --> 04:20:41,540
而且成本分配报告可以根据组织使用的任何标签方案来细分支出，这就是共享存储桶如何向各团队计费的方式。
And cost allocation reports can break spent down by whatever tag scheme the organization uses, which is how a shared bucket gets charged back to teams.

2694
04:20:42,350 --> 04:20:45,092
最后一项是值得了解的界限。
The last bullet is the boundary worth knowing.

2695
04:20:45,568 --> 04:20:53,348
标签不能帮助查询引擎裁剪数据，因为引擎读取的是对象键和分区结构，而不是对象元数据。
Tags do not help a query engine prune data because engines read object keys and partition structure rather than object metadata.

2696
04:20:53,888 --> 04:20:56,036
标记是为了策略和核算。
Tagging is for policy and accounting.

2697
04:20:56,430 --> 04:20:58,116
分区是为了查询。
Partitioning is for queries.

2698
04:20:59,630 --> 04:21:05,408
一个分析团队使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Amazon S3 中的 40TB 数据集。
An analytics team queries a 40TB dataset in Amazon S3 with Amazon Athena.

2699
04:21:05,568 --> 04:21:10,532
数据以 GZip 压缩的 CSV 文件形式存储，并按年份和月份进行分区。
The data is stored as Gazep compressed CSV files partitioned by year and month.

2700
04:21:11,086 --> 04:21:15,652
每个分区大约有 600 个文件，平均每个文件为 60 MB。
There are about 600 files per partition, averaging 60 MB each.

2701
04:21:16,526 --> 04:21:21,412
查询通常只过滤一个月的数据，并从 90 列中读取 4 列。
Queries typically filter on a single month and read 4 columns out of 90.

2702
04:21:21,678 --> 04:21:25,284
目前它们扫描的数据量远超预期，而且运行缓慢。
They currently scan far more data than expected and are slow.

2703
04:21:25,808 --> 04:21:28,804
团队希望同时优化成本和运行时间。
The team wants both cost and runtime improved.

2704
04:21:29,648 --> 04:21:32,004
哪种更改效果最显著？
Which change will have the largest effect?

2705
04:21:32,494 --> 04:21:36,196
A. 将数据按天而不是按月进行重分区。
a Repartition the data by day instead of by month.

2706
04:21:36,814 --> 04:21:37,143
B。
B.

2707
04:21:38,190 --> 04:21:42,020
将文件转换为带有 snappy 压缩的 Apache Parquet 格式。
Convert the files to Apache Parquet with snappy compression.

2708
04:21:42,608 --> 04:21:45,968
C. 增加 Athena 工作组的查询结果。
C Increase the Athena workgroup's query result.

2709
04:21:46,414 --> 04:21:47,556
重用窗口。
Reuse window.

2710
04:21:48,048 --> 04:21:48,368
D
D

2711
04:21:49,294 --> 04:21:51,408
将数据移动到 S3 Standard。
Move the data to S3 standard.

2712
04:21:52,206 --> 04:21:54,500
IA 以降低存储成本。
IA to reduce storage cost.

2713
04:21:54,958 --> 04:21:56,260
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2714
04:22:02,958 --> 04:22:07,012
答案是 B，题目中的比例关系起到了关键作用。
The answer is B, and the ratio in the question is doing the work.

2715
04:22:08,078 --> 04:22:13,956
从基于行的格式中读取四列意味着要读取全部 90 列并丢弃 86 列。
Reading four columns from a row based format means reading all 90 and discarding 86.

2716
04:22:14,414 --> 04:22:17,476
所以 Athena 会对查询从未使用的那些数据计费。
So Athena charges for data the query never uses.

2717
04:22:18,958 --> 04:22:20,996
列式存储只读取那四列。
Columna storage reads only the four.

2718
04:22:21,870 --> 04:22:26,212
压缩方式的改变也很重要，因为 Gzip 是不可分割的。
The compression change matters as well because Gizip is not splitable.

2719
04:22:26,702 --> 04:22:33,348
这就是为什么 660 MB 的文件无法像预期那样高效地并行处理。
That is why 660 MB files are not being processed in parallel as effectively as they could be.

2720
04:22:34,542 --> 04:22:39,648
选项 D 是给那些看到「成本」和「S3」关键词就直接匹配的人设下的陷阱。
Option D is the trap for anyone pattern matching on the words cost and S3.

2721
04:22:40,654 --> 04:22:46,724
这是因为它优化的是存储成本，而 Athena 是按扫描字节数计费的。
That is because it optimizes storage cost while Athena charges for bytes scanned.

2722
04:22:48,366 --> 04:22:54,916
考试大纲将删除数据以满足业务和法律要求列为一项独立技能。
The exam guide names deleting data to meet business and legal requirements as a skill in its own right.

2723
04:22:55,168 --> 04:22:57,732
这比听起来要微妙得多。
It is more subtle than it first sounds.

2724
04:22:58,048 --> 04:23:02,372
这里有两个相反的义务，成熟的组织都会兼顾这两者。
There are two opposite obligations and a mature organization has both.

2725
04:23:03,310 --> 04:23:12,196
保留规则规定某些数据必须在特定期限内保留，且即使是管理员也不允许误删。
Retention rules say certain data must survive for a defined period and must not be removable even by an administrator, even by mistake.

2726
04:23:13,838 --> 04:23:21,156
隐私法规要求的删除规则则要求在指定时间内根据请求删除特定记录。
Deletion rules of the kind privacy legislation creates say specific records must be erased on request within a stated window.

2727
04:23:22,030 --> 04:23:27,328
设计良好的数据湖能同时满足这两者，而两者的机制完全不同。
A well-designed lake satisfies both and the mechanisms have nothing in common.

2728
04:23:27,694 --> 04:23:32,740
一个是让删除变得不可能，另一个是让删除变得精准。
One is about making deletion impossible, the other about making it precise.

2729
04:23:33,646 --> 04:23:36,324
接下来的几页幻灯片将分别讲解这两点。
The next few slides cover each in turn.

2730
04:23:37,134 --> 04:23:45,124
本模块的第三个案例研究是当这两个义务同时作用于同一个存储桶时会发生什么。
The third worked scenario in this module is about what happens when both obligations land on the same bucket.

2731
04:23:46,574 --> 04:23:55,012
在为本课程分析的题库中，出现了 10 次对象锁定，而治理与合规之间的区别是这些题目考察的关键点。
Object lock appeared 10 times in the bank analyzed for this course, and the governance against compliance distinction is what those questions turn on.

2732
04:23:55,950 --> 04:24:06,208
治理模式可以防止意外和常规错误，同时仍允许拥有明确绕过权限的人员删除对象。
Governance mode protects against accident and routine mistakes while still allowing someone who holds an explicit bypass permission to remove an object.

2733
04:24:06,448 --> 04:24:10,852
当你需要安全网而不是法律保证时，这就是正确的选择。
That is the right choice when you want a safety net rather than a legal guarantee.

2734
04:24:11,566 --> 04:24:20,932
合规模式不允许任何人，包括账户根用户和 AWS 自身，在保留周期届满前删除对象。
Compliance mode allows nobody at all, including the account root user and AWS itself, to delete the object before its retention period expires.

2735
04:24:21,728 --> 04:24:29,508
这种绝对性是符合金融监管机构要求的，但也意味着任何错误都是永久且无法修复的。
That absoluteness is what makes it acceptable to financial regulators, and it also means a mistake is permanent and unfixable.

2736
04:24:30,382 --> 04:24:36,004
所以，如果题目描述的是想要带有逃生通道的保护，就是在描述治理模式。
So, a question describing wanting protection with an escape hatch is describing governance mode.

2737
04:24:36,288 --> 04:24:40,740
如果题目提到监管机构或法律保留，就是在描述合规模式。
A question naming a regulator or a legal hold is describing compliance.

2738
04:24:42,510 --> 04:24:46,468
这很容易让人混淆，所以值得清晰地区分开来。
This causes real confusion, so it is worth separating clearly.

2739
04:24:47,278 --> 04:24:49,173
有两个东西叫 Glacier。
There are two things called Glacier.

2740
04:24:50,048 --> 04:24:57,540
一个是存储类别，它是普通 S3 对象的属性，也是本模块中所有内容都在描述的那个。
The storage classes, which are properties of ordinary S3 objects and which everything in this module has described.

2741
04:24:58,350 --> 04:25:05,572
另一个是最初独立的 Glacier 服务，它有自己的保险库和自己的 API，且早于现在的服务。
And the original standalone Glacier service with its own vaults and its own API, which predates them.

2742
04:25:06,030 --> 04:25:08,420
保险库锁定 属于那个较旧的服务。
Vault Lock belongs to that older service.

2743
04:25:08,910 --> 04:25:16,004
它在功能上与合规模式下的对象锁定相同，都能让保留政策变得无法更改。
It does the same job as object lock in compliance mode, making a retention policy permanently unchangeable.

2744
04:25:16,750 --> 04:25:21,220
它出现在旧的资料中，作为监管保留问题的答案。
It appears in older material as the answer to regulatory retention questions.

2745
04:25:21,728 --> 04:25:26,852
对于任何新情况，在 Glacier 存储类别上使用对象锁定是目前的方法。
For anything new, object lock on a Glacier storage class is the current approach.

2746
04:25:28,768 --> 04:25:33,828
第二点是难点，也是为什么开放表格式很重要的原因。
The second point is the hard one, and it is why open table formats matter.

2747
04:25:34,208 --> 04:25:43,364
删除一名客户的隐私请求意味着要找到该客户的所有记录，而这些记录与成千上万其他客户的数据一起存在于 Parquet 文件中。
A privacy request to erase one customer means finding every record for that customer, which sits inside Parquet files alongside thousands of other customers.

2748
04:25:43,808 --> 04:25:45,860
删除文件会把所有人都删掉。
Deleting the file removes everyone.

2749
04:25:46,638 --> 04:25:53,088
必须在不包含该客户的情况下重写文件，而手动在整个数据湖中这样做是不切实际的。
Rewriting the file without that customer is what has to happen, and doing that by hand across a lake is impractical.

2750
04:25:53,518 --> 04:26:00,608
Apache Iceberg 让它变成一条删除语句，这也是考试指南加入开放表格式的主要原因之一。
Apache ICBUb makes it a delete statement, which is a large part of why the exam guide added open table formats.

2751
04:26:01,550 --> 04:26:04,388
最后一项是真正的设计冲突。
The last bullet is a genuine design conflict.

2752
04:26:04,848 --> 04:26:11,524
处于合规锁下的数据无法按要求删除，因此不要将个人数据放入被锁定的存档中。
Data under a compliance lock cannot be erased on request, so keep personal data out of locked archives.

2753
04:26:13,198 --> 04:26:16,164
考试指南将 S3 版本控制和 DynamoDB 放在一起。
The exam guide pairs S3 versioning and DynamoDB.

2754
04:26:16,558 --> 04:26:20,452
它们都具备生存时间这一项技能，这告诉你它在考查平行的对应关系。
Time to live in a single skill, which tells you it wants the parallel draw.

2755
04:26:20,928 --> 04:26:24,132
两者都不会有人去运行任务，就能根据年龄删除数据。
Both delete data by age without anyone running a job.

2756
04:26:24,590 --> 04:26:27,008
这两个注意事项是题目考察的重点。
The two caveats are what questions test.

2757
04:26:27,886 --> 04:26:32,708
删除是一个后台进程，所以项在过期的一瞬间并不保证一定消失。
Deletion is a background process, so an item is not guaranteed gone the moment it expires.

2758
04:26:33,008 --> 04:26:35,748
在此期间，它仍可能出现在查询结果中。
It can still appear in query results in the meantime.

2759
04:26:36,718 --> 04:26:42,468
如果要求是过期的数据绝不能返回，那么你还需要在查询时对时间戳进行过滤。
If a requirement is that expired data must never be returned, you filter on the timestamp in the query as well.

2760
04:26:43,022 --> 04:26:45,540
流处理功能提供了一种常见的模式。
The streams point enables a common pattern.

2761
04:26:46,048 --> 04:26:53,648
生存时间 删除会触发一个 Lambda 函数，在项目消失前将其写入 S3。
A TTL deletion triggers a lambda function which writes the item to S3 before it disappears.

2762
04:26:55,008 --> 04:27:02,628
这些不是竞争选项。它们是两个服务中的相同概念，题目考查的是你是否知道哪个属于哪个服务。
These are not competing options. They are the same idea in two services and questions test whether you know which belongs where.

2763
04:27:03,168 --> 04:27:07,204
生命周期规则是基于天数的存储桶级别策略。
A lifecycle rule is a bucket level policy expressed in days of age.

2764
04:27:08,368 --> 04:27:11,556
生存时间是每个独立项目的属性。
Time to live is an attribute on each individual item.

2765
04:27:12,430 --> 04:27:19,888
这意味着根据设定的业务规则，两个在同一时刻写入的项目可能会在几个月后才过期。
That means two items written at the same moment can expire months apart, according to whatever business rules set them.

2766
04:27:20,368 --> 04:27:26,848
这种针对单个项目的灵活性是真正的区别。比如一个会话记录在最后使用 30 分钟后过期。
That per item flexibility is the real difference. A session record expiring 30 minutes after last use.

2767
04:27:27,598 --> 04:27:33,988
一个在付费期限结束时过期的订阅记录，无法用单一的基于年龄的规则来表达。
A subscription record expiring at the end of a paid term cannot be expressed as a single age-based rule.

2768
04:27:35,246 --> 04:27:39,588
这个强调区分了三个题目中故意混淆在一起的概念。
The call out separates three ideas that questions deliberately blur together.

2769
04:27:40,078 --> 04:27:49,892
持久性意味着 S3 不会因为硬件故障而丢失你的对象，而 11.9s 让这在至少三个可用区中变得几乎确定。
Durability means S3 will not lose your object through hardware failure, and 11.9s makes that effectively certain across at least three availability zones.

2770
04:27:50,688 --> 04:27:56,292
可用性意味着你现在就能访问它，这是受可用区故障影响的因素。
Availability means you can reach it right now, which is a thing an availability zone outage affects.

2771
04:27:56,846 --> 04:28:03,236
这两者都无法保护你免受因错误数据覆盖正确数据，或工程师删除错误前缀导致的后果。
Neither of them protects you from a job that overrides good data with bad or from an engineer deleting the wrong prefix.

2772
04:28:03,726 --> 04:28:05,568
只有版本控制可以做到这一点。
Only versioning does that.

2773
04:28:05,966 --> 04:28:10,372
所以关于从意外覆盖中恢复的问题，答案是版本控制。
So a question about recovering from an accidental overwrite has a versioning answer.

2774
04:28:10,798 --> 04:28:17,732
复制明确不是那个选项，因为复制会忠实且迅速地将错误复制到第二个区域。
Replication is specifically not it because replication faithfully and promptly copies the mistake to the second region.

2775
04:28:18,688 --> 04:28:27,620
第二点中的单可用区例外值得记住，因为它以较低的价格提供三可用区的持久性。
The one zone exception on the second bullet is worth holding because it rates that three availability zone durability for a lower price.

2776
04:28:29,088 --> 04:28:32,740
第二点是值得带入考试的细节。
The second bullet is the detail worth carrying into the exam.

2777
04:28:33,198 --> 04:28:40,228
在已经包含 10 年数据的存储桶上启用复制，根本不会复制任何历史数据。
Enabling replication on a bucket that already holds 10 years of data replicates nothing historical at all.

2778
04:28:40,910 --> 04:28:42,756
它从那一刻起才开始生效。
It applies from that moment forward.

2779
04:28:43,438 --> 04:28:48,868
而且现有的对象需要显式运行 S3 批量复制。
And the existing objects need S3 batch replication run against them explicitly.

2780
04:28:49,806 --> 04:28:58,500
所以，一个描述新启用的复制规则且目标存储桶看起来异常空的内容，就是在描述这种情况。
So a question describing a newly enabled replication rule and a destination bucket that looks suspiciously empty is describing exactly that.

2781
04:28:58,848 --> 04:29:01,508
第四点出于不同的原因很重要。
The fourth bullet matters for a different reason.

2782
04:29:02,542 --> 04:29:13,796
特定版本的永久删除在设计上永远不会被复制，否则恶意或错误的删除就会传播到旨在保护你的副本中。
Permanent deletion of a specific version never replicates by design, because otherwise a malicious or mistaken deletion would propagate to the copy meant to protect you.

2783
04:29:15,502 --> 04:29:17,648
加密将在稍后的模块中单独讲解。
Encryption gets its own module later.

2784
04:29:17,728 --> 04:29:20,772
所以这是阅读数据湖问题所需的简短版本。
So this is the short version needed to read a lake question.

2785
04:29:21,422 --> 04:29:27,620
自 2023 年起，每个新的 S3 对象默认都使用 S3 管理密钥进行静态加密。
Since 2023, every new S3 object is encrypted at REST by default with S3 managed keys.

2786
04:29:28,302 --> 04:29:33,188
因此，提议在存储桶上启用加密的选项描述的是一个已经成立的事实。
So an option proposing to enable encryption on a bucket is describing something already true.

2787
04:29:33,454 --> 04:29:35,968
题目真正考查的是密钥控制。
What questions actually turn on is key control.

2788
04:29:36,654 --> 04:29:44,900
KMS 密钥为你提供每次解密的审计追踪，以及通过更改密钥策略撤销访问权限和跨账户控制的能力。
KMS keys give you an audit trail of every decryption, the ability to revoke access by changing a key policy and cross account control.

2789
04:29:45,710 --> 04:29:51,888
这就是为什么受监管的工作负载指定使用 SSE-KMS 而不是 SSE-S3。
That is why regulated workloads specify SSEKMS rather than SSES3.

2790
04:29:52,782 --> 04:29:55,236
第 19 模块会涵盖这些细节。
Module 19 covers the detail.

2791
04:29:56,974 --> 04:30:06,180
AWS Backup 在官方的在考服务清单中，但在几乎所有的学习资料里都没出现。所以了解它的独特之处很有必要。
AWS backup is on the official inScope service list and appears in almost no study material. So it is worth knowing what distinguishes it.

2792
04:30:06,670 --> 04:30:08,452
版本控制保护的是一个 S3 bucket。
Versioning protects one bucket.

2793
04:30:09,006 --> 04:30:11,076
复制功能复制的是一个 S3 bucket。
Replication copies one bucket.

2794
04:30:11,662 --> 04:30:20,484
AWS Backup 能同时在多个不同的服务中应用一套保留和备份策略，并报告其合规情况。
AWS backup applies one retention and backup policy across many different services at once and reports on compliance with it.

2795
04:30:20,942 --> 04:30:22,692
所以这里的关键点是范围。
So the signal is scope.

2796
04:30:23,408 --> 04:30:28,288
关于保护 S3 bucket 的问题，答案通常是版本控制或复制。
A question about protecting an S3 bucket has a versioning or replication answer.

2797
04:30:28,878 --> 04:30:38,020
如果题目描述的是涵盖 S3、RDS 和 DynamoDB 的单一可审计保留策略，那就是在描述 AWS Backup。
A question about a single auditable retention policy covering S3, RD, S and DynamoDB together is describing AWS backup.

2798
04:30:38,574 --> 04:30:42,052
否则，就得分别配置三种不同的机制。
The alternative is configuring three different mechanisms separately.

2799
04:30:43,726 --> 04:30:46,912
这是本模块的可用性警示。
This is the availability warning for this module.

2800
04:30:47,246 --> 04:30:47,908
S3。
S3.

2801
04:30:48,432 --> 04:30:56,452
S3 Select 让你可以对单个对象运行简单的 SQL 表达式，并只返回匹配的行。
Select Let You Run a Small SQL expression against a single object and get back only the matching rows.

2802
04:30:56,974 --> 04:31:02,980
这非常有用，也是目前流传的几个题目中的正确答案。
That was genuinely useful and is the marked correct answer to several questions in circulation.

2803
04:31:03,822 --> 04:31:07,172
它在 2024 年 7 月停止对新客户开放。
It closed to new customers in July 2024.

2804
04:31:08,526 --> 04:31:16,452
S3 Lambda（在获取对象时转换对象）直到 2025 年 11 月才对现有客户开放。
S3 object Lambda, which transformed objects as they were retrieved, became existing customers only in November 2025.

2805
04:31:17,390 --> 04:31:19,876
但这两者仍出现在考试范围的资料中。
Both still appear in exam scope material.

2806
04:31:20,526 --> 04:31:22,596
所以指导原则和以往一样。
So the guidance is the same as always.

2807
04:31:23,470 --> 04:31:29,444
如果题目描述的是获取一个对象的子集，S3 Select 可能仍是预设的答案。
If a question describes retrieving a subset of one object, S3 select may still be the intended answer.

2808
04:31:29,952 --> 04:31:32,356
Athena 是你实际会使用的工具。
Hethina is what you would actually build with.

2809
04:31:33,792 --> 04:31:38,564
第四点是一个值得识别的模式，因为它能回答一类问题。
The fourth point is a pattern worth recognizing because it answers a class of question.

2810
04:31:39,072 --> 04:31:42,532
某些操作可能需要针对数百万个现有对象执行。
Something may need to happen to millions of existing objects.

2811
04:31:43,022 --> 04:31:47,556
比如复制、重新打标签、从 Glacier 恢复或删除一部分内容。
Copying, re-tagging, restoring from Glacier or deleting a subset.

2812
04:31:48,270 --> 04:31:51,172
列出整个 bucket 来找出哪些目标是不切实际的。
Listing the bucket to work out which ones is impractical.

2813
04:31:52,110 --> 04:31:56,032
S3 库存 会按计划提供每个对象的清单文件。
S3 Inventory delivers a manifest of every object on a schedule.

2814
04:31:56,334 --> 04:32:04,100
你用 Athena 查询那个清单文件来筛选出你想要的内容，然后把结果交给 S3 批量操作去执行任务。
You query that manifest with Athena to select the ones you want. You hand the result to S3 batch operations to do the work.

2815
04:32:04,942 --> 04:32:12,228
存储类分析是另一个值得记住的，因为它决定了你应该如何设置生命周期规则。
Storage class analysis is the other one worth naming because it answers how you decide what a lifecycle rule should say.

2816
04:32:13,902 --> 04:32:21,572
提示框里的这一串逻辑值得作为一个整体来记忆，因为它能解决那些看起来需要自定义代码的问题。
The chain in the callout is worth memorizing as a unit because it answers questions that otherwise look like they need custom code.

2817
04:32:22,112 --> 04:32:29,092
假设监管机构要求将所有带有特定分类标签的对象移动到锁定存档中。
Suppose a regulator asks for every object tagged with a particular classification to be moved to a locked archive.

2818
04:32:29,966 --> 04:32:34,340
在包含 8000 万个对象的 bucket 中列出它们来查找目标是不切实际的。
Listing a bucket of 80 million objects to find them is impractical.

2819
04:32:35,310 --> 04:32:39,204
S3 库存 报告会列出每个对象及其元数据。
An S3 inventory report lists every object with its metadata.

2820
04:32:40,462 --> 04:32:44,484
你用 Athena 查询那个文件，就能生成准确的列表。
You query that file with Athena to produce exactly the list you want.

2821
04:32:45,294 --> 04:32:48,580
你把那个清单作为清单文件交给批处理操作。
You hand that list to batch operations as a manifest.

2822
04:32:49,422 --> 04:32:56,004
然后它会对每一个对象执行操作，重试失败的项，并生成一份完成报告。
It then performs the action on each one, retries failures, and produces a completion report.

2823
04:32:58,094 --> 04:32:59,492
你可以把这个给监管机构看。
You can show the regulator.

2824
04:33:00,942 --> 04:33:10,468
一家金融服务公司必须在 Amazon S3 中保留交易记录 7 年。任何员工，包括管理员，都不得修改或删除它们。
A financial services company must retain trade records in Amazon S3 for 7 years. No employee, including administrators, may alter or delete them.

2825
04:33:10,912 --> 04:33:17,955
另外，同一个存储桶里存放着客户支持的通话记录，这些记录必须在收到客户删除请求后的 30 天内清除。
Separately, the same bucket holds customer support transcripts that must be erased within 30 days of a customer's deletion request.

2826
04:33:18,702 --> 04:33:28,112
一名数据工程师建议在具有 7 年保留周期的存储桶上启用合规模式的 S3 对象锁定。问题是什么，应该怎么做？
A data engineer proposes enabling S3 object lock in compliance mode on the bucket with a 7-year retention period. What is the problem and what should be

2827
04:33:28,112 --> 04:33:29,955
A. 无需操作。
done? A. Nothing.

2828
04:33:30,592 --> 04:33:33,154
合规模式能同时满足这两个要求。
Compliance mode satisfies both requirements.

2829
04:33:33,838 --> 04:33:34,112
B
B

2830
04:33:36,558 --> 04:33:39,812
合规模式会导致支持通话记录无法被删除。
Compliance mode would make the support transcripts undeletable.

2831
04:33:40,670 --> 04:33:45,187
将这两种数据类型分别放入具有不同策略的不同存储桶中。
Separate the two data types into different buckets with different policies.

2832
04:33:45,792 --> 04:33:46,032
C。
C.

2833
04:33:46,702 --> 04:33:52,258
改用治理模式，这样管理员在收到要求时可以删除通话记录。
Use governance mode instead so administrators can delete transcripts when asked.

2834
04:33:52,830 --> 04:33:53,072
D。
D.

2835
04:33:53,678 --> 04:33:58,723
启用版本控制而不是对象锁定，并按要求删除旧版本。
Enable versioning instead of object lock and delete old versions as required.

2836
04:34:00,044 --> 04:34:01,392
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2837
04:34:08,032 --> 04:34:16,192
答案是 B，而选项 C 是一个具有误导性的错误答案，因为它是一个看似能兼顾两个要求但实际上只是折中的方案。
The answer is B, and option C is the instructive wrong answer because it is a compromise that feigns both requirements

2838
04:34:16,432 --> 04:34:18,242
它只是在稍微满足其中一个需求，而不是完美符合任何一个。
slightly rather than one badly.

2839
04:34:19,950 --> 04:34:23,876
治理模式可以让通话记录被删除，这符合目标。
Governance mode makes the transcripts deletable, which was the goal.

2840
04:34:24,812 --> 04:34:32,644
但同时也会让任何拥有绕过权限的人都能删除交易记录，这违反了“任何员工都不能移除它们”的要求。
Simultaneously makes the trade records deletable by anyone holding the bypass permission, which breaks the requirement that no employee can remove them.

2841
04:34:33,966 --> 04:34:40,740
当两个要求在同一个对象上产生真实冲突时，考试要求的做法是分离，而不是寻找折中设置。
When two requirements genuinely conflict on the same objects, the exam expects separation rather than a middle setting.

2842
04:34:41,934 --> 04:34:49,886
这种逻辑不仅适用于对象锁定，也同样适用于加密密钥、权限和生命周期规则。
That generalizes well beyond object lock and it applies to encryption keys, permissions, and lifecycle rules

2843
04:34:50,046 --> 04:34:50,687
同样适用。
too.

2844
04:34:51,822 --> 04:34:58,242
这些内容作为干扰项出现的频率比作为正确答案的频率要高。所以，知道在什么时候它们不起作用才是有用的部分。
These come up as distractors more often than as answers. So knowing when each does nothing is the useful part.

2845
04:34:58,608 --> 04:35:07,684
传输加速的工作原理是让上传进入附近的边缘节点，然后通过 AWS 的骨干网传送到目的地。
Transfer acceleration works by having the upload enter the AWS network at a nearby edge location and travel the rest of the way over AWS's backbone.

2846
04:35:08,558 --> 04:35:12,516
这在悉尼的用户上传到爱尔兰的存储桶时很有用。
That helps when a user in Sydney is uploading to a bucket in Ireland.

2847
04:35:13,006 --> 04:35:17,828
但对于同区域内 EC2 实例上传到存储桶的情况，它完全不起作用。
It does nothing at all for an EC2 instance uploading to a bucket in the same region.

2848
04:35:18,542 --> 04:35:22,052
这是因为不存在需要缩短的漫长公共互联网路径。
That is because there is no long public internet path to shorten.

2849
04:35:22,956 --> 04:35:30,948
而多部分上传是之前提到的“不完整的多部分生命周期规则”存在的原因，因为当上传中断时，这些部分会保留下来。
And multi-part upload is the reason the incomplete multi-part lifecycle rule from earlier exists, because those parts persist when an upload is interrupted.

2850
04:35:32,448 --> 04:35:38,628
每 GB 的存储成本是每个人都在考虑的因素，但它往往不是决定题目答案的关键点。
Storage per gigabyte is the number everyone thinks about, and it is often not the one that decides a question.

2851
04:35:39,182 --> 04:35:43,716
请求这一行解释了为什么小文件问题在整个课程中反复出现。
The request row is why the small file problem keeps recurring across this course.

2852
04:35:44,526 --> 04:35:51,108
这是因为一个涉及 5000 万个对象的查询，在读取任何有用的内容之前，就会产生 5000 万次请求。
That is because a query touching 50 million objects makes 50 million requests before it reads anything useful.

2853
04:35:51,488 --> 04:35:58,850
检索这一行解释了为什么将频繁读取的数据移动到不频繁访问类别可能会增加总费用，而不是减少费用。
The retrieval row is why moving frequently read data to infrequent access can increase the total bin rather than reduce it.

2854
04:35:59,630 --> 04:36:06,562
这是因为现在每次读取都会按每 GB 计费。而传输这一行有一个值得记住的规则。
That is because you now pay per gigabyte every time it is read. And the transfer row has a rule worth memorizing.

2855
04:36:07,246 --> 04:36:08,996
进入 S3 的数据是免费的。
Data into S3 is free.

2856
04:36:09,454 --> 04:36:14,276
区域内的数据传输是免费的，但传到互联网或到另一个区域的就不免费。
Data within a region is free, data out to the internet or to another region is not.

2857
04:36:15,886 --> 04:36:21,732
这个表格汇总了模块内容，第五行值得重点强调。
This table collects the module and the fifth row deserves the emphasis.

2858
04:36:22,768 --> 04:36:32,292
将数据移动到更便宜的类别是明显的成本杠杆，但它有两种可能适得其反的情况，而考试都会考查这两点。
Moving data to a cheaper class is the obvious cost lever and it has two ways of backfiring, both of which the exam tests.

2859
04:36:33,166 --> 04:36:40,484
在不频繁访问和 Glacier 类中，小于 128 KB 的对象也会按 128 KB 计费。
Objects below 128 KB are billed at 128 KB in the infrequent access and glacier classes.

2860
04:36:40,848 --> 04:36:46,116
而且在达到最小存储时长之前被删除或转换的对象，仍会被收取剩余时间的费用。
And objects deleted or transitioned before the minimum duration are charged for the remainder anyway.

2861
04:36:46,990 --> 04:36:55,268
因此，如果不检查对象大小分布和保留周期就编写生命周期规则，真的可能会增加支出。
So, a life cycle rule written without checking the object size distribution and the retention period can genuinely increase spend.

2862
04:36:56,046 --> 04:36:58,532
这是一个值得思考的问题。
That is a satisfying question to be asked.

2863
04:37:00,174 --> 04:37:03,300
一家公司的 S3 账单在一年内稳步增长。
A company's S3 bill has grown steadily for a year.

2864
04:37:03,648 --> 04:37:08,687
与此同时，团队已知的数据量一直保持在 30TB 左右。
Meanwhile, the volume of data the team knows about has stayed roughly constant at 30TB.

2865
04:37:11,054 --> 04:37:14,948
存储透视报告显示该桶中有约 90 TB 的构建存储。
Storage Lens reports about 90 TB of build storage in the bucket.

2866
04:37:16,686 --> 04:37:20,098
在发生意外删除后，两年前启用了版本控制。
Versioning was enabled two years ago after an accidental deletion.

2867
04:37:20,910 --> 04:37:24,036
一个每晚运行的任务会覆盖一组聚合文件。
A nightly job overrides a set of aggregate files.

2868
04:37:24,206 --> 04:37:31,330
过去一年中，一些来自不稳定的本地部署连接的大型上传失败了。哪种组合能解释这种差距并解决问题？
Some large uploads from a flaky on-premises connection have failed over the year. Which combination explains the gap and fixes it?

2869
04:37:31,728 --> 04:37:33,634
A. 启用 S3。
a Enable S3.

2870
04:37:34,574 --> 04:37:38,562
智能分层，让很少访问的数据移动到更便宜的层级。
Intelligent tiering so infrequently accessed data moves to cheaper tiers.

2871
04:37:40,430 --> 04:37:50,340
B. 添加生命周期规则来过期非当前版本并中止未完成的多部分上传。C. 禁用版本控制以停止旧版本的堆积。
Add lifecycle rules to expire non-current versions and to abort incomplete multipart uploads. C. Disable versioning to stop old versions accumulating.

2872
04:37:50,848 --> 04:37:55,844
D. 启用跨区域复制，以便从主桶中删除数据。
D. Enable cross region replication so data can be deleted from the primary bucket.

2873
04:37:56,526 --> 04:37:57,604
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2874
04:38:04,238 --> 04:38:11,396
答案是 B，这个问题的设计逻辑是让情况中的每个细节都对应到答案的一半内容上。
The answer is B, and this question is constructed so that each detail in the situation maps to one half of the answer.

2875
04:38:13,664 --> 04:38:18,820
每晚覆盖加上版本控制解释了旧版本的堆积。
The nightly override plus versioning explains the accumulating old versions.

2876
04:38:19,598 --> 04:38:28,228
不稳定的连接和失败的大型上传解释了那些会被计费且在列出桶内容时不可见的未完成多部分组件。
The flaky connection and failed large uploads explains the incomplete multi-part parts which are billed and do not appear when you list the bucket.

2877
04:38:30,144 --> 04:38:35,651
选项 C 值得注意，因为它是一个直觉反应，但它是双重错误的。
Option C is worth noting because it is the intuitive response and it is doubly wrong.

2878
04:38:36,142 --> 04:38:42,788
它会让所有现有版本保留在原位，并且会移除团队在丢失数据后特意添加的保护措施。
It leaves every existing version in place and it removes the protection the team deliberately added after losing data.

2879
04:38:43,184 --> 04:38:49,504
通过移除安全机制来解决成本问题，是考试中经常扣分的题型。
Fixing a cost problem by removing a safety mechanism is a shape the exam consistently marks down.

2880
04:38:50,990 --> 04:38:57,220
本模块中的场景 3 是对提示框中规则的应用，所以值得通俗地说明一下。
Scenario 3 in this module was an application of the rule in the callout, so it is worth stating generally.

2881
04:38:57,838 --> 04:39:00,419
前缀是免费且具有无限灵活性的。
Prefixes are free and infinitely flexible.

2882
04:39:00,910 --> 04:39:06,692
除了生命周期过滤规则或 IAM 路径所能表达的内容外，它们不包含任何自身的策略。
They carry no policy of their own beyond what a lifecycle filter or an IAM path can express.

2883
04:39:07,534 --> 04:39:09,504
存储桶包含策略。
Buckets carry policy.

2884
04:39:10,062 --> 04:39:18,304
保留设置、默认加密、复制配置、对象锁定和所有权都关联在
Retention settings, default encryption, replication configuration, object lock, and ownership all attach at

2885
04:39:18,464 --> 04:39:19,204
存储桶级别。
bucket level.

2886
04:39:21,198 --> 04:39:25,060
所以设计上的问题从来不是一个存储桶里有多少数据。
So the design question is never how much data goes in a bucket.

2887
04:39:25,966 --> 04:39:29,348
而是其中的所有内容是否能共用一套规则。
It is whether everything in it can share one set of rules.

2888
04:39:30,254 --> 04:39:36,484
最后一个要点将引向第 17 模块，在那里我们将专门讲解跨账户的访问模式。
The last bullet points forward to module 17 where access patterns across accounts get proper treatment.

2889
04:39:37,966 --> 04:39:42,144
访问点是解决大型数据湖普遍面临的一个问题的现代方案。
Access points are the modern answer to a problem every large lake develops.

2890
04:39:42,384 --> 04:39:46,916
一个最初很简洁的单一存储桶策略，会随着每个消费团队的加入而增加相应的条款。
A single bucket policy that started clean grows a clause per consuming team.

2891
04:39:48,864 --> 04:39:55,396
两年后，没人能安全地修改它，因为没人知道哪个条款保护了什么内容。
After two years, nobody can safely change it because nobody knows which clause protects what.

2892
04:39:56,304 --> 04:40:01,316
访问点是连接到存储桶的命名端点，并拥有自己的策略。
An access point is a named endpoint attached to the bucket with its own policy.

2893
04:40:01,744 --> 04:40:07,268
这样每个消费者都有一个适合他们规模的入口，而存储桶策略依然保持简单。
So each consumer gets a door sized for them and the bucket policy stays simple.

2894
04:40:09,230 --> 04:40:11,588
「请求者付费」这一条的适用范围更窄。
The requester pays bullet is narrower.

2895
04:40:12,526 --> 04:40:20,612
它出现在关于发布大型公共数据集的问题中，其中发布者不希望为所有人的下载付费。
It appears in questions about publishing a large public dataset where the publisher does not want to fund everyone as his downloads.

2896
04:40:21,902 --> 04:40:27,012
一个应用程序将会话记录写入 Amazon DynamoDB 表。
An application writes session records to an Amazon DynamoDB table.

2897
04:40:27,726 --> 04:40:33,668
每个会话在最后一次活动后应保留正好 90 天，然后删除。
Each session should be retained for exactly 90 days after its last activity, then removed.

2898
04:40:34,446 --> 04:40:38,788
由于各会话的生命周期差异很大，它们的过期日期也不同。
Sessions have widely different lifespans, so their expiry dates differ.

2899
04:40:39,630 --> 04:40:47,044
团队还需要在这些会话消失前将过期的会话归档到 Amazon S3，用于年度报告。
The team also needs expired sessions archived to Amazon S3 for annual reporting before they disappear.

2900
04:40:47,630 --> 04:40:54,404
一个提议是运行一个每晚执行的 Lambda 函数来扫描表并删除过期项目。
A proposal is to run a nightly lambda function that scans the table and deletes expired items.

2901
04:40:55,790 --> 04:40:58,244
数据工程师应该采用什么方案？
What should the data engineer implement instead?

2902
04:41:00,430 --> 04:41:06,276
A. 保留每晚扫描，但增加表的预置读取容量，以便更快完成。
Keep the nightly scan but increase the table's provisioned read capacity so it completes faster.

2903
04:41:07,022 --> 04:41:15,236
B. 对过期属性启用 Dynamo DB 生存时间，并利用 Dynamo DB 流将删除的项目归档到 Amazon S3。
b Enable Dynamo DB TTL on an expired attribute and use Dynamo DB streams to archive deleted items to Amazon S3.

2904
04:41:15,824 --> 04:41:21,316
C. 对 DynamoDB 表应用 90 天的 S3 生命周期过期规则。
C. Apply an S3 lifecycle expiration rule of 90 days to the DynamoDB table.

2905
04:41:21,984 --> 04:41:22,304
D。
D.

2906
04:41:22,784 --> 04:41:27,844
每 90 天将表导出到 Amazon S3 并重新创建一个空表。
Export the table to Amazon S3 every 90 days and recreate it empty.

2907
04:41:30,670 --> 04:41:32,004
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2908
04:41:38,542 --> 04:41:44,260
答案是 B，决定这一点的词汇是「会话具有不同的生命周期」。
The answer is B, and the phrase that decides it is that sessions have different lifespans.

2909
04:41:44,560 --> 04:41:52,196
任何基于数据整体年龄的机制都会失败，因为在同一天写入的两条记录应该在几个月后才过期。
Any mechanism based on the age of the data as a whole fails because two records written on the same day should expire months apart.

2910
04:41:52,560 --> 04:41:56,580
生存时间是针对每个项目的，因此每条记录都有自己的过期时间。
Time to live is per item, so each record carries its own expiry.

2911
04:41:57,134 --> 04:42:06,980
归档这一部分让 B 选项不仅是正确，而且是完整的，因为 生存时间 删除会发出包含该项目的流记录。
The archiving half is what makes B complete rather than merely correct because a TTL deletion emits a stream record containing the item.

2912
04:42:07,470 --> 04:42:11,236
所以 Lambda 函数可以在数据传出时将其写入 S3。
So a lambda function can write it to S3 on the way out.

2913
04:42:11,950 --> 04:42:18,980
选项 C 是一个值得提到的类别错误，因为生命周期规则只属于 S3，不属于其他任何东西。
Option C is the category error worth naming since lifecycle rules belong to S3 and nothing else.

2914
04:42:20,622 --> 04:42:21,680
共 5 道题。
5 questions.

2915
04:42:21,998 --> 04:42:30,800
而第四题是这个领域中最常出现的、用来区分两个看似合理的选项的题目。存储类别的更改会影响你存储数据的费用。
And the fourth is the one that separates two plausible options, most often in this domain. Storage class changes affect what you pay to keep data.

2916
04:42:31,118 --> 04:42:35,140
分区和文件格式的更改会影响你读取数据的费用。
Partitioning and file format changes affect what you pay to read it.

2917
04:42:35,790 --> 04:42:39,440
Athena 的计费是按扫描字节数计算的，与存储类别无关。
Athena bills bytes scanned regardless of storage class.

2918
04:42:39,600 --> 04:42:51,140
因此，将数据移动到标准-低频访问对查询账单没有任何影响，反而会增加检索费用。搞清楚这个区别可以排除掉几乎所有关于 S3 成本问题的干扰项。
So moving data to standard infrequent access does nothing for a query bill and adds a retrieval charge. Getting that distinction right eliminates a distractor in almost every S3 cost question.

2919
04:42:51,822 --> 04:42:56,772
下一个模块涵盖开放表格式，这是出现很多问题的部分。
Next module covers open table formats, which is where several problems.

2920
04:42:57,280 --> 04:42:59,428
这个模块之前只能描述为……
This module could only describe.

2921
04:43:01,033 --> 04:43:02,213
现在终于解决了。
Finally gets solved.

2922
04:43:03,854 --> 04:43:09,200
这是当前考试与市面上所有题库之间差距最大的模块。
This is the module with the largest gap between the current exam and every question bank in circulation.

2923
04:43:09,550 --> 04:43:14,020
在针对本课程的题库分析中，Apache Iceberg 相关内容出现了 29 次。
Apache IC work appeared 29 times in the bank analyze for this course.

2924
04:43:14,446 --> 04:43:19,236
这些题目中的每一个，都是作为与 Parquet 和 ORC 并列的文件格式出现的。
Every one of those was as a file format sitting alongside Parquet and ORC.

2925
04:43:20,174 --> 04:43:22,960
但这不再是考试大纲要求的考点。
That is not what the exam guide now asks about.

2926
04:43:23,200 --> 04:43:29,668
开放表格式在 2025 年 12 月发布的 1.1 版本中成为一项明确的技能。
Open table formats became a named skill in version 1.1 published in December 2025.

2927
04:43:30,000 --> 04:43:33,892
S3 表格也在同一时间被添加到考核范围的服务列表中。
S3 tables was added to the in-scope service list at the same time.

2928
04:43:34,880 --> 04:43:40,160
模块 1、2 和 3 都承诺这个模块会妥善涵盖这些内容。
Modules 1, 2, and 3 each promised that this module would cover it properly.

2929
04:43:40,526 --> 04:43:41,200
它确实涵盖了。
It does.

2930
04:43:41,440 --> 04:43:43,044
四个工作场景。
Four worked scenarios.

2931
04:43:44,558 --> 04:43:51,236
你不需要背诵这个层级结构，理解它的结构就能解释该模块中的所有内容。
You will not be asked to recite this hierarchy, and understanding its shape explains everything else in the module.

2932
04:43:51,790 --> 04:43:58,852
读取一个表意味着向下追踪链条，并且在每一层，都有足够的信息来跳过整个分支。
Reading a table means following the chain downward, and at each level there is enough information to skip whole branches.

2933
04:43:59,502 --> 04:44:05,252
清单文件记录了它所列出的所有文件中每个列的最小值和最大值。
A manifest records the minimum and maximum value of each column across the files it lists.

2934
04:44:06,126 --> 04:44:12,740
因此，针对日期的查询可以丢弃整个清单文件，而无需打开任何数据文件。
So a query filtering on a date can discard entire manifests without opening a single data file.

2935
04:44:13,582 --> 04:44:21,860
这就是为什么 Iceberg 查询规划在拥有数百万个文件的表中依然保持高效，而在这些情况下，列出 S3 前缀可能需要几分钟。
That is why IZBERG query planning stays fast on tables with millions of files, where listing an S3 prefix would take minutes.

2936
04:44:23,200 --> 04:44:28,900
而提交操作仅仅是在链条下方写入新文件，然后更换顶部的指针。
And a commit is simply writing new files down the chain, then swapping the pointer at the top.

2937
04:44:30,478 --> 04:44:36,516
从真正存在问题的地方开始，因为只有在明确问题后，解决方案才有意义。
Start with what is actually broken, because the solution only makes sense once the problem is clear.

2938
04:44:38,094 --> 04:44:43,840
当查询引擎读取数据湖时，它会列出前缀下的文件并读取它们。
When a query engine reads a data lake, it lists the files under a prefix and reads them.

2939
04:44:44,366 --> 04:44:52,932
没有任何地方记录哪些文件属于一起、上周二的模式是什么，或者写入是完成了还是在中途失败了。
Nothing anywhere records which files belong together, what the schema was last Tuesday, or whether a write finished or died halfway.

2940
04:44:54,606 --> 04:44:57,636
所有“表”这个词所隐含的内容都不存在。
Everything the word table implies is absent.

2941
04:44:58,958 --> 04:45:03,840
原子性、一致性视图，以及修改单行数据的能力。
Atomicity, a consistent view, the ability to change one row.

2942
04:45:04,462 --> 04:45:11,492
对于仅追加数据来说，这没问题，因为没人去编辑它，而很多真实的数据集就是这样的。
That works perfectly well for append-only data, nobody ever edits, which describes a great many real datasets.

2943
04:45:12,206 --> 04:45:17,860
但一旦需要为了满足隐私请求而修正或删除数据时，情况就变了
It falls apart the moment data must be corrected or deleted to satisfy a privacy request

2944
04:45:18,638 --> 04:45:21,348
或者在有人读取的同时进行写入。
or written at the same time as somebody is reading it.

2945
04:45:22,318 --> 04:45:26,180
这三个需求正是催生开放表格式的原因。
Those three requirements are what created open table formats.

2946
04:45:27,726 --> 04:45:32,676
记住这五个点，因为它们每一个都在本课程中出现过。
Recognize these five because every one of them has already appeared in this course.

2947
04:45:33,294 --> 04:45:35,396
模块 2 讲解了 DMS。
Module 2 described DMS.

2948
04:45:35,680 --> 04:45:40,516
将变更记录写入 S3 以及将这些记录与当前状态进行对账的难度。
Writing change records into S3 and the difficulty of reconciling them into current state.

2949
04:45:41,102 --> 04:45:49,380
模块 8 描述了一个针对单个客户的隐私删除请求，而该客户的记录位于与其他数千人共享的文件中。
Module 8 described a privacy deletion request for a single customer whose records sit inside files shared with thousands of others.

2950
04:45:49,902 --> 04:45:55,652
模块 3 介绍了流式写入，它产生的中间状态可能会被读取者在传输过程中捕捉到。
Module 3 describes streaming rights, producing partial state that a reader might catch mid-flight.

2951
04:45:56,494 --> 04:46:00,400
它们并不是需要五个不同解决方案的五个独立问题。
They are not 5 separate problems needing 5 separate solutions.

2952
04:46:00,782 --> 04:46:07,268
它们都是同一个底层缺陷造成的，即文件目录上方缺乏一个事务层。
They are all the same underlying gap, which is that a directory of files has no transactional layer above it.

2953
04:46:07,982 --> 04:46:10,276
Iceberg 正是增加了这个层。
Iceberg adds precisely that layer.

2954
04:46:11,086 --> 04:46:17,252
一旦你这样理解，一类考试题目就会简化为一个清晰可辨的考点。
Once you see them that way, a whole class of exam question collapses into a single recognizable question.

2955
04:46:18,926 --> 04:46:24,420
这个机制比人们预想的要简单，值得作为一个整体概念来掌握。
The mechanism is simpler than people expect and worth holding as a single idea.

2956
04:46:24,910 --> 04:46:33,604
除了数据文件外，Iceberg 还维护元数据，记录在每个时间点哪些文件构成该表。
Alongside the data files, Heisenberg maintains metadata recording precisely which files constitute the table at each point in time.

2957
04:46:34,286 --> 04:46:38,116
读取者会查阅这些元数据，而不是直接列出所有文件。
A reader consults that metadata rather than listing it directly.

2958
04:46:38,958 --> 04:46:45,540
写入者添加新的数据文件，然后原子性地发布指向这些新文件的元数据。
A writer adds new data files and then atomically publishes new metadata pointing at them.

2959
04:46:46,080 --> 04:46:53,440
在最终的发布完成之前，读取者仍能看到之前的状态，它是完整且一致的，不会出现部分结果。
Until that final publish happens, readers continue to see the previous state, complete and consistent, with no partial results.

2960
04:46:53,680 --> 04:46:56,132
只需更改一个指针，表的内容就会改变。
Change one pointer and the table changes.

2961
04:46:56,974 --> 04:47:01,028
这一个核心思想就涵盖了下一页上的所有功能。
That single idea produces every capability on the next slide.

2962
04:47:01,358 --> 04:47:08,228
事务、时间旅行、安全的架构变更以及并发写入，都源于同一个机制。
Transactions, time travel, safe schema changes, and concurrent writers all fall out of the same mechanism.

2963
04:47:08,782 --> 04:47:12,996
这就是为什么它们是成套出现的，而不是作为独立功能存在的。
That is why they arrive together rather than as separate features.

2964
04:47:14,670 --> 04:47:21,924
分区演进值得特别提一下，因为模块 8 说布局决策实际上是永久性的，而这是个例外。
Partition evolution deserves the call out because module 8 said layout decisions are effectively permanent, and this is the exception.

2965
04:47:22,318 --> 04:47:29,188
在普通的数据湖中，从按月到按日切换分区意味着要重写你拥有的每一个对象。
In a plain lake, changing from monthly to daily partitions means rewriting every object you have.

2966
04:47:29,920 --> 04:47:34,756
Iceberg 将分区方案作为每个快照的一部分记录在元数据中。
Iceberg records the partitioning scheme as part of the metadata per snapshot.

2967
04:47:35,040 --> 04:47:44,836
因此，新数据可以按天写入，而 5 年的月度历史数据仍保持原样。跨越这两者的查询也能在两种架构下正确执行。
So new data can be written daily while 5 years of monthly history stays exactly where it is. A query spanning both is planned correctly across the two schemes.

2968
04:47:45,838 --> 04:47:50,596
这是一项真正的功能，无论你怎么精心命名目录都无法实现。
That is a genuine capability, no amount of careful directory naming provides.

2969
04:47:52,160 --> 04:47:59,524
这是 Iceberg 内部最值得理解的一点，因为它解释了一个否则看起来很神秘的性能问题。
This is the iceberg internal most worth understanding because it explains a performance complaint that otherwise looks mysterious.

2970
04:48:00,320 --> 04:48:07,268
写时复制在写入时完成工作，重写整个数据文件并剔除已删除的行。
Copy on write does the work at write time, rewriting whole data files without the deleted rows.

2971
04:48:08,160 --> 04:48:11,396
这样读取者看到的是干净的表，且不需要额外付费。
So readers see a clean table and pay nothing extra.

2972
04:48:12,302 --> 04:48:17,572
读时合并在写入时只做最少的工作，只是记录哪些行不再计入。
Merge on read does the minimum at write time, recording separately which rows no longer count.

2973
04:48:17,920 --> 04:48:22,020
随后每一个读取者在扫描时都必须应用这些删除操作。
Every subsequent reader then has to apply those deletes while scanning.

2974
04:48:22,894 --> 04:48:29,188
这使得流式更新的写入成本较低，但会导致查询变慢，直到合并将删除文件折叠进去为止。
That makes streaming updates cheap to write and gradually makes queries slower until compaction folds the delete files in.

2975
04:48:30,030 --> 04:48:36,676
因此，一个频繁进行小更新且速度不断变慢的表，通常是采用了读时合并但合并次数不足。
So a table taking frequent small updates and getting steadily slower is often merged on read without enough compaction.

2976
04:48:38,414 --> 04:48:42,160
这解决了在纯数据泄露中造成实际金钱损失的问题。
This solves a problem that costs real money in plain data leaks.

2977
04:48:42,800 --> 04:48:49,988
假设一个表按包含日期的字符串列进行分区，而分析师却根据事件时间戳进行过滤。
Suppose a table is partitioned by a string column holding the date and an analyst filters on the event timestamp instead.

2978
04:48:50,894 --> 04:48:59,460
这个过滤条件在逻辑上是正确的，结果也是正确的，但由于引擎无法将时间戳与分区列关联，因此不会进行任何裁剪。
The filter is logically correct, the results are right, and the engine prunes nothing at all because it cannot connect the timestamp to the partition column.

2979
04:49:00,622 --> 04:49:03,236
查询会扫描所有内容，账单也会反映出这一点。
The query scans everything and the bill reflects it.

2980
04:49:03,822 --> 04:49:10,788
Iceberg 将这种关系存储为转换，因此它知道分区源自时间戳的日期部分。
Iceberg stores that relationship as a transform so it knows the partition derives from the day part of the timestamp.

2981
04:49:11,120 --> 04:49:18,948
这样对时间戳的过滤就能自动进行裁剪，分析师也不再需要了解物理布局就能编写高效查询。
A filter on the timestamp then prunes automatically, and analysts stop needing to know the physical layout to write an efficient query.

2982
04:49:20,686 --> 04:49:26,884
列标识符这一点是核心机制，值得理解而不是死记硬背。
The column identifier point is the mechanism and it is worth understanding rather than memorizing.

2983
04:49:27,726 --> 04:49:30,596
在基于名称的格式中，匹配是按名称进行的。
In a name-based format, matching happens by name.

2984
04:49:30,990 --> 04:49:36,196
在重命名之前写入的文件和在重命名后写入的文件看起来就像拥有完全不同的列。
A file written before a rename and one written after look like they have different columns entirely.

2985
04:49:37,070 --> 04:49:44,004
Iceberg 在创建时为每个列分配一个稳定的数字标识符，并单独跟踪名称。
Iceberg assigns each column a stable numeric identifier at creation and tracks the name separately.

2986
04:49:44,910 --> 04:49:51,972
重命名列后，所有历史文件仍能正确映射，因为标识符从未改变。
Rename the column and every historical file still maps correctly because the identifier never changed.

2987
04:49:52,782 --> 04:50:01,924
这就是为什么 Iceberg 的架构变更被描述为安全的，而对普通的 Parquet 数据集执行相同操作则是一个迁移项目。
That is why iceberg schema changes are described as safe, while the same operation on a plain parquet dataset is a migration project.

2988
04:50:03,502 --> 04:50:06,756
这个特别提醒描述了考试喜欢的场景。
The call-out describes the scenario the exam likes.

2989
04:50:07,088 --> 04:50:13,540
一个转换作业有 Bug，并在表中写入错误的值，而且没人注意到这种情况持续了一整天。
A transformation job has a bug and writes wrong values over a table and nobody notices for a day.

2990
04:50:14,478 --> 04:50:23,248
如果没有 Iceberg，恢复需要从备份中还原或从原始数据重新处理，这两者都需要时间且会丢失自那时起写入的所有内容。
Without iceberg, the recovery is restoring from backup or reprocessing from raw, both of which take time and lose anything written since.

2991
04:50:23,950 --> 04:50:30,916
有了 Iceberg，只需将表回滚到错误作业运行前的快照，因为没有数据移动，这几乎是瞬间完成的。
With Iceberg, it is a rollback to the snapshot before the bad job ran, which is close to instantaneous because no data moves.

2992
04:50:31,854 --> 04:50:34,128
只有元数据指针发生了变化。
Only a metadata pointer changes.

2993
04:50:34,606 --> 04:50:37,476
可重复性这一点对于受监管的报告非常重要。
The reproducibility point matters for regulated reporting.

2994
04:50:38,382 --> 04:50:44,388
展示在发布数据时，数据究竟是什么样子的，是审计的要求。
Showing exactly what the data looked like when a figure was published is an audit requirement.

2995
04:50:45,678 --> 04:50:50,820
正确的审计发布模式值得了解，因为它回答了本课程反复提到的问题。
The right audit publish pattern is worth knowing because it answers something this course has raised repeatedly.

2996
04:50:51,566 --> 04:50:56,208
第 7 模块强调了：作业成功并不代表数据是正确的。
Module 7 made the point that a job succeeding tells you nothing about whether the numbers are right.

2997
04:50:56,494 --> 04:50:59,460
分支让这种检查变得强制执行，而不仅仅是建议性的。
Branches make the check enforceable rather than advisory.

2998
04:51:00,334 --> 04:51:07,968
作业写入到分支中，质量检查在那个分支上运行，只有通过后才会合并到主分支。
The job writes into a branch, quality checks run against that branch, and only if they pass does it merge into main.

2999
04:51:08,942 --> 04:51:12,804
用户始终查询主分支，永远不会看到中间状态。
Consumers query main throughout and never see the intermediate state at all.

3000
04:51:13,678 --> 04:51:21,408
相比之下，在发布后才检查质量，意味着错误的数字会暴露给所有人，直到检查完成为止。
Compare that with checking quality after publishing, where wrong numbers were visible to everyone for however long the check took to run.

3001
04:51:22,798 --> 04:51:29,060
本模块中的场景 3 要求你将表回滚到故障任务之前的快照。
Scenario 3 in this module asks you to roll a table back to the snapshot from before a faulty job.

3002
04:51:29,646 --> 04:51:31,300
这张幻灯片展示了如何找到它。
This slide is how you find it.

3003
04:51:31,886 --> 04:51:37,412
快照元数据表列出了每一个快照及其时间戳和标识符。
The snapshots metadata table lists every snapshot with its timestamp and its identifier.

3004
04:51:38,254 --> 04:51:42,692
因此，根据任务开始时间进行过滤的查询就能准确返回你需要的那一个。
So a query filtering on the time the job started returns exactly the one you need.

3005
04:51:43,054 --> 04:51:49,540
这让恢复工作从盲目猜测变成了常规查询，当有 200 名分析师在等待时，这一点非常重要。
That turns a recovery from an anxious guess into an ordinary lookup, which matters when 200 analysts are waiting.

3006
04:51:50,414 --> 04:51:56,964
文件表是另一个在操作上很有用的表，因为它报告了每个数据文件的大小。
The files table is the other operationally useful one because it reports the size of every data file.

3007
04:51:57,422 --> 04:52:03,396
这就是你证明一个表出现了小文件问题，而不仅仅是怀疑它的一种方法。
That is how you demonstrate a table has accumulated a small file problem rather than merely suspecting it.

3008
04:52:05,070 --> 04:52:10,724
这三种方式在很大程度上解决了相同的问题，考试不会考查它们内部机制的对比。
All three solve broadly the same problem, and the exam does not test their internals against each other.

3009
04:52:11,278 --> 04:52:16,580
它测试的是 AWS 构建了哪一种，这个答案是明确的。
What it tests is which one AWS has built around, and the answer is unambiguous.

3010
04:52:17,422 --> 04:52:22,756
Iceberg 是考试大纲中提到的名称，也是 S3 表格构建的基础。
Iceberg is the format named in the exam guide scale. The format S3 tables is built on.

3011
04:52:23,694 --> 04:52:28,836
它是唯一在 Athena、Redshift、EMR、Glue 和 Firehose 中都获得原生支持的格式。
The one with native support across Athena, Redshift, EMR, GUE and Firehose.

3012
04:52:29,248 --> 04:52:34,788
Hudi 和 Delta 虽然确实受到 Glue 和 EMR 支持，但它们只是作为备选项出现。
Houdi and Delta are genuinely supported by BU and EMR, and they appear as options.

3013
04:52:35,598 --> 04:52:36,688
规则很简单。
The rule is simple.

3014
04:52:36,928 --> 04:52:41,252
如果问题明确提到了 Hudi 或 Delta，就选那个。
If the question names Hoodi or Delta explicitly, work with that.

3015
04:52:41,934 --> 04:52:45,124
如果它描述的是某种需求，就选 Iceberg。
If it describes a requirement, answer iceberg.

3016
04:52:46,862 --> 04:52:55,968
一家医疗公司将 10 年的患者互动记录作为 Parquet 文件存储在 Amazon S3 中，按月分区，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行查询。
A healthcare company stores 10 years of patient interaction records as parquet files in Amazon S3, partitioned by month, queried with Amazon Athena.

3017
04:52:56,334 --> 04:53:02,852
根据隐私法规，公司必须在收到请求后的 30 天内删除特定患者的所有记录。
Under privacy legislation, the company must erase all records for a given patient within 30 days of a request.

3018
04:53:03,598 --> 04:53:06,500
每月收到大约 40 个此类请求。
Receives around 40 such requests a month.

3019
04:53:07,342 --> 04:53:14,628
目前，工程师需要识别每一个受影响的文件，重写每个不包含该患者行的文件，并进行替换。
Currently, an engineer identifies every affected file, rewrites each one without the patient's rows, and replaces it.

3020
04:53:15,168 --> 04:53:21,924
这个过程每个请求需要两天时间，并且在重写中途失败时，曾两次导致分区损坏。
The process takes two days per request and has twice produced corrupted partitions when a rewrite failed midway.

3021
04:53:22,830 --> 04:53:24,388
公司应该采用什么方案？
What should the company implement?

3022
04:53:25,070 --> 04:53:31,076
a 将数据集转换为 Apache Iceberg 表并使用 delete 语句来删除行。
a convert the dataset to Apache ICWork tables and use delete statements to remove the rows.

3023
04:53:31,662 --> 04:53:37,572
b 按患者标识符对数据进行分区，以便按请求删除整个文件。
b Partition the data by patient identifier so entire files can be deleted per request.

3024
04:53:39,086 --> 04:53:39,328
C
C

3025
04:53:40,590 --> 04:53:45,988
启用 S3 版本控制，以便失败的重写可以回滚到之前的版本。
Enable S3 versioning so a failed rewrite can be rolled back to the previous version.

3026
04:53:46,448 --> 04:53:46,688
D。
D.

3027
04:53:47,168 --> 04:53:51,364
将数据迁移到支持 delete 语句的 Amazon Redshift。
Move the data to Amazon Redshift where delete statements are supported.

3028
04:53:51,982 --> 04:53:53,124
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3029
04:53:59,854 --> 04:54:01,552
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3030
04:54:02,606 --> 04:54:06,212
题目中提到的两个弊端，都可以通过同一种改变来解决。
Two harms in the question are both addressed by the same change.

3031
04:54:07,790 --> 04:54:12,484
删除操作变成了一条语句，而不是要花上两天时间去手动处理文件。
Deletion becomes a single statement rather than two days of manual file surgery.

3032
04:54:12,992 --> 04:54:20,516
因为写入是原子性的，如果中途失败，表的状态会保持不变，而不会导致分区损坏。
Because the right is atomic, a failure midway leaves the table exactly as it was rather than corrupting a partition.

3033
04:54:21,454 --> 04:54:30,468
选项 B 值得研究，因为如果考生只学了分区但没了解它的局限性，就会选这个答案。
Option B is worth studying because it is the answer a candidate reaches for if they have learned partitioning without learning its limits.

3034
04:54:30,752 --> 04:54:38,980
使用像患者 ID 这样高基数的键进行分区，会导致模块 8 中提到的过度分区问题。
Partitioning by a high cardinality key like patient identifier creates the overpartitioning failure module 8 warned about.

3035
04:54:39,886 --> 04:54:45,028
它优化了极少数的删除操作，但代价是影响每一次普通的查询。
It optimizes for the rare deletion at the cost of every ordinary query.

3036
04:54:46,766 --> 04:54:52,196
这是那些热情洋溢的介绍中忽略的部分，也是很多考题所在的地方。
This is the part left out of enthusiastic descriptions and it is where several exam questions live.

3037
04:54:53,550 --> 04:54:57,124
Iceberg 通过从不原地修改文件来实现原子性。
Iceberg achieves atomicity by never modifying files in place.

3038
04:54:57,472 --> 04:55:04,032
更新操作会写入新的数据文件和新的元数据，旧文件依然存在但不再被引用。
An update writes new data files and new metadata, leaving the old ones present but unreferenced.

3039
04:55:04,592 --> 04:55:10,180
删除操作可能会写入一个记录哪些行需要忽略的删除文件，而不是真的移除任何内容。
A delete may write a delete file recording which rows to ignore rather than removing anything.

3040
04:55:10,512 --> 04:55:19,748
这样做成千上万次后，就会堆积小文件、过时的快照以及陈旧的数据，这些都会增加存储成本并降低查询速度。
Do that thousands of times and you accumulate small files, stale snapshots, and often data, all of which cost storage and slow queries down.

3041
04:55:20,622 --> 04:55:24,452
维护不是可选的家务活，你迟早得去处理它。
Maintenance is not optional housekeeping, you get to the eventually.

3042
04:55:24,910 --> 04:55:31,364
它是运行 Iceberg 的必要环节，任何没人维护的表，其性能每周都会明显下降。
It is a required part of running iceberg and a table nobody maintains gets measurably worse every week.

3043
04:55:32,110 --> 04:55:35,524
这就是为什么接下来的几张幻灯片和之前的核心功能一样重要。
That is why the next few slides matter as much as the capabilities did.

3044
04:55:37,166 --> 04:55:42,628
记住这三个术语的名字，因为 S3 表的定义就是为你执行这些操作。
Learn these three by name because S3 tables is defined by performing them for you.

3045
04:55:44,078 --> 04:55:53,252
合并解决了本课程在四个不同模块中提到的小文件问题，现在这些问题作为频繁写入的后果出现了。
Compaction addresses the small file problem this course has raised in four separate modules now appearing as a consequence of frequent writes.

3046
04:55:54,158 --> 04:55:57,924
快照过期是那个值得理解的权衡点。
Snapshot expiration is the one with the trade-off worth understanding.

3047
04:55:58,702 --> 04:56:06,084
快照是实现时间旅行和回滚的关键，它们保留了原本会被删除的数据文件引用。
Snapshots are what make time travel and rollback possible, and they hold references to data files that would otherwise be deleted.

3048
04:56:06,958 --> 04:56:13,284
如果你把它们保留 90 天，你就可以回溯 90 天，但你要为这 90 天的过时数据付费。
Keep them for 90 days and you can travel back 90 days and you pay for 90 days of superseded data.

3049
04:56:13,742 --> 04:56:18,564
那个保留设置是一个真正的业务决策，而不是技术上的默认选项。
That retention setting is a genuine business decision rather than a technical default.

3050
04:56:19,982 --> 04:56:26,788
考生往往认为这是在「S3 表」和「自己构建合并作业」之间二选一。
Candidates tend to see this as a binary between S3 tables and building compaction jobs yourself.

3051
04:56:26,992 --> 04:56:29,284
但还有一个值得了解的折中方案。
And there is a middle option worth knowing.

3052
04:56:30,062 --> 04:56:38,512
Glue 数据目录可以对存储在普通通用存储桶中的 Iceberg 表执行表优化。
The Glue data catalog can run table optimization on iceberg tables living in ordinary general purpose buckets.

3053
04:56:39,118 --> 04:56:43,652
它会按照你配置的计划，执行相同的合并和快照管理。
It performs the same compaction and snapshot management on a schedule you configure.

3054
04:56:44,046 --> 04:56:49,156
当团队想要托管维护但无法将数据移动到表存储桶时，这一点就很重要。
That matters when a team wants managed maintenance but cannot move data into table buckets.

3055
04:56:49,392 --> 04:56:54,596
也许同一个存储桶里还有其他对象，或者已经设置了特定的生命周期规则。
Perhaps the same bucket holds other objects or specific lifecycle rules are already in place.

3056
04:56:55,470 --> 04:57:00,932
最后一项是诚实的默认选项，也正是场景 2 所描述的情况。
The last bullet is the honest default and it is exactly what scenario 2 describes happening.

3057
04:57:02,542 --> 04:57:08,804
排序和 Zorder 合并在 2025 年才推出，旧的资料里没有涵盖它们，所以值得了解。
Sort and Zorder compaction arrived in 2025 and no older material covers them, so they are worth knowing.

3058
04:57:09,312 --> 04:57:11,844
这与模块 8 的联系非常直接。
The connection to module 8 is direct.

3059
04:57:12,112 --> 04:57:18,052
数据包存储每个块的最小值和最大值，查询时可以跳过范围不匹配的块。
Packet stores minimum and maximum values per block, and a query can skip a block whose range cannot match.

3060
04:57:18,830 --> 04:57:23,652
在随机排序的数据中，每个块都覆盖整个范围，没有任何内容可以跳过。
On randomly ordered data, every block spans the whole range and nothing is skippable.

3061
04:57:24,398 --> 04:57:30,500
排序合并在合并过程中对行进行物理重排，从而使这些统计数据变得有意义。
Sort compaction physically reorders rows during compaction so those statistics become meaningful.

3062
04:57:31,278 --> 04:57:34,276
ZORDER 能同时在多个列上执行同样的操作。
ZORDER does the same across several columns at once.

3063
04:57:35,152 --> 04:57:42,244
当查询过滤的是两个或三个字段的不同组合，而不是始终是同一个字段时，你就需要这个功能。
That is what you want when queries filter on different combinations of two or three fields rather than always the same one.

3064
04:57:43,854 --> 04:57:48,132
第 8 模块介绍了通用存储桶和目录存储桶。
Module 8 introduced general purpose buckets and directory buckets.

3065
04:57:48,942 --> 04:57:50,820
表存储桶是第三种类型。
Table buckets are the third type.

3066
04:57:51,566 --> 04:57:55,108
它们是在 2024 年 12 月的 reInvent 上发布的。
They were announced at reInvent in December 2024.

3067
04:57:55,726 --> 04:58:01,792
在一年后的 1.1 版本修订中，它们被添加到考试范围服务列表中。
Added to the exams in Scope Service list a year later in the version 1.1 revision.

3068
04:58:02,352 --> 04:58:11,972
它们的区别不在于它们存储 Iceberg 表，因为通用存储桶也能很好地做到这一点，而且许多机构也正以这种方式使用它。
The distinguishing feature is not that they store iceberg tables because a general purpose bucket does that perfectly well and many organizations use it that way.

3069
04:58:12,432 --> 04:58:21,316
而是指前几页提到的维护工作会自动按计划进行，无需任何人去编写或操作合并作业。
It is that the maintenance described on the previous slides happens automatically on a schedule without anyone writing or operating a compaction job at all.

3070
04:58:21,632 --> 04:58:23,588
这就是它的核心主张。
That is the entire proposition.

3071
04:58:24,366 --> 04:58:33,700
这让 S3 表成为一个“运维开销”答案，而不是“功能性”答案，而这正是考试会采用的表述方式。
It makes S3 tables an operational overhead answer rather than a capability answer, which is exactly how the exam will frame it.

3072
04:58:35,312 --> 04:58:40,723
权限点比看起来更重要，它能回答一类问题。
The permissions point is more significant than it looks and it answers a class of question.

3073
04:58:43,438 --> 04:58:53,348
在普通存储桶中，授予团队访问一个表的权限意味着针对 S3 前缀编写策略，并希望布局永远不改变。
In an ordinary bucket, granting a team access to one table means writing a policy against an S3 prefix and hoping the layout never changes.

3074
04:58:54,030 --> 04:59:01,316
表存储桶中的表是第一类资源，它们拥有自己的 ARN 和自己的资源策略。
A table bucket has tables as first class resources with their own ARNs and their own resource policies.

3075
04:59:01,934 --> 04:59:04,612
所以权限授予是真正针对表的。
So a grant is genuinely on the table.

3076
04:59:05,998 --> 04:59:07,844
集成点也很重要。
The integration bullet matters too.

3077
04:59:08,974 --> 04:59:12,900
表存储桶不会自动被 Athena 和 Redshift 识别。
Table buckets are not automatically visible to Athena and Redshift.

3078
04:59:13,838 --> 04:59:21,732
你需要将存储桶与 SageMaker Lakehouse 集成，这样这些表才能被分析服务发现。
You integrate the bucket with SageMaker Lakehouse, and that is what makes the tables discoverable to the analytics services.

3079
04:59:23,470 --> 04:59:27,872
客观的说法是，托管维护并不是免费的维护。
The honest framing is that managed maintenance is not free maintenance.

3080
04:59:28,112 --> 04:59:31,172
它是你购买的维护，而不是你自己构建的。
It is maintenance you buy rather than build.

3081
04:59:31,632 --> 04:59:35,972
合并是由对象数量和它处理的 GB 数量决定的。
Compaction is build by the objects and the gigabytes it processes.

3082
04:59:36,272 --> 04:59:43,204
因此，一个接收大量小写入的表会产生大量的合并操作并产生相应的费用。
So a table receiving constant small writes generates a great deal of compaction and a corresponding charge.

3083
04:59:44,142 --> 04:59:52,752
对于一个支持 15 条流水线的三人团队来说，这几乎肯定是正确的权衡，因为另一种选择会消耗他们并不具备的工程时间。
For a team of three supporting 15 pipelines, that is almost certainly the right trade because the alternative consumes engineering time

3084
04:59:52,912 --> 04:59:53,796
他们没有这些时间。
they do not have.

3085
04:59:54,542 --> 05:00:02,532
对于一个拥有现有 Spark 基础设施和可预测批处理权限的大型平台团队，自己运行合并可能更便宜。
For a large platform team with existing Spark infrastructure and predictable batch rights, running compaction themselves may well be cheaper.

3086
05:00:04,206 --> 05:00:08,068
考试会通过描述团队的情况来提示你处于哪种情形。
The exam signals which situation you are in by describing the team.

3087
05:00:09,710 --> 05:00:16,356
两者都存储 Iceberg 表，并且都与相同的查询引擎配合工作。所以问题永远不是关于功能。
Both store iceberg tables and both work with the same query engines. So the question is never about capability.

3088
05:00:17,312 --> 05:00:19,460
而是关于谁来执行维护。
It is about who runs the maintenance.

3089
05:00:20,430 --> 05:00:28,912
如果场景提到一个没有能力操作合并作业的团队，或者描述了因为没人维护而导致性能下降的表，
If the scenario mentions a team without capacity to operate compaction jobs or describes tables degrading because nobody maintains

3090
05:00:29,358 --> 05:00:31,588
那么，答案就是 S3 表。
them, that is, S3 tables.

3091
05:00:32,334 --> 05:00:35,204
通用型 bucket 保留了更多的灵活性。
A general purpose bucket keeps more flexibility.

3092
05:00:36,110 --> 05:00:44,260
当场景需要特定的生命周期规则、特定的存储类别，或者表数据与其他对象并存时，就使用它。
Use it when the scenario needs specific lifecycle rules, particular storage classes, or table data sitting beside other objects.

3093
05:00:45,454 --> 05:00:54,020
这些性能数据值得记住，因为 AWS 支持最高快 3 倍的查询速度和高出 10 倍的每秒事务数。
The performance figures are worth remembering because AWS codes up to 3 times faster queries and 10 times the transactions per second.

3094
05:00:55,214 --> 05:01:05,072
一家零售商使用 Amazon Data Firehose 将销售点交易流式传输到通用型 Amazon S3 bucket 中的 Apache ICB 表中。
A retailer streams point of sale transactions into Apache ICB tables in a general purpose, Amazon S3 bucket using Amazon Data Firehose.

3095
05:01:05,326 --> 05:01:10,272
数据持续到达，且表经常有频繁的小更新。
Lights arrive continuously and the tables receive frequent small updates.

3096
05:01:10,894 --> 05:01:17,220
在六个月内，查询时间大约增加到三倍，而存储成本的增长速度快于数据量的增长。
Over six months, query times have roughly tripled and storage costs have grown faster than the data volume.

3097
05:01:17,632 --> 05:01:25,732
数据平台团队只有三个人，负责支持 15 条其他流水线，没有能力去构建并运行表维护作业。
The data platform team is three people supporting 15 other pipelines and has no capacity to build and operate table maintenance jobs.

3098
05:01:26,638 --> 05:01:27,908
团队应该怎么做？
What should the team do?

3099
05:01:30,432 --> 05:01:38,180
A. 将这些表迁移到 Amazon S3 表，它可以自动执行合并和快照管理。
Migrate the tables to Amazon S3 tables which performs compaction and snapshot management automatically.

3100
05:01:39,246 --> 05:01:45,956
B. 编写一个计划的 AWS Glue作业，在每晚运行合并并过期快照。
b Write a scheduled AWS glue job to run compaction and expire snapshots nightly.

3101
05:01:46,318 --> 05:01:52,324
C. 增加 Firehose 的缓冲间隔，以便写入更少、体积更大的文件。
C. Increase the firehose buffer interval so fewer larger files are written.

3102
05:01:53,312 --> 05:01:53,632
D
D

3103
05:01:54,926 --> 05:02:00,516
D. 将这些表移动到 Amazon Redshift，这样存储就可以由数据仓库来管理。
Move the tables to Amazon Redshift so that storage is managed by the warehouse.

3104
05:02:01,134 --> 05:02:02,372
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

3105
05:02:09,072 --> 05:02:10,832
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3106
05:02:11,232 --> 05:02:13,924
这两个症状结合在一起就是诊断依据。
The two symptoms together are diagnostic.

3107
05:02:14,254 --> 05:02:22,980
查询变慢指向的是堆积的小文件，而存储增长快于数据量则指向了没有任何内容过期、且存在快照和孤立文件的现象。
Queries slowing points at accumulating small files and storage growing faster than the data points at snapshots and orphan files that nothing has expired.

3108
05:02:23,312 --> 05:02:25,860
这两者都是之前提到的维护债务。
Both are the maintenance debt described earlier.

3109
05:02:26,638 --> 05:02:30,432
选项 B 是干扰项，用来测试你是否读到了约束条件。
Option B is the distractor that tests whether you read the constraint.

3110
05:02:30,702 --> 05:02:37,792
这是因为从技术上讲它确实是正确的修复方法，但题目明确说明团队没有能力去操作它。
That is because it is genuinely the right technical fix, and the question explicitly says the team has no capacity to operate it.

3111
05:02:38,190 --> 05:02:41,636
这和模块 3 中的场景 2 情况一致。
That is the same shape as scenario 2 in module 3.

3112
05:02:42,478 --> 05:02:48,292
对于一个要求更少运行成本的团队，Glue作业是提供的正确优化方案。
A blue job was the correct optimization offered to a team that had asked for less to run.

3113
05:02:49,870 --> 05:02:56,228
模块 1 将湖仓理念描述为：一份数据只被描述一次，且能被每个引擎读取。
Module 1 described the lake house idea as one copy of the data described once, readable by every engine.

3114
05:02:56,846 --> 05:02:58,948
这张幻灯片就是对该主张的具体化。
This slide is that claim made specific.

3115
05:02:59,406 --> 05:03:02,752
Athena 这一行是改变了日常可能性的关键点。
The Athena row is the one that changes what is possible day to

3116
05:03:02,752 --> 05:03:09,764
这是因为在湖数据上进行合并、更新和删除是普通的 SQL 操作，而不是流水线操作。
day. That is because merge, update, and delete on lake data are ordinary SQL rather than a pipeline.

3117
05:03:10,510 --> 05:03:12,996
Firehose 这一行连接到模块 3。
The firehose row connects to module 3.

3118
05:03:13,838 --> 05:03:20,900
Iceberg 表被列在目标中，并被标记为支持更新和删除，而不仅仅是追加。
Iceberg tables were listed among the destinations there and flagged as expressing updates and deletes rather than only appends.

3119
05:03:21,742 --> 05:03:27,460
这对于流式传输服务来说并不寻常，而正是这种细节区分了两个选项。
That is unusual for a streaming delivery service, and it is the kind of detail that separates two options.

3120
05:03:29,072 --> 05:03:37,060
这种组合出现在题目中是因为它确实很有用，并且确实会产生本模块一直在描述的问题。
This combination appears in questions because it is genuinely useful and it genuinely creates the problem this module has been describing.

3121
05:03:37,472 --> 05:03:44,708
流式处理能在几秒内提供数据。Iceberg 让您能够在这些数据中更新和删除行。
Streaming gives you data within seconds. Iceberg gives you the ability to update and delete rows within that data.

3122
05:03:45,646 --> 05:03:51,940
两者结合可以让湖表与操作数据库保持同步，这是一个真实且常见的需求。
Together they let a lake table stay current with an operational database, which is a real and common requirement.

3123
05:03:52,432 --> 05:04:00,644
代价是每隔几秒写入一次的流会每天产生数千个小文件，如果涉及更新，还会产生删除文件。
The cost is that a stream writing every few seconds produces thousands of small files a day, plus delete files if updates are involved.

3124
05:04:01,294 --> 05:04:09,604
这正是未维护的表性能下降最快的工作负载，这也是本模块中的场景 2 是流式处理场景的原因。
That is precisely the workload where unmaintained tables degrade fastest, and it is why scenario 2 in this module is a streaming scenario.

3125
05:04:11,214 --> 05:04:19,012
SageMaker Lake House 是课程一直在构建的一个概念，而不是一个需要从头学习的新概念。
SageMaker Lake House is a name for something the course has been building towards rather than a new concept to learn from scratch.

3126
05:04:22,126 --> 05:04:25,668
数据存储在 S3 表和 Redshift 中。
Data sits in S3 tables and in Redshift.

3127
05:04:25,872 --> 05:04:32,932
它被定义一次，在 Lake Formation 中授权一次，并通过符合 Iceberg 标准的目录进行展示。
It is described once, permissioned once in lake formation, and exposed through a catalog that speaks the Iceberg standard.

3128
05:04:33,870 --> 05:04:38,212
因此任何理解 Iceberg 的引擎都可以查询它，而无需专门的连接器。
So any engine that understands Iceberg can query it without a bespoke connector.

3129
05:04:38,862 --> 05:04:44,512
考试指南在 2025 年 12 月的修订版中加入了它，所以旧教材里没有相关内容。
The exam guide added it in the December 2025 revision, so no older material covers it.

3130
05:04:45,102 --> 05:04:54,852
模块 12 详细讲解目录管理，模块 20 涵盖治理层。所以把这张幻灯片看作是一个框架，而不是全部内容。
Module 12 covers cataloging in detail and module 20 covers the governance layer. So treat this slide as the shape rather than the whole picture.

3131
05:04:56,494 --> 05:05:03,812
一名数据工程师运行一个每晚执行的 Glue 作业，用于重建由 200 名分析师使用的精选 Iceberg 表。
A data engineer runs a nightly blue job that rebuilds a curated iceberg table used by 200 analysts.

3132
05:05:04,526 --> 05:05:11,632
昨晚，该作业在错误的连接条件下运行，导致整个表写入了错误的值。
Last night, the job ran with a faulty join condition and wrote incorrect values across the entire table.

3133
05:05:11,872 --> 05:05:14,372
错误在今天上午 10 点被发现。
The error was discovered at 10 this morning.

3134
05:05:15,214 --> 05:05:19,108
原始源数据在 Amazon S3 中是完整的。
The raw source data is intact in Amazon S3.

3135
05:05:20,302 --> 05:05:23,460
从原始数据重新构建该表大约需要 4 小时。
Rebuilding the table from RAW takes about 4 hours.

3136
05:05:24,174 --> 05:05:27,844
自作业完成后，分析师一直在查询错误的数据。
Analysts have been querying the incorrect data since the job completed.

3137
05:05:28,686 --> 05:05:31,076
恢复正确数据的最快方法是什么？
What is the fastest way to restore correct data?

3138
05:05:32,112 --> 05:05:32,432
A
a

3139
05:05:33,646 --> 05:05:37,732
使用 S3 版本控制从之前的版本中恢复 S3 对象。
Restore the S3 objects from the previous versions using S3 versioning.

3140
05:05:38,192 --> 05:05:43,012
B 将 Iceberg 表回滚到故障作业运行前的快照。
b Roll the ICBug table back to the snapshot taken before the faulty job ran.

3141
05:05:43,552 --> 05:05:43,872
C
C.

3142
05:05:44,462 --> 05:05:48,260
D 修复连接条件并重新运行作业，从原始数据中重建。
Fix the join condition and rerun the job to rebuild from raw data.

3143
05:05:48,686 --> 05:05:48,992
D
D.

3144
05:05:49,358 --> 05:05:52,912
从最近的 AWS 备份恢复点还原表。
Restore the table from the most recent AWS backup recovery point.

3145
05:05:54,352 --> 05:05:55,172
然后做出选择。
And decide.

3146
05:06:01,550 --> 05:06:10,192
答案是 B，它优于其他选项的原因是没有任何数据移动。故障作业之前的数据文件仍然存在。
The answer is B, and the reason it beats every other option is that nothing moves. The data files from before the faulty job are still present.

3147
05:06:10,352 --> 05:06:16,356
这是因为 Iceberg 从未删除它们，且之前的快照仍指向完全正确的一组数据。
That is because iceberg never deleted them and the previous snapshot still points at exactly the right set.

3148
05:06:16,752 --> 05:06:19,460
回滚只是改变当前是哪个快照。
Rolling back changes which snapshot is current.

3149
05:06:20,174 --> 05:06:25,252
这是一个在几秒钟内即可完成的元数据操作，而重新处理则需要 4 小时。
That is a metadata operation measured in seconds against 4 hours of reprocessing.

3150
05:06:26,158 --> 05:06:29,220
选项 C 作为最终步骤并不是错误的。
Option C is not wrong as an eventual step.

3151
05:06:30,512 --> 05:06:33,156
你今晚去修复连接并重新运行。
You will fix the join and rerun tonight.

3152
05:06:34,030 --> 05:06:41,508
题目要求的是现在恢复正确数据的最快方法，而此时有 200 名分析师正在查询错误的数据，你却在犹豫不决。
The question asked for the fastest way to restore correct data now, and 200 analysts are querying wrong numbers while you decide.

3153
05:06:43,232 --> 05:06:49,316
第四个要点是实际迁移中容易出错的地方，所以它是一个合理的考题。
The fourth bullet is where migrations go wrong in practice and it makes a fair exam question.

3154
05:06:49,902 --> 05:06:56,260
一旦表变成了 Iceberg，元数据就是判定哪些文件属于该表的最终依据。
Once a table is iceberg, the metadata is the definitive statement of which files belong to it.

3155
05:06:57,166 --> 05:07:06,276
一个被忽略的任务仍在将 Parquet 文件写入前缀，产生的这些文件在物理上是存在的，但任何查询都查不到它们。
A job that was overlooked, still writing parquet files into the prefix produces files that physically exist and are invisible to every query.

3156
05:07:06,990 --> 05:07:08,832
没有任何元数据引用它们。
No metadata references them.

3157
05:07:08,912 --> 05:07:10,308
任何地方都不会报错。
Nothing errors anywhere.

3158
05:07:10,766 --> 05:07:15,792
数据就这么丢了，可能要过几周甚至几周时间，才有人发现总数变低了。
Data simply goes missing and it can be weeks before anyone notices a total is low.

3159
05:07:16,272 --> 05:07:21,312
所以迁移清单的第一步是找出每一个写入者，而不是从转换开始。
So the migration checklist starts with finding every writer, not with converting the

3160
05:07:21,312 --> 05:07:31,204
原地转换选项之所以吸引人，正是因为它不需要移动 PB级数据就能开始，这让转换本身变成了简单的一环。
data. The in place option is attractive precisely because it does not require moving petabytes to get started, which makes the conversion itself the easy part.

3161
05:07:32,846 --> 05:07:35,620
Iceberg 模糊了一道曾经清晰的界限，
Iceberg blurs a line that used to be clear,

3162
05:07:36,366 --> 05:07:39,716
所以有必要重申这条界限现在在哪里。
so it is worth restating where that line now sits.

3163
05:07:41,678 --> 05:07:49,536
在开放表格式出现之前，任何需要更新的内容都必须存放在数据仓库中，因为数据湖根本无法表达这些内容。
Before open table formats, anything needing updates had to live in a warehouse because a lake simply could not express them.

3164
05:07:50,254 --> 05:07:55,140
现在情况变了，决定因素回到了我们提到的那个维度。
That is no longer true, and the deciding factor has moved back to the one module one gave you.

3165
05:07:55,534 --> 05:07:59,108
查询频率是多少？有多少人同时在查询？
How often is it queried and by how many people at once?

3166
05:07:59,662 --> 05:08:06,180
Redshift 将数据保存在其控制的格式中，并针对预期的查询对排序键和分布键进行了优化。
Redshift keeps data in a format it controls with sort keys and distribution keys tuned for the queries it expects.

3167
05:08:06,816 --> 05:08:10,788
它能以低延迟支持数百个并发用户。
It serves hundreds of concurrent users at low latency.

3168
05:08:11,296 --> 05:08:18,180
S3 中的 Iceberg 表是开放的、成本低廉的，任何引擎都能在秒级而非毫秒级读取。
An iceberg table in S3 is open, cheap, and readable by any engine at seconds rather than milliseconds.

3169
05:08:19,886 --> 05:08:24,676
知道什么时候不需要某种技术，和知道它何时有帮助一样重要。
Knowing when a technology is unnecessary is worth as much as knowing when it helps.

3170
05:08:25,294 --> 05:08:28,740
考试中确实会出现 Iceberg，但在某些情况下它根本不起任何作用。
The exam does offer iceberg where it adds nothing at all.

3171
05:08:29,358 --> 05:08:37,188
到达的日志数据是可查询且从不修改的，没有更新问题、删除问题，也没有并发写入问题。
Log data that arrives is queried and is never modified, has no update problem, no delete problem, and no concurrent write problem.

3172
05:08:38,030 --> 05:08:45,924
在这种情况下加入 Iceberg，只是为了换取一些没人会去用的功能，而引入了一个元数据层和永久的维护负担。
Adding iceberg to it buys a metadata layer and a permanent maintenance obligation in exchange for capabilities nobody will ever use.

3173
05:08:46,542 --> 05:08:53,696
第四点是个值得明确说明的界限，因为 Iceberg 虽然提供事务，但人们往往会过度解读这个词。
The fourth point is a boundary worth stating plainly because iceberg does provide transactions and people overread that word.

3174
05:08:54,350 --> 05:09:01,296
它是为定期写入的分析型表设计的，而不是为了每秒成千上万个并发的小事务。
It is designed for analytical tables taking periodic writes, not for thousands of concurrent small transactions per second.

3175
05:09:01,536 --> 05:09:06,116
正如模块 1 所述，那仍然是运营数据库的工作。
That remains a job for an operational database as module 1 set out.

3176
05:09:07,470 --> 05:09:14,276
一家物流公司将 GPS 定位记录作为 Parquet 格式追加到 Amazon S3 中，并按日期进行分区。
A logistics company appends GPS ping records to Amazon S3 as parquet, partitioned by date.

3177
05:09:15,246 --> 05:09:21,540
这些记录从不更新或删除，而且保留策略会在两年后让整个分区过期。
Records are never updated or deleted, and the retention policy expires whole partitions after two years.

3178
05:09:22,190 --> 05:09:25,856
查询总是基于日期范围过滤，并读取四个列。
Queries always filter on a date range and read four columns.

3179
05:09:26,414 --> 05:09:35,556
一位新架构师提议将数据集转换为 Amazon S3 表中的 Apache Iceberg 表，理由是 ACID 事务和时间旅行。
A new architect has proposed converting the dataset to Apache ICBerg tables in Amazon S3 tables citing ACID transactions and time travel.

3180
05:09:36,110 --> 05:09:37,956
数据工程师该如何回应？
How should the data engineer respond?

3181
05:09:39,982 --> 05:09:44,196
同意。Iceberg 是目前 AWS 数据湖的最佳实践。
Agree. ICBerg is the current best practice for data lakes on AWS.

3182
05:09:44,816 --> 05:09:46,244
b 选项，予以拒绝。
b pushback.

3183
05:09:47,086 --> 05:09:54,020
工作负载是仅追加且具有完整分区过期，因此 Iceberg 会增加维护成本，却没能解决公司现有的问题。
The workload is append only with whole partition expiry, so iceberg adds maintenance without solving a problem the company has.

3184
05:09:54,416 --> 05:09:54,656
C。
C.

3185
05:09:55,086 --> 05:10:00,256
同意，但改用 Apache Hudi，因为它更适合仅追加的数据。
Agree, but use Apache Hoodie instead, as it is better suited to append only data.

3186
05:10:00,576 --> 05:10:00,816
D。
D.

3187
05:10:01,536 --> 05:10:06,788
同意，并额外按车辆标识进行分区以提高查询性能。
Agree and additionally partition by vehicle identifier to improve query performance.

3188
05:10:08,096 --> 05:10:09,188
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3189
05:10:15,598 --> 05:10:19,940
答案是 B，这个场景特意与第一个场景成对出现。
The answer is B, and this scenario pairs with the first one deliberately.

3190
05:10:20,686 --> 05:10:26,660
在这里，Iceberg 是正确的选择，因为必须从共享文件内部删除行。
There, ICBerg was clearly right because rows had to be deleted from inside shared files.

3191
05:10:27,534 --> 05:10:30,692
而在当前情况下，它提供的每一项功能都没用到。
Here, every capability it offers goes unused.

3192
05:10:31,630 --> 05:10:39,940
没有更新，没有删除，单行操作，保留策略在分区粒度上生效，且查询已经能高效执行裁剪。
Nothing updates, nothing deletes, individual rows, retention works at partition granularity, and queries already prune efficiently.

3193
05:10:40,654 --> 05:10:43,684
Iceberg 带来的只会是维护负担。
What iceberg would add is a maintenance obligation.

3194
05:10:44,334 --> 05:10:50,948
识别出某种好的技术并不适用于特定情况，这是考试刻意考查的判断力。
Recognizing that a good technology is wrong for a specific situation is a judgment the exam test deliberately.

3195
05:10:51,376 --> 05:10:55,620
这和模块 1 中的流式处理场景逻辑一致。
It is the same reasoning as the streaming scenario in module 1.

3196
05:10:57,198 --> 05:11:01,060
第三行是值得记住的，因为它的症状描述非常模糊。
The third row is the one worth carrying because the symptom is so unhelpful.

3197
05:11:01,486 --> 05:11:07,620
文件存在于存储桶中，摄取任务报告成功，但查询却查不到这些数据。
Files exist in the bucket, the ingestion job reports success, and queries return nothing for that data.

3198
05:11:07,856 --> 05:11:11,108
直觉会让你去检查查询语句或权限。
Every instinct says to look at the query or the permissions.

3199
05:11:11,950 --> 05:11:17,412
实际原因是 Iceberg 读取的是元数据，而不是列出目录。
The actual cause is that iceberg reads its metadata rather than listing the directory.

3200
05:11:17,678 --> 05:11:21,028
所以一个没有任何指向的、或者在五月之前就不存在的文件的引用也会导致问题。
So a file nothing points at May as well not exist.

3201
05:11:22,670 --> 05:11:30,276
这种情况通常发生在部分迁移后，或者有人添加新任务时复制了旧脚本，而那个旧脚本只读纯 Parquet 文件。
That happens after a partial migration or when someone adds a new job and copies an old script that lights plain parquet.

3202
05:11:31,184 --> 05:11:36,132
这值得记住，因为系统中没有任何地方报错。
It is worth recognizing because nothing in the system reports an error.

3203
05:11:37,710 --> 05:11:43,716
共 5 道题。第一题就是为了防止你过度套用本模块学到的所有内容。
5 questions. And the first is the one that stops you over applying everything this module taught.

3204
05:11:44,304 --> 05:11:48,932
考试会给出不需要 Iceberg 的情况，就像场景 4 一样。
The exam offers iceberg where it is unnecessary, exactly as scenario 4 did.

3205
05:11:49,904 --> 05:11:54,372
同意一个并不能解决已知问题的最佳实践，是错误的答案。
Agreeing with a best practice that solves no stated problem is a wrong answer.

3206
05:11:55,264 --> 05:11:58,304
第三题是本模块中最清晰的区分点。
The third is the cleanest split in the module.

3207
05:11:58,670 --> 05:12:07,524
这是因为 S3 表和自管理的 Iceberg 功能相同，仅在谁来执行工作上有所不同。
That is because S3 tables and self-managed Iceberg have identical capabilities and differ only in who does the work.

3208
05:12:08,304 --> 05:12:13,860
下一个模块是 Amazon Redshift，是本课程中最大的单项模块。
Next module is Amazon Redshift, the largest single module in this course.

3209
05:12:14,784 --> 05:12:19,076
它涵盖了题库中的 325 个考点。
It covers 325 appearances in the question bank.

3210
05:12:20,464 --> 05:12:23,044
这是课程中规模最大的模块。
This is the largest module in the course.

3211
05:12:23,344 --> 05:12:32,836
Amazon Redshift 在题库中出现了 325 次，在本次课程分析中仅次于 AWS Glue 和 Amazon S3。
Amazon Redshift appeared 325 times in the bank, analyzed for this course behind only AWS Glue and Amazon S3.

3212
05:12:33,504 --> 05:12:37,984
它比考试中的任何其他服务都有更多的内部细节。
It also has more internal detail than any other service on the exam.

3213
05:12:38,574 --> 05:12:45,828
这是因为 Redshift 的性能取决于你在设计表时的选择，而不是后期增加的容量。
That is because performance in Redshift depends on choices you make when you design a table rather than on capacity you add afterwards.

3214
05:12:46,144 --> 05:12:53,636
我们将涵盖架构、决定一切的两个关键选择：加载与卸载，以及保持数据仓库的高速运行。
We cover the architecture, the two key choices that decide everything loading and unloading, keeping a warehouse fast.

3215
05:12:54,446 --> 05:12:57,892
Redshift 读取数据的四种不同方式。
The four different ways Redshift reads data.

3216
05:12:59,150 --> 05:13:06,564
它包含四个工作场景，以及一个近期改变标准考试答案的重大变化。
It does not store four worked scenarios and one very recent change that alters a standard exam answer.

3217
05:13:08,238 --> 05:13:11,172
两个属性解释了后续的大部分内容。
Two properties explain most of what follows.

3218
05:13:11,694 --> 05:13:14,500
列式存储意味着每个列都是单独存储的。
Columnar means each column is stored separately.

3219
05:13:15,184 --> 05:13:23,184
因此，一个读取 90 列中 3 列的查询只触及一小部分数据，正如第 8 模块中描述的
So a query reading 3 columns of 90 touches a fraction of the data, exactly as module 8 described for

3220
05:13:23,313 --> 05:13:23,733
Parquet。
Parquet.

3221
05:13:24,846 --> 05:13:33,316
大规模并行意味着工作被分配到各个节点以及每个节点内的切片上。因此，查询的速度取决于最慢的那个切片。
Massively parallel means the work is divided across nodes and across slices within each node. So a query is only as fast as its slowest slice.

3222
05:13:34,158 --> 05:13:37,060
将这两者结合起来，你就得到了 Redshift 的核心原则。
Put those together and you get the central redshift principle.

3223
05:13:37,584 --> 05:13:41,284
性能源于减少读取量和均匀分配工作。
Performance comes from reading less and from dividing work evenly.

3224
05:13:42,094 --> 05:13:47,460
每一个分布键、排序键和压缩决策都是为了实现这两个目标之一。
Every distribution key, sort key, and compression decision serves one of those two goals.

3225
05:13:47,918 --> 05:13:52,100
那些看起来像调优琐事的题目，实际上是在问哪一个环节出了问题。
Questions that look like tuning trivia are really asking which of the two is broken.

3226
05:13:53,614 --> 05:13:58,468
「切片」是需要记住的核心概念，因为它是后续所有环节中最重要的单位。
The slice is the concept to hold on to because it is the unit that matters for everything later.

3227
05:13:59,182 --> 05:14:07,140
集群的总并行度是节点数量乘以每个节点的切片数，且每张表的数据都分布在这些切片上。
A cluster's total parallelism is the number of nodes multiplied by the slices per node, and every table's data is spread across those slices.

3228
05:14:08,078 --> 05:14:13,796
当一个切片包含的行数远多于其他切片时，该切片处理时间就会变长，整个查询都会等待。
When one slice holds far more rows than the others, that slice takes longer and the whole query waits.

3229
05:14:14,382 --> 05:14:17,540
这就是在数据仓库中出现的、第 5 模块提到的倾斜问题。
That is the skew problem from module 5 appearing in a warehouse.

3230
05:14:19,214 --> 05:14:21,380
「交换步骤」是另一个需要记住的要点。
The exchange step is the other one to remember.

3231
05:14:22,286 --> 05:14:28,772
为了满足连接操作而在节点之间移动数据，是 Redshift 查询中成本最高的操作。
Moving data between nodes to satisfy a join is the single most expensive thing a redshift query does.

3232
05:14:29,230 --> 05:14:32,260
分布键存在的全部意义就是为了避免这种情况。
The entire point of distribution keys is to avoid it.

3233
05:14:33,838 --> 05:14:36,292
这个表格的两端都有警告提示。
Both ends of this table carry warnings.

3234
05:14:36,864 --> 05:14:44,452
DC2 已于 2025 年 4 月弃用，AWS 指导客户转向 RA3 或无服务器架构。
DC2 was deprecated in April 2025 with AWS directing customers to RA3 or serverless.

3235
05:14:46,062 --> 05:14:50,244
它仍出现在旧材料中，作为小型集群的一个合理选择。
It still appears in older material as a reasonable choice for small clusters.

3236
05:14:50,894 --> 05:14:58,916
在另一端，RG 实例于 2026 年 5 月发布，这比当前的考试指南发布晚了 5 个月。
At the other end, RG instances launched in May 2026, which is 5 months after the current exam guide was published.

3237
05:14:59,470 --> 05:15:03,876
因此，考试几乎肯定会将 RA3 描述为当前一代。
So the exam will almost certainly describe RA3 as the current generation.

3238
05:15:04,784 --> 05:15:12,036
下一张幻灯片涵盖 RG 的变化，因为其中一项变化会影响关于 Spectrum 的标准考试答案。
The next slide covers what RG changes because one of those changes affects a standard exam answer about spectrum.

3239
05:15:13,998 --> 05:15:15,748
你应该了解这两个版本。
And you should know both versions.

3240
05:15:17,390 --> 05:15:22,244
第四个要点是对于考试题目有意义的，而不仅仅是架构上的考量。
The fourth bullet is the one that matters for exam answers rather than for architecture.

3241
05:15:23,086 --> 05:15:33,124
Redshift Spectrum 一直都是通过将查询发送到一组独立的 AWS 管理节点来运行，这些节点负责扫描 S3 并按扫描的每 TB 字节计费，这部分费用是在集群成本之外额外计算的。
Redshift Spectrum has always worked by sending queries to a separate fleet of AWS managed nodes that scan S3, charging you per terabyte scanned on top of your cluster cost.

3242
05:15:34,030 --> 05:15:42,948
有几个标准考试答案取决于这项计费的存在，因为它决定了分区和列式存储格式对 Spectrum 查询的重要性。
Several standard exam answers depend on that charge existing because it is what makes partitioning and columnar formats matter for spectrum queries.

3243
05:15:43,184 --> 05:15:49,344
在 RG 上，那组节点已经不存在了，扫描是在你自己的集群节点上进行的，且没有额外的费用。
On RGE, that fleet is gone and the scanning happens on your own cluster nodes with no separate charge.

3244
05:15:49,584 --> 05:15:51,268
考试内容是在此变化之前制定的。
The exam predates this.

3245
05:15:51,790 --> 05:15:57,508
请按 Spectrum 按每 TB 计费来回答，并知晓在当前的硬件上它并不这样计费。
Answer as though spectrum bins per terabyte and know that on current hardware it does not.

3246
05:15:59,024 --> 05:16:05,860
共享目录是值得记住的重点，因为它将本模块与第 8 和第 12 模块联系起来。
The shared catalog is the point worth carrying because it connects this module to modules 8 and 12.

3247
05:16:06,510 --> 05:16:10,916
外部表并不是包含元数据副本的 Redshift 对象。
An external table is not a redshift object with a copy of the metadata.

3248
05:16:11,662 --> 05:16:14,052
它就是同一个 Glue 数据目录表。
It is the same Glue Data Catalog table.

3249
05:16:14,446 --> 05:16:23,524
Athena 也会读取它，因此只需定义一次，就可以让两个引擎都使用同一个架构和一套 Lake Formation 权限。
Athena reads So defining it once makes it available to both engines with one schema and one set of lake formation permissions.

3250
05:16:24,462 --> 05:16:26,500
第四个要点是故障模式。
The fourth bullet is the failure mode.

3251
05:16:27,086 --> 05:16:33,984
写入到新分区前缀的文件在这些分区被注册到目录之前，对查询是不可见的。
Files written into a new partition prefix are invisible to queries until that partition is registered in the catalog.

3252
05:16:34,766 --> 05:16:42,084
这就是为什么第 2 模块花时间讲解启用更新目录和爬虫的原因。
That is why module 2 spent time on enable update catalog and on crawlers.

3253
05:16:43,822 --> 05:16:50,564
这与课程中其他地方的论点一致，但 Redshift 有一个值得了解的特殊情况。
This is the same argument as everywhere else in the course, and Redshift has one wrinkle worth knowing about.

3254
05:16:50,864 --> 05:16:58,500
按小时计费的预置集群可以暂停，这会完全停止计算费用，同时保留所有数据。
A provision cluster built by the hour can be paused, which stops compute charges entirely while retaining all the data.

3255
05:16:59,406 --> 05:17:05,412
这使得它成为每周仅使用几个小时的开发数据仓库的一个非常好的选择。
That makes it a genuinely good answer for a development warehouse used a few hours a week.

3256
05:17:06,944 --> 05:17:11,108
Serverless 则会自动执行同样的操作，无需任何人记得去暂停。
Serverless does the same thing automatically without anyone remembering to pause it.

3257
05:17:12,046 --> 05:17:14,692
决定性因素通常是可预测性。
The deciding factor is usually predictability.

3258
05:17:15,694 --> 05:17:22,724
对于一个在每个工作日的整天里都有稳定查询需求的业务，使用预置节点会更便宜。
A warehouse serving a business that queries it steadily all day, every working day, is cheaper on reserved provision nodes.

3259
05:17:23,278 --> 05:17:29,540
而对于在不可预测的爆发式需求中使用，或者还没有人测量过使用情况的数据仓库，Serverless 则更便宜。
A warehouse used in unpredictable bursts or one nobody has measured yet is cheaper on serverless.

3260
05:17:31,214 --> 05:17:34,532
基础容量底线发生了变化，这改变了答案。
The base capacity floor moved and it changes an answer.

3261
05:17:35,086 --> 05:17:48,388
到 2025 年 6 月之前，最低限额是 8 RPS，这使得 Serverless 对于小型或间歇性的工作负载来说相对昂贵。旧的指导建议使用较小的 DC2 集群进行开发。
Until June 2025, the minimum was 8 RPS, which made serverless comparatively expensive for a small or intermittent workload. Older guidance says to use a small DC2 cluster for development instead.

3262
05:17:49,134 --> 05:17:54,852
随着 4 RPU 底线和现在已弃用的 DC2 的变化，这一指导意见已经反转了。
With a 4 RPU floor and DC2 now deprecated, that guidance is inverted.

3263
05:17:55,854 --> 05:18:00,324
最后一个要点中的价格性能目标值得记住其名称。
The price performance target on the last bullet is worth recognizing by name.

3264
05:18:01,614 --> 05:18:10,052
这是因为这是一个单一设置，它告诉 Redshift 是要消耗更多容量以获得更快的结果，还是为了节省成本而保留资源。
That is because it is a single setting that tells Redshift whether to spend more capacity for faster results or hold back to save money.

3265
05:18:11,790 --> 05:18:16,420
托管存储是使得后续所有内容成为可能的架构变革。
Managed storage is the architectural change that made everything after it possible.

3266
05:18:16,624 --> 05:18:19,460
而第四个要点解释了它为什么重要。
And the fourth bullet explains why it mattered.

3267
05:18:22,414 --> 05:18:31,108
在旧的密集计算节点上，存储位于节点本身。因此，不断增长的数据集会迫使你仅仅为了容纳数据而增加节点。
On the older dense compute nodes, storage lies on the node itself. So a growing dataset forces you to add nodes purely to hold it.

3268
05:18:31,854 --> 05:18:38,820
你最终会为不需要且无法使用的计算资源付费，这正是成本类问题的典型特征。
You end up paying for compute you do not need and cannot use, which is exactly the shape of a cost question.

3269
05:18:39,438 --> 05:18:47,584
有了托管存储，两者可以独立扩展，热数据留在本地 SSD 上，而冷数据会自动移动到 S3。
With managed storage, the two scale independently and hot data sits on local SSD while colder data moves to S3

3270
05:18:47,744 --> 05:18:48,516
自动地。
automatically.

3271
05:18:49,264 --> 05:18:55,300
这种分离也是支持本模块后续提到的数据共享和零EDL的原因。
That separation is also what enables data sharing and 0EDL later in this module.

3272
05:18:55,664 --> 05:19:00,580
这是因为存储层不再被限制在单个集群的本地磁盘中。
That is because the storage layer is no longer trapped inside one cluster's local disks.

3273
05:19:02,062 --> 05:19:05,892
这是将 Redshift 与课程中其他所有服务区分开来的部分。
This is the section that separates Redshift from every other service in the course.

3274
05:19:06,384 --> 05:19:09,892
在其他地方，性能问题通常可以通过配置来解决。
Elsewhere, performance problems are usually solved by configuration.

3275
05:19:10,064 --> 05:19:11,492
你可以在之后再更改。
You can change afterwards.

3276
05:19:12,398 --> 05:19:20,784
在 Redshift 中，最重要的两个决策是表的属性，在创建时选择，更改它们意味着要重建表。
In Redshift, the two decisions that matter most are properties of the table, chosen at creation, and changing them means rebuilding the table.

3277
05:19:21,024 --> 05:19:28,356
分布决定了每一行所在的切片，从而决定连接时是否需要在节点间移动数据。
Distribution decides which slice each row lives on, which decides whether a join needs to move data between nodes.

3278
05:19:29,134 --> 05:19:35,844
排序决定了每个切片内行的物理顺序，从而决定过滤查询需要读取多少表内容。
Sort decides the physical order of rows within each slice, which decides how much of the table a filtered query has to read.

3279
05:19:36,270 --> 05:19:38,276
两个都选对，就能拥有一个集群。
Get both right and a cluster.

3280
05:19:38,606 --> 05:19:40,324
一半的大小就足够快了。
Half the size is fast enough.

3281
05:19:41,870 --> 05:19:45,348
AUTO 是默认选项，而且确实很合理。
AUTO is the default and it is genuinely sensible.

3282
05:19:45,632 --> 05:19:56,164
它将小表初始设为 ALL，随着增长将其移至 EVEN 或 KEY。因此当题目要求你明确选择时，要寻找它给出的原因。
It starts small tables as ALL, then moves them to EVEN or KEY as they grow. So when a question has you choose explicitly, look for the reason it gives.

3283
05:19:57,038 --> 05:20:02,752
一个大型事实表与另一个基于相同列的大型表重复连接的情况是 KEY 情况。
A large fact table repeatedly joined to another large table on the same column is the KEY case.

3284
05:20:02,912 --> 05:20:07,172
这是因为将这些行协同存放可以完全消除网络交换。
That is because co-locating those rows removes the network exchange entirely.

3285
05:20:07,472 --> 05:20:11,460
一个与所有内容连接的小维度表是 ALL 情况。
A small dimension table joined to everything is the ALL case.

3286
05:20:11,982 --> 05:20:19,076
这是因为在每个节点上都保留完整副本意味着完全不需要移动，且足够小使得复制成本很低。
That is because a full copy on every node means no movement at all and small enough makes the duplication cheap.

3287
05:20:19,598 --> 05:20:25,092
EVEN 是用于不参与连接或没有列能良好分布的表的。
Ev E N is for tables that are not joined or where no column distributes well.

3288
05:20:26,670 --> 05:20:28,996
模块 5 描述了 Spark 中的数据倾斜。
Modin 5 described data skew in Spark.

3289
05:20:29,552 --> 05:20:34,436
一个包含大部分行的主键会导致单个任务承担大部分工作
One key holding most of the rows leaves a single task doing most of the work

3290
05:20:35,472 --> 05:20:37,252
而其他任务则处于闲置状态。
while the others sit idle.

3291
05:20:37,966 --> 05:20:42,148
Redshift 中的数据分布倾斜是不同服务中的同一种现象。
Distribution skew in Redshift is the same phenomenon in a different service.

3292
05:20:43,086 --> 05:20:50,532
将一个包含 1 亿行、在具有四个值的状态列上进行分布的表，会将四分之一的表内容发送到四个切片中的每一个。
Distributing a 100 million row table on a status column with four values sends a quarter of the table to each of four slices.

3293
05:20:51,086 --> 05:20:53,732
集群中其他的切片都处于空置状态。
Every other slice in the cluster sits empty.

3294
05:20:54,318 --> 05:20:59,012
增加节点不会改变任何情况，因为键仍然哈希到四个位置。
Adding nodes changes nothing because the key still hashes to four places.

3295
05:21:00,032 --> 05:21:08,512
考试将此作为一种症状来考查，描述一个增加容量却无济于事的集群，这始终是
The exam tests this as a symptom, describing a cluster where adding capacity did not help, which is always the signature of

3296
05:21:08,672 --> 05:21:10,992
倾斜而非短缺的特征。
skew rather than shortage.

3297
05:21:12,398 --> 05:21:20,548
复合和交错的区别是一个合理的考试题目，而实际答案几乎总是复合。
The compound and interleaved distinction is a fair exam question, and the practical answer is nearly always compound.

3298
05:21:21,230 --> 05:21:30,020
复合排序键按第一个列排序，然后在该范围内按第二个列排序，就像按多个列对电子表格进行排序一样。
A compound sort key sorts by the first column, then within that by the second, exactly like sorting a spreadsheet by several columns.

3299
05:21:30,832 --> 05:21:37,220
这意味着对首选列的过滤可以大幅裁剪，而仅对第三列的过滤几乎不能裁剪。
That means a filter on the leading column prunes enormously and a filter on only the third column prunes very little.

3300
05:21:37,472 --> 05:21:45,444
交错让每个列具有同等权重，因此任何一个都能较好地进行裁剪，但代价是添加数据时维护成本更高。
Interleaved gives every column equal weight, so any of them prunes reasonably well at the cost of much heavier maintenance when data is added.

3301
05:21:46,254 --> 05:21:52,036
如果题目描述的查询每次都在不同的列上进行过滤，那么考点就在“交错”上。
If a question describes queries that filter on different columns each time, interleaved is being pointed at.

3302
05:21:54,862 --> 05:22:04,003
区域映射是排序键起作用的原因，它们的工作原理与 Parquet 的最小值和最大值统计模块完全相同，正如它
Zone maps are the reason a sort key matters and they work identically to the parquet minimum and maximum statistics module it

3303
05:22:04,272 --> 05:22:04,932
所描述的那样。
described.

3304
05:22:05,742 --> 05:22:11,844
每个列的每 1 MB 数据块都包含其包含的最小值和最大值。
Every 1 MB block of every column carries the smallest and largest value it contains.

3305
05:22:12,750 --> 05:22:20,932
过滤上周日期的查询可以丢弃所有范围在上周之前结束的块，而无需读取其中的任何字节。
A query filtering on last week's dates can discard every block whose range ends before last week without reading a single byte of it.

3306
05:22:21,152 --> 05:22:25,668
对于按日期排序的表，这意味着从数千个块中只需读取一小部分。
On a table sorted by date, that means reading a handful of blocks out of thousands.

3307
05:22:25,872 --> 05:22:29,092
在未排序的表中，日期是均匀分布的。
On an unsorted table, dates are scattered evenly.

3308
05:22:30,030 --> 05:22:37,472
因此每个块都包含一些近期的值。没有任何块可以被跳过，查询必须读取整个列。
So every block contains some recent values. No block can be skipped and the query reads the entire column.

3309
05:22:37,934 --> 05:22:41,572
数据相同，查询相同，但工作量却相差百倍。
Same data, same query, a hundredfold difference in work.

3310
05:22:43,182 --> 05:22:48,580
一个零售商有一个包含 20 亿行销售记录的事实表，以及一个包含 800 家商店的维度表。
A retailer has a fact table of 2 billion sales rows and a dimension table of 800 stores.

3311
05:22:49,326 --> 05:22:55,972
几乎每个查询都通过商店 ID 将这两个表连接起来，然后过滤出过去 30 天内的交易日期范围。
Almost every query joins the two on store ID, then filters on a transaction date range covering the last 30 days.

3312
05:22:56,432 --> 05:23:01,188
事实表目前使用“均匀”分布，且没有排序键。
The fact table currently uses EVEN distribution with no sort key.

3313
05:23:02,094 --> 05:23:04,752
维度表也使用“均匀”分布。
The dimension table also uses EVEN.

3314
05:23:05,966 --> 05:23:12,068
查询需要几分钟时间，监控显示在连接过程中节点之间存在大量的数据重分布。
Queries take several minutes and monitoring shows heavy data redistribution between nodes during the join.

3315
05:23:12,814 --> 05:23:15,716
哪种组合最能提高查询性能？
Which combination will most improve query performance?

3316
05:23:16,750 --> 05:23:20,868
A. 向集群添加节点，让更多分片共享工作。
a Add nodes to the cluster so more slices share the work.

3317
05:23:22,992 --> 05:23:31,392
B. 按商店 ID 分布事实表，将商店表设为“全部”，并对交易日期添加复合排序键。
Distribute the fact table on store ID, set the store table to ALL and add a compound sort key on transaction date.

3318
05:23:32,334 --> 05:23:40,036
C. 将两个表都设置为按商店 ID 的“键”分布，并对每个过滤列添加交错排序键。
C. Set both tables to KEY distribution on store ID and add an interleaved sort key on every filtered column.

3319
05:23:40,942 --> 05:23:45,316
D. 启用并发扩展，让额外的集群吸收负载。
d Enable concurrency scaling so additional clusters absorb the load.

3320
05:23:46,192 --> 05:23:48,388
思考一下，然后做决定。
Query Pause and decide.

3321
05:23:54,830 --> 05:23:56,592
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3322
05:23:57,312 --> 05:24:00,996
情况中有两个细节，每个细节对应其中的一个问题。
Two details in the situation, each point at one half of it.

3323
05:24:02,958 --> 05:24:06,468
连接期间的大量重分布是一个分布问题。
Heavy redistribution during the join is a distribution problem.

3324
05:24:07,118 --> 05:24:15,716
只有 800 行的维度表足够小，在每个节点上复制一份几乎不耗费成本，这可以完全消除数据移动。
A dimension table of 800 rows is small enough that a full copy on every node costs almost nothing, which removes the movement completely.

3325
05:24:16,622 --> 05:24:20,772
对包含 20 亿行数据的表过滤过去 30 天的数据是一个排序键问题。
Filtering on the last 30 days of a 2 billion row table is a sort key problem.

3326
05:24:20,992 --> 05:24:24,868
对交易日期进行复合排序可以让区域映射发挥作用。
A compound sort on transaction date makes zone maps do the work.

3327
05:24:25,152 --> 05:24:31,940
选项 A 和 D 都属于容量问题，只是两种不同的形式，它们都没能解决为什么单个查询变慢的问题。
Options A and D are both capacity, offered in two different forms, and neither addresses why an individual query is slow.

3328
05:24:33,552 --> 05:24:40,836
在 Redshift 中，压缩现在是按列进行的且基本是自动的，这使得它比以前是一个较小的考试考点。
Completion in Redshift is per column and mostly automatic now, which makes it a smaller exam topic than it once was.

3329
05:24:41,312 --> 05:24:44,292
重点强调的部分正是仍值得深入了解的内容。
The callout is the part still worth knowing well.

3330
05:24:44,752 --> 05:24:51,472
当你将数据复制到空表中时，Redshift 会对数据进行采样，并为每个列选择合适的编码。
When you copy data into an empty table, Redshift samples it and picks an appropriate encoding for each column.

3331
05:24:52,014 --> 05:24:57,252
这就是为什么构建表时的推荐做法是先创建空表，然后再进行数据导入。
That is why the recommended way to build a table is to create it empty and copy into it.

3332
05:24:58,510 --> 05:25:04,228
使用 insert 语句逐行加载相同的数据会完全跳过采样过程。
Loading the same data row by row with insert statements bypasses that sampling entirely.

3333
05:25:05,038 --> 05:25:12,484
这些列将保持不压缩状态，导致生成的表在后续使用中体积更大、扫描速度更慢。
The columns stay uncompressed and you end up with a table that is permanently larger and slower to scan for the rest of its life.

3334
05:25:13,038 --> 05:25:14,852
而系统永远不会提醒你这一点。
That nothing will ever tell you about.

3335
05:25:16,430 --> 05:25:22,724
考试指南将 Amazon S3 和 Redshift 之间的加载与卸载列为一项独立技能。
The exam guide names loading and unloading between Amazon S3 and Redshift as a skill in its own right.

3336
05:25:23,342 --> 05:25:25,060
这一部分非常重要。
This section carries real weight.

3337
05:25:26,192 --> 05:25:30,052
核心要点是理解 copy 命令是并行执行的。
The essential thing to understand is that a copy command is parallel.

3338
05:25:30,752 --> 05:25:35,140
集群中的每个分片都会同时拉取一部分数据。
Every slice in the cluster pulls part of the data simultaneously.

3339
05:25:36,078 --> 05:25:41,540
这就是为什么它比逐条插入数据快几个数量级的原因。
That is why it loads orders of magnitude faster than inserting rows one at a time.

3340
05:25:42,062 --> 05:25:46,032
下一页的所有内容都是关于如何为这种并行性提供支持。
Everything on the next slide is about giving that parallelism something to work with.

3341
05:25:46,318 --> 05:25:53,156
单个大文件无法在多个分片间拆分，这会将大规模并行加载变成单线程处理。
A single large file cannot be split across slices, so it turns a massively parallel load into a single threaded one.

3342
05:25:54,126 --> 05:25:57,952
本模块中的第二个场景完全建立在这个基础之上。
The second word scenario in this module is built entirely on that.

3343
05:25:58,318 --> 05:26:03,204
copy 不仅负责加载，还会分析数据并应用压缩。
Copy also does work beyond loading because it analyzes the data and applies compression.

3344
05:26:04,782 --> 05:26:10,500
前两个要点是同一个概念的两个维度，它们都是可考查的知识点。
The first two bullets are the same idea from two directions and they are examinable numbers.

3345
05:26:10,926 --> 05:26:15,908
假设一个集群有 16 个分片，而你给 copy 提供一个文件。
Suppose a cluster has 16 slices and you give copy a single file.

3346
05:26:17,294 --> 05:26:19,972
那么 15 个分片都要等待那一个分片在工作。
15 slices watch one slice work.

3347
05:26:20,512 --> 05:26:23,844
如果你提供 16 个文件，每个分片都会加载一个。
Give it 16 files and every slice loads one.

3348
05:26:24,782 --> 05:26:28,352
如果提供 32 个，每个分片就会均衡地加载两个。
Give it 32 and every slice loads two evenly.

3349
05:26:28,974 --> 05:26:32,036
清单文件的要点比较微妙，它解决了一个特定的问题。
The manifest point is subtler and answers a specific problem.

3350
05:26:32,942 --> 05:26:35,908
从前缀（前缀）复制会加载任何恰好存在于那里的文件。
Copying from a prefix loads whatever happens to be sitting there.

3351
05:26:36,430 --> 05:26:43,472
因此，仍处于写入中的文件或失败运行留下的残留文件会被静默加载，且没有任何报错。
So a file still being written or a leftover from a failed run gets loaded silently and nothing reports it.

3352
05:26:44,014 --> 05:26:53,508
清单文件指定了要加载的确切文件，这使得操作具有确定性和可重复性。这对我们涵盖的第 6 模块重试机制很重要。
A manifest names the exact files to load, which makes the operation deterministic and repeatable. And that matters for the reruns module 6 covered.

3353
05:26:55,182 --> 05:27:02,192
模块 3 涵盖了流式路径，模块 2 涵盖了零 ETL。所以这一页是它们的交汇点。
Module 3 covered the streaming path and module 2 covered 0 ETL. So this slide is where they all meet.

3354
05:27:02,352 --> 05:27:05,860
决定考题的关键区别在于延迟和开销。
The distinctions that decide questions are latency and overhead.

3355
05:27:06,112 --> 05:27:11,780
自动复制（Autocopy）去除了批处理加载中的调度环节，文件到达后即可加载，无需任何编排。
Autocopy removes the scheduling from a batch load, so files load on arrival with nothing to orchestrate.

3356
05:27:12,590 --> 05:27:19,792
流式摄入将数据仓库直接连接到流中，并在几秒钟内生成行，无需通过 S3 中转。
Streaming ingestion connects the warehouse directly to a stream and materializes rows in seconds without staging through S3.

3357
05:27:20,206 --> 05:27:27,552
Firehose 总是通过 S3 进行中转并执行 copy，所以它比流式摄入慢，但不需要消费者。
Fire hose always stages through S3 and issues a copy, so it is slower than streaming ingestion but needs no consumer.

3358
05:27:28,503 --> 05:27:34,020
零 ETL 让操作数据库保持同步，完全不需要任何流水线。
0ETL keeps an operational database in sync with no pipeline at all.

3359
05:27:35,438 --> 05:27:41,312
卸载（Unload）的作用比表面上看起来更强，第二个和第三个要点都是正确的。
Unload is more useful than it first appears, and the second and third bullets are Y.

3360
05:27:41,806 --> 05:27:48,836
它可以将按列划分的 Parquet 文件直接写入数据湖布局中，让 Athena 和 Glue 能立即读取。
It can write parquet partitioned by a column directly into a lake layout that Athena and Drew can read immediately.

3361
05:27:49,742 --> 05:27:57,632
这使得它成为从数据仓库中发布精选数据以供更广泛使用的自然机制，而不需要
That makes it the natural mechanism for publishing curated data out of the warehouse for wider consumption without a

3362
05:27:57,903 --> 05:27:59,012
中间经过一个 Glue作业。
blue job in between.

3363
05:27:59,854 --> 05:28:05,348
第四个要点描述了考试中作为干扰项提供的反模式。
The fourth bullet describes the anti-pattern the exam offers as a distractor.

3364
05:28:06,112 --> 05:28:11,556
向客户端运行返回 5000 万行数据的查询，会将所有数据通过单个主节点传输。
Running a select that returns 50 million rows to a client sends all of them through the single leader node.

3365
05:28:11,872 --> 05:28:14,564
这很慢，并且可能导致集群不稳定。
That is slow and can destabilize the cluster.

3366
05:28:16,110 --> 05:28:22,628
这就是变更数据在数据仓库中实际应用的方式，它在题目中以一种设计方案出现。
This is how change data actually gets applied in a warehouse and it appears in questions as a design.

3367
05:28:23,246 --> 05:28:24,900
模块 4 所描述的内容。
Module 4 described.

3368
05:28:25,614 --> 05:28:32,740
DMS 写入带有操作列的变更记录，标记每一条记录为插入、更新或删除。
DMS writing change records with an operation column marking each as insert, update or delete.

3369
05:28:33,646 --> 05:28:39,652
在 Redshift 中，你将该批次复制到暂存表中，因为复制是并行的，所以速度很快。
In Redshift, you copy that batch into a staging table, which is fast because copy is parallel.

3370
05:28:40,238 --> 05:28:45,860
然后运行一条合并语句，在一个事务中对目标应用所有变更。
Then run one merge statement that applies every change against the target in a single transaction.

3371
05:28:47,726 --> 05:28:52,388
读取者看到的是旧状态或新状态，绝不会看到中间的任何状态。
Readers see the old state or the new state and never anything in between.

3372
05:28:52,846 --> 05:29:03,172
另一种做法是为每一行发布单独的更新语句，这可行但慢到无法使用，因为列式存储重写的是块而不是行。
The alternative issuing individual update statements per row works and is unusably slow because a columnar store rewrites blocks rather than rows.

3373
05:29:04,654 --> 05:29:12,160
这会让来自事务型数据库的人感到意外，而且它是一个很好的考试题目，因为这种失败是无声的。
This surprises people coming from a transactional database and it makes a good exam question because the failure is silent.

3374
05:29:12,480 --> 05:29:20,612
在 Redshift 中声明主键会告诉查询规划器这些值是唯一的，这确实能帮助它选择更好的计划。
Declaring a primary key in Redshift tells the query planner that values are unique, which genuinely helps it choose better plans.

3375
05:29:21,358 --> 05:29:24,100
它并不会阻止你插入两次相同的行。
It does not stop you inserting the same row twice.

3376
05:29:24,878 --> 05:29:33,412
因此，在失败后重新运行并依赖主键来拒绝已加载行的流水线，会简单地再次加载它们。
So a pipeline that reruns after a failure and relies on the primary key to reject the rows it already loaded will simply load them again.

3377
05:29:34,286 --> 05:29:37,760
唯一的症状就是计数过高。
The only symptom is that a count is too high.

3378
05:29:38,318 --> 05:29:43,012
这就是模块 2 所描述的相同重复问题，解决方法也一样。
That is the same duplicate problem module 2 described and the fix is the same.

3379
05:29:43,662 --> 05:29:47,396
让加载过程具有幂性，这在 Redshift 中意味着使用合并语句。
Make the load idempotent, which in Redshift means merge.

3380
05:29:49,102 --> 05:29:53,920
一个每晚运行的进程将 12GB 的订单数据加载到 Amazon Redshift。
A nightly process loads 12GB of order data into Amazon Redshift.

3381
05:29:54,320 --> 05:30:01,188
数据作为单个未压缩的 CSV 文件生成在 Amazon S3 中，并使用复制命令进行加载。
The data is produced as a single uncompressed CSV file in Amazon S3 and loaded with a copy command.

3382
05:30:02,254 --> 05:30:05,796
集群拥有四个 R3.4x large 节点。
The cluster has four R3.4x large nodes.

3383
05:30:06,702 --> 05:30:13,796
加载大约需要 90 分钟，监控显示有一个分片处于满载状态，而其余分片处于空闲状态。
The load takes about 90 minutes and monitoring shows one slice at full utilization while the rest are idle.

3384
05:30:14,414 --> 05:30:19,972
数据量每月增长约 5%，且加载必须在 4 小时的窗口内完成。
Data volume grows about 5% a month and the load must finish inside a 4 hour window.

3385
05:30:20,622 --> 05:30:22,564
数据工程师应该做哪些更改？
What should the data engineer change?

3386
05:30:24,622 --> 05:30:30,436
将文件拆分为多个压缩文件，最好是集群分片数量的倍数。
Split the file into multiple compressed files, ideally a multiple of the cluster's slice count.

3387
05:30:30,958 --> 05:30:36,164
b 将集群从 4 个节点增加到 8 个，以便提供更多分片。
b Increase the cluster from 4 nodes to 8 so more slices are available.

3388
05:30:36,640 --> 05:30:36,880
C。
C.

3389
05:30:37,440 --> 05:30:41,892
用并行运行的批量插入语句替换复制命令。
Replace the copy command with batched insert statements running in parallel.

3390
05:30:42,414 --> 05:30:42,720
用并行运行的批处理插入语句替换复制命令。
D.

3391
05:30:43,726 --> 05:30:48,868
启用并发扩展，让负载在额外的集群上运行。
Enable concurrency scaling so the load runs on an additional cluster.

3392
05:30:49,838 --> 05:30:51,012
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3393
05:30:57,710 --> 05:30:58,960
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3394
05:30:59,374 --> 05:31:03,588
题目描述的症状是诊断性的，应该能立刻识别出来。
The symptom stated is diagnostic and it should be recognizable instantly.

3395
05:31:03,918 --> 05:31:09,604
只有一个分片处于满载状态而其他分片闲置，意味着工作无法被拆分。
One slice at full utilization while the rest are idle means the work cannot be divided.

3396
05:31:11,214 --> 05:31:14,212
在执行 copy 操作时，这意味着输入数据无法被拆分。
During a copy, that means the input cannot be divided.

3397
05:31:15,118 --> 05:31:22,880
选项 B 是和场景一样的陷阱，只是换了个包装，为一个不是容量问题的问题提供了容量方案。
Option B is the same trap as scenario, one in a different costume, offering capacity for a problem that is not capacity.

3398
05:31:24,398 --> 05:31:28,964
值得注意的是，这个模块现在已经两次提到这一点了。
It is worth noticing that this module has now offered that twice.

3399
05:31:29,934 --> 05:31:37,284
给一个只能使用一个分片的任务增加更多分片，是本课程中关于“优化前先诊断”最典型的例子。
Adding slices to a job that can only use one slice is the clearest example in the course of why diagnosing before optimizing matters.

3400
05:31:39,022 --> 05:31:43,588
在第 9 个模块后你会觉得这很熟悉，因为背后的原因基本一致。
This will sound familiar after module 9 because the underlying reason is much the same.

3401
05:31:44,014 --> 05:31:52,036
Redshift 删除行是标记它们而不是直接删除，并且插入新行是在表格末尾而不是按排序位置插入。
Redshift deletes rows by marking them rather than removing them and inserts new rows at the end of a table rather than in sorted position.

3402
05:31:52,910 --> 05:32:02,980
所以一个被写入数月的表会保留标记为已删除的行并占用空间。它还会包含未排序区域，这会破坏让查询变快的区域映射。
So a table written to for months holds marked deleted rows, taking up space. It also holds unsorted regions which defeat the zone maps that make queries fast.

3403
05:32:03,280 --> 05:32:10,660
Redshift 现在在后台自动处理大部分这些操作，这就是为什么这个考点在考试中比以前占比更小了。
Redshift now handles most of this automatically in the background, which is why this topic is smaller than it once was on this exam.

3404
05:32:11,438 --> 05:32:18,180
考查的内容是了解这些自动进程的作用以及它们滞后的具体情况。
Knowing what the automatic processes do and the specific situations where they fall behind is what is still examined.

3405
05:32:18,638 --> 05:32:21,060
接下来的三张幻灯片就涵盖了这些内容。
The next three slides cover exactly that.

3406
05:32:22,702 --> 05:32:27,908
自动清理处理普通情况，在集群不忙碌时运行。
Automatic vacuum handles the ordinary case, running when the cluster is not busy.

3407
05:32:28,302 --> 05:32:32,452
所以考试现在不太考如何调度它了。
So the exam is less interested in scheduling one than it used to be.

3408
05:32:33,294 --> 05:32:37,348
但在发生单次非常大的变更后，仍会出现手动清理的情况。
A manual vacuum still appears after a single very large change.

3409
05:32:38,254 --> 05:32:43,844
删除 1 亿行数据会留下 1 亿个标记过的行占用块。
Deleting 100 million rows leaves 100 million marked rows occupying blocks.

3410
05:32:44,400 --> 05:32:49,444
等待后台处理赶上可能比你预想的要长得多。
Waiting for background processing to catch up may take considerably longer than you want.

3411
05:32:50,222 --> 05:32:55,748
同样的情况也适用于大规模加载后，这会在表末尾留下一个巨大的未排序区域。
The same applies after a very large load, which leaves a big unsorted region at the end of the table.

3412
05:32:56,654 --> 05:33:03,680
值得注意的是 reindex 形式，因为它只存在于那些本身就不寻常的交错排序键中。
The reindex form is worth recognizing because it exists only for interleaved sort keys that are themselves unusual.

3413
05:33:03,760 --> 05:33:09,440
所以提到这两个词的题目是在保持逻辑一致性，而不是在考你冷知识。
So a question mentioning both is being internally consistent rather than testing you on trivia.

3414
05:33:11,118 --> 05:33:16,964
这个提示描述了一个值得识别的症状，因为从查询中完全看不出原因。
The callout describes a symptom worth recognizing because the cause is completely invisible from the query.

3415
05:33:17,424 --> 05:33:19,104
查询没有改变。
The query has not changed.

3416
05:33:19,342 --> 05:33:24,676
数据并没有大幅增长，但优化器选择的执行计划现在是错误的。
The data has not grown dramatically, and yet the plan the optimizer chooses is now wrong.

3417
05:33:25,184 --> 05:33:28,612
它认为一个表比实际情况要小得多。
It believes a table is far smaller than it has become.

3418
05:33:29,166 --> 05:33:34,820
因此它选择了错误的连接策略，原本耗时 10 秒的查询现在需要 10 分钟。
So it picks the wrong join strategy and a query that took 10 seconds now takes 10 minutes.

3419
05:33:36,430 --> 05:33:41,188
运行分析可以恢复正确的状况，并在下次执行时恢复原有的计划。
Running analyze restores a correct picture and the plan reverts on the next execution.

3420
05:33:42,544 --> 05:33:46,308
自动分析让这种情况比以前少见得多。
Automatic analyze makes this rarer than it once was.

3421
05:33:47,214 --> 05:33:51,652
它仍会出现在描述突然且原因不明的变慢情况的题目中
It still appears in questions describing a sudden unexplained slowdown

3422
05:33:52,494 --> 05:33:58,052
在大量负载之后，因为加载任务在后台进程赶上之前就已完成。
after a large load because the load finished before the background process caught up.

3423
05:33:59,662 --> 05:34:06,916
自动表优化是场景1略显人为的原因，这一点值得承认。
Automatic table optimization is why scenario 1 is slightly artificial and it is worth acknowledging that.

3424
05:34:07,264 --> 05:34:13,572
在实践中，设为自动模式的表最终会自动获得合理的键。
In practice, a table left on AUTO would eventually acquire reasonable keys by itself.

3425
05:34:14,464 --> 05:34:20,580
考试仍要求你明确选择，因为它在测试你是否理解这些键的作用。
The exam still asks you to choose explicitly because it is testing whether you understand what the keys do.

3426
05:34:21,262 --> 05:34:23,908
第四个要点才是真正的限制条件。
The fourth bullet is the genuine limitation.

3427
05:34:24,384 --> 05:34:32,260
优化需要查询历史来学习，因此新表或用户即将完全改变的表就没有参考依据了。
Optimization needs query history to learn from, so a new table or one whose user is about to change completely has nothing to go on.

3428
05:34:33,038 --> 05:34:38,468
这正是题目提供访问模式并期望你据此采取行动的时候。
That is exactly when a question hands you the access pattern and expects you to act on it.

3429
05:34:39,982 --> 05:34:46,436
工作负载管理的存在是为了防止一个工作负载饿死另一个，考试也是按这个逻辑来考的。
Workload management exists to stop one workload starving another, and the exam frames it that way.

3430
05:34:47,374 --> 05:34:52,548
经典情况是深夜的 EDL 作业与早晨的仪表盘数据竞争资源。
The classic situation is an overnight EDL jog competing with morning dashboards.

3431
05:34:53,358 --> 05:35:03,396
带有查询优先级的自动 工作负载管理 是现代解决方案，允许你在不手动分配内存的情况下将仪表板工作负载标记为高优先级。
Automatic WLM with query priorities is the modern answer, letting you mark the dashboard workload as high priority without hand allocating memory.

3432
05:35:03,824 --> 05:35:08,944
当题目要求保证份额时，仍会出现手动 工作负载管理。
Manual WLM still appears when a question requires a guaranteed share.

3433
05:35:09,358 --> 05:35:14,692
这是因为它无论运行什么其他内容，都会为每个队列预留固定比例的内存。
That is because it reserves a fixed percentage of memory per queue regardless of what else is running.

3434
05:35:16,334 --> 05:35:25,092
查询监控规则是强制执行层，它们用于回答关于由于失控查询消耗集群资源的题目，因为规则可以自动终止它。
Query monitoring rules are the enforcement layer and they answer questions about a runaway query consuming the cluster because a rule can abort it automatically.

3435
05:35:26,766 --> 05:35:33,188
这个提示是考试测试的区别点，并且在本模块中已经作为干扰项出现过两次了。
The call out is the distinction the exam tests and it has already appeared twice in this module as a distractor.

3436
05:35:34,062 --> 05:35:38,276
当问题是同时到达的查询过多时，并发扩展会有所帮助。
Concurrency scaling helps when the problem is too many queries arriving at once.

3437
05:35:38,958 --> 05:35:42,724
这样它们就会在队列中排队，用户等待轮到他们。
So they queue behind one another and users wait for their turn.

3438
05:35:43,694 --> 05:35:48,784
对于因为缺少排序键而耗时 4 分钟的单个查询，它毫无作用。
It does nothing whatsoever for a single query that takes 4 minutes because of a missing sort

3439
05:35:49,742 --> 05:35:53,828
键。这是因为该查询在额外的集群 2 上也要跑 4 分钟。
key. That is because that query takes 4 minutes on the extra cluster 2.

3440
05:35:54,414 --> 05:35:56,004
所以要仔细阅读症状。
So read the symptom carefully.

3441
05:35:56,654 --> 05:35:56,893
问。
Q.

3442
05:35:58,062 --> 05:36:01,028
等待时间上升意味着并发扩展。
Wait time rising means concurrency scaling.

3443
05:36:01,998 --> 05:36:05,476
执行时间上升意味着表设计或统计信息。
Execution time rising means table design or statistics.

3444
05:36:07,214 --> 05:36:14,624
每天一小时的免费时长也值得记住，因为这意味着许多突发性工作负载根本不需要支付并发扩展费用。
The free hour per day is worth remembering as well because it means many bursty workloads never pay for concurrency scaling at all.

3445
05:36:15,822 --> 05:36:23,236
在 Redshift 和 RDS 中管理锁是一项特定技能，而且其症状足够独特，值得识别。
Managing locks in Redshift and RDS is a name skill, and the symptom is distinctive enough to be worth recognizing.

3446
05:36:23,982 --> 05:36:31,588
一个查询正在运行，它没有消耗显著资源，也没有失败，且永远不会完成。
A query is running, it is not consuming meaningful resources, it is not failing, and it never completes.

3447
05:36:32,558 --> 05:36:38,980
这是一个锁权重问题而非性能问题，无论增加多少容量或进行何种调优都无法影响它。
That is a lock weight rather than a performance problem, and no amount of capacity or tuning affects it.

3448
05:36:40,334 --> 05:36:47,652
通常原因是某个会话开启了一个事务，执行了一些操作，然后在未提交或回滚的情况下断开了连接。
The usual cause is a session that opened a transaction, did something, and then went away without committing or rolling back.

3449
05:36:48,366 --> 05:36:50,436
通常是因为应用程序崩溃了。
Often because an application crashed.

3450
05:36:51,342 --> 05:36:57,348
该锁会一直存在直到该会话被终止，这就是第四个要点所做的事情。
The lock survives until that session is terminated, which is what the fourth bullet does.

3451
05:36:58,704 --> 05:37:04,580
这个重点提示是本模块最后五个阅读题中的第一题的实战答案。
The callout is the practical answer to the first of the five reading questions at the end of this module.

3452
05:37:05,134 --> 05:37:07,812
查询历史会分别记录这两个数值。
Query history records both numbers separately.

3453
05:37:08,384 --> 05:37:15,076
所以，区分“等待中的查询”和“运行缓慢的查询”，不是主观判断，而是两个不同的列。
So the distinction between a query that waited and a query that ran slowly is not a judgment call, it is two columns.

3454
05:37:15,918 --> 05:37:22,692
Redshift Advisor 值得记住这个名字，因为它提供的正是本模块一直在教你的内容。
Redshift Advisor is worth knowing by name because it is the service telling you what this module has been teaching.

3455
05:37:22,944 --> 05:37:32,068
它会检查你的实际工作负载，并报告某个特定表是否能从排序键中受益，或者某种分布样式是否导致了重分布。
It inspects your actual workload and reports that a particular table would benefit from a sort key or that a distribution style is causing redistribution.

3456
05:37:32,942 --> 05:37:34,564
这就是同样的诊断结果。
That is the same diagnosis.

3457
05:37:35,024 --> 05:37:37,764
题目要求你根据症状做出判断。
A question asks you to make from symptoms.

3458
05:37:39,438 --> 05:37:46,180
一个 Amazon Redshift 集群为大约 200 名分析师在每个工作日的早晨使用的商业智能仪表板提供服务。
An Amazon Redshift cluster serves a business intelligence dashboard used by around 200 analysts each weekday morning.

3459
05:37:48,270 --> 05:37:54,148
它还运行一个 ETL 作业，在夜间加载并转换数据，有时会延时到早上。
It also runs an ETL job that loads and transforms data overnight and sometimes overruns into the morning.

3460
05:37:55,118 --> 05:38:02,468
当 ETL 作业延时时，仪表板查询需要几分钟才能开始。一旦开始，它们就在两秒内完成。
When the ETL job overruns, dashboard queries take several minutes to start. Once they start, they complete in under two seconds.

3461
05:38:02,832 --> 05:38:05,924
单个查询的执行时间没有变化。
Individual query execution times are unchanged.

3462
05:38:07,950 --> 05:38:10,148
公司不会推迟 ETL 作业。
The company will not delay the ETL job.

3463
05:38:10,432 --> 05:38:12,772
哪种组合最能解决这个问题？
Which combination best addresses the problem?

3464
05:38:16,750 --> 05:38:21,060
A. 为仪表板表添加复合排序键以加快执行速度。
Add a compound sort key to the dashboard tables to speed up execution.

3465
05:38:21,486 --> 05:38:30,592
b 在仪表板队列上启用并发扩展，并使用 工作负载管理 查询优先级将仪表板排在 ETL 之上。
b Enable concurrency scaling on the dashboard queue and use WLM query priority to rank dashboards above ETL.

3466
05:38:31,086 --> 05:38:31,312
C
C

3467
05:38:32,366 --> 05:38:36,580
在每天早晨 ETL 作业完成后运行清理和分析。
Run vacuum and analyze after the ETL job completes each morning.

3468
05:38:37,326 --> 05:38:37,552
D。
D.

3469
05:38:38,766 --> 05:38:42,020
调整集群大小，将节点数量翻倍。
Resize the cluster to double the number of nodes.

3470
05:38:42,286 --> 05:38:43,684
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3471
05:38:50,350 --> 05:38:51,712
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3472
05:38:52,512 --> 05:38:57,284
这个场景正是直接考查并发扩展重点提示的内容。
And this scenario is the concurrency scaling callout tested directly.

3473
05:38:58,192 --> 05:39:01,252
题目刻意区分了这两个数值。
The question separates the two numbers deliberately.

3474
05:39:02,112 --> 05:39:07,300
启动时间是几分钟，而执行时间不到两秒。
Time to start is several minutes, and time to execute is under two seconds.

3475
05:39:07,950 --> 05:39:09,860
关于执行过程的一切都是正常的。
Everything about the execution is healthy.

3476
05:39:10,158 --> 05:39:14,052
所以，任何旨在改进执行速度的选项都在回答一个没人问过的问题。
So every option that improves execution is answering a question nobody asked.

3477
05:39:15,246 --> 05:39:17,508
选项 A 和 C 确实都是很好的做法。
Options A and C are both genuinely good.

3478
05:39:18,158 --> 05:39:23,300
Redshift 的最佳实践被放在了错误的地方，这是本课程反复强调的一种考题套路。
Redshift practice offered in the wrong place, which is a pattern this course has flagged repeatedly.

3479
05:39:24,174 --> 05:39:30,468
而选项 D 又是关于容量的问题，对于一个间歇性出现的问题，这种做法既昂贵又永久。
And option D is capacity again, this time expensive and permanent for an intermittent problem.

3480
05:39:31,982 --> 05:39:38,756
这就是领域 2 中很多分数所在的地方，因为有四个功能听起来很相似，并且经常被同时作为选项提供。
This is where a lot of domain 2 marks sit because four capabilities sound similar and are routinely offered as options together.

3481
05:39:39,694 --> 05:39:42,020
Spectrum 读取位于数据湖中的文件。
Spectrum reads files sitting in a data lake.

3482
05:39:42,734 --> 05:39:45,508
联邦查询读取运营数据库。
Federated query reads an operational database.

3483
05:39:45,952 --> 05:39:46,468
实时的。
Live.

3484
05:39:46,958 --> 05:39:48,548
在你发起请求的那一刻。
At the moment you ask.

3485
05:39:49,262 --> 05:39:53,380
数据共享在不复制任何内容的情况下读取另一个 Redshift 数据仓库。
Data sharing reads another redshift warehouse without copying anything.

3486
05:39:53,792 --> 05:39:59,108
零 ETL 持续复制运营数据库并保持其最新。
Zero ETL copies an operational database in continuously and keeps it current.

3487
05:39:59,472 --> 05:40:05,284
它们在三个属性上有所不同，记住这三个点就能快速做对题目。
They differ on three attributes, and holding those three straight is what makes the questions quick.

3488
05:40:05,792 --> 05:40:07,908
问数据物理上存放在哪里。
Ask where the data physically lives.

3489
05:40:08,782 --> 05:40:11,300
问是移动数据还是原位读取。
Ask whether it moves or is read in place.

3490
05:40:11,792 --> 05:40:14,820
还要问你看到的数据到底有多新。
And ask how fresh what you see actually is.

3491
05:40:16,014 --> 05:40:23,620
过一遍接下来的五张幻灯片，问这三个问题，最后的对比就会变得显而易见了。
Work through each of the next five slides, asking those three questions, and the comparison at the end will already be obvious.

3492
05:40:24,878 --> 05:40:28,900
这两者很容易混淆，考试会刻意把它们区分开。
These two are easy to blur and the exam separates them deliberately.

3493
05:40:29,934 --> 05:40:35,012
跨数据库查询是在同一个 Redshift 数据仓库内的不同数据库中进行查询。
A cross-database query reaches into a different database inside the same Redshift warehouse.

3494
05:40:35,598 --> 05:40:39,716
那是组织模式的一种方式，而不是团队间共享的手段。
That is a way of organizing schemas rather than a way of sharing between teams.

3495
05:40:40,622 --> 05:40:44,612
所有内容仍然属于一个集群、一份账单和一套计算资源。
Everything is still one cluster, one bill, and one set of compute.

3496
05:40:46,062 --> 05:40:54,948
数据共享完全跨越了数据仓库边界，包括到其他账户和其他区域，且每个消费者使用自己的计算资源。
Data sharing crosses warehouse boundaries entirely, including into other accounts and other regions, and each consumer brings its own compute.

3497
05:40:55,822 --> 05:41:00,512
Lake Formation 这个要点对领域 4 很重要，现在值得标注一下。
The lake formation bullet matters for domain 4 and is worth flagging now.

3498
05:41:01,070 --> 05:41:05,060
数据共享本身授予对整个对象的访问权限。
A data share on its own grants access to whole objects.

3499
05:41:05,870 --> 05:41:12,964
在 Lake Formation 中注册它，就能增加模块 18 所涵盖的行级和列级控制。
Registering it with lake formation adds the column and row level controls that module 18 covers properly.

3500
05:41:14,734 --> 05:41:17,700
Spectrum 能解决一个经常出现的考点。
Spectrum answers a question that comes up constantly.

3501
05:41:18,254 --> 05:41:24,708
这就是处理那些必须可查询但又不值得在数据仓库中存储的多年历史数据的做法。
That is what to do with years of history that must remain queryable but does not justify warehouse storage.

3502
05:41:26,414 --> 05:41:33,988
将近几个月的数据加载到查询速度快的 Redshift 中，其余内容作为 Parquet 保存在 S3 中，并在其上定义外部表。
Load the recent months into Redshift where queries are fast, leave the rest as parquet in S3, define external tables over it.

3503
05:41:34,894 --> 05:41:36,868
写一个同时涵盖这两部分的查询。
Write one query that spans both.

3504
05:41:37,710 --> 05:41:39,940
用户无法分辨界限在哪里。
The user cannot tell where the boundary is.

3505
05:41:40,462 --> 05:41:47,684
RA3 按每 TB 收费，这就是为什么分区和列式存储格式在这里非常重要，就像在 Athena 中一样。
The per terabyte charge on RA3 is why partitioning and columnar formats matter here exactly as they do for Athena.

3506
05:41:48,462 --> 05:41:54,500
值得注意的是 RG 的变化，因为它取消了那项费用并改变了成本结构。
It is worth noting the RG change again because it removes that charge and changes the economics.

3507
05:41:56,206 --> 05:42:02,052
模块 5 提到了 Athena Federated Query 的这个点，这里同样适用。
Module 5 made this point about Athena Federated Query and it applies identically here.

3508
05:42:02,510 --> 05:42:07,492
直接从生产数据库读取很优雅，根本不需要任何流水线，
Reading directly from a production database is elegant, requires no pipeline at all,

3509
05:42:08,430 --> 05:42:12,964
但它会将分析负载放在一个实际任务是为应用程序服务的系统上。
puts analytical load on a system whose actual job is serving an application.

3510
05:42:13,966 --> 05:42:20,900
对于将少量参考行与数据仓库查询进行连接，这是理想选择，且由于没有复制延迟，数据的鲜度也完美无缺。
For joining a handful of reference rows to a warehouse query, it is ideal and the freshness is perfect because there is no replication lag.

3511
05:42:21,422 --> 05:42:26,116
对于高强度的分析扫描，对该数据库支持的任何功能来说都是巨大的风险。
For a heavy analytical scan, it is a genuine risk to whatever that database supports.

3512
05:42:26,894 --> 05:42:32,292
所以，描述偶尔查询参考数据的问题指向的是联邦查询。
So a question describing occasional lookups of reference data points at federated query.

3513
05:42:33,680 --> 05:42:42,628
而描述针对运营数据库进行常规报表工作负载的问题，则指向零 ETL 或复制流水线。
A question describing a regular reporting workload against an operational database points at zero ETL or a replication pipeline instead.

3514
05:42:44,334 --> 05:42:52,580
数据共享解决的是组织问题多于技术问题，这就是为什么题目措辞往往描述团队而非吞吐量。
Data sharing solves an organizational problem more than a technical one, which is why the question wording tends to describe teams rather than throughput.

3515
05:42:53,230 --> 05:43:00,080
财务团队和营销团队都需要相同的销售数据，而不需要在同一个集群中共享内容。
A finance team and a marketing team both need the same sales data without sharing their content for one cluster.

3516
05:43:00,622 --> 05:43:08,356
或者有人建立一个流水线将数据复制到第二个集群并永久维护，但副本可能会出现偏差。
Or somebody builds a pipeline to copy data into a second cluster and maintains it forever, with the copies drifting apart.

3517
05:43:09,006 --> 05:43:14,240
数据共享让每个团队都有自己的计算读取，且只有一个权威副本。
Data sharing gives each team its own compute reading, one authoritative copy.

3518
05:43:14,862 --> 05:43:21,828
最后一项是一个真正的约束条件，它与节点类型幻灯片相关联，因为托管存储是实现它的关键。
The last bullet is a real constraint and it connects back to the node type slide because managed storage is what makes it possible.

3519
05:43:23,342 --> 05:43:28,580
模块 2 介绍了零 ETL，而这里就是它最合适的应用场景。
Module 2 introduced 0ETL and this is where it lands properly.

3520
05:43:29,134 --> 05:43:38,084
它之所以能在“开销最小”的问题中胜出，是因为真的没有什么需要操作的，不需要估算 DMS 任务规模，也不需要调度 Glue作业，
The reason it wins least overhead questions so decisively is that there is genuinely nothing to operate, no DMS task to size, no blue job to schedule,

3521
05:43:39,022 --> 05:43:44,132
不需要监控复制实例，也不需要在凌晨三点处理故障。
no replication instance to monitor, and no failure to handle at 3 in the morning.

3522
05:43:44,718 --> 05:43:47,940
这两个约束条件是它能在考试中被选为正确答案的原因。
The two constraints are what make it answerable in an exam.

3523
05:43:49,966 --> 05:43:57,124
源和目标对必须受支持，目前包括将 Aurora、Amazon RDS 和 Dynamo DB 导入 Redshift。
The source and target pair must be supported, currently Aurora, Amazon RDS and Dynamo DB into Redshift.

3524
05:43:57,902 --> 05:44:03,620
而且数据以原样到达，因此任何重塑都在之后通过 SQL 在 Redshift 中完成。
And the data arrives exactly as it is, so any reshaping happens in Redshift afterwards with SQL.

3525
05:44:04,160 --> 05:44:12,708
如果题目描述的是需要用于分析的运营数据，且未提到转换并强调开销，就是在描述这种情况。
A question describing operational data needed for analytics with no transformation mentioned and overhead emphasized is describing this.

3526
05:44:14,478 --> 05:44:18,404
这是模块 1 的访问模式规则应用于第五种情况。
This is Module 1's access pattern rule applied to a fifth situation.

3527
05:44:18,880 --> 05:44:22,400
一个月查询几次的数据应该留在原地。
Data queried a few times a month should stay where it is.

3528
05:44:22,560 --> 05:44:29,028
因为复制它意味着要支付存储第二个副本的费用，并构建一套系统来保持数据最新。
That is because copying it means paying to store a second copy and building something to keep it current.

3529
05:44:29,806 --> 05:44:38,820
每天有数百人查询的数据，应该在 Redshift 自己的优化存储中，并在仓库中按这些查询进行排序和分布。
Data queried by hundreds of people every morning should be in the warehouse in Redshift's own optimized storage, sorted and distributed for those queries.

3530
05:44:39,040 --> 05:44:43,588
折中的方案很有意思，而这正是数据共享所在的位置。
The middle ground is the interesting one and it is where data sharing sits.

3531
05:44:44,078 --> 05:44:49,764
这是因为它提供了给消费者的仓库性能，而消费者不需要拥有副本。
That is because it gives the consumer warehouse performance without the consumer needing a copy.

3532
05:44:51,406 --> 05:44:56,356
一家公司在 Amazon Redshift 中保留三年的交易数据，总计 40 太字节。
A company keeps three years of transactions in Amazon Redshift totaling 40 Tabytes.

3533
05:44:56,640 --> 05:44:59,588
分析师不断查询最近 90 天的数据。
Analysts query the most recent 90 days constantly.

3534
05:44:59,918 --> 05:45:04,836
超过一年的数据可能每季度仅被查询两次，用于合规性报告，
Data older than a year is queried perhaps twice a quarter for regulatory reporting,

3535
05:45:05,710 --> 05:45:10,980
但必须能在单个 SQL 语句中与近期数据一起查询。
but must remain queryable alongside recent data in a single SQL statement.

3536
05:45:11,502 --> 05:45:14,852
存储成本已成为 Redshift 账单中最大的项目。
Storage costs have become the largest line on the Redshift bill.

3537
05:45:15,374 --> 05:45:19,588
公司希望在不改变分析师编写查询方式的情况下降低这些成本。
The company wants to reduce them without changing how analysts write queries.

3538
05:45:20,782 --> 05:45:22,852
数据工程师应该实施什么？
What should the data engineer implement?

3539
05:45:24,846 --> 05:45:32,720
将超过一年的数据卸载到 Amazon S3 作为分区 Parquet，定义外部表并使用
Unload data older than one year to Amazon S3 as partition parquet, define external tables and query them with

3540
05:45:32,880 --> 05:45:33,988
Redshift Spectrum 进行查询。
Redshift Spectrum.

3541
05:45:34,702 --> 05:45:42,340
B 将超过一年的数据卸载到 Amazon S3，并让分析师使用 Amazon Athena 进行历史查询。
b Unload data older than one year to Amazon S3 and tell analysts to use Amazon Athena for historical queries.

3542
05:45:43,680 --> 05:45:48,868
C 将旧数据移到第二个 Redshift 集群并使用数据共享。
C Move the older data to a second Redshift cluster and use data sharing.

3543
05:45:49,806 --> 05:45:53,600
d 启用并发扩展并缩小集群规模。
d Enable concurrency scaling and reduce the cluster size.

3544
05:45:54,160 --> 05:45:55,268
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3545
05:46:01,998 --> 05:46:06,500
答案是 A，其中一个条款排除了最接近的干扰项。
The answer is A, and one clause eliminates the closest competitor.

3546
05:46:07,008 --> 05:46:16,036
数据必须能在单个 SQL 语句中与近期数据一起查询。选项 B 虽然省钱效果一样，但无法满足这一要求。
Data must remain queryable alongside recent data in a single SQL statement. Option B saves exactly the same money and fails that.

3547
05:46:16,846 --> 05:46:23,728
这是因为 Athena 和 Redshift 是独立的查询引擎，跨越两者的连接不是一条语句。
That is because Athena and Redshift are separate query engines and a join across them is not one statement.

3548
05:46:24,048 --> 05:46:30,628
Spectrum 存在的目的正是为了让外部表能在同一个查询中与仓库表进行连接。
Spectrum exists precisely so that an external table can be joined to a warehouse table in the same query.

3549
05:46:31,566 --> 05:46:34,276
选项 D 有一个特殊的理由值得注意。
Option D is worth noting for a specific reason.

3550
05:46:35,054 --> 05:46:43,588
在托管存储上，缩小集群可以降低计算成本，而不会影响存储，因为这两者是独立构建的。
On managed storage, shrinking the cluster reduces compute cost and does nothing to storage because the two are built independently.

3551
05:46:45,230 --> 05:46:51,728
这些计划关键词值得识别，因为它们能把模糊的猜想变成确凿的证据。
The plan keywords are worth recognizing because they turn a vague suspicion into evidence.

3552
05:46:52,174 --> 05:46:58,148
当考试描述 Join 操作过程中有大量的重分布时，这就是有人为了确认这一点而查看的内容。
When the exam describes heavy redistribution during a join, this is what somebody looked at to see it.

3553
05:46:58,830 --> 05:47:05,380
DS 这个 none 意味着连接的两侧都已经位于正确的切片上，没有任何移动，这正是我们的目标。
DS This none means both sides of the join are already on the right slices and nothing moves, which is the goal.

3554
05:47:05,728 --> 05:47:14,436
DS_broadcast_inner 意味着其中一张表正在广播到每个节点，这对小表没问题，但对大表来说成本很高。
DSBcast inner means one table is being broadcast to every node, which is fine for a small table and expensive for a large one.

3555
05:47:15,086 --> 05:47:25,284
DS_DIST_BOTH 意味着两边都在进行重分布，这是成本最高的后果，也是分布键设置错误的最明确信号。
DS DIST both means both sides are being redistributed, which is the most expensive outcome and the clearest signal that the distribution keys are wrong.

3556
05:47:26,958 --> 05:47:34,724
对于一个每天运行数百次相同昂贵聚合操作的仪表板，物化视图是标准答案。
Materialized views are the standard answer to a dashboard running the same expensive aggregation hundreds of times a day.

3557
05:47:35,374 --> 05:47:40,804
只需计算一次，存储结果，并在底层数据变化时进行刷新。
Compute it once, store the result, and refresh it as the underlying data changes.

3558
05:47:41,774 --> 05:47:47,556
第四个要点中的自动重写功能非常有用，但很容易被忽略。
The automatic rewriting capability in the fourth bullet is genuinely useful and very easy to overlook.

3559
05:47:48,110 --> 05:47:51,716
分析师继续像以前一样对基础表编写查询。
Analysts keep writing queries against the base tables exactly as before.

3560
05:47:52,206 --> 05:47:58,180
Redshift 会识别出物化视图已经包含了答案，并静默地使用它来代替。
Redshift recognizes that a materialized view already contains the answer and quietly uses it instead.

3561
05:47:59,086 --> 05:48:03,684
不需要告诉任何人存在这个视图，也不需要更改任何 SQL。
Nobody has to be told the view exists or change any SQL.

3562
05:48:04,048 --> 05:48:06,980
最后一个要点与第三模块的内容相关联。
And the last bullet connects back to module 3.

3563
05:48:07,342 --> 05:48:17,572
这是因为 Redshift 流式摄入会将流记录物化到这种特定的结构中，这就是为什么这两个主题共享同一种机制。
That is because Redshift streaming ingestion materializes stream records into precisely this structure, which is why the two topics share a mechanism.

3564
05:48:19,246 --> 05:48:21,956
可用性警告是需要记住的要点。
The availability warning is the item to carry.

3565
05:48:22,318 --> 05:48:29,156
Redshift 中 Python 用户自定义函数将在 2026 年 6 月底停止支持。
Python user-defined functions in RedshiftReach end of support at the end of June 2026.

3566
05:48:29,408 --> 05:48:34,148
旧版本的材料提供了一种在查询中运行自定义逻辑的方法。
Older material offers them as the way to run custom logic inside a query.

3567
05:48:35,054 --> 05:48:40,260
对于任何可以用 SQL 表达的内容，替代方案都是 SQL 用户自定义函数。
The replacements are SQL user-defined functions for anything expressible in SQL.

3568
05:48:53,808 --> 05:48:54,128
它
It

3569
05:48:54,128 --> 05:49:01,924
让你能够训练一个模型，然后在普通 SQL 中调用它，由 SageMaker 在底层执行工作。
lets you train a model and then call it in ordinary SQL with SageMaker doing the work underneath.

3570
05:49:03,566 --> 05:49:09,156
表级恢复值得了解，因为它会改变恢复类问题的答案。
The table level restore is worth knowing because it changes the answer to a recovery question.

3571
05:49:09,870 --> 05:49:18,724
损坏了一个表的工作不需要将整个 40TB 集群恢复到新端点并让所有应用重新指向它。
A job that corrupted one table does not require restoring an entire 40TB cluster to a new endpoint and repointing every application at it.

3572
05:49:19,566 --> 05:49:25,220
你只需从快照中将那一个表恢复到运行中的集群即可继续工作。
You restore that one table from a snapshot into the running cluster and carry on.

3573
05:49:26,542 --> 05:49:30,180
对比一下第 9 模块中的 Iceberg 回滚，
Compare that with the iceberg rollback from module 9,

3574
05:49:31,150 --> 05:49:36,516
那个更快，因为根本不需要移动数据，只需要更改元数据指针。
which is faster still because no data moves at all, only a metadata pointer.

3575
05:49:38,126 --> 05:49:42,820
最后一项关于调整大小的区别会出现在迁移相关的题目中。
The resize distinction on the last bullet appears in migration questions.

3576
05:49:43,630 --> 05:49:47,072
弹性调整（Elastic resize）是更改节点数量的快速路径。
Elastic resize is a quick path for changing node count.

3577
05:49:47,232 --> 05:49:52,868
经典调整（Classic resize）处理节点类型的变更，比如从 VC2 迁移到 RA3。
Classic resize handles a change of node type, such as moving from VC2 to RA3.

3578
05:49:54,350 --> 05:49:56,996
这个主题比 S3 的对应内容要小一些。
This is a smaller topic than the equivalent for S3.

3579
05:49:57,422 --> 05:49:59,652
这是因为 Redshift 集群属于计算资源。
That is because a Redshift cluster is compute.

3580
05:50:00,078 --> 05:50:03,780
你是在配置一个实例，而不是默认跨越多个可用区的区域性服务。
You provision rather than a regional service that spans zones by default.

3581
05:50:04,654 --> 05:50:08,388
除非另有说明，否则集群只运行在一个可用区内。
A cluster lives in one availability zone unless you say otherwise.

3582
05:50:09,358 --> 05:50:16,548
因此，如果该可用区故障，意味着需要从快照恢复到另一个可用区，这所需的时间与数据量成正比。
So losing that zone means restoring from a snapshot into another one, which takes time roughly proportional to the volume of data.

3583
05:50:16,912 --> 05:50:25,988
多可用区（Multi-AZ）在两个可用区运行数据仓库，并在不改变端点的情况下提供自动故障转移。因此应用无需重新连接到新位置。
Multi-AZ runs the warehouse across two zones with automatic failover behind an unchanged endpoint. So applications do not reconnect anywhere new.

3584
05:50:26,752 --> 05:50:30,820
当题目说明“不可接受停机”时，这就是正确答案。
That is the answer when a question states that an outage is unacceptable.

3585
05:50:31,152 --> 05:50:36,100
它的计算成本大约翻倍，这正是题目要求你权衡的权衡点。
It costs roughly double the compute, which is the trade the question is really asking you to weigh up.

3586
05:50:37,614 --> 05:50:45,412
领域 4 涵盖了所有这些内容，其中三项值得现在了解，因为它们会出现在领域 2 的题目中。
Domain 4 covers all of this properly, and three items are worth knowing now because they appear in domain 2 questions.

3587
05:50:46,062 --> 05:50:49,316
关于 IAM 角色的这一点是实用的。
The IAM role point is the practical one.

3588
05:50:50,318 --> 05:50:53,732
从 S3 读取的复制命令不携带凭证。
A copy command reading from S3 does not carry credentials.

3589
05:50:54,318 --> 05:50:56,644
它指定的是关联到集群的角色。
It names a role attached to the cluster.

3590
05:50:57,486 --> 05:51:04,164
因访问错误而失败的复制，几乎总是角色或存储桶策略问题，而不是语法问题。
A copy that fails with an access error is almost always a role or bucket policy problem rather than a syntax problem.

3591
05:51:04,494 --> 05:51:09,188
这里值得记住“角色级安全”和“动态数据脱敏”这两个术语。
Role level security and dynamic data masking are worth recognizing by name here.

3592
05:51:10,032 --> 05:51:17,956
这是因为它们能让同一个表服务于具有不同可见性要求的不同受众，这在第 19 模块中会详细讲解。
That is because they let one table serve different audiences with different visibility, which module 19 returns to in detail.

3593
05:51:19,632 --> 05:51:22,724
这个表格是把该模块内容压缩成的一个查询表。
This table is the module compressed into a lookup.

3594
05:51:23,406 --> 05:51:29,540
值得作为一个整体来学习，因为 Redshift 的题目往往是故障诊断类而非架构类。
It is worth learning as a unit because redshift questions are so often diagnostic rather than architectural.

3595
05:51:30,350 --> 05:51:39,108
第二行值得特别注意，因为相同的症状有两个完全不同的原因，仅由发生的时间点来区分。
The second row deserves particular attention because the same symptom has two entirely different causes, distinguished only by when it happens.

3596
05:51:39,790 --> 05:51:44,512
在加载过程中出现一个繁忙切片（busy slice），意味着有一个无法拆分的输入文件。
One busy slice during a load means a single input file that cannot be split.

3597
05:51:44,672 --> 05:51:48,516
在查询过程中出现一个繁忙切片，意味着数据分布倾斜。
One busy slice during queries means distribution skew.

3598
05:51:49,262 --> 05:51:55,428
两者在监控中看起来一模一样，生成的图表也相同，但解决方法完全不同。
Both look identical in monitoring, both produce the same graph, and the fixes have nothing in common.

3599
05:51:56,078 --> 05:52:01,572
这是一个很好的考题，也是区分两个看似合理的选项的关键点。
That is a fair exam question and exactly the kind of distinction that separates two plausible options.

3600
05:52:02,446 --> 05:52:09,060
最后一行是场景 4 涉及的内容，而且它是这里唯一关于金钱而非时间的一行。
The last row is the one scenario 4 turns on, and it is the only row here about money rather than time.

3601
05:52:10,606 --> 05:52:17,392
这个标注是场景4提到的重点，因为它不符合直觉，所以值得单独说明。
The callout is the point scenario 4 turned on, and it is worth stating separately because it is counterintuitive.

3602
05:52:17,632 --> 05:52:26,500
在托管存储中，节点数量和存储数据量是分开计费的。这就是计算与存储分离带来的全部好处。
On managed storage, the number of nodes and the amount of data stored are priced independently. That is the whole benefit of separating compute and storage.

3603
05:52:27,342 --> 05:52:32,644
这意味着成本问题需要你识别出这两个维度中哪一个才是真正庞大的部分。
It means a cost question needs you to identify which of the two is actually large.

3604
05:52:33,294 --> 05:52:40,900
如果集群的资源过剩，导致查询负载不足，这就是计算问题，可以通过调整规模或使用预留容量来解决。
A cluster that is overprovisioned for its query load is a compute problem, answered by resizing or by reserved capacity.

3605
05:52:41,838 --> 05:52:48,036
如果集群中存储了多年的冷数据历史，这就是存储问题，可以通过将这些历史数据迁移到S3来解决。
A cluster holding years of cold history is a storage problem, answered by moving that history to S3.

3606
05:52:49,518 --> 05:52:57,796
共有五个问题，第一个是整个模块中价值最高的，因为它能立即排除掉一大类题目中的一半选项。
Five questions, and the first is the highest value in the whole module because it eliminates half the options immediately on a large family of questions.

3607
05:52:58,382 --> 05:53:04,420
Q8和执行时间这两个问题的答案完全不同，但用户都会把它们描述为“查询缓慢”。
Q8 and execution time have entirely different answers and both are described as slow queries by users.

3608
05:53:05,326 --> 05:53:11,876
第三个是需要内化的表设计核心点，因为它将两个关键选择对应到查询的两种操作上。
The third is the one to internalize for table design because it maps the two key choices onto the two things a query does.

3609
05:53:12,910 --> 05:53:15,812
如果字段在连接中，就看分布情况。
If the pane is in the join, look at distribution.

3610
05:53:16,206 --> 05:53:19,268
如果字段在过滤中，就看排序键。
If the pane is in the filter, look at the sort key.

3611
05:53:20,526 --> 05:53:24,612
下一个模块将跳出数据仓库，进入其他的存储系统。
Next module moves outside the warehouse to the rest of the data stores.

3612
05:53:25,454 --> 05:53:31,812
这包括在最新修订版考试指南中加入的向量索引类型。
That includes the vector index types added to the exam guide in the latest revision.

3613
05:53:33,358 --> 05:53:36,836
第10个模块深入探讨了一个特定的存储系统。
Module 10 covered one store in enormous depth.

3614
05:53:37,806 --> 05:53:44,260
本模块涵盖了8种系统，且深度符合考试要求，其实远比你担心的要少。
This module covers 8 of them in the depth the exam actually requires, which is far less than you might fear.

3615
05:53:44,750 --> 05:53:48,544
考试不会考你如何操作DynamoDB或调优Aurora。
You are not being examined on operating Dynamo DB or tuning Aurora.

3616
05:53:49,422 --> 05:54:02,052
考查的是从四个选项中选出正确的那一个，这是一种不同且更容易掌握的技能。这就是为什么本模块包含8个实战案例而不是4个。
You are being examined on picking the right one from a list of four, which is a different and much more learnable skill. That is why this module carries 8 worked scenarios rather than 4.

3617
05:54:02,798 --> 05:54:10,756
它还涵盖了2025年12月进入考试指南的向量存储和向量索引类型
It also covers vector storage and vector index types that entered the exam guide in December 2025

3618
05:54:11,024 --> 05:54:13,764
这些内容在旧教材中完全没有出现过。
and appear in no older material at all.

3619
05:54:15,342 --> 05:54:24,036
第1模块中的规则是：数据量几乎从不决定选择哪种存储系统，因为这里的每个服务都能处理海量数据。
The rule from module 1 was that volume almost never decides a data store because every service here handles large volumes.

3620
05:54:24,224 --> 05:54:26,628
真正决定选择的是数据的读取方式。
What decides it is how the data is read.

3621
05:54:27,374 --> 05:54:31,876
是按键查询单条记录，还是聚合数百万行数据。
One item at a time by a key or millions of rows aggregated.

3622
05:54:33,070 --> 05:54:35,876
是针对固定已知查询，还是进行自由文本搜索。
Fixed known queries or free text search.

3623
05:54:39,438 --> 05:54:41,156
这个规则能帮你通过第1模块。
That rule got you through module 1.

3624
05:54:41,806 --> 05:54:49,508
但对于同时提供DynamoDB、Aurora、DocumentDB和Key Spaces的题目来说，这个规则太粗糙了，因为它们都能按键存储数据。
It is too coarse for a question offering DynamoDB, Aurora, Document DB, and Key Spaces, all of which store items by key.

3625
05:54:50,350 --> 05:54:56,004
本模块将这一逻辑细化，而这种细化主要取决于了解每个服务最初是为什么目的构建的。
This module sharpens it and the sharpening is mostly a matter of knowing what each service was originally built for.

3626
05:54:57,664 --> 05:55:03,108
这个标注是一个捷径，能一步到位解决大量问题。
The callout is the shortcut that resolves a surprising number of questions in a single step.

3627
05:55:03,664 --> 05:55:10,724
DocumentDB之所以存在，是因为企业在运行MongoDB。Key Spaces存在是因为他们在运行Cassandra。
DocumentDB exists because organizations run MongoDB. Key Spaces exist because they run Cassandra.

3628
05:55:11,504 --> 05:55:14,464
MemoryDB存在是因为他们正在运行Redis。
MemoryDB exists because they run Redis.

3629
05:55:15,470 --> 05:55:21,504
Aurora部分原因是他们运行PostgreSQL和MySQL，并希望提高性能。
Aurora exists partly because they run PostgreSQL and MySQL and want them faster.

3630
05:55:21,744 --> 05:55:28,900
所以当题目提到现有应用使用这些技术之一时，答案就是对应的兼容服务。
So when a question mentions an existing application using one of those technologies, the answer is the compatible service.

3631
05:55:29,902 --> 05:55:34,624
这和在第三模块中，现有的 Kafka 代表 Amazon MSK 是同一个原因。
It is the same reason existing Kafka meant Amazon MSK in module 3.

3632
05:55:35,086 --> 05:55:38,532
将一个运行中的应用程序重写到不同的
Rewriting a working application onto a different

3633
05:55:39,598 --> 05:55:42,660
API 会产生不必要的迁移成本。
API is the unnecessary migration cost.

3634
05:55:42,958 --> 05:55:45,060
考试中，这种选项始终是错误的。
The exam consistently marks wrong.

3635
05:55:45,424 --> 05:55:49,316
在对比任何技术细节之前，确认这一点是值得的。
It is worth checking for before you compare anything technical.

3636
05:55:50,958 --> 05:55:56,228
基于时间的索引模式是值得掌握的，因为它解决了保留问题。
The time-based index pattern is the one worth knowing because it solves retention.

3637
05:55:56,750 --> 05:55:59,300
这是分区在数据湖中解决该问题的方式。
The way partitioning solves it in a data lake.

3638
05:56:00,494 --> 05:56:03,780
日志会进入按天或按月命名的索引中。
Logs go into an index name for the day or the month.

3639
05:56:04,430 --> 05:56:10,372
因此，删除 90 天前的旧数据意味着删除整个索引，这几乎是瞬间完成的。
So removing 90-day old data means deleting one whole index, which is close to instantaneous.

3640
05:56:11,278 --> 05:56:21,348
而匹配日期范围来删除单个文档则很慢、成本高，且空间只能等到后台合并时才能回收。
Deleting individual documents, matching a date range instead is slow, expensive, and leaves the space to be reclaimed later by a background merge.

3641
05:56:21,998 --> 05:56:30,384
索引状态管理可以自动化整个生命周期，将旧索引移动到更便宜的存储层，并最终
Index state management automates the entire lifecycle, moving older indices to cheaper storage tiers and eventually

3642
05:56:30,704 --> 05:56:33,028
按照你定义的计划将其删除。
deleting them on a schedule you define.

3643
05:56:33,504 --> 05:56:40,484
这就是 OpenSearch 中对应模块 8 的 S3 生命周期规则，题目也会把它们视为同类情况。
That is the open search equivalent of the S3 lifecycle rule from module 8, and questions treat them the same way.

3644
05:56:42,094 --> 05:56:46,596
第四题是最重要的，有一点必须明确说明。
The fourth question is the most important and it is worth stating starkly.

3645
05:56:47,104 --> 05:56:52,452
本模块中的每一个存储系统都是为了让应用程序快速检索特定记录而构建的。
Every store in this module is built to retrieve specific records quickly for an application.

3646
05:56:52,784 --> 05:56:58,596
Redshift 和 Athena 是为了分析时扫描并聚合海量数量的记录而构建的。
Redshift and Athena are built to scan and aggregate enormous numbers of records for analysis.

3647
05:56:59,214 --> 05:57:02,980
它们不是计算选项，它们处于流水线的不同位置。
They are not computing options, they sit at different points in a pipeline.

3648
05:57:03,598 --> 05:57:10,660
任何描述汇总三年销售数据的仪表板问题都不是 DynamoDB 的考题，无论涉及多少数据量。
A question describing a dashboard aggregating three years of sales is not a DynamoDB question, no matter how much data is involved.

3649
05:57:11,566 --> 05:57:18,980
模块 12 的工作场景故意犯了同样的错误，即从 Athena 中进行按用户查询。
Module 12nd Works Scenario made exactly this mistake deliberately, serving per user lookups from Athena.

3650
05:57:19,566 --> 05:57:22,084
这是相反方向上的同样错误。
This is the same error in the opposite direction.

3651
05:57:23,790 --> 05:57:31,140
关系型数据库允许你在高度规范的模式下执行任何你想要的查询，并自动计算如何回答它。
A relational database lets you write any query you like against a well-normalized schema and works out how to answer it.

3652
05:57:31,854 --> 05:57:33,284
DynamoDB 不行。
DynamoDB does not.

3653
05:57:33,902 --> 05:57:41,380
你需要围绕打算运行的查询来设计表，而那些你没设计的查询要么无法执行，要么成本高昂。
You design the table around the queries you intend to run, and queries you did not design for are either impossible or expensive.

3654
05:57:42,254 --> 05:57:48,996
作为交换，你在无需容量规划的情况下，能获得在基本无限规模下的毫秒级响应。
In exchange, you get single-digit millisecond responses at essentially unlimited scale with no capacity planning.

3655
05:57:49,264 --> 05:57:53,504
这种权衡就是该服务的核心特性，也是题目考查的内容。
That trade is the entire character of the service and it is what questions test.

3656
05:57:54,094 --> 05:58:00,516
当场景描述已知且重复的访问模式以及对低延迟的要求时，DynamoDB 是合适的选择。
When a scenario describes known, repeated access patterns and demanding latency, DynamoDB fits.

3657
05:58:01,454 --> 05:58:07,364
当描述分析师以意想不到的方式探索数据时，它就不合适了。
When it describes analysts exploring data in ways nobody anticipated, it does not.

3658
05:58:08,814 --> 05:58:14,244
查询和扫描之间的区别是 Dynamo DB 中最常被考查的内容。
The distinction between query and scan is the most reliably examined thing about Dynamo DB.

3659
05:58:14,624 --> 05:58:21,220
查询直接进入一个分区并读取所需的项，这就是它又快又便宜的原因。
A query goes straight to one partition and reads the items it needs, which is why it is fast and cheap.

3660
05:58:21,774 --> 05:58:26,084
而扫描会读取表中的每一个项，然后再丢弃不匹配的那些。
A scan reads every item in the table and then discards the ones that do not match.

3661
05:58:26,926 --> 05:58:30,660
所以你为了获取几行数据，却要为整个表付费。
So you pay for the whole table to retrieve a handful of rows.

3662
05:58:31,790 --> 05:58:33,956
这个特别提醒是考试中的考点。
The callout is the exam consequence.

3663
05:58:34,446 --> 05:58:38,084
当某个选项涉及“扫描”时，通常就是为了让你排除掉它。
When an option involves scanning, it is usually there to be rejected.

3664
05:58:38,510 --> 05:58:43,108
更好的答案是使用索引，让访问模式变成“查询”。
The better answer is an index that makes the access pattern a query instead.

3665
05:58:44,784 --> 05:58:50,468
第三个要点是一个真实的约束条件而非调优选择，它决定了问题的走向。
The third bullet is a genuine constraint rather than a tuning choice and it decides questions.

3666
05:58:50,784 --> 05:58:55,460
全局二级索引是在基础表写入后异步维护的。
A global secondary index is maintained asynchronously after the base table is written.

3667
05:58:56,206 --> 05:58:59,748
因此会有一个短暂的窗口期，此时它可能不反映最新的数据。
So there is a brief window where it does not reflect the newest item.

3668
05:59:00,398 --> 05:59:06,852
这对于排行榜来说没问题，但对于检查用户名是否已被占用这类操作来说是不可接受的。
That is fine for a leaderboard and unacceptable for say checking whether a username is already taken.

3669
05:59:07,406 --> 05:59:16,132
所以当场景要求读取必须反映最近写入的内容时，任何通过全局二级索引进行的选项都是错误的。
So when a scenario states that a read must reflect the most recent write, any option routing it through a global secondary index is wrong.

3670
05:59:17,134 --> 05:59:25,540
“特定点恢复”值得记住这个术语，因为它是 Dynamo DB 中对应模块 10 所讲的快照恢复功能。
Point in time, recovery is worth knowing by name because it is the Dynamo DB equivalent of the snapshot restore module 10 covered.

3671
05:59:27,054 --> 05:59:33,344
两者都允许你对非主键的字段进行查询，而提示中的约束条件通常是决定因素。
Both let you query on something other than the primary key and the constraint in the call out is what usually decides.

3672
05:59:33,664 --> 05:59:39,588
本地二级索引必须在创建表时定义，之后永远无法添加。
A local secondary index must be defined when the table is created and can never be added afterwards.

3673
05:59:40,430 --> 05:59:47,172
因此，任何描述现有表并引入新访问模式的场景，通过排除法都是全局二级索引问题。
So any scenario describing an existing table with a new access pattern is a global secondary index question by elimination.

3674
05:59:47,566 --> 05:59:55,824
全局索引也更灵活，允许使用完全不同的分区键，而当新查询需要以不同方式对项目进行分组时，你就需要这个。
Global indexes are also more flexible, allowing a completely different partition key, which is what you need when the new query groups items differently.

3675
05:59:56,366 --> 06:00:02,404
代价是最终一致性和独立的容量，这有时也是考题的切入点。
The cost is eventual consistency and separate capacity, which is occasionally the point of a question.

3676
06:00:04,110 --> 06:00:10,276
第三个要点应该让你感到熟悉，因为模块 3 在 Kinesis 数据流中详细描述了这一点。
The third bullet should feel familiar because module 3 described exactly this in Kinesis data streams.

3677
06:00:10,926 --> 06:00:17,700
当整体利用率看起来较低时仍发生限流，是因为流量集中在某一个键上，而不是分布在所有键上。
Throttling occurs while overall utilization looks low because traffic concentrates on one key rather than spreading across all of them.

3678
06:00:18,542 --> 06:00:27,744
自适应容量通过将吞吐量转向繁忙的分区来缓解这一问题，这确实有帮助，但无法解决根本性的倾斜
Adaptive capacity mitigates it by shifting throughput towards the busy partition, which genuinely helps and does not solve a fundamentally skewed

3679
06:00:27,904 --> 06:00:28,260
设计。
design.

3680
06:00:28,782 --> 06:00:31,780
真正的答案与 Kinesis 的情况相同。
The real answer is the same one as for kinesis.

3681
06:00:32,544 --> 06:00:35,236
更改键，让流量分布开来。
Change the key so traffic distributes.

3682
06:00:36,110 --> 06:00:41,668
在上面的容量模式选择中，信号词与本课程中的其他地方一致。
On the capacity mode choice above it, the signal words are the same as everywhere in this course.

3683
06:00:42,478 --> 06:00:46,436
“不可预测”、“突发”和“多变”指向按需模式。
Unpredictable, spiky, and variable point at on demand.

3684
06:00:47,982 --> 06:00:51,236
带有明确吞吐量数值的题目，指向预制型。
Study with a stated throughput figure, points at provisioned.

3685
06:00:52,910 --> 06:00:59,780
一家游戏公司在 Amazon DynamoDB 中存储玩家资料，并将玩家 ID 作为分区键。
A gaming company stores player profiles in Amazon DynamoDB with player ID as the partition key.

3686
06:01:00,206 --> 06:01:08,996
一个新功能必须显示每个区域前 100 名玩家的排行榜，要求实时更新，并且被所有打开应用的玩家读取。
A new feature must show a leaderboard of the top 100 players per region refreshed constantly and read by every player who opens the app.

3687
06:01:09,614 --> 06:01:14,660
目前的实现是扫描整个表并在应用程序中对结果进行排序。
The current implementation scans the whole table and sorts the results in the application.

3688
06:01:15,184 --> 06:01:20,868
该表包含 4000 万名玩家，且读取成本已成为账单中最大的一项。
The table holds 40 million players and read costs have become the largest line on the bill.

3689
06:01:21,966 --> 06:01:24,324
数据工程师应该如何实现？
What should the data engineer implement?

3690
06:01:26,318 --> 06:01:31,104
增加表的预制读取容量，以便扫描能更快完成。
Increase the table's provision read capacity so the scan completes faster.

3691
06:01:31,424 --> 06:01:31,664
b.
b.

3692
06:01:32,224 --> 06:01:40,544
B. 添加一个按区域分区并按分数排序的全局二级索引。C. 添加一个按分数排序的本地二级索引。
Add a global secondary index partitioned by region and sorted by score. C. Add a local secondary index sorted by score.

3693
06:01:40,942 --> 06:01:43,664
D. 将表导出到 Amazon S3。
D. Export the table to Amazon S3.

3694
06:01:44,206 --> 06:01:47,140
每晚执行一次，并使用 Amazon Athena 查询排行榜。
Nightly and query the leaderboard with Amazon Athena.

3695
06:01:47,822 --> 06:01:48,964
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3696
06:01:55,342 --> 06:02:00,644
答案是 B，而选项 C 有两个明显的错误，这一点值得注意。
The answer is B, and option C fails twice over, which is worth noticing.

3697
06:02:01,966 --> 06:02:05,028
本地二级索引保留表的分区键。
A local secondary index keeps the table's partition key.

3698
06:02:06,798 --> 06:02:12,272
因此项目仍将按玩家分组而非按区域分组，查询无法得到结果。
So items would still be grouped by player rather than by region, and the query could not be answered.

3699
06:02:12,814 --> 06:02:17,072
另外，现有表中无法添加本地索引。
Separately, a local index cannot be added to a table that already exists.

3700
06:02:17,390 --> 06:02:19,428
这两个原因中的任何一个都能排除该选项。
Either of those alone eliminates it.

3701
06:02:21,006 --> 06:02:24,228
选项 D 是针对运营问题的分析类答案。
Option D is the analytical answer to an operational question.

3702
06:02:24,512 --> 06:02:30,752
这就是“四个问题幻灯片”警告过的错误，而不断更新的阶段信息排除了它。
That is the error the four question slide warned about and the phase refreshed constantly is what rules it out.

3703
06:02:32,110 --> 06:02:36,996
Aurora 在 2025 年 12 月的修订版中被加入到入选服务列表中。
Aurora was added to the InScope service list in the December 2025 revision.

3704
06:02:38,094 --> 06:02:41,828
因此，预计它出现的频率会比旧材料显示的更高。
So expect it to appear more often than older material suggests.

3705
06:02:42,798 --> 06:02:45,028
这个区别本身很简单。
The distinction itself is straightforward.

3706
06:02:45,806 --> 06:02:49,668
Aurora 仅兼容 MySQL 和 PostgreSQL。
Aurora is compatible with MySQL and PostgreSQL only.

3707
06:02:50,574 --> 06:02:58,596
在这两者中，它提供跨越 3 个可用区的存储层、更快的复制速度以及多达 15 个只读副本。
Within those two, it offers the storage layer spanning 3, availability zones, considerably faster replication, and up to 15 read replicas.

3708
06:02:59,152 --> 06:03:05,924
因此，涉及 Oracle、SQL Server、MariaDB 或 DB2 的问题将完全排除 Aurora。
So a question involving Oracle, SQL Server, MariaDB or DB2 rules Aurora out entirely.

3709
06:03:07,726 --> 06:03:10,724
那么通过排除法，Amazon RDS 就是正确答案。
Amazon RDS is then the answer by elimination.

3710
06:03:11,598 --> 06:03:19,472
如果涉及 MySQL 或 PostgreSQL 并提到高可用性、读取扩展或增长，那么考题就在指向 Aurora
If it involves MySQL or PostgreSQL and mentions high availability, read scaling or growth, the team is worried about Aurora

3711
06:03:19,632 --> 06:03:20,612
相关内容。
is being pointed at.

3712
06:03:22,190 --> 06:03:28,484
大多数 Aurora 功能超出了数据工程师的范畴，而这里的三个项目正属于其核心范围。
Most Aurora capability sits outside a data engineer scope and three items here are squarely inside it.

3713
06:03:28,814 --> 06:03:36,676
Redshift 是模块 10 花费时间研究的一个模块。这也是 Aurora 出现在分析类问题中的主要原因。
0ETL2 Redshift is the one module 10 spent time on. It is the main reason Aurora appears in Analytics questions at on.

3714
06:03:37,518 --> 06:03:44,420
对于明确要求多区域的题目，全局数据库很重要，其中需要记住的关键数据是亚秒级的复制延迟。
Global database matters for questions stating a multi-region requirement, where sub-second replication lag is the figure to remember.

3715
06:03:44,832 --> 06:03:50,916
而 PG vector 是让 Aurora 成为向量数据库的关键，本模块最后一部分详细介绍了这一点。
And PG vector is what makes Aurora a vector store, which the last section of this module covers in detail.

3716
06:03:51,950 --> 06:03:56,100
最后一项的更名非常近，因此两个名称目前都在流通。
The renaming on the final bullet is recent enough that both names circulate freely.

3717
06:03:56,590 --> 06:04:03,684
因此，请将 Aurora Serverless version 2 和 Aurora Serverless 视为同一个产品，只是名字优化了一下。
So recognize Aurora Serverless version 2 and Aurora Serverless as the same product with a tidied up name.

3718
06:04:04,974 --> 06:04:10,788
关于内存数据库的要点值得注意，因为考生往往会出于习惯去选择 ElastiCache。
The memory DB point deserves attention because candidates reach for Elastic Cache by habit.

3719
06:04:11,246 --> 06:04:15,632
缓存存储的是同时也存在于权威源中的数据副本。
A cache holds a copy of data that also lives somewhere authoritative.

3720
06:04:15,712 --> 06:04:18,980
因此，丢失缓存只会影响性能，而不会导致数据丢失。
So losing it costs performance rather than data.

3721
06:04:19,886 --> 06:04:26,052
MemoryDB 是内存型且持久化的，并且在不同可用区之间有事务日志支持。
MemoryDB is in memory and durable with a transaction log across availability zones.

3722
06:04:26,432 --> 06:04:31,172
因此，它可以作为需要微秒级访问的数据主要存储。
So it can be the primary store for data that needs microsecond access.

3723
06:04:32,302 --> 06:04:38,372
注意，MemoryDB 出现在本次考试的“在考范围”服务列表中，而 ElastiCache 没有。
Note also that memory DB appears on this exam's InScope service list and ElastiCache does not.

3724
06:04:39,278 --> 06:04:43,204
这告诉你 AWS 希望你在这种情况下选择哪一个。
That tells you which one AWS expects you to reach for here.

3725
06:04:43,872 --> 06:04:51,716
Neptune 的价值在于它传达了一个信号：即问题是关于事物之间的关系，而不是事物的属性。
Neptune is worth recognizing for one signal, which is a question about relationships between things rather than attributes of things.

3726
06:04:53,006 --> 06:04:58,660
OpenSearch 回答两种截然不同的问题类型，值得我们有意识地将它们区分开来。
Open search answers two quite different question shapes and it is worth separating them deliberately.

3727
06:04:59,072 --> 06:05:09,252
第一种是真正的搜索，即用户输入单词并期望获得相关结果，排序依据是匹配程度，包括部分匹配和同义词。
The first is genuine search, where a user types words and expects relevant results langed by how well they match, including partial matches and synonyms.

3728
06:05:09,712 --> 06:05:12,164
本模块中的其他任何服务都不具备这种功能。
No other service in this module does that.

3729
06:05:13,070 --> 06:05:21,316
第二种是日志分析，即对操作日志进行索引并进行交互式探索，第 14 模块会妥善处理这一部分。
The second is log analytics, where operational logs are indexed and explored interactively and module 14 returns to it properly.

3730
06:05:22,062 --> 06:05:28,292
最后一项是较新内容，也是 OpenSearch 越来越多出现在数据工程问题中的原因。
The last bullet is newer and increasingly the reason OpenSearch shows up in data engineering questions at all.

3731
06:05:29,166 --> 06:05:37,796
这是因为支持向量搜索，使其成为检索增强生成（RAG）的常规生产选择，本模块的向量部分将涵盖这一内容。
That is because Xboutem Vector Search makes it the usual production choice for retrieval augmented generation, which the vector section of this module covers.

3732
06:05:39,406 --> 06:05:45,604
一家零售商在 Amazon EC2 上运行的自管理 MongoDB 集群中维护产品目录。
A retailer runs a product catalog on a self-managed MongoDB cluster on Amazon EC2.

3733
06:05:46,112 --> 06:05:50,404
大约有 60 个微服务使用 MongoDB 驱动程序来查询它。
Around 60 microservices query it using MongoDB drivers.

3734
06:05:51,086 --> 06:05:57,316
运维团队花费大量时间去打补丁和管理副本集，并希望减少这些工作量。
The operations team spends significant time patching and managing replica sets and wants to reduce that work.

3735
06:05:58,272 --> 06:06:06,372
目前有一个提议：由于 Amazon DynamoDB 是全托管的且扫描性能更好，建议将目录迁移到 DynamoDB。
A proposal on the table is to migrate the catalog to Amazon DynamoDB on the grounds that it is fully managed and scans better.

3736
06:06:07,662 --> 06:06:09,636
数据工程师应该如何回应？
How should the data engineer respond?

3737
06:06:10,478 --> 06:06:11,392
A. 同意。
A. Agree.

3738
06:06:11,982 --> 06:06:15,588
DynamoDB 是全托管的，消除了运维工作。
DynamoDB is fully managed and eliminated the operational work.

3739
06:06:18,158 --> 06:06:24,644
建议使用 Amazon DocumentDB，它兼容 MongoDB，且不会改变这 60 个服务。
Recommend Amazon DocumentDB, which is MongoDB compatible and leaves the 60 services unchanged.

3740
06:06:25,262 --> 06:06:25,552
C。
C.

3741
06:06:26,112 --> 06:06:32,036
建议使用支持 JSONB 列的 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 来存储文档。
Recommend Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL using JSONB columns for the documents.

3742
06:06:32,432 --> 06:06:32,752
D。
D.

3743
06:06:33,152 --> 06:06:37,380
建议使用能够处理大规模文档负载的 Amazon Keyspaces。
Recommend Amazon Key Spaces which handles document workloads at scale.

3744
06:06:37,792 --> 06:06:39,108
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3745
06:06:45,838 --> 06:06:51,812
答案是 B，这是直接应用了单行表中的兼容性规则。
The answer is B, and this is the compatibility rule from the one-line table applied directly.

3746
06:06:54,670 --> 06:07:00,452
“60 个应用程序”这一项涉及特定 KPI，是一个约束条件，而不是细节。
60 applications, speaking a particular KPI is a constraint, not a detail.

3747
06:07:02,414 --> 06:07:09,472
选项 A 和 C 虽然能满足运维要求，但会产生一个巨大的迁移项目。
Options A and C both satisfy the operational requirement by creating an enormous migration project.

3748
06:07:10,030 --> 06:07:16,036
这与模块 3 的逻辑一致：现有的 Kafka 意味着选择 Amazon MSK 而不是 Kinesis。
This is the same shape as module 3, where existing Kafka meant Amazon MSK rather than Kinesis.

3749
06:07:17,646 --> 06:07:22,116
还有模块 4，供应商使用 SFTP 意味着选择传输系列。
Module 4, where suppliers using SFTP meant transfer family.

3750
06:07:22,912 --> 06:07:29,060
每当问题计算依赖于某种接口的应用程序数量时，它都在告诉你该接口不能更改。
Whenever a question counts the applications depending on an interface, it is telling you the interface cannot change.

3751
06:07:30,702 --> 06:07:38,948
考试指南将为 Redshift、Dynamo DB 和 Lake Formation 设计模式列为一项单一技能。
The exam guide names designing schemas for Redshift, Dynamo DB, and Lake Formation as a single skill.

3752
06:07:40,014 --> 06:07:44,036
在你看出其中的逻辑之前，这个分组可能有点奇怪。
That is a slightly odd grouping until you see the point behind it.

3753
06:07:44,782 --> 06:07:53,060
它们都是针对“如何组织数据”这一问题的不同答案，而这种安排完全取决于谁来读取这些数据。
Each is a different answer to the same question of how to arrange data, and the arrangement follows entirely from what will read it.

3754
06:07:53,966 --> 06:08:02,436
操作型存储旨在优化单个记录的写入和更新且不产生不一致，因此每个事实都存放在一个地方。
An operational store is optimized for writing and updating individual records without inconsistency, so each fact lives in one place.

3755
06:08:03,054 --> 06:08:08,036
分析型存储则优化了对海量记录的读取和聚合。
An analytical store is optimized for reading enormous numbers of records and aggregating them.

3756
06:08:08,352 --> 06:08:11,588
所以为了避免连接而重复某些值是一种合理的权衡。
So repeating a value to avoid a join is a good trade.

3757
06:08:12,494 --> 06:08:20,512
这两个目标确实是冲突的，这就是为什么在大多数组织中，相同的数据最终会被建模两次，也是为什么零
Those goals genuinely conflict, which is why the same data ends up modeled twice in most organizations and why zero

3758
06:08:20,672 --> 06:08:22,052
ETL 存在的原因。
ETL exists.

3759
06:08:23,758 --> 06:08:29,060
星型模型值得记住这个名字，因为 Redshift 的题目通常默认使用它。
The star schema is worth knowing by name because redshift questions assume it.

3760
06:08:29,632 --> 06:08:34,180
中心事实表包含度量值，每个事务对应一行。
A center fact table holds the measurements, one row per transaction.

3761
06:08:34,832 --> 06:08:41,188
围绕它的维度表持有描述性属性，每个客户、产品或门店对应一行。
Dimension tables around it hold the descriptive attributes, one row per customer or product or store.

3762
06:08:42,126 --> 06:08:45,796
正是这种结构，才让第 10 模块的第一个场景能够按预期运行。
That shape is why module 10's first scenario worked as it did.

3763
06:08:46,192 --> 06:08:50,596
事实表很大，并且在连接列上获得分布键。
The fact table is large and gets a distribution key on the join column.

3764
06:08:51,022 --> 06:08:54,628
维度表较小，并采用全分布。
The dimension tables are small and get ALL distribution.

3765
06:08:55,374 --> 06:09:03,712
雪花模型进一步规范化这些维度，这可以节省一点空间但会增加连接，而考试通常更倾向于星型模型。
A Snowflake schema normalizes those dimensions further, which saves a little space and adds joins, and the exam generally prefers the star.

3766
06:09:05,198 --> 06:09:11,204
单表设计是最让人们感到意外的理念，但一旦说明了原因，逻辑就很简单。
Single table design is the idea that surprises people most, and the reasoning is straightforward once stated.

3767
06:09:11,566 --> 06:09:18,672
DynamoDB 不支持连接，因此从两个表中检索订单及其明细意味着需要两次请求。
DynamoDB has no joins, so retrieving an order and its line items from two tables means two requests.

3768
06:09:19,182 --> 06:09:26,832
如果相反，如果订单和它的明细共享同一个分区键，那么一次查询就能在单次往返中返回所有内容。
If instead the order and its line items share a partition key, one query returns all of them together in a single round trip.

3769
06:09:27,072 --> 06:09:32,708
这就是为什么经验丰富的 Dynamo DB 表看起来往往很奇怪，因为它同时包含多种实体类型。
That is why an experienced Dynamo DB table often looks strange, holding several entity types at once.

3770
06:09:32,912 --> 06:09:36,228
考试不会要求你从头开始设计一个。
The exam does not ask you to design one from scratch.

3771
06:09:36,750 --> 06:09:42,980
它确实期望你能识别出，按照关系型数据库的方式将实体拆分到不同表中在这里是一个错误。
It does expect you to recognize that splitting entities into separate tables the relational way is a mistake here.

3772
06:09:44,494 --> 06:09:53,828
一家物流公司需要回答诸如哪些司机送货到了哪些仓库，以及两批货物如何连接到共享处理设施等问题。
A logistics company needs to answer questions like which drivers have delivered to which depots and how two shipments are connected to shared handling facilities.

3773
06:09:54,478 --> 06:09:58,756
这些关系有好几层深，而且深度因问题而异。
The relationships are several layers deep and the depth varies by question.

3774
06:09:59,758 --> 06:10:07,684
数据目前存储在用于 PostgreSQL 的 Amazon RDS 中，而这些查询需要递归连接，耗时数分钟才能返回。
The data currently sits in Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL and these queries require recursive joins that take minutes to return.

3775
06:10:08,192 --> 06:10:10,564
哪种存储最符合这种访问模式？
Which store best fits this access pattern?

3776
06:10:11,232 --> 06:10:15,172
A 用 Amazon Neptune 将关系作为图形进行查询。
a Amazon Neptune querying the relationships as a graph.

3777
06:10:15,726 --> 06:10:20,612
B 使用带全局二级索引的 Amazon Dynamo DB，针对每种关系类型。
B Amazon Dynamo DB with a global secondary index per relationship type.

3778
06:10:21,102 --> 06:10:25,444
C 加载表并使用窗口函数的 Amazon Redshift。
C Amazon Redshift loading the tables and using window functions.

3779
06:10:26,094 --> 06:10:30,532
D 将关系作为文档进行索引的 Amazon OpenSearch Service。
D Amazon Open Search Service indexing the relationships as documents.

3780
06:10:31,310 --> 06:10:32,388
停下来思考一下，然后做决定。
Pause and decide

3781
06:10:39,086 --> 06:10:44,784
答案是 A，决定性的短语是“深度随问题而变化”。
The answer is A, and the phrase that decides it is that the depth varies by question.

3782
06:10:45,166 --> 06:10:49,184
SQL 中的连接（join）是为固定数量的跳数编写的。
A join in SQL is written for a fixed number of hops.

3783
06:10:49,806 --> 06:10:59,812
因此，通过未知数量中间设施连接两个货运信息的查询无法清晰表达，并会变成性能较差的递归查询。
So a query connecting two shipments through an unknown number of intermediate facilities cannot be expressed cleanly and becomes a recursive query that performs badly.

3784
06:11:00,464 --> 06:11:07,620
图数据库将遍历边作为其原生操作，所以深度是一个参数，而不是结构性问题。
Graph databases traverse edges as their native operation, so depth is a parameter rather than a structural problem.

3785
06:11:08,558 --> 06:11:15,460
Neptune 在这次考试中很少出现，但一旦出现，信号几乎总是这个。
Neptune appears rarely on this exam, and when it does, the signal is almost always this one.

3786
06:11:16,142 --> 06:11:20,004
查询的对象是关系，而不是属性。
Relationships are the thing being queried rather than attributes.

3787
06:11:21,518 --> 06:11:27,466
考试指南将 Redshift、DynamoDB 和 Lake Formation 的模式设计归为一项技能。
The exam guide groups Redshift, DynamoDB, and Lake Formation schema design into one skill.

3788
06:11:28,142 --> 06:11:33,124
Lake Formation 让人们觉得奇怪，因为它是一个权限服务，而不是存储。
Lake Formation is the one people find odd because it is a permission service rather than a store.

3789
06:11:33,904 --> 06:11:38,020
其中的联系是：表的形状决定了可以被治理的内容。
The connection is that the shape of a table decides what can be governed.

3790
06:11:38,894 --> 06:11:45,796
模块 2 的第 6 个场景正好涉及这一点，即列级权限需要通过目录进行读取。
Module 2's 6th scenario turned on exactly this, where column level permissions required reading through the catalog.

3791
06:11:46,224 --> 06:11:52,132
如果敏感列分散在宽表中，每个消费者都需要一个列级策略。
If sensitive columns are scattered through a wide table, every consumer needs a column level policy.

3792
06:11:52,814 --> 06:12:00,772
如果它们被分组或保存在单独的表中，并在需要时进行连接，那么访问规则就会简单到可以推导出来。
If they are grouped or held in a separate table, joined when needed, the access rules become simple enough to reason about.

3793
06:12:02,286 --> 06:12:06,340
最新修订版中加入了两项技能。
Two skills entered the exam guide in the latest revision.

3794
06:12:06,784 --> 06:12:07,984
第一项是
One names

3795
06:12:08,718 --> 06:12:13,284
包括 HNSW 和 IVF 在内的向量索引类型。
vector index types including HNSW and IVF.

3796
06:12:13,966 --> 06:12:19,108
另一项是向量化概念和 Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases。
The other names vectorization concepts and Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases.

3797
06:12:19,854 --> 06:12:25,060
旧的题库都不包含这两者，所以这个部分完全是新内容。
No older question bank covers either, so this section is entirely new material.

3798
06:12:25,966 --> 06:12:29,124
这些概念比词汇量更不容易让人望而却步。
The concept is less intimidating than the vocabulary.

3799
06:12:29,870 --> 06:12:37,732
嵌入将一段文本或图像转换为一系列数字，使得相似的事物在位置上靠近彼此。
An embedding turns a piece of text or an image into a list of numbers positioned so that similar things sit near each other.

3800
06:12:38,702 --> 06:12:45,892
寻找相似内容就变成了寻找附近的点，这是一个几何问题，而不是文本匹配问题。
Finding similar content then becomes finding nearby points, which is a geometry problem rather than a text matching problem.

3801
06:12:47,584 --> 06:12:55,684
这个特别提醒是看清向量搜索究竟能带来什么的最清晰方式。那两个短语没有任何显著的共同词汇。
The callout is the clearest way to see what vector search actually buys you. Those two phrases share no significant words at all.

3802
06:12:55,904 --> 06:12:57,860
所以关键词搜索找不到任何东西。
So keyword search finds nothing.

3803
06:12:58,144 --> 06:13:01,796
然而，对于人类读者来说，它们显然意思相同。
And yet they obviously mean the same thing to a human reader.

3804
06:13:02,638 --> 06:13:08,868
嵌入将它们放在一起，是因为生成它们的模型已经从语言中学习到了这种关系。
Embeddings place them close together because the model that produced them has learned that relationship from language.

3805
06:13:09,184 --> 06:13:12,964
最后两点是诚实的权衡，而且对考试很重要。
The last two bullets are the honest balance and they matter for the exam.

3806
06:13:13,902 --> 06:13:21,904
向量搜索在关键词搜索擅长的领域表现较弱，比如精确的标识符，例如零件编号
Vector search is weak precisely where keyword search is strong on exact identifiers like a part number,

3807
06:13:22,064 --> 06:13:24,068
错误代码或政策编号。
an error code, or a policy number.

3808
06:13:24,464 --> 06:13:31,716
这就是为什么严肃的生产系统同时运行两者并合并结果，而这种组合就是混合搜索的含义。
That is why serious production systems run both and combine the results, and that combination is what hybrid search means.

3809
06:13:33,584 --> 06:13:42,788
缩写为 HNSW 的分层可导航小世界构建了一个分层的图，其中每个向量都链接到其近邻。
Hierarchical navigable small world abbreviated HNSW builds a layered graph where each vector links to its near neighbors.

3810
06:13:43,278 --> 06:13:48,036
因此，搜索是在图中跳向答案，而不是检查所有内容。
So a search hops through the graph towards the answer rather than checking everything.

3811
06:13:48,846 --> 06:13:53,636
它速度快且准确，因为它把整个结构都保存在内存中，但代价是成本高。
It is fast and accurate and it holds the whole structure in memory, which is the cost.

3812
06:13:54,286 --> 06:13:55,344
转换后的文件
Converted file

3813
06:13:56,814 --> 06:14:01,476
而是将向量分组到集群中，并只搜索最近的几个集群。
instead groups vectors into clusters and searches only the nearest few clusters.

3814
06:14:02,222 --> 06:14:07,652
这使用的内存少得多，但可能会漏掉那些刚好在所查集群之外的结果。
That uses far less memory and can miss a result sitting just outside the clusters it examined.

3815
06:14:08,590 --> 06:14:10,148
两者都是近似值。
Both are approximate.

3816
06:14:10,766 --> 06:14:17,668
Flat 是精确匹配并与每个向量进行比较，这对于成千上万个数据没问题，但处理数百万个时就不可能了。
Flat is exact and compares against every vector, which is fine for thousands and impossible for millions.

3817
06:14:19,406 --> 06:14:23,812
有 6 个地方，而考试主要考查的是推理逻辑，而不是背诵列表。
6 places and the exam mostly tests the reasoning rather than the list.

3818
06:14:25,390 --> 06:14:27,460
前两个选项涵盖了大部分题目。
The first two carry most of the questions.

3819
06:14:27,758 --> 06:14:34,756
考虑这样一个场景：已经在运行 Aurora PostgreSQL，并希望在关系型数据旁边增加嵌入。
Consider a scenario already running Aurora Postgree SQL that wants embeddings beside its relational data.

3820
06:14:35,374 --> 06:14:39,556
PG vector 将所有内容保存在同一个数据库中，避免了引入第二个系统。
Pig vector keeps everything in one database and avoids a second system.

3821
06:14:40,494 --> 06:14:46,688
如果场景描述的是具有过滤和相关性的大规模生产级语义搜索，那么 OpenSearch 就是答案。
If a scenario describes production semantic search at scale with filtering and relevance, open search is the answer.

3822
06:14:46,928 --> 06:14:55,044
S3 是最新加入的选项，它遵循本课程反复提到的存储模式，用延迟换取更低的价格。
S3 vectors is the newest entry and it follows the storage pattern this course keeps returning to, trading latency for a much lower price.

3823
06:14:55,728 --> 06:15:00,324
这适用于偶尔查询的大量嵌入存档。
That suits large archives of embeddings that are queried occasionally.

3824
06:15:01,902 --> 06:15:06,468
让这个问题变得可考查的逻辑，正是本课程应用于所有内容的逻辑。
The framing that makes this examinable is the one this course applies to everything.

3825
06:15:06,928 --> 06:15:13,124
自行构建检索意味着要将文档拆分成分块，并为每个分块调用一个嵌入模型。
Building retrieval yourself means splitting documents into chunks and calling an embedding model for each.

3826
06:15:14,126 --> 06:15:15,844
然后存储这些向量，
Then storing the vectors,

3827
06:15:16,526 --> 06:15:21,284
在文档变化时保持它们更新，并编写检索逻辑。
keeping them current as document change, and writing the retrieval logic.

3828
06:15:22,254 --> 06:15:25,156
这是一个真正的流水线，且涉及真实的维护工作。
That is a genuine pipeline with genuine maintenance.

3829
06:15:25,488 --> 06:15:33,508
知识库通过配置来完成所有这些操作，代价是对细节的控制力较弱，尤其是关于文档如何分块的部分。
A knowledge base does all of it as configuration at the cost of less control over the details, particularly how documents are chunked.

3830
06:15:34,350 --> 06:15:46,528
因此，强调“运维开销最低”的问题指向知识库，而描述特定分块或过滤要求的题目则指向自行构建。
So a question emphasizing least operational overhead points at knowledge bases and one describing a specific chunking or filtering requirement points at building it.

3831
06:15:47,822 --> 06:15:53,668
一家保险公司在 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 上运行其保单管理系统。
An insurance company runs its policy administration system on Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL.

3832
06:15:54,734 --> 06:16:05,316
它想在保单文档上增加语义搜索，这样当理赔员搜索因水管破裂造成的漏水损失时，即使措辞不同也能找到相关的条款。
It wants to add semantic search over policy documents so that an adjuster searching for cover for water damage from a burst pipe finds relevant clauses even when the wording differs.

3833
06:16:06,158 --> 06:16:08,516
大约有 200 万个文档分块。
There are around 2 million document chunks.

3834
06:16:09,568 --> 06:16:16,356
搜索还必须按保单类型和生效日期进行过滤，这些都是 Aurora 数据库中已有的列。
Searches must also filter by policy type and effective date, which are columns already in the Aurora database.

3835
06:16:17,230 --> 06:16:20,388
团队规模较小，并希望避免运行另一个系统。
The team is small and wants to avoid running another system.

3836
06:16:21,326 --> 06:16:23,396
数据工程师应该推荐什么？
What should the data engineer recommend?

3837
06:16:25,454 --> 06:16:31,652
A. 使用 PG vector 并配合 HNSW 索引，将嵌入存储在 Aurora PostgreSQL 中。
store the embeddings in Aurora PostgreSQL using PG vector with an HNSW index.

3838
06:16:32,048 --> 06:16:37,284
B. 部署一个 Amazon OpenSearch 服务并在其中对嵌入进行索引。
b Deploy an Amazon OpenSource Service Domain and index the embeddings there.

3839
06:16:37,678 --> 06:16:42,768
C. 将嵌入存储在 Amazon MemoryDB 中，以获得尽可能低的延迟。
C. Store the embeddings in Amazon MemoryDB for the lowest possible latency.

3840
06:16:43,150 --> 06:16:43,408
D
D

3841
06:16:44,526 --> 06:16:49,728
使用 Amazon Athena 来查询存储在 Amazon S3 中的文档文本。
Use Amazon Athena to search the document text stored in Amazon S3.

3842
06:16:50,350 --> 06:16:51,780
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

3843
06:16:58,510 --> 06:17:01,988
答案是 A，而选项 B 的干扰性很强。
The answer is A, and option B is deliberately strong.

3844
06:17:02,448 --> 06:17:10,532
在有高要求搜索需求的大规模生产环境中，OpenSearch 确实是更好的选择。而且两张幻灯片前我们就讲到过这一点。
Open search genuinely is the better production choice at large scale with demanding search requirements. And this course said so two slides ago.

3845
06:17:11,374 --> 06:17:20,836
这里提示点在于：一个小团队想要一个系统，更关键的是过滤列已经存在于 Aurora 中。
What tips it here is the combination of a small team wanting one system and more decisively the filter columns already living in Aurora.

3846
06:17:22,222 --> 06:17:28,964
使用 PG vector 时，按策略类型过滤并按相似度搜索只需要一条 SQL 语句。
With PG vector, filtering by policy type and searching by similarity is one SQL statement.

3847
06:17:29,870 --> 06:17:35,044
而使用 OpenSearch 时，向量在系统中，过滤属性在另一个系统中。
With OpenSearch, the vectors are in one system and the filter attributes in another.

3848
06:17:35,374 --> 06:17:39,108
所以要么你得复制它们，要么你就得查询两次然后合并结果。
So either you duplicate them or you query twice and combine.

3849
06:17:40,846 --> 06:17:45,808
一家媒体公司正在为 80 多万篇帮助文章构建一个支持助手。
A media company is building a support assistant over 800,000 help articles.

3850
06:17:46,126 --> 06:17:53,572
它需要语义检索、针对精确产品代码的关键词匹配、按产品线过滤以及相关性微调。
It needs semantic retrieval, keyword matching for exact product codes, filtering by product line, and relevance tuning.

3851
06:17:55,182 --> 06:17:59,844
查询量很大，且延迟必须控制在 200 毫秒以内。
Query volume is high and latency must stay under 200 milliseconds.

3852
06:18:00,558 --> 06:18:04,260
该公司有一个平台团队，有能力运营基础设施。
The company has a platform team with capacity to operate infrastructure.

3853
06:18:04,654 --> 06:18:06,564
哪种向量数据库最合适？
Which vector store fits best?

3854
06:18:07,054 --> 06:18:12,164
A. 对于这个规模的语料库，使用 Amazon S3 以获得最低的存储成本。
a Amazon S3 vectors for the lowest storage cost at this corpus size.

3855
06:18:12,718 --> 06:18:18,084
B. 使用带有 HNSW 索引和混合搜索的 Amazon OpenSearch 服务。
B Amazon Open Search Service with HNSW indexing and hybrid search.

3856
06:18:18,448 --> 06:18:18,688
C
C

3857
06:18:19,726 --> 06:18:24,196
Aurora PostgreSQL，配合 PG vector 和 IVF flat 索引。
Aurora PostgreSQL with PG vector and an IVF flat index.

3858
06:18:24,608 --> 06:18:24,848
D。
D.

3859
06:18:25,326 --> 06:18:29,252
Amazon Neptune Analytics，将文章视为连接的节点。
Amazon Neptune Analytics treating articles as connected nodes.

3860
06:18:30,126 --> 06:18:31,332
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

3861
06:18:38,062 --> 06:18:41,764
答案是 B，这个题目特意和之前的场景做了对比。
The answer is B, and this pairs with the previous scenario on purpose.

3862
06:18:43,214 --> 06:18:48,324
在那个例子中，Aurora 胜出是因为过滤列就在里面，且团队想要一个系统。
There, Aurora won because the filter columns already lived there and the team wanted one system.

3863
06:18:49,486 --> 06:18:56,004
而在本题中，并没有涉及关系型数据。要求明确提到了语义匹配和精确关键词匹配。
Here there is no relational data in the picture. The requirement explicitly names both semantic and exact keyword matching.

3864
06:18:56,878 --> 06:18:59,268
这里有一个能够运行基础设施的团队。
There is a team able to run infrastructure.

3865
06:19:00,366 --> 06:19:08,964
在语义含义的同时包含精确的产品代码，这就是混合搜索的定义，而这也是 OpenSearch 的强项。
Exact product codes alongside semantic meaning is the definition of hybrid search, which is open search's particular strength.

3866
06:19:09,806 --> 06:19:19,012
选项 A 在一个明确提到的数值上失败了，注意到延迟预算排除了成本优化型存储，是这里的一个通用技能。
Option A fails on a single stated number, and noticing that a latency budget rules out a cost-optimized store is a transferable skill here.

3867
06:19:20,718 --> 06:19:27,044
模块 1 的计费单位规则在这里同样适用，有两行内容值得特别强调一下。
Module 1's billing unit rule applies here, unchanged, and two rows are worth calling out specifically.

3868
06:19:27,502 --> 06:19:36,452
Dynamo DB 在清晰提供两种模型并允许在不中断的情况下切换之间非常特殊，这使得切换本身成为一个真正的成本杠杆。
Dynamo DB is unusual in offering both models cleanly and letting you switch between them without downtime, which makes the switch itself a genuine cost lever.

3869
06:19:37,358 --> 06:19:44,464
题目描述了一个流量波动巨大的表运行在预留容量上，这就指向了按需模式。
A question describing a table with widely variable traffic sitting on provision capacity is pointing at on demand.

3870
06:19:45,038 --> 06:19:48,196
本模块中的第六个实战案例正是这种情况。
The sixth worked scenario in this module is exactly that.

3871
06:19:48,624 --> 06:19:51,626
OpenSearch Serverless 有最低容量底线。
Open search serverless carries a minimum capacity floor.

3872
06:19:52,224 --> 06:19:55,332
这使得它在处理小负载时成本出奇地高。
That makes it surprisingly expensive for a small workload.

3873
06:19:56,110 --> 06:20:02,180
对于一个规模较小、且有严格成本约束的向量数据库，题目可能会指向完全不同的选项。
A question about a modest vector store with tight cost constraints may point somewhere else entirely.

3874
06:20:02,704 --> 06:20:08,196
MemoryDB 在这里每 GB 的成本高出很多，因为内存是
Memory DB is the costliest per gigabyte here by a wide margin because memory is

3875
06:20:09,806 --> 06:20:16,064
一个应用将会话状态写入 Amazon Dynamo DB，其提供的写入容量单位为 4000。
an application writes session state to Amazon Dynamo DB with provision capacity of 4000.

3876
06:20:16,544 --> 06:20:18,064
写入容量单位。
Ride capacity units.

3877
06:20:18,304 --> 06:20:24,304
流量高度集中在每天晚上的 2 小时窗口内，其余时间几乎为零。
Traffic is heavily concentrated in a 2 hour window each evening and near zero for the rest of the day.

3878
06:20:24,464 --> 06:20:27,652
在高峰期，写入操作偶尔会被限流。
During the peak, writes are occasionally throttled.

3879
06:20:28,366 --> 06:20:35,492
在高峰期之外，利用率低于 5%。团队希望降低成本并停止限流。
Outside it, utilization sits below 5%. The team wants to reduce cost and stop the throttling.

3880
06:20:36,398 --> 06:20:38,020
数据工程师应该怎么做？
What should the data engineer do?

3881
06:20:38,798 --> 06:20:47,748
A. 将写入容量单位增加到 8000，B. 将表切换到按需容量模式。
a increase provision capacity to 8000, write capacity units, b switch the table to on-demand capacity mode.

3882
06:20:49,104 --> 06:20:49,424
C
C

3883
06:20:50,670 --> 06:20:55,364
启用 Dynamo DB 自动扩缩容，保持相同的最小值并提高最大值。
Enable Dynamo DB auto scaling with the same minimum and a higher maximum.

3884
06:20:55,824 --> 06:20:56,144
D。
D.

3885
06:20:56,654 --> 06:20:59,460
添加全局二级索引来分散负载。
Add a global secondary index to spread the right load.

3886
06:21:00,046 --> 06:21:01,380
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3887
06:21:08,078 --> 06:21:09,444
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3888
06:21:09,744 --> 06:21:16,516
选项 C 值得考虑，因为自动扩缩容是解决此类问题的有效方案，也是许多团队的做法。
Option C deserves respect because autoscaling is a real answer to this shape of problem and it is what many teams do.

3889
06:21:16,704 --> 06:21:22,276
但它忽略了一个细节：自动扩缩容是在监测到使用情况后才进行调整。
It loses on the detail that autoscaling responds to observed usage adjusting after load rises.

3890
06:21:23,022 --> 06:21:29,028
因此，在容量赶上需求之前，剧烈的 2 小时高峰可能会导致限流。
So a sharp 2 hour spike can throttle during the ramp before capacity catches up.

3891
06:21:31,662 --> 06:21:33,924
选项 D 是可以排除的。
Option D is the one to be sure about.

3892
06:21:34,304 --> 06:21:38,384
全局二级索引并不是一种负载分担机制。
A global secondary index is not a load spreading mechanism.

3893
06:21:38,798 --> 06:21:42,864
写入基础表中的每一次操作，都会同时产生一次对索引的写入。
Every write to the base table generates a write to the index as well.

3894
06:21:43,086 --> 06:21:47,972
所以增加一个索引会增加写入容量消耗，而不是减少它。
So adding one increases consume write capacity rather than reducing it.

3895
06:21:49,422 --> 06:21:53,636
这个提醒是一个非常有用的细节，并且经常出现在题目中。
The callout is a genuinely useful detail and it appears in questions.

3896
06:21:53,984 --> 06:22:01,476
通过扫描将大型 DynamoDB 表复制到数据湖时，会读取每个项目并为所有项收取读取容量费用。
Copying a large DynamoDB table into a data lake by scanning it reads every item and charges read capacity for all of them.

3897
06:22:02,030 --> 06:22:06,144
这可能会非常昂贵，并且会影响共享该容量的应用程序。
That can be expensive and can affect the application sharing that capacity.

3898
06:22:06,798 --> 06:22:10,212
而导出到 S3 功能则是从持续备份中读取。
The export to S3 feature reads from a continuous backup instead.

3899
06:22:10,624 --> 06:22:15,108
因此它完全不消耗表容量，也不会与生产流量产生竞争。
So it consumes no table capacity at all and does not compete with production traffic.

3900
06:22:15,584 --> 06:22:23,584
当一个选项提供通过扫描来提取数据用于分析，而另一个选项提供导出到 S3 时，通常选后者。
When an option offers a scan to extract data for analytics and another offers export to S3, the export is almost always intended.

3901
06:22:24,782 --> 06:22:28,324
一家公司在 Amazon DynamoDB 中存储订单记录。
A company stores order records in Amazon DynamoDB.

3902
06:22:28,654 --> 06:22:34,276
分析团队需要将包含约 2 亿条项目的完整订单历史记录，每天导入到数据湖中用于报告。
The analytics team needs the full order history in the data lake daily for reporting around 200 million items.

3903
06:22:34,544 --> 06:22:37,252
目前的流程是在夜间运行并行扫描。
The current process runs a parallel scan overnight.

3904
06:22:37,902 --> 06:22:47,396
该扫描消耗了大部分表的预置读取容量，导致面向客户的应用程序在夜间时段出现被限流的读取。
The scan consumes most of the table's provisioned read capacity, and the customer-facing application has started seeing throttled reads during the overnight window.

3905
06:22:47,886 --> 06:22:49,956
数据工程师应该采取什么措施？
What should the data engineer implement?

3906
06:22:50,734 --> 06:22:57,028
a 使用 Dynamo DB 导出到 Amazon S3，这不消耗表的读取容量。
a Use Dynamo DB export to Amazon S3, which consumes no table read capacity.

3907
06:22:59,118 --> 06:23:03,460
b 为夜间时段增加表的预置读取容量。
Increase the table's provisioned read capacity for the overnight window.

3908
06:23:04,046 --> 06:23:09,744
c. 以较低的速率限制运行扫描，这样虽然耗时更长，但消耗的容量更少。
C. Run the scan with a lower rate limit so it takes longer but uses less capacity.

3909
06:23:10,064 --> 06:23:10,384
d。
D.

3910
06:23:10,734 --> 06:23:15,684
d. 启用 Dynamo DB 流并根据变更记录重建完整的历史记录。
Enable Dynamo DB streams and rebuild the full history from the change records.

3911
06:23:17,006 --> 06:23:18,148
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3912
06:23:24,878 --> 06:23:26,436
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3913
06:23:27,200 --> 06:23:39,492
选项 B 和 C 都承认导出操作会与应用程序产生竞争，并试图去管理这种竞争。一个是购买更多容量，另一个是放慢导出速度。
Options B and C both accept that the export competes with the application and try to manage that competition. One buys more capacity, the other slows the export down.

3914
06:23:40,334 --> 06:23:46,692
导出功能不是在管理竞争，而是消除了竞争，因为它根本不会触及表的吞吐量。
The export feature removes the competition rather than managing it because it never touches the table's provision throughput.

3915
06:23:47,470 --> 06:23:49,892
选项 D 作为一种类别错误值得了解。
Option D is worth knowing as a category error.

3916
06:23:50,240 --> 06:23:56,516
Dynamo DB 流会实时传输变更，并提供 24 小时的保留时间，正如模块 8 所涵盖的内容。
Dynamo DB streams carry changes as they happen with 24 hours of retention as module 8 covered.

3917
06:23:57,070 --> 06:24:01,348
因此它们只能保持副本处于最新状态，无法生成早于这些记录的历史数据。
So they can keep a copy current and cannot produce a history that predates them.

3918
06:24:02,958 --> 06:24:10,756
这张表是作为查阅项存在的，第一行值得跨领域记忆，而不是仅仅作为 Dynamo DB 的一个事实点。
This table is the module as a lookup, and the first row is worth carrying between domains rather than learning as a dynamo DB fact.

3919
06:24:12,398 --> 06:24:19,280
当整体利用率看起来正常但仍发生限流时，意味着负载是集中分布的，而非过载。
Throttling that occurs while overall utilization looks comfortable means the load is concentrated rather than excessive.

3920
06:24:19,920 --> 06:24:27,748
这同样适用于模块 3 中的 Kinesis 分片、这里的 Dynamo DB 分区以及模块 10 中的 Redshift 切片。
That is equally true of kinesis shards in module 3, dynamo DB partitions here, and redshift slices in module 10.

3921
06:24:28,080 --> 06:24:33,860
在每种情况下，增加容量都无法解决问题，因为集中分布依然存在，而更改键值则能成功。
In every case, adding capacity fails because the concentration survives it and changing the key succeeds.

3922
06:24:34,478 --> 06:24:40,740
识别出换了不同服务名称但本质相同的故障模式，是本次考试中价值最高的技能之一。
Recognizing a familiar failure mode wearing a different services name is one of the highest value skills for this exam.

3923
06:24:41,902 --> 06:24:45,572
模块 21 关于混淆对的内容会特意回到这个点。
Module 21 on confusion pairs returns to it deliberately.

3924
06:24:46,254 --> 06:24:50,020
第四行是最新的内容，值得作为独立的答案来记住。
The fourth row is the newest and worth remembering as its own answer.

3925
06:24:51,726 --> 06:24:54,660
一家公司正在为四种工作负载选择存储方案。
A company is choosing a store for four workloads.

3926
06:24:54,960 --> 06:24:59,172
一种是按客户 ID 读取的购物车，要求毫秒级延迟。
A shopping cart read by customer ID with millisecond latency.

3927
06:25:00,110 --> 06:25:05,348
一种是分析师查询的三年销售历史，涉及各种即席 SQL 查询。
A three-year sales history queried by analysts with varied ad hoc SQL.

3928
06:25:06,830 --> 06:25:09,540
一种是购物者输入自由文本的产品搜索。
A product search where shoppers type free text.

3929
06:25:10,542 --> 06:25:15,716
一种是追踪账户间连接到任意深度的欺诈调查工具。
A fraud investigation tool tracing connections between accounts to arbitrary depth.

3930
06:25:17,454 --> 06:25:25,380
一位架构师建议将这四项全部放入 Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL 中，以保证一致性并减少系统的数量。
An architect proposes putting all four in Amazon Aurora Post-Gree SQL for consistency and to reduce the number of systems.

3931
06:25:26,734 --> 06:25:28,868
数据工程师该如何回答？
How should the data engineer respond?

3932
06:25:29,550 --> 06:25:30,880
A. 同意。
a agree.

3933
06:25:31,886 --> 06:25:36,484
一个系统更易于操作，而且 PostgreSQL 可以满足这四个需求。
One system is simpler to operate and PostgreSQL can serve all four.

3934
06:25:37,006 --> 06:25:44,484
B. 分别推荐 Dynamo DB、Redshift、OpenSearch 和 Neptune，让每个工作负载匹配其对应的访问模式。
b Recommend Dynamo DB, Redshift, OpenSearch and Neptune respectively, matching each workload to its access pattern.

3935
06:25:45,038 --> 06:25:51,108
C. 为这四个需求全部推荐 Amazon Redshift，因为它既能处理操作性查询也能处理分析型查询。
C. Recommend Amazon Redshift for all four since it handles both operational and analytical queries.

3936
06:25:52,800 --> 06:25:52,960
D。
D.

3937
06:25:54,190 --> 06:25:57,860
前两个推荐 Aurora，后两个推荐 OpenSearch。
Recommend Aurora for the first two and OpenSearch for the other two.

3938
06:25:58,510 --> 06:25:59,620
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3939
06:26:06,318 --> 06:26:13,988
答案是 B。这个模块到此结束，因为它属于不同领域中第 5 个模块的最后一个场景。
The answer is B and this closes the module deliberately because it is module 5's final scenario in a different domain.

3940
06:26:15,054 --> 06:26:21,700
在那道题里，四个工作负载对应四个处理引擎，而那个诱人的错误选项是统一使用一个系统。
There, four workloads pointed at four processing engines, and the tempting wrong answer was to standardize on one.

3941
06:26:22,606 --> 06:26:29,124
在这里，四个访问模式指向四个存储系统，同样的直觉会导致同样的错误。
Here, four access patterns point at four stores, and the same instinct produces the same failure.

3942
06:26:29,840 --> 06:26:34,724
标准化确实是工程上的优点，考试并不反对这种做法。
Standardization is a real engineering virtue, and the exam is not against it.

3943
06:26:35,374 --> 06:26:42,660
但它反对在工作负载本质特征迥异时强行统一，而这道题已经非常清晰地描述了这四个不同的形态。
It is against applying it where the workloads have genuinely different shapes, and this question describes four shapes as clearly as it can.

3944
06:26:44,366 --> 06:26:49,120
一共五个问题，其中第二个是本模块中能最快排除掉的选项。
Five questions, and the second is the fastest elimination available in this module.

3945
06:26:49,280 --> 06:26:55,044
这是因为特定的技术名称通常能在一步之内将四个选项缩小到一个。
That is because a name technology usually reduces four options to one in a single step.

3946
06:26:55,760 --> 06:27:01,220
第四个问题值得练习，因为题目中的延迟数值绝非装饰性的。
The fourth is worth practicing because latency numbers in questions are never decorative.

3947
06:27:02,190 --> 06:27:10,788
微秒意味着内存处理，毫秒意味着键值或关系型存储，而秒级则意味着分析引擎。
Microseconds means in memory, milliseconds means a key value or relational store, and seconds means an analytical engine.

3948
06:27:13,454 --> 06:27:21,732
题目给出一个没有任何选项能达到的数值，就是为了排除掉最具有吸引力的干扰项，这正是场景 5 中发生的情况。
A stated number that no option can meet is how a question eliminates its most attractive distractor, which is exactly what happened in scenario 5.

3949
06:27:22,606 --> 06:27:29,540
下一个模块涵盖目录管理，这是让本模块和上一个模块中的所有内容都能被发现的关键。
Next module covers cataloging, which is how everything in this module and the last becomes discoverable.

3950
06:27:31,200 --> 06:27:40,836
这个模块结束了领域 2，并兑现了我们在第 2 个模块中做出的承诺，即在这里会涵盖目录和爬虫。
This module closes domain 2 and it delivers a promise made back in module 2, which said the catalog and crawlers would be covered here.

3951
06:27:41,520 --> 06:27:47,716
它包含了考试指南中的 9 项独立技能，是整个课程中内容最多的模块之一。
It carries 9 separate skills from the exam guide, the second highest of any module in the course.

3952
06:27:48,622 --> 06:27:57,892
之所以包含这么多内容，是因为目录处于核心位置：一侧是存储，另一侧是查询引擎，上方则是权限层。
So much lands here because a catalog sits between everything else storage on one side, query engines on the other, and permissions layered on top of it.

3953
06:27:58,702 --> 06:28:02,852
如果没有目录，数据湖就只是一堆没人能找到的文件。
Without a catalog, a data lake is a collection of files nobody can find.

3954
06:28:03,758 --> 06:28:11,108
我们将涵盖技术目录、表和分区如何进入其中，以及当模式发生变化时会发生什么。
We cover the technical catalog, how tables and partitions get into it, what happens when schemas change.

3955
06:28:12,558 --> 06:28:17,732
然后是随着最新考试指南修订而加入的业务目录和血缘层。
Then the business catalog and lineage layer that arrived with the latest exam guide revision.

3956
06:28:19,278 --> 06:28:24,420
本课程中的每一个查询引擎都是通过读取目录来工作的，而不是直接查看文件。
Every query engine in this course reads through a catalog rather than looking at files directly.

3957
06:28:25,056 --> 06:28:32,740
Athena、Redshift Spectrum、Amazon、EMR 和 AWS Glue 都会首先询问同一个问题。
Athena, Redshift Spectrum, Amazon, EMR, and AWS Glue all ask the same question first.

3958
06:28:34,542 --> 06:28:35,600
“有哪些表存在？”
What tables exist?

3959
06:28:35,886 --> 06:28:37,188
“它们有哪些列？”
What columns do they have?

3960
06:28:37,454 --> 06:28:39,300
“数据到底存储在哪里？”
And where does the data actually live?

3961
06:28:40,302 --> 06:28:49,040
Glue 数据目录一次性回答了这些问题，同时解决了所有问题，这就是湖仓架构成为可能的原因
The Glue Data Catalog answers that question once, for all of them at the same time, which is what makes a lake house possible

3962
06:28:49,200 --> 06:28:49,540
根本原因。
at all.

3963
06:28:50,414 --> 06:28:59,140
这就是为什么它在词频分析中出现了 52 次，尽管它是一个元数据存储，而不是处理数据的组件。
That is why it appeared 52 times in the bank analyze for discourse, despite being a metadata store rather than something that processes data.

3964
06:29:00,078 --> 06:29:05,540
如果目录搞错了，下游的每一个引擎都会以完全相同的方式出错。
Get the catalog wrong, and every engine downstream is wrong in exactly the same way.

3965
06:29:06,254 --> 06:29:10,724
这就是它如此重要且值得专门设立一个模块的原因。
That is what makes it so examinable and why it earns a module of its own.

3966
06:29:12,480 --> 06:29:16,676
这个区别贯穿整个模块，所以现在就把它搞清楚。
This distinction runs through the whole module, so fix it now.

3967
06:29:17,038 --> 06:29:21,252
技术目录的存在是为了让查询引擎能够规划查询。
A technical catalog exists so that a query engine can plan a query.

3968
06:29:21,934 --> 06:29:29,604
它知道一个表有 14 个列，其中第三个是时间戳，并且数据位于特定的 S3 前缀下。
It knows a table has 14 columns, that the third one is a timestamp and that the data sits under a particular S3 prefix.

3969
06:29:30,446 --> 06:29:33,860
但它对这个表代表什么意义一无所知。
It knows nothing whatsoever about what the table means.

3970
06:29:34,160 --> 06:29:39,172
业务目录的存在是为了让用户能够找到他们不知道存在的那些数据。
A business catalog exists so that a person can find data they did not know existed.

3971
06:29:39,520 --> 06:29:45,092
这样他们就可以判断这是否是正确的数据集，查看谁拥有它，并申请访问权限。
They can then judge whether it is the right data set, see who owns it, and request access.

3972
06:29:46,094 --> 06:29:53,764
考试指南 1.1 版本将业务目录作为一项独立技能加入，因此现在题目可能会涉及其中任何一种。
Version 1.1 of the exam guide added business catalogs as a separate skill, so questions can now be about either one.

3973
06:29:55,278 --> 06:29:59,200
最后一项会误导一些人，它是一个非常合理的考题。
The last bullet catches people out and it makes a fair exam question.

3974
06:29:59,502 --> 06:30:03,844
从数据目录中删除一个表只是删除了数据所在位置的描述
Dropping a table from the data catalog removes the description of where the data is,

3975
06:30:05,582 --> 06:30:10,500
它并不会移动任何文件，文件的存储位置和成本保持不变。
leaves every file exactly where it was, costing exactly what it did before.

3976
06:30:11,214 --> 06:30:14,820
这有时是你想要的，但更多时候这是一个意外情况。
That is occasionally what you want, and it is more often a surprise.

3977
06:30:15,534 --> 06:30:25,280
特别强调的高 Metastore 兼容性是目录如此核心的原因。Apache Hive 多年前就定义了 Metastore 接口。
The high Metastore compatibility in the call out is the reason the catalog is so central to everything. Apache Hive defined a Metastore interface years ago.

3978
06:30:25,454 --> 06:30:30,596
整个开源生态系统都支持它，而 Glue 数据目录实现了这一标准。
The whole open source ecosystem speaks it and the Glue Data Catalog implements it.

3979
06:30:31,278 --> 06:30:39,492
因此 EMR 上的 Spark 可以直接将其作为元数据存储，无需转换层，迁移过来的 Hadoop 环境也能正常运行。
So Spark on EMR uses it as its metastore with no translation layer, and a migrating Hadoop estate simply keeps working.

3980
06:30:41,134 --> 06:30:48,036
考试指南将为目录创建源和目标连接列为一项独立技能，这就是这张幻灯片存在的意义。
The exam guide names creating source and target connections for cataloging as its own skill, which is why this slide exists.

3981
06:30:48,974 --> 06:30:51,556
值得理解的能力是第四个要点。
The capability worth understanding is the fourth bullet.

3982
06:30:52,494 --> 06:31:01,988
将爬虫指向 JDBC 连接会读取数据库自身的元数据，并创建描述它的目录表，而无需复制任何一行数据。
Pointing a crawler at a JDBC connection reads the database's own metadata and creates catalog tables describing it without copying a single row.

3983
06:31:02,446 --> 06:31:10,692
这能让你清晰地看到运营数据库中存在的内容，这通常是规划迁移或集成的第一步。
That gives you a searchable picture of what exists in an operational database, which is often the first step in planning a migration or an integration.

3984
06:31:11,694 --> 06:31:17,508
最后一个要点是一个实际的警告，也是模块 2 连接部分的规则再次适用。
The last bullet is the practical warning, and it is module 2's connectivity section applying again.

3985
06:31:18,126 --> 06:31:22,820
如果连接无法到达数据库，那么在任何目录建立之前就无法进行。
A connection that cannot reach the database phase before any cataloging happens.

3986
06:31:24,366 --> 06:31:29,796
爬虫是知名度最高的选项，但往往不是最佳选择，这就是为什么这个提示很重要。
Crawlers are the best known option and frequently not the best one, which is why the callout matters.

3987
06:31:31,150 --> 06:31:38,212
模块 2 提到了启用更新目录的要点，即 Glue 作业在写入数据时自动注册自己的分区。
Module 2 made this point about enable update catalog where a blue job registers its own partitions as it writes them.

3988
06:31:39,086 --> 06:31:47,108
这从设计中移除了一个整个定时组件，同时也消除了数据落地到可查询之间的时间延迟。
That removes an entire scheduled component from the design, along with the delay between data landing and becoming queryable.

3989
06:31:47,568 --> 06:31:52,228
当模式已知且稳定时，显式 DDL 是正确的答案。
Explicit DDL is the right answer when a schema is known and stable.

3990
06:31:53,134 --> 06:32:00,036
这是因为推断一个你已经知道的模式是多余的工作，而且有很大可能出错。
That is because inferring a schema you already know is unnecessary work with a real risk of getting it wrong.

3991
06:32:00,622 --> 06:32:06,084
所以，爬虫是当你确实不知道数据中包含什么内容时的探索工具。
So a crawler is a discovery tool for when you genuinely do not know what is in the data yet.

3992
06:32:07,598 --> 06:32:14,084
模块 2 中提到的 10 分钟计费最小时长在这里值得重申，因为它会产生一个特定的成本问题。
The 10-minute billing minimum from module 2 is worth repeating here because it produces a specific cost question.

3993
06:32:14,734 --> 06:32:22,288
如果每 5 分钟运行一次爬虫来获取新文件，而每次运行仅需 30 秒，系统仍会按 10 分钟计费。
A crawler scheduled every 5 minutes to pick up new files is billed for 10 minutes each time it runs for 30 seconds.

3994
06:32:22,862 --> 06:32:27,876
这在成本上并不划算，而“启用更新目录”功能可以免费提供同样的实时性。
That is a poor trade for freshness that enable update catalog would have given you for nothing.

3995
06:32:28,368 --> 06:32:30,948
分类器这一点的考量是实用的。
The classifier point is the practical one.

3996
06:32:31,408 --> 06:32:39,408
如果爬虫读取了不寻常的 CSV 方言或它无法识别的日志格式，会生成一个全是单字符串的
A crawler reading an unusual CSV dialect or a log format it does not recognize produces a table full of single string

3997
06:32:39,568 --> 06:32:40,036
列。
columns.

3998
06:32:41,008 --> 06:32:47,908
带有丢弃模式或定义分隔符的自定义分类器能告诉它如何正确读取文件。
A custom classifier with a drop pattern or a defined delimiter tells it how to read the file properly.

3999
06:32:49,646 --> 06:32:56,644
前两个设置是爬虫常见的问题所在，因为它们决定了当实际情况与目录不符时该如何处理。
The first two settings are where crawler questions usually live because they decide what happens when reality disagrees with the catalog.

4000
06:32:59,790 --> 06:33:02,692
假设上游系统开始发送一个额外的列。
Suppose an upstream system starts sending an extra column.

4001
06:33:03,214 --> 06:33:08,228
在“更新策略”下，爬虫会将该列添加到表中，下游的所有内容都能看到它出现。
With the update policy, the crawler adds it to the table and everything downstream sees it appear.

4002
06:33:09,070 --> 06:33:16,036
在“忽略策略”下，表保持原样，除非有人主动操作，否则新列是不可见的。
With the ignore policy, the table stays as it was and the new column is invisible until somebody acts deliberately.

4003
06:33:16,654 --> 06:33:18,148
通常情况下，两者都不是最优解。
Neither is right in general.

4004
06:33:18,956 --> 06:33:23,940
为受监管报告提供数据的精选表，可能更需要稳定性并触发警报。
A curated table feeding regulated reports probably wants stability and an alert.

4005
06:33:24,558 --> 06:33:27,844
探索区域则可能希望目录能够追踪实际情况。
A discovery area probably wants the catalog to track reality.

4006
06:33:28,782 --> 06:33:33,124
考试总是会说明你处于哪种情况中。
The exam always states which situation you are in.

4007
06:33:34,382 --> 06:33:39,408
大多数题目假设使用 Glue 数据目录，了解其他替代方案也很有价值。
Most questions assume the Blue Data catalog and it is worth knowing the alternatives exist.

4008
06:33:39,808 --> 06:33:51,140
迁移 Hadoop 环境的组织通常带有包含多年表定义的 Hive 元数据。在任何东西运行之前重写所有内容并不是好的开始方式。
An organization migrating a Hadoop estate frequently arrives with a hive metastore holding years of table definitions. Rewriting all of it before anything can run is a poor place to start.

4009
06:33:51,726 --> 06:34:01,328
目录联邦允许 Glue 将这些外部元数据与原生表一起呈现，这样 Athena 和 EMR 就可以查询，而无需先进行迁移项目
Catalog Federation lets Blue present that external metastore alongside native tables, so Athena and EMR query, both without a migration project

4010
06:34:01,488 --> 06:34:01,764
首先。
first.

4011
06:34:02,606 --> 06:34:07,396
Iceberg REST 目录是最新加入的项，并与模块 9 相关联。
The iceberg REST catalog is the newest entry and connects to module 9.

4012
06:34:08,238 --> 06:34:17,124
这是因为它作为 SageMaker Lakehouse 的开放接口，用于将表暴露给任何支持 Iceberg 的引擎。
That is because it is the open interface SageMaker Lakehouse uses to expose tables to any iceberg capable engine.

4013
06:34:18,798 --> 06:34:24,676
一个 Glue 作业按 Hive 风格的日期分区，将每日 Parquet 输出写入 Amazon S3。
A blue job writes daily parquet output to Amazon S3 under a hive style date partition.

4014
06:34:24,942 --> 06:34:33,028
每 15 分钟安排一次爬虫来注册新分区，以便分析师可以使用 Amazon Athena 查询当天的数据。
A crawler is scheduled every 15 minutes to register new partitions so that analysts can query the current day with Amazon Athena.

4015
06:34:34,318 --> 06:34:36,196
财务部门查询了 Glue 的账单。
Finance has queried the blue bill.

4016
06:34:37,008 --> 06:34:45,028
爬虫占了很大一部分费用，且分析师仍在抱怨新数据需要长达 15 分钟才能变为可见。
The crawler accounts for a large share of it and analysts still complain that new data takes up to 15 minutes to become visible.

4017
06:34:45,328 --> 06:34:47,428
数据工程师应该做些什么更改？
What should the data engineer change?

4018
06:34:48,302 --> 06:34:53,604
A. 将爬虫计划缩短到每 5 分钟，以便数据能更快显示。
a reduce the crawler schedule to every 5 minutes so data becomes visible sooner.

4019
06:34:56,814 --> 06:35:04,196
B. 在 Glue 作业上启用“更新目录”，让它自动注册自己的分区并移除爬虫。
Enable Enable Update Catalog on the glue job so it registers its own partitions and remove the crawler.

4020
06:35:04,768 --> 06:35:10,276
C. 配置爬虫仅抓取新文件夹，并保留 15 分钟的计划。
C. Configure the crawler to crawl new folders only and keep the 15 minute schedule.

4021
06:35:11,248 --> 06:35:16,868
D. 在 Athena 中将表切换到分区投影并删除已注册的分区。
D. Switch the table to partition projection in Athena and delete the registered partitions.

4022
06:35:17,550 --> 06:35:18,820
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4023
06:35:25,262 --> 06:35:30,500
答案是 B，值得注意的是这两个投诉共享同一个原因。
The answer is B, and it is worth noticing that the two complaints share one cause.

4024
06:35:32,462 --> 06:35:39,268
爬虫的存在是为了发现作业已经知道的信息，因为作业在写入文件时就选择了那个分区路径。
The crawler exists to discover something the job already knew because the job chose that partition path when it wrote the file.

4025
06:35:40,814 --> 06:35:45,124
在正确的时间进行注册可以同时消除成本和延迟。
Registering it at right time removes both the cost and the delay at once.

4026
06:35:46,094 --> 06:35:54,496
选项 D 是一个有趣的干扰项，因为分区投影确实是解决另一个问题的良策。
Option D is the interesting distractor because partition projection is genuinely a good answer to a different question.

4027
06:35:54,894 --> 06:36:02,148
它只在 Athena 中有效，因此任何读取同一张表的其他引擎都会完全失去分区感知。
It works only in Athena, so any other engine reading the same table loses partition awareness entirely.

4028
06:36:02,976 --> 06:36:09,508
本课程已经用了两个模块来强调一个目录可以为多个引擎提供服务。
This course has spent two modules establishing that one catalog serves many engines.

4029
06:36:10,990 --> 06:36:14,496
第 9 模块就提到了关于 Iceberg 的这一点，其中文件……
Module 9 made this point about iceberg, where files.

4030
06:36:14,896 --> 06:36:17,348
如果没有引用，那么它最好根本不存在。
Nothing references may as well not exist.

4031
06:36:18,222 --> 06:36:22,180
对于 Hive 风格的目录来说也是一样的，只是原因略有不同。
The same is true of a hive style catalog for a slightly different reason.

4032
06:36:23,182 --> 06:36:27,696
查询引擎不会列出 S3 前缀来发现存在哪些分区。
A query engine does not list the S3 prefix to discover what partitions exist.

4033
06:36:28,656 --> 06:36:33,668
这是因为在每次查询时列出数百万个对象会导致速度慢到无法使用。
That is because listing millions of objects would be unusably slow on every query.

4034
06:36:34,096 --> 06:36:38,948
它会去询问目录，然后只读取目录命名的路径。
It asks the catalog instead and then reads only the paths the catalog names.

4035
06:36:39,886 --> 06:36:49,188
因此，一个将新一天的写入到正确命名文件夹但未注册的作业，产生的数据在物理上是存在的且格式正确，
So a job that writes a new day's data into a correctly name folder without registering it produces data that is physically present and correctly formatted,

4036
06:36:49,678 --> 06:36:51,620
但在查询时不会返回任何内容。
returns nothing at all when queried.

4037
06:36:52,334 --> 06:36:53,732
任何地方都不会报错。
Nothing errors anywhere.

4038
06:36:54,670 --> 06:37:01,092
这种沉默正是它成为一个好考题的原因，也是本模块症状表的第一行。
That silence is exactly what makes it a good exam question, and it is the first row of this module symptom table.

4039
06:37:02,830 --> 06:37:08,452
最后一行是值得深入理解的一行，因为它解决了与其他不同的问题。
The last row is the one worth understanding properly because it solves a different problem from the others.

4040
06:37:09,422 --> 06:37:14,020
其他所有方法都是注册分区，以便目录可以列出它们。
Every other approach registers partitions so that the catalog can list them.

4041
06:37:14,958 --> 06:37:17,636
而分区投影则是告诉 Athena 规律。
Partition projection instead tells Athena the pattern.

4042
06:37:17,856 --> 06:37:21,572
例如，这些分区是 2020 年到今天之间的日期。
For example, that partitions are dates between 2020 and today.

4043
06:37:21,936 --> 06:37:26,052
Athena 在不咨询目录的情况下计算出要读取哪些路径。
Athena calculates which paths to read without consulting the catalog at all.

4044
06:37:26,638 --> 06:37:34,020
对于拥有数万个分区的表，这去除了已经成为查询最慢部分的元数据查询。
On a table with tens of thousands of partitions, that removes a metadata lookup which had become the slowest part of the query.

4045
06:37:34,670 --> 06:37:37,252
限制在于这是一个 Athena 特有的功能。
The limitation is that it is an Athena feature.

4046
06:37:37,870 --> 06:37:42,980
因此 Redshift Spectrum 和 EMR 在读取同一张表时无法从中获益。
So Redshift Spectrum and EMR reading the same table gain nothing from it.

4047
06:37:44,718 --> 06:37:47,780
这种症状非常明显，值得在考试中识别出来。
This symptom is distinctive and worth recognizing on site.

4048
06:37:48,016 --> 06:37:55,588
查询尚未开始扫描任何内容，数据量并不特殊，但在任何工作开始前有明显的延迟。
The query has not started scanning anything, the data volume is unremarkable, and there is a noticeable delay before any work begins at all.

4049
06:37:56,110 --> 06:38:01,776
那是引擎正在询问目录存在哪些分区，并收到一个非常长的列表。
That is the engine asking the catalog which partitions exist and getting back a very long list.

4050
06:38:02,638 --> 06:38:09,348
分区索引和投影。两者都直接解决这个问题，而正确的答案往往是最后一项。
Partition indexes and projection. Both attack that directly, and the honest answer is often the last bullet instead.

4051
06:38:10,030 --> 06:38:16,772
一个按小时分区、但总是按月查询的表，其分区数量比实际需要的多了 24 倍。
A table partitioned by hour that is always queried by month has 24 times more partitions than it needs.

4052
06:38:19,950 --> 06:38:24,176
粗化分区可以从根本上解决成本问题，而不是在现有结构上做优化。
Coarsening it fixes the cost rather than optimizing around it.

4053
06:38:25,518 --> 06:38:31,620
一个按小时采集的流程会将文件写入 Amazon S3，并按年、月、日和小时进行分区。
An hourly ingestion process writes files to Amazon S3 under year, month, day and hour partitions.

4054
06:38:31,856 --> 06:38:35,684
该表现在包含约 90,000 个覆盖 10 年的数据分区。
The table now holds around 90,000 partitions covering 10 years.

4055
06:38:35,936 --> 06:38:39,908
分析师仅按日期范围查询，从不按小时查询。
Analysts query it exclusively by date range, never by hour.

4056
06:38:40,494 --> 06:38:47,716
无论日期过滤条件多么精确，Athena 查询在开始扫描前都要耗费 12 到 20 秒。
Athena queries take 12 to 20 seconds before scanning begins, regardless of how narrow the date filter is.

4057
06:38:48,302 --> 06:38:51,524
一旦开始扫描，查询就会很快完成。
Once scanning starts, queries complete quickly.

4058
06:38:52,110 --> 06:38:53,988
哪种改动最有效？
What is the most effective change?

4059
06:38:54,990 --> 06:38:58,564
A. 在分区键上添加分组分区索引。
a add a group partition index on the partition keys.

4060
06:39:00,430 --> 06:39:00,736
B
B

4061
06:39:02,030 --> 06:39:06,692
仅按年、月、日重新分区数据，移除小时分区。
Repartition the data by year, month and day only, removing the hour partition.

4062
06:39:07,136 --> 06:39:07,456
C。
C.

4063
06:39:08,046 --> 06:39:10,948
增加 Athena 工作组的查询超时时间。
Increase the Athena workgroups query timeout.

4064
06:39:11,536 --> 06:39:11,856
D。
D.

4065
06:39:12,302 --> 06:39:16,644
运行 MSCK repair table 来刷新分区元数据。
Run MSCK repair table to refresh the partition metadata.

4066
06:39:17,358 --> 06:39:18,496
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

4067
06:39:25,230 --> 06:39:28,900
答案是 B，而选项 A 是故意设计的干扰项。
The answer is B, and option A is deliberately reasonable.

4068
06:39:30,990 --> 06:39:37,988
分区索引确实能加快查找速度，如果确实需要按小时分区，那么它就是正确的答案。
A partition index genuinely does speed up lookup, and if the hourly partitioning were needed, it would be the right answer here.

4069
06:39:38,478 --> 06:39:42,628
但题目明确说明分析师从不按小时查询，因此排除了这个选项。
The question rules that out by stating that analysts never query by hour.

4070
06:39:43,566 --> 06:39:48,672
这意味着每 24 个分区中就有 23 个根本没用。
That means 23 out of every 24 partitions exist for nobody at all.

4071
06:39:48,910 --> 06:39:55,748
这就是模块 8 警告过的“过度分区”故障，它表现为目录层面的症状而非存储层面的问题。
This is the overpartitioning failure module 8 warned about, arriving as a catalog symptom rather than a storage one.

4072
06:39:56,718 --> 06:40:04,004
扫描前的延迟是关键诊断细节，因为它能区分出是元数据问题还是数据量问题。
The delay before scanning is the diagnostic detail because it separates a metadata problem from a data volume problem.

4073
06:40:05,486 --> 06:40:13,764
考试指南将处理数据特征的变化列为一项技能，而“架构变更”是这一技能最典型的体现。
The exam guide names addressing changes to the characteristics of data as a skill, and schema change is the sharpest version of it.

4074
06:40:14,446 --> 06:40:18,032
上游团队在没通知任何人的情况下增加了一个字段。
An upstream team adds a field without telling anyone.

4075
06:40:18,606 --> 06:40:25,988
一个原本一直是整数的列开始出现字符串，因为有人允许了“不适用”这一含义的代码。
A column that was always an integer starts arriving as a string because somebody allowed a code meaning not applicable.

4076
06:40:27,214 --> 06:40:31,300
源系统在没人阅读的发布版本中重命名了一个字段。
A field is renamed in a source system on a release nobody read.

4077
06:40:32,110 --> 06:40:37,552
这些情况都不罕见，而且它们都会影响到已经建立好的流水线。
None of these are unusual, and all of them reach a pipeline written before they happened.

4078
06:40:38,094 --> 06:40:44,004
区分稳健设计和脆弱设计的标准不是变化是否会发生，因为变动总会发生。
What separates a robust design from a fragile one is not whether the change happens because it will.

4079
06:40:44,558 --> 06:40:49,636
而是这种变化会导致严重的报错、静默的错误结果，还是根本没反应。
It is whether the change causes a loud failure, a silent wrong answer, or nothing at all.

4080
06:40:50,350 --> 06:40:53,392
接下来的几张幻灯片将讨论这些情况分别属于哪一种。
The next few slides work through which is which.

4081
06:40:55,150 --> 06:40:57,764
类型变更这一行值得强调。
The type change row deserves the emphasis.

4082
06:40:58,414 --> 06:41:01,572
当一个数值列开始偶尔接收字符串时，
When a numeric column starts receiving occasional strings,

4083
06:41:02,286 --> 06:41:06,372
严格的 Leader 会报错，这虽然不方便但很诚实。
a strict leader fails loudly, which is inconvenient and honest.

4084
06:41:07,406 --> 06:41:15,472
宽松的 Reader 可能会将无法解析的值强制转为 null，然后对该列求和时会静默返回一个过低的数字。
A permissive reader may coerce the unparsable values to null instead, and a sum over that column then quietly returns a number that is too low.

4085
06:41:15,662 --> 06:41:18,948
没人收到警报，任务成功了，但报告是错的。
Nobody is alerted, the job succeeds, and a report is wrong.

4086
06:41:19,950 --> 06:41:32,100
模块 2 对此的对策是带有“解析选择”的动态帧，它保留两种可能性，让你做出明确决策而不是去猜。
Module 2's answer to this was the blue dynamic frame with resolve choice, which keeps both possibilities alive and makes you decide deliberately rather than guessing.

4087
06:41:32,814 --> 06:41:35,712
这就是动态帧存在的全部原因。
That is the whole reason dynamic frames exist.

4088
06:41:36,270 --> 06:41:39,108
而这正是它们存在的典型场景。
And this is precisely the scenario they exist for.

4089
06:41:40,814 --> 06:41:45,412
CSV 这一行解释了题目描述中提到的一个具体的生产事故。
The CSV row explains a specific production disaster that questions describe.

4090
06:41:45,870 --> 06:41:48,484
CSV 文件内部没有列名。
CSV has no column names inside the file.

4091
06:41:49,070 --> 06:41:55,588
因此，如果上游系统在中间插入了一个列，所有后续的列都会向左偏移一位。
So a column inserted in the middle by an upstream system shifts every subsequent column one place to the left.

4092
06:41:56,078 --> 06:41:59,492
从那一点之后的每个值都会被读入错误的字段中。
Every value after that point is then read into the wrong field.

4093
06:42:00,366 --> 06:42:06,244
日期会进入金额列，任务可能仍能成功，但数据是乱码。
Dates land in an amount column, the job may still succeed and the data is nonsense.

4094
06:42:06,574 --> 06:42:09,540
使用自描述格式就不会发生这种情况。
That cannot happen with a self-describing format.

4095
06:42:09,792 --> 06:42:12,516
Avro 是值得单独记住的行。
Avro is the row worth remembering separately.

4096
06:42:13,454 --> 06:42:21,220
因为它专为演进而设计，因此是架构经常变动的摄入层中的明智选择。
That is because it was designed for evolution and is therefore the sensible choice for an ingestion layer where schemas change often.

4097
06:42:22,894 --> 06:42:28,512
注册表是预防性方案，它能在发现模式问题的地方进行拦截。
The registry is the preventive answer and it changes where a schema problem gets discovered.

4098
06:42:28,686 --> 06:42:35,172
如果没有它，生产者开始发送变更记录。流会接受它，因为流只接收字节。
Without it, a producer starts sending a change record. The stream accepts it because a stream accepts bytes.

4099
06:42:36,078 --> 06:42:38,724
故障会在下游的某个消费者处暴露出来。
The failure surfaces in a consumer somewhere downstream.

4100
06:42:39,694 --> 06:42:44,164
那可能发生在几个小时后，而且可能是错误的数据而非报错提示。
That might be hours later, and it might be wrong data rather than an error.

4101
06:42:44,432 --> 06:42:52,100
有了注册表和兼容性规则，在尝试不兼容的更改时，生产者的行为就会被立即拒绝。
With a registry and a compatibility rule, the producer's own right is rejected at the moment the incompatible change is attempted.

4102
06:42:52,782 --> 06:43:00,132
模块 3 在提到 Amazon MSK 时顺带提到了这一点，而且它同样适用于 Kinesis 和 Flink。
Module 3 mentioned this in passing under Amazon MSK, and it is worth knowing that it works with Kinesis and Flink too.

4103
06:43:01,632 --> 06:43:05,124
这是容易被忽略的一半技能。
This is the half of the skill that gets overlooked.

4104
06:43:06,030 --> 06:43:12,868
模式本身没有变化，但由于内部数据不同，流水线依然会出现性能下降。
Nothing about the schema changed and the pipeline degrades anyway because the data inside it is different.

4105
06:43:13,550 --> 06:43:21,604
一个原本能将流量均匀分布到 100 个客户的分区键，当其中一个客户增长到占据 60% 的流量时就会出现倾斜。
A partition key that distributed traffic evenly across a hundred customers becomes skewed when one customer grows to 60% of the volume.

4106
06:43:22,542 --> 06:43:27,396
突然之间，承载该客户的 Redshift 分片或 Dynamo DB 分区就会触发限流。
Suddenly the redshift slice or Dynamo DB partition holding that customer is throttling.

4107
06:43:28,270 --> 06:43:33,060
一个按去年数据量正确配置的视图任务，无法应对今年的数据量。
A view job correctly sized for last year's volume is not sized for this year's.

4108
06:43:33,998 --> 06:43:41,508
这些都是模块 10 和 11 所描述的同类故障，只是它们是随着时间的推移产生的，而不是由于设计缺陷导致的。
These are the same failures, modules 10 and 11 described, arriving through the passage of time rather than through bad design.

4109
06:43:43,216 --> 06:43:48,740
这一页的存在是为了在进入之前将领域 2 与领域 4 连接起来。
This slide exists to connect domain 2 to domain 4 before you get there.

4110
06:43:49,216 --> 06:43:56,548
Lake Formation 不授予 S3 前缀的权限，它授予的是在数据目录中注册的表和列的权限。
Lake Formation does not grant permissions on S3 prefixes, it grants them on tables and columns registered in the data catalog.

4111
06:43:57,326 --> 06:44:04,420
这就是为什么在模块 2 的医疗场景中，在授予权限之前需要更改读取路径。
That is why module 2's healthcare scenario required changing the read path before any grant could take effect.

4112
06:44:05,294 --> 06:44:12,324
现在值得记住第二个要点中的「基于标签的方法」，因为它比按表授权更具扩展性。
The tag-based approach on the second bullet is worth recognizing by name now because it scales in a way per table grants do not.

4113
06:44:13,102 --> 06:44:20,100
你只需给一个包含个人数据的表打上标签，关于个人数据的策略就会自动应用于该表。
You tag a table as containing personal data once, and a policy about personal data applies to it automatically.

4114
06:44:20,494 --> 06:44:23,236
模块 18 会详细讲解相关的机制。
Module 18 covers the mechanics properly.

4115
06:44:24,526 --> 06:44:29,796
一个 Glue作业从合作伙伴处读取 JSON 事件，并将其写入到一个精选的 Parquet 表中。
A Glue job reads JSON events from a partner and writes parquet to a curated table.

4116
06:44:30,286 --> 06:44:33,732
上周，合作伙伴更改了一个原本一直是整数的字段。
Last week, the partner changed a field that had always been an integer.

4117
06:44:34,382 --> 06:44:39,300
现在大约 2% 的记录包含一个编码字符串，代表一个未知值。
About 2% of records now carry it as a coded string, representing an unknown value.

4118
06:44:39,918 --> 06:44:41,828
该作业仍然报告成功。
The job still reports success.

4119
06:44:42,416 --> 06:44:49,668
分析师注意到，每日总数比源系统报告的低约 2%。任何日志中都没有出现错误。
Analysts have noticed that a daily total is roughly 2% lower than the source system reports. No error appears in any log.

4120
06:44:50,222 --> 06:44:53,124
发生了什么情况？最合适的修复方法是什么？
What is happening and what is the most appropriate fix?

4121
06:44:53,616 --> 06:44:56,516
A. Glue作业正在丢弃记录。
a The blue job is dropping records.

4122
06:44:57,038 --> 06:45:00,164
增加 DPU 分配，以便处理所有记录。
Increase the DPU allocation so it processes all of them.

4123
06:45:02,510 --> 06:45:05,252
无法解析的值被强制转换为 null。
unpassable values are being coerced to null.

4124
06:45:05,646 --> 06:45:11,300
作为动态帧读取，并使用 解析选择 来显式处理这两种类型。
Read as a dynamic frame and use resolve choice to handle both types explicitly.

4125
06:45:12,238 --> 06:45:12,496
C。
C.

4126
06:45:13,056 --> 06:45:15,204
爬虫已经更新了模式。
The crawler has updated the schema.

4127
06:45:15,758 --> 06:45:18,724
将架构变更策略设置为忽略更改。
Set the schema change policy to ignore changes.

4128
06:45:19,470 --> 06:45:19,696
D。
D.

4129
06:45:20,430 --> 06:45:24,996
启用作业书签，这样作业就不会重新处理受影响的记录。
Enable job bookmarks so the job does not reprocess the affected records.

4130
06:45:26,734 --> 06:45:28,256
停下来思考一下并做决定。
Pause and decide.

4131
06:45:34,574 --> 06:45:38,276
答案是 B，数据本身就说明了原因。
The answer is B, and the numbers do the work for you.

4132
06:45:40,526 --> 06:45:45,348
2% 的记录包含无法解析的值，而总数正好低了 2%。
2% of records carry an unparsable value, and the total is 2% low.

4133
06:45:46,446 --> 06:45:48,132
这并不是巧合。
That is not a coincidence.

4134
06:45:48,816 --> 06:45:51,044
考试会故意设置干扰项让你选错。
The exam expects you to miss.

4135
06:45:51,662 --> 06:45:58,116
作业之所以成功，是因为宽松的读取将这些值变成了 null，而对 null 求和时会自动忽略它们。
The job succeeded because a permissive read turned those values into nulls and a sum over nulls simply omits them.

4136
06:45:58,446 --> 06:46:03,876
这就是在模块 6、7 以及这里的这种「静默错误」故障。
This is the silent wrongness failure that has now appeared in modules 6, 7, and here.

4137
06:46:04,334 --> 06:46:08,816
这种情况总是需要选择正确性相关的答案，而不是容量或调度相关的答案。
It always needs a correctness answer rather than a capacity or scheduling one.

4138
06:46:09,390 --> 06:46:18,372
Resolve choice 是 B。使用特定的机制让你进行转换，或者将两种类型作为独立的列保留，或者将问题记录分流到一边。
Resolve choice is Buse specific mechanism letting you cast, keep both types as separate columns or route the problem records aside.

4139
06:46:20,078 --> 06:46:27,716
模块 4 引入了这一点，它也属于这里，因为架构转换既是目录管理技能，也是迁移技术。
Module 4 introduced this and it belongs here too, because schema conversion is a cataloging skill as much as a migration.

4140
06:46:30,478 --> 06:46:30,976
1。
1.

4141
06:46:31,630 --> 06:46:34,372
值得补充的一点是评估报告。
The point worth adding is the assessment report.

4142
06:46:35,278 --> 06:46:41,764
在转换任何内容之前，工具会检查源数据并生成一个可以自动转换的对象列表。
Before converting anything, the tool inspects the source and produces a list of objects it can convert automatically.

4143
06:46:42,096 --> 06:46:43,844
需要人工处理的对象。
Objects needing manual attention.

4144
06:46:44,110 --> 06:46:45,988
完全无法转换的物体。
Objects it cannot convert at all.

4145
06:46:46,446 --> 06:46:51,716
这个清单能让异构迁移从一种猜测变成一个有规模的计划。
That list is what turns a heterogeneous migration from a guess into a plan with a size.

4146
06:46:52,558 --> 06:47:05,476
最后两项中的矛盾是真实存在的，值得了解。在“范围内服务列表”中删除了 AWSSCD，但在同一个任务陈述中仍保留了它的名称。
The contradiction on the last two bullets is real and worth knowing about. The InScope Service List dropped AWSSCD in the very same division where a task statement still names it.

4147
06:47:07,150 --> 06:47:14,724
考试指南的 1.1 版本将业务数据目录和 Amazon SageMaker 目录 作为命名技能添加进去了。
Version 1.1 of the exam guide added business data catalogs and Amazon SageMaker catalog as a named skill.

4148
06:47:15,214 --> 06:47:19,428
所以这个部分是旧版考纲不涵盖的新内容。
So this section is new material that older banks do not cover at all.

4149
06:47:20,046 --> 06:47:23,780
它解决的是组织层面的问题，而非技术层面的问题。
The problem it addresses is organizational rather than technical.

4150
06:47:24,736 --> 06:47:28,900
想象一下一家拥有跨三个账户、共 400 张表的公司。
Picture a company with 400 tables across three accounts.

4151
06:47:29,296 --> 06:47:36,004
一个需要按区域统计收入的分析师无法判断九个可能的表中哪一个是权威数据。
An analyst who needs revenue by region cannot tell which of nine plausible tables is authoritative.

4152
06:47:36,782 --> 06:47:44,996
他们无法判断这些数字是否是最新的、谁负责维护它、是否还有其他人信任它，或者如何在不四处询问的情况下获取访问权限。
They cannot tell whether the numbers are current, who owns it, whether anyone else trusts it, or how to get access without asking around.

4153
06:47:45,582 --> 06:47:50,596
Glue 数据目录无法提供任何帮助，因为这些都不是技术元数据。
The blue data catalog cannot help with any of that because none of it is technical metadata.

4154
06:47:51,086 --> 06:47:53,604
这是一个需要不同层级来解决的不同问题。
This is a different problem needing a different layer.

4155
06:47:55,278 --> 06:47:59,876
这个命名值得直接说明一下，因为这两个版本都出现在当前的文档中。
The naming is worth addressing directly because both versions appear in current documentation.

4156
06:48:00,430 --> 06:48:08,036
Amazon DataZone 是服务名称，而同样的这种能力在下一代 SageMaker 中以 SageMaker Catalog 的形式出现。
Amazon DataZone is the service, and the same capability appears inside the next generation of SageMaker as SageMaker Catalog.

4157
06:48:10,126 --> 06:48:13,348
把它们看作是从两个维度描述的同一件事。
Treat them as the same thing described from two directions.

4158
06:48:13,870 --> 06:48:20,100
最后一项中的订阅工作流是改变组织实际运作方式的关键环节。
The subscription workflow on the last bullet is the piece that changes how an organization actually works.

4159
06:48:20,590 --> 06:48:26,948
如果没有它，获取数据集权限意味着要找到正确的工程师并要求他们编写策略。
Without it, getting access to a dataset means finding the right engineer and asking them to write a policy.

4160
06:48:27,918 --> 06:48:36,580
有了它，用户请求订阅，数据所有者批准后，底层的 Lake Formation 权限就会自动授予。
With it, a consumer requests a subscription, the data owner approves it, and the underlying lake formation permissions are granted automatically.

4161
06:48:38,160 --> 06:48:45,200
这种结构出现在两个领域、四个技能中，也包含在这一项里，这说明 AWS 认为它很重要。
This structure appears in two domains, four skills as well as in this one, which tells you AWS considers it important.

4162
06:48:45,440 --> 06:48:50,116
其核心思想是：权限源于你正在从事的工作，而不是源于你是谁。
The idea is that access follows from what you are working on rather than from who you are.

4163
06:48:50,894 --> 06:48:59,812
一个人加入项目，该项目拥有某些数据集的订阅，成员身份会自动授予底层的权限。
A person joins a project, the project holds subscriptions to certain data sets, and membership grants the underlying permissions automatically.

4164
06:49:00,558 --> 06:49:03,716
当他们离开项目时，这些访问权限也会随之撤销。
When they leave the project, that access goes with them.

4165
06:49:04,590 --> 06:49:13,444
这与给个人授予表权限的模式有显著不同，后者是导致权限在多年内泛滥的原因。
It is a meaningfully different model from granting individuals permissions on tables, which is how access sprawl accumulates over years.

4166
06:49:13,998 --> 06:49:17,476
第 20 模块会从治理问题的角度再次讨论它。
Module 20 returns to it as a governance question.

4167
06:49:19,118 --> 06:49:27,360
数据血缘在 2024 年 12 月正式发布，并于一年后进入考试指南，所以这是本次考试的新内容。
Data lineage became generally available in December 2024 and entered the exam guide a year later, so it is new material for this exam.

4168
06:49:27,600 --> 06:49:32,420
标题中的两个问题是你遍历它的两个方向，两者都很重要。
The two questions in the heading are the two directions you traverse it and both matter.

4169
06:49:33,262 --> 06:49:40,132
上游：一个不信任某个数字的分析师可以追溯该数据经过的所有转换，直到源系统。
Upstream, an analyst who distrusts a figure can trace it back through every transformation to the source system.

4170
06:49:42,542 --> 06:49:48,068
这就是让一个数字在审计面前具有可信度，而不仅仅是凭空断言的原因。
That is what makes a number defensible to an auditor rather than merely asserted.

4171
06:49:48,974 --> 06:49:57,636
在下游方向，工程师在修改表之前可以看到所有读取该表的内容，这让变更从一种猜测变成了一种评估。
Downstream, an engineer about to change a table can see everything that reads it, which turns a change from a guess into an assessment.

4172
06:49:58,318 --> 06:50:04,900
一旦组织拥有超过几个流水线，仅凭记忆就无法可靠地回答这两个问题。
Both are impossible to answer reliably from memory once an organization has more than a handful of pipelines.

4173
06:50:05,806 --> 06:50:09,604
本模块中的第四个工作场景正是这种情况。
The fourth work scenario in this module is exactly that situation.

4174
06:50:11,310 --> 06:50:16,000
最后一项是框架限制，它出现在关于完整性的题目中。
The last bullet is the harness limitation and it appears in questions about completeness.

4175
06:50:16,240 --> 06:50:19,876
血缘是由处理引擎发出的事件组合而成的。
Lineage is assembled from events that processing engines emit.

4176
06:50:20,160 --> 06:50:25,040
因此，由不发出这些事件的组件执行的转换，在链条中会出现断裂。
So a transformation performed by something that does not emit them appears as a break in the

4177
06:50:25,040 --> 06:50:29,956
例如，在 EC2 实例上运行的手写脚本。
chain. A handwritten script on an EC2 instance, for example.

4178
06:50:32,000 --> 06:50:36,324
第二项中的开放血缘兼容性就是针对此问题的答案。
The open lineage compatibility on the second bullet is the answer to that.

4179
06:50:37,518 --> 06:50:42,820
这是因为它是一个开放标准，任何东西都可以被配置为向同一个图表中发布事件。
That is because it is an open standard and anything can be made to publish events into the same graph.

4180
06:50:43,630 --> 06:50:51,876
版本控制这一点值得记住，用于审计类题目，这类题目的要求是展示在数据发布时当时的血缘情况。
The versioning point is worth remembering for audit questions, where the requirement is to show what the lineage was at the time a figure was published.

4181
06:50:53,678 --> 06:50:59,360
一个数据工程团队准备更改一个广泛使用的精选表中的列的数据类型。
A data engineering team is about to change the data type of a column in a widely used curated table.

4182
06:50:59,630 --> 06:51:08,132
他们不知道哪些下游作业、仪表板和报告读取了该列，而之前一次类似的更改破坏了三个没人通知他们的报告。
They do not know which downstream jobs, dashboards, and reports read that column, and a previous similar change broke three reports nobody had been told about.

4183
06:51:08,750 --> 06:51:16,960
该环境使用 AWS Glue 进行转换，使用 Amazon Redshift 作为数据仓库，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行即时查询。
The estate uses AWS Blue for transformation, Amazon Redshift for the warehouse, and Amazon Athena for ad hoc queries.

4184
06:51:17,120 --> 06:51:20,516
团队希望在做出更改之前评估其影响。
The team wants to assess the impact before making the change.

4185
06:51:21,006 --> 06:51:22,372
团队应该使用什么？
What should the team use?

4186
06:51:22,894 --> 06:51:29,124
a 查询包含该名称列的每个表的 Glue 数据目录。
a query the AWS Blue Data Catalog for every table containing a column of that name.

4187
06:51:29,680 --> 06:51:30,000
b
b

4188
06:51:31,086 --> 06:51:36,585
使用 Amazon SageMaker Catalog 中的数据血缘来追踪列级别的下游消费者。
Use data lineage in Amazon SageMaker catalog to trace downstream consumers at column level.

4189
06:51:37,200 --> 06:51:37,520
c
C.

4190
06:51:37,760 --> 06:51:42,212
d 在 AWS CloudTrail 中搜索引用该表的 API call。
Search AWS CloudRail for AP. I call that reference the table.

4191
06:51:42,670 --> 06:51:47,716
e 启用 Glue 作业书签，以便受影响的作业可以在更改后重新处理。
D. Enable Blue job bookmarks so affected jobs can be reprocessed after the change.

4192
06:51:48,526 --> 06:51:49,764
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

4193
06:51:56,430 --> 06:51:57,508
答案是
The answer is

4194
06:52:00,174 --> 06:52:10,308
b。选项 c 是一个看似合理的错误选项，因为 CloudTrail 确实记录了谁调用了什么，而且没有血缘信息的工程师可能会从那里开始。
B Option C is the thoughtful wrong answer because Cloud Trail genuinely does record who called what, and an engineer without lineage would probably start there.

4195
06:52:10,766 --> 06:52:14,852
其中的差距在于，Cloud Trail 记录的是针对资源的 API 调用。
The gap is that Cloud Trail records API calls against resources.

